INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '0-fool', 'en', 'The Fool', '愚者', '{"keywords":["New Beginnings","Adventure","Innocence","Freedom","Trust"],"arcana":"major","number":0}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Fool symbolizes a fresh beginning and limitless possibility. This card suggests that you may be about to set out on an adventurous journey, meeting the unknown with an open mind and a sense of curiosity. It may be time to put down old baggage and welcome new experiences without assuming you already know how they will turn out. The Fool encourages you to take a first step even when the road ahead is uncertain. This is an energy of freedom and spontaneity, well suited to trying something new, learning a skill, or beginning a project. Stay lighthearted rather than becoming consumed by the outcome, and allow life to unfold as you move forward.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Fool invites you to be more careful and thoughtful. You may be making a rushed choice without considering its risks or consequences. This card can point to a lack of planning, an unclear direction, or an overly naive attitude that could make things harder for you. This may not be the moment to leap blindly; pause, assess the situation, and prepare what you need. You might be hesitating because you fear failure, or acting with so much confidence that you overlook important details. The reversed Fool suggests building a steadier foundation before you act and asking whether this choice truly fits you.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["New Beginnings","Adventure","Freedom","Innocence","Trust"],"reversed":["Recklessness","Indecision","Lack of Planning","Naivety","Fear"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Fool marks the beginning of a life journey and a willingness to explore without being ruled by prejudice or fear. As card zero, it holds many possibilities and has not yet been narrowed by experience. Its energy is light, free, and hopeful, like a child meeting the world with fresh curiosity. You do not need every answer at this stage; openness and flexibility may serve you better. The Fool’s step toward the cliff can look dangerous, yet it also represents trust in what cannot be seen. This is a leap-of-faith moment: you are invited to believe that the path can appear as you take your first steps.","reversedExplanation":"The reversed Fool can show you wavering between two extremes: being so cautious that you miss an opportunity, or acting so impulsively that you are unprepared. Innocence may become naivety, while freedom may become a lack of direction. Past pain may make you afraid to take another chance, or overconfidence may keep you from seeing practical risks. Wisdom does not mean never taking a leap; it means looking at the situation before you do. Sometimes this card appears when you are ready but fear is keeping you in place. In that case, what you need may not be more preparation, but the courage to face the fear."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Forward","type":"Outgoing and exploratory","description":"This is an outward-moving energy that explores the unknown. The Fool is curious and lively, taking steps without being bound by the past. Its flow is open and spontaneous rather than tightly controlled."},"timing":{"speed":"Fast","description":"Things may begin to unfold quickly, and an opportunity may arrive with little warning. This card favors taking a timely first step rather than waiting indefinitely. A noticeable beginning or change may appear within one to three weeks, though timing is never guaranteed."},"advice":{"upright":"Set fear aside, listen to your intuition, and take one first step. Your plan does not have to be perfect before you begin. Stay open to what you learn along the way and make room for the unexpected.","reversed":"Pause to assess the risks and make a basic plan before acting. Do not let an impulse make the decision for you; give yourself time to think it through. Ask someone you trust for another perspective and check for details you may have missed."},"chakra":{"primary":"Crown Chakra and Root Chakra","issue":"You may feel disconnected from a sense of meaning or direction (crown), or lack the grounding and security needed to move forward (root).","healingNote":"If you feel afraid or stuck, grounding practices may help you reconnect with steadiness and safety. If you are acting recklessly, consider balancing reflection with practical planning. Crystal practices can be used as a personal ritual, but they are not medical treatment; consult a qualified professional for health concerns."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your inner voice may be calling you toward a new journey. This does not have to mean acting carelessly; it can be an invitation to trust your own wisdom and take the first step. You do not need to know the entire route before you begin. Many meaningful journeys start with one brave choice.","reversed":"This card invites you to practice wise courage. It is not asking you to remain still, but to connect with your inner judgment before you act. Freedom comes from clear awareness rather than a blind leap. Give yourself enough time to prepare, while noticing whether fear is keeping you from moving forward."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '1-magician', 'en', 'The Magician', '魔術師', '{"keywords":["Manifestation","Action","Focus","Creation","Resources"],"arcana":"major","number":1}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Magician suggests that you already have many of the tools and resources needed to pursue your goal. This card is associated with creativity and the ability to turn an idea into something tangible. You may have the skills, knowledge, and determination to take initiative and influence your surroundings. The Magician brings focus and action together: it is not only about imagining what could be, but also about choosing how to begin. Make use of the opportunities available to you, trust the abilities you have developed, and let your work speak for itself. Whether you are focused on a career, learning, or personal growth, a clear intention paired with practical effort can help you make meaningful progress.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Magician asks you to look carefully at how you are using your abilities and resources. You may be doubting your skills or struggling to put your ideas into practice. The card can also point to manipulation, dishonesty, or a temptation to take a shortcut, whether that behavior is coming from you or someone around you. Your effort may not be producing the outcome you expected, or you may feel unable to make use of what you have. Reconsider your motives and methods, and make sure your actions are honest and aligned with your values. Avoid trying to force an outcome through deception or misuse of influence; those approaches tend to create further problems.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Manifestation","Initiative","Focus","Creativity","Resources at Hand"],"reversed":["Manipulation","Self-Doubt","Misused Ability","Deception","Blocked Action"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Magician represents the ability to work with what is already available to you. The card’s central idea is, “I have something I can begin with.” You do not necessarily need to wait for perfect conditions or endless preparation; the skills and resources you have gathered can be put to use now. The Magician’s gesture between sky and ground is a symbol of connecting vision with practical action. When this energy is balanced, your attention is clear and your efforts have direction: you know what you are trying to make and can identify a next step. This is a moment to act thoughtfully rather than staying in planning mode. Let your intention guide your tools, while remaining open to feedback from the real world.","reversedExplanation":"The reversed Magician can indicate that your abilities are being blocked or used in a way that does not reflect your values. You may have useful tools but feel unqualified to use them, or you may be attempting to control an outcome through pressure, deception, or a shortcut. The creative energy of the Magician can turn into cleverness used to avoid an honest conversation. You might feel like an impostor, or you might overestimate your ability to control circumstances and other people. This card invites you to look at the difference between influence and manipulation. Real capability includes recognizing limits, asking for help, and being truthful about what you can offer. If your efforts are not working, return to honesty and humility, then choose a more grounded approach."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"From vision into action","type":"Focused expression and transformation","description":"The Magician connects an idea with a practical form. Attention gathers around a clear intention and moves toward concrete action. This is active, creative energy: instead of waiting for every opportunity to arrive, you can make a deliberate opening for one."},"timing":{"speed":"Fast-moving","description":"A situation may begin to move quickly once you take action. The Magician favors getting started and making timely use of an opportunity. Early signs of progress may appear within one or two weeks, though this is a reflective timing cue rather than a guarantee."},"advice":{"upright":"Begin with the resources you already have. You do not need to wait for a perfect moment. Choose a clear goal, focus on the next practical step, and trust yourself enough to try. Let your actions show what you can do.","reversed":"Pause and review your motives before acting. Do not rely on pressure, manipulation, or misleading promises to get the result you want. Rebuild confidence by being honest about both your strengths and the areas you still need to develop."},"chakra":{"primary":"Solar Plexus Chakra","issue":"You may feel unsure of your personal agency, struggle to express confidence, or try to control too much when you do not feel secure.","healingNote":"The Solar Plexus is commonly associated with agency and self-confidence. If you feel powerless or overly controlling, grounding routines and realistic goals may help you reconnect with your sense of choice. Crystals such as citrine or tiger’s eye can be used as personal ritual objects, but they are not medical treatment; consult a qualified professional for health concerns."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your inner wisdom may be reminding you that you already have a place to begin. This is less about collecting one more tool and more about using what you have learned. You can choose how to direct your attention and effort. As you take a thoughtful step, notice what becomes possible through your own participation.","reversed":"The reversed Magician invites you to remember that lasting influence comes from integrity, not control. If you gain something by misleading someone, trust may be damaged and the result may not last. Be willing to look honestly at the parts of yourself you would rather hide, acknowledge what you still need to learn, and rebuild your confidence from a more truthful foundation."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '2-high-priestess', 'en', 'The High Priestess', '女祭司', '{"keywords":["Intuition","Wisdom","Mystery","Subconscious","Inner Knowing"],"arcana":"major","number":2}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The High Priestess embodies wisdom and intuition, guarding the realms of hidden knowledge and the subconscious. When this card appears, it reminds you to listen to your inner voice and trust your intuition. This is not a time to rely only on logical analysis; go deeper and explore the wisdom within. The High Priestess encourages meditation and a connection with your spiritual self so that you can find answers inwardly. This period may support the study of esoteric subjects, spiritual practice, or a deeper understanding of your subconscious. Remain patient and receptive, because some things need time to be revealed. The High Priestess also represents secrets and hidden knowledge, reminding you that some information may not yet be fully visible.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed High Priestess suggests that you may be ignoring your intuition or allowing external noise to drown out your inner voice. You may be relying too heavily on rational thought while suppressing your emotional and spiritual sides. This card can also suggest that a secret is being withheld or that you are refusing to see important information. You may feel disconnected from your inner wisdom and unable to access a deeper understanding. Rebuild your connection with intuition through time alone and honest reflection. The reversed High Priestess also asks you to face yourself truthfully rather than hiding the truth or avoiding deep feelings. Balance reason and feeling so that you can make the wisest decision.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Intuition","Inner Wisdom","Mystery","Waiting","Receiving Messages"],"reversed":["Ignoring Intuition","Overthinking","Hidden Secrets","Disconnection from Self","Unclear Information"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the High Priestess is a gateway to subconscious and spiritual wisdom. Seated between the black and white pillars, she guards hidden knowledge and symbolizes the balance of opposites behind a veil of mystery. This card asks you to stop searching outward and turn inward instead. Your intuition may be more reliable than logic right now, and your dreams may reveal more than your waking thoughts. The High Priestess does not offer answers immediately; she waits until you are ready to receive them. This is a quiet, inward, receptive energy, better suited to observing, waiting, and listening than taking action. The answer will emerge naturally at the right time.","reversedExplanation":"The reversed High Priestess shows that your connection with inner wisdom may have been severed. The noise of the outside world may be so loud that you cannot hear your inner voice. You may be relying on rational analysis to calculate every step while ignoring intuitive guidance. This card can also indicate a hidden secret or a truth you have chosen not to see. You may be afraid to face what lies within, using busyness to avoid being alone. The High Priestess reminds you that the truth does not disappear because you refuse to look at it. Be honest with yourself and rebuild your inner connection. Turn down the outside noise so that you can hear your own wisdom."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Inward","type":"Receptive","description":"The High Priestess carries an inward, receptive energy that waits rather than pushes forward. Seated between the black and white pillars, she guards the doorway to the subconscious. This is the energy of stillness, observation, and receiving spiritual messages."},"timing":{"speed":"Slow","description":"This situation needs time to develop, so do not rush. The High Priestess suggests that the timing is not yet right and may bring a waiting period of one to three months. The answer will appear naturally at the right time; forcing it will only make things harder."},"advice":{"upright":"Do not make a decision yet. Quiet yourself and listen to your intuition. Spend time meditating, being alone, and observing. The answer is already within you, even if it has not reached your conscious mind. Stay patient and let the message come to you.","reversed":"Reconnect with your intuition. Reduce external noise, step away from social media, and give yourself a quiet space. If there is a secret, face it honestly. Do not keep avoiding your inner voice; it has been trying to tell you the truth."},"chakra":{"primary":"Third Eye Chakra","issue":"Your intuition may feel blocked, making it difficult to receive spiritual insight, or you may be relying too heavily on logical thinking.","healingNote":"The High Priestess is closely connected with the Third Eye Chakra, a center commonly associated with intuition and inner vision. If you feel disconnected from intuition or unable to receive insight, you may benefit from practices that create quiet and reflection. Crystals such as amethyst or labradorite can be used as personal ritual objects, but they are not medical treatment; consult a qualified professional for health concerns."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that the answer is not outside you, but within you. The wisdom you have been seeking is something you already know. Stop searching outward and return to inner stillness. In that silence, you may hear what the universe has been saying to you all along.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that you have drifted too far from yourself. The noise of the outside world has drowned out what is true within you. It is time to face honestly the truth you have been avoiding. Your intuition is still there; you have simply chosen not to listen. Come back to yourself."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '3-empress', 'en', 'The Empress', '皇后', '{"keywords":["Abundance","Nurturing","Creativity","Beauty","Plenty"],"arcana":"major","number":3}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Empress embodies the energy of abundance, nourishment, and creativity. She represents the richness of nature and the loving care of the mother, bringing growth and prosperity to life. When this card appears, it can point to a harvest season approaching, whether through material plenty or emotional and spiritual fulfillment. The Empress encourages you to connect with nature, enjoy life''s beautiful offerings, and treat yourself and others with love and care. This is an excellent time to nurture a creative project, build a home, or tend to relationships. The Empress also represents sensual pleasure and artistic beauty, reminding you to appreciate harmony and the loveliness around you. Her energy is gentle yet powerful, bringing healing and growth so that everything can thrive when nourished by love.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Empress may show blocked creativity or a lack of nourishment. You may be relying too heavily on others, or caring for everyone else while neglecting your own needs. This card can also point to overprotection or a suffocating relationship, whether you are controlling someone or being controlled. You may feel disconnected from your creativity or feminine energy, or experience material and emotional scarcity. The reversed Empress asks you to restore the balance of self-care and learn to set healthy boundaries. Do not let responsibility for others overwhelm you, and do not control people out of fear of losing them. Reconnect with nature and your body, and cultivate self-love and self-worth so that you can genuinely offer love and support.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Abundance","Nourishment","Creativity","Feminine Energy","Harvest"],"reversed":["Scarcity","Overgiving","Blocked Creativity","Imbalance","Suffocating Relationship"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Empress represents the abundance of the Earth Mother: creation, nourishment, and unconditional love. She sits in nature among ripe fields and flowing water, symbols of life''s fullness and growth. This card brings the accepting, gentle, patient strength that allows things to flourish. The Empress does not force anything to grow; she provides the best environment and lets life develop in its own time. This is feminine energy expressed not through conquest or control, but through love and care. The upright Empress reminds you that abundance is part of your nature, not something you must struggle to earn. When you care for yourself well, plenty can flow toward you naturally.","reversedExplanation":"The reversed Empress shows that nourishing energy has become unbalanced. You may care for others so intensely that you forget yourself and become an exhausted giver. Or you may have completely ignored your creativity and your need to be loved. Feminine energy can turn into suffocation and overprotection, leading you to control someone in the name of doing what is best for them. This card can also point to a lost connection with your body and the natural world, leaving you feeling empty and deprived. The reversed Empress reminds you that you cannot pour from an empty cup. Stop overgiving and give love to yourself first. True abundance comes from inner fullness, not external accumulation."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Outward expansion","type":"Nourishing expression","description":"The Empress flows like the generous energy of the Earth Mother. She nourishes and supports growth, allowing everything to thrive in love. This is creative energy, but it is not hurried; it patiently waits for the fruit to ripen."},"timing":{"speed":"Natural pace","description":"Things will develop at a natural pace, like a seed that needs time to sprout. You may see results within one to two months. Do not rush the process; let it grow in its own time."},"advice":{"upright":"Take good care of your body, mind, and spirit. Spend time in nature and enjoy beautiful things. This is a good time to create and nurture something, but be patient. Love yourself well so that your love can flow freely to others.","reversed":"Stop overgiving. You are not responsible for being everyone''s parent, so care for yourself first. If you feel deprived, look at whether you have been ignoring your own needs. Learn to say no and set clear boundaries."},"chakra":{"primary":"Heart Chakra and Sacral Chakra","issue":"Overgiving may be draining your Heart Chakra, or creative energy may be blocked in the Sacral Chakra.","healingNote":"The Empress connects the Heart Chakra, associated with love and giving, with the Sacral Chakra, associated with creativity. If overgiving has left you exhausted, your heart needs replenishment. If creativity feels stuck, gentle creative practices may help restore movement. Crystals such as rose quartz or moonstone can be used as personal ritual objects, but they are not medical treatment; consult a qualified professional for health concerns."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that you deserve to be nourished and to enjoy beautiful things. Life is not only about giving and working; it also includes receiving and enjoying. Allow yourself to be loved and allow abundance to flow toward you. You are a child of the Earth, and fullness is part of your nature.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that you have forgotten how to receive. You are used to being the giver, but do not know how to accept. This imbalance is draining your energy. It is time to stop and give love to yourself first. You do not need to prove your worth through constant giving."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '4-emperor', 'en', 'The Emperor', '皇帝', '{"keywords":["Authority","Structure","Leadership","Stability","Paternal Wisdom"],"arcana":"major","number":4}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Emperor represents authority, structure, and stability. He embodies leadership, organizational ability, and the wisdom to create order. When this card appears, it reminds you to approach matters with reason and logic, and to establish clear rules and boundaries. The Emperor encourages you to take responsibility and lead with firmness and fairness. This can be a good time to build a career, make plans, or consolidate what you have achieved. His energy is steady and dependable, offering protection and a sense of security. He reminds you that discipline and determination, sustained through effort and perseverance, can help you work toward long-term goals. The Emperor also represents paternal wisdom and experience, offering practical advice and support.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Emperor warns that you may be becoming too authoritarian or controlling. You may be misusing power, treating others harshly, or becoming so rigid that you cannot adapt to change. This card can also point to a lack of discipline or direction, making it difficult to manage yourself or others effectively. You may be avoiding responsibility, struggling to lead, or resisting authority. The reversed Emperor asks you to find balance between control and flexibility. Do not let fear drive you to control everything, but do not abandon structure and order altogether. Exercise authority with greater openness and consideration, and respect other people''s autonomy. Also ask whether you rely too heavily on external authority while overlooking your own inner wisdom.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Authority","Structure","Self-Mastery","Leadership","Stability"],"reversed":["Overcontrol","Authoritarianism","Lack of Discipline","Avoiding Responsibility","Rigidity"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Emperor represents the stabilizing force of paternal energy, embodying order, authority, and the ability to build. He sits on a stone throne with rugged mountains behind him, symbols of an unshakable foundation. This card brings rational, logical, and strategic thinking. Rather than relying on emotion or intuition, the Emperor makes decisions through experience and wisdom. He establishes rules, sets boundaries, and creates structure so that things can be kept in order. This is masculine energy expressed through leadership and control in the service of protection and stability. The upright Emperor reminds you that sometimes you must be the sovereign of your own life, creating an order and discipline that are truly yours.","reversedExplanation":"The reversed Emperor shows that the energy of authority has become distorted or is missing. You may be excessively controlling, using strict rules to pressure yourself or others and turning protection into constraint. At the other extreme, you may lack discipline and direction, avoid responsibilities you need to take on, or struggle to lead. Paternal energy can become authoritarian and oppressive, with disagreement silenced in the name of doing what is best for everyone. This card can also point to resistance to authority and a rejection of all rules and structure. The reversed Emperor reminds you that true strength is not control, but flexibility within stability. Seek a balance between order and freedom."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Top-down","type":"Constructive leadership and control","description":"The Emperor''s energy directs and builds from the top down; it is a guiding, masculine force. He establishes order, sets rules, and takes charge. This is steady, practical, and methodical energy."},"timing":{"speed":"Steady and gradual","description":"Things are likely to move forward steadily according to plan rather than happen suddenly. The Emperor represents long-term building, and it may take two to six months to see solid results. This is a marathon, not a sprint."},"advice":{"upright":"Create a clear plan and structure. Set boundaries and take responsibility for leading. What is needed now is discipline and strategy, not emotion or impulse. Think like a CEO and make decisions rationally.","reversed":"Loosen your need for control. You cannot control everything, and you do not need to. Consider whether you are controlling others in the name of protecting them. If you have been too undisciplined, this may be the time to establish some structure. Look for balance."},"chakra":{"primary":"Solar Plexus Chakra and Root Chakra","issue":"Your sense of power may be out of balance: you may be trying to control too much or feel completely out of control, with insecurity driving the need to take charge.","healingNote":"The Emperor connects the Solar Plexus Chakra, associated with personal power, and the Root Chakra, associated with security. Excessive control often comes from inner insecurity. If you need to control everything to feel safe, it may be worth tending to your sense of grounding. Practices involving crystals such as obsidian or red jasper can be used as a personal ritual for cultivating security. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade; crystal practices are not medical treatment, so consult a qualified professional for health concerns."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that true strength comes from a stable foundation. You have the ability to build your own empire, but it takes patience and strategy. Take responsibility instead of avoiding it. You are more capable of directing your circumstances than you may think.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that control can be another expression of fear. If you need to manage everything before you can feel at ease, you may not be trusting life''s flow. Or are you avoiding a responsibility that is yours to carry? True strength is not control, but trust rooted in stability."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '5-hierophant', 'en', 'The Hierophant', '教皇', '{"keywords":["Tradition","Education","Faith","Mentor","Wisdom"],"arcana":"major","number":5}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Hierophant represents traditional wisdom, spiritual teachers, and formal learning. He safeguards cultural, religious, and social values, offering moral and spiritual guidance. When this card appears, you may be seeking deeper meaning and spiritual understanding. This is a time to learn from a mentor, join a community, or follow an established system. The Hierophant encourages you to respect traditions and customs and draw on the wisdom of those who came before you. This period is well suited to formal education, religious ceremonies, or spiritual guidance. The Hierophant also represents commitment and loyalty, and may relate to marriage, joining an organization, or another formal union. He reminds you of the importance of cultural inheritance and collective wisdom, as well as the stability that comes from following ethical principles.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Hierophant suggests that you may be challenging tradition or questioning an established belief system. You want to follow your own path rather than blindly obey rules set by others. This card may point to rebellion, unconventional ideas, or distrust of authority. You may feel that the current system is too rigid to meet your needs and values. The reversed Hierophant encourages you to develop your own beliefs and philosophy instead of following external dogma without question. At the same time, it cautions you not to oppose something merely for the sake of opposition; consider your path carefully. As you pursue personal freedom, remain open to the value of some traditional wisdom. Finding balance between respect for tradition and personal innovation can help you forge a path of your own.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Tradition","Mentor","Learning","Belief System","Formal Commitment"],"reversed":["Rebellion","Questioning Authority","Breaking with Tradition","Personal Beliefs","Spiritual Freedom"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Hierophant represents the transmission of traditional wisdom and spiritual authority. He is a bridge between heaven and earth, the sacred and the everyday, safeguarding the values of culture, religion, and society. This card brings formal learning, a mentor''s guidance, and respect for established principles. The Hierophant does not forge a new path; he points toward roads that have been tested by those before you. This is a time to learn from tradition and deepen your understanding through ceremony, education, or commitment. The upright Hierophant reminds you that not every wheel needs to be reinvented. Standing on the shoulders of those who came before, you can see farther.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, the Hierophant shows that you are questioning or rejecting external authority and tradition. You may feel that an established belief system no longer meets your spiritual needs, or that customary practices are limiting your growth. This rebellious energy can be liberating, but it can also become indiscriminate. You may be forming your own beliefs and no longer need a mentor or religion to tell you what is true. Yet this card also cautions against opposing things simply for the sake of opposition or becoming a cynical rebel. The reversed Hierophant reminds you that spiritual freedom does not mean rejecting every tradition; it means wisely choosing what suits you and what you are ready to release."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Passed down from mentor to student","type":"Teaching and receiving","description":"The Hierophant''s energy is one of transmission, flowing from teacher to student and from tradition to the present. It is the energy of learning, receiving guidance, and becoming part of a system. This is not about innovation, but about absorbing wisdom that already exists."},"timing":{"speed":"Follows an established process (moderate to slow)","description":"Matters are likely to proceed according to traditional or formal steps rather than move quickly. Formal commitments, education, or certification may take three to six months. Following the right steps matters more than speed."},"advice":{"upright":"Seek guidance from a mentor or qualified expert. Rather than trying to work everything out alone, learn from someone with experience. Follow established rules and processes instead of looking for shortcuts. If you are making a commitment, such as marriage or signing a contract, this may be a favorable time.","reversed":"Question the rules you have always followed: do they truly fit you? Do not follow tradition or authority blindly, but do not oppose them just for the sake of it. Choose your own path thoughtfully and build a belief system of your own."},"chakra":{"primary":"Throat Chakra and Crown Chakra","issue":"Difficulty expressing your authentic beliefs (Throat Chakra), or following external authority blindly and losing connection with your higher self (Crown Chakra).","healingNote":"The Hierophant connects the Throat Chakra, associated with authentic expression, and the Crown Chakra, associated with spiritual connection. If you cannot express your beliefs or follow another''s doctrines blindly, these chakras may need balance. Lapis lazuli and clear quartz can support authentic spiritual expression through crystal practices. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that learning from those who came before you does not mean losing yourself. There is wisdom in tradition; do not overlook a path that has already proven effective just to be different. Find a mentor you can trust and let yourself stand on the shoulders of giants.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that no external authority can define your spiritual truth. The answers you seek are not in any religion or with any mentor; they are within you. It is time to reclaim your spiritual sovereignty and build a belief system of your own."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '6-lovers', 'en', 'The Lovers', '戀人', '{"keywords":["Love","Choice","Harmony","Partnership","Union"],"arcana":"major","number":6}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Lovers represents deep connection, harmony in relationships, and important choices. It symbolizes not only romantic love, but also deep bonds and partnerships of many kinds. When this card appears, it may point to an important decision that calls for you to stay true to your values and beliefs. The Lovers encourages you to seek harmony and balance, and to build mutual respect and understanding in your relationships. This can be a time to deepen intimacy, form an important partnership, or make a choice aligned with your values. The card also represents inner integration, bringing opposing parts together into a harmonious whole. The Lovers reminds you that love begins with self-acceptance: only when you can be authentically yourself can you build a truly deep and meaningful connection.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Lovers may point to imbalance, misunderstanding, or conflicting values in a relationship. You may be going through difficulties and feeling out of harmony with a partner or someone important to you. This card can also reflect confusion around an important decision, difficulty choosing, or a choice that does not align with your deepest wishes. You may have compromised your values or lost a sense of yourself in a relationship. The reversed Lovers asks you to reconsider your relationships and choices and make sure they reflect your core values. Do not sacrifice your authenticity just to please someone else. This is also a time to reflect on inner conflict and disharmony, practice self-love, and make choices that genuinely fit who you are.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["True Love","Soulmate","Aligned Values","Important Choice","Inner Integration"],"reversed":["Conflicting Values","Relationship Imbalance","Difficulty Choosing","Self-Betrayal","Disharmony"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Lovers represents a soul-level connection and a meaningful choice. This is not only about romantic love, but about alignment: with another person, with your values, and with a higher purpose. In the imagery, the angel Raphael blesses the scene from above, symbolizing a sacred union. The upright card emphasizes choosing in a way that is true to yourself. Whether you are choosing a relationship, a job, or a direction in life, ask whether it aligns with your core values. The Lovers is not about compromise for its own sake; it is about two whole people choosing to walk together. The upright Lovers reminds you that real love helps you become more fully yourself rather than lose yourself.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, the Lovers points to conflicting values or imbalance in a relationship. You may be sacrificing your values to keep a relationship, or be caught in a connection where you cannot be yourself. In the imagery, the angel''s blessing is blocked, suggesting that the connection lacks a sense of sacred alignment. You may face a difficult choice and feel unable to decide because every option seems to betray part of you. Or you may have already chosen while knowing inwardly that the choice is not right for you. The reversed Lovers reminds you that if a relationship requires you to give yourself up in order to keep it, it is not true love. Be honest with yourself: do your choices reflect who you really are?"},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Mutual exchange","type":"Union and integration","description":"The Lovers'' energy is mutual, equal, and flows in both directions. It is not one person giving while the other receives; it is two currents meeting, integrating, and creating a new harmony. This is the energy of yin and yang and the unity of dualities."},"timing":{"speed":"A pivotal moment","description":"The Lovers signals that the time to decide is now. This is not a gradual process but a clear point of choice. Within the coming weeks, you may face or already be facing an important decision."},"advice":{"upright":"Make choices that stay true to your values. Do not compromise your core beliefs just to please others. If the question is about a relationship, make sure your values are aligned. Real love helps you become more fully yourself rather than lose yourself.","reversed":"Look at your relationship or choice: are you betraying yourself? Do not sacrifice your authenticity just to keep a relationship. If you cannot decide, ask yourself which choice helps you feel more like your true self."},"chakra":{"primary":"Heart Chakra","issue":"Heart Chakra imbalance: you may be so open that you lose your boundaries, or so closed off that genuine connection feels difficult.","healingNote":"The Lovers centers on the Heart Chakra and the balance of giving and receiving love. If a relationship leaves you feeling depleted, your boundaries may need attention. If you find it difficult to connect deeply, you may want to explore what would help you feel safer opening up. Rose quartz and green aventurine can be used as personal reflection and grounding practices. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that true love is a recognition between souls. When you meet the right person or face the right choice, your soul will know. Do not analyze everything with your mind; listen to your heart. Real love does not require you to change who you are; it allows you to be your most authentic self.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that if you have to pretend in order to be loved, it is not true love. You deserve a relationship that lets you be freely yourself. Stop compromising your soul to maintain a connection that is not right for you. Sometimes the most loving choice you can make for yourself is to leave."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '7-chariot', 'en', 'The Chariot', '戰車', '{"keywords":["Victory","Willpower","Control","Progress","Determination"],"arcana":"major","number":7}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Chariot symbolizes victory, willpower, and unwavering determination. It shows how focus and self-discipline can help you overcome obstacles and reach your goals. The charioteer guides two opposing forces, representing the ability to integrate conflicting energies and move in a clear direction. When this card appears, success may be within reach, but it calls for a steady will and a clear aim. This is a time to act, show determination, and meet challenges directly. The Chariot encourages you to trust your abilities and not let outside distractions shake your resolve. With discipline and focus, you can steer your course toward your goals. The card can also signify travel and progress, whether through a literal journey or movement along your life''s path.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Chariot suggests that you may have lost your sense of direction or control. You may feel pulled by opposing forces and unable to make a decision or act consistently. It can also point to aggression, forcefulness, or a lack of self-discipline. You may be rushing toward a goal or trying to force an outcome, creating conflict and resistance. The reversed Chariot asks you to regain your inner balance and direction. Do not let outside pressure or inner conflict keep you from moving forward. Meet challenges with greater flexibility and openness instead of pushing ahead at all costs. Pause to reassess your goals and methods, make sure you are on the right path, and choose a more harmonious way to pursue them.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Victory","Willpower","Steering Your Course","Breakthrough","Strong Momentum"],"reversed":["Loss of Control","Unclear Direction","Aggression","Inner Conflict","Lack of Discipline"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Chariot represents victory achieved through willpower and self-discipline. The charioteer guides two contrasting forces, symbolizing the integration of opposing energies in pursuit of a clear goal. This card is about taking charge—not controlling the outside world, but directing your own energy and course. You know where you want to go and have the resolve to face obstacles along the way. The Chariot advances through will and focus rather than brute force. It reminds you that when you are internally aligned and your aim is clear, the way forward becomes easier to see. This is a moment to commit yourself fully; victory is within reach.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, the Chariot shows a loss of direction or control. Opposing forces pull you apart, leaving you unable to move forward. You may be pushing too aggressively and creating more resistance, or you may have lost momentum and become stuck. Perhaps you have a goal but cannot follow through, or you are acting decisively in the wrong direction. Before charging ahead, bring your inner opposites into alignment. Hesitation and excessive force can both come from inner division. Pause, recalibrate your direction, and then begin again."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Forward momentum","type":"Focused breakthrough","description":"The Chariot''s energy is highly focused and moves powerfully in one direction. It breaks through barriers, overcomes resistance, and advances toward a goal. This energy is linear, purposeful, and undivided."},"timing":{"speed":"Rapid progress","description":"Matters may develop quickly, with noticeable progress. The Chariot marks a period of acceleration, and a significant breakthrough may appear within two to four weeks. Maintaining momentum is important."},"advice":{"upright":"Give your full effort without getting distracted. This is a time to act, not just plan. Stay focused and direct your energy toward one clear aim. Victory calls for discipline and determination, so keep going.","reversed":"Pause and reassess your direction. Resolve the inner conflict that is pulling you in different ways. Do not try to force your way through; first bring your opposing impulses into alignment. If you have become too passive, this may also be a time to rebuild your momentum."},"chakra":{"primary":"Solar Plexus Chakra and Sacral Chakra","issue":"Low willpower or overexertion that leads to fatigue, with blocked motivation or difficulty taking action.","healingNote":"The Chariot connects the Solar Plexus Chakra, associated with willpower, and the Sacral Chakra, associated with movement and vitality. If you feel unable to move forward or are pushing yourself into exhaustion, these centers may need balance. Citrine and amber can be included in personal grounding or reflection practices. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that you can achieve what you truly set your heart on. When your will is aligned with your deeper self, obstacles need not define your path. This is not the moment to doubt yourself, but to give your effort wholeheartedly. Trust yourself and keep moving; victory is yours to pursue.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that inner conflict is pulling you apart. One part of you wants to move forward while another resists. Before you can make real progress, bring these opposing parts into conversation. Or ask whether you are applying effort in the wrong direction. Listen inwardly, and you can find where you truly want to go."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '8-strength', 'en', 'Strength', '力量', '{"keywords":["Courage","Patience","Compassion","Inner Strength","Self-Control"],"arcana":"major","number":8}', '{"uprightMeaning":"Strength is not about brute force; it is about gentleness, patience, and inner courage. This card shows the ability to meet instinct with love and compassion rather than domination. When Strength appears, it reminds you that real strength comes from within—from accepting and understanding yourself and others. This is a time to be courageous, face your fears, and meet challenges with gentle resolve. Strength encourages you to trust your inner resources; you do not need force or violence to reach your goals. With patience, self-restraint, and compassion, you can work through obstacles. The card also speaks to emotional steadiness and resilience, reminding you to remain calm and graceful even in difficult moments. True strength transforms fear through love and eases conflict through understanding.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Strength card may point to a period of self-doubt, vulnerability, or low confidence. Fear and insecurity may be keeping you from expressing your real strength. It can also indicate excessive force or impatience: you may be trying to control a situation through pressure rather than guiding it gently. The reversed card asks you to reconnect with your inner courage and resources. Do not let outside criticism or inner fear erode your confidence. Treat yourself with compassion and patience, and accept your flaws and imperfections. Real strength comes from accepting and integrating every part of yourself, including the parts you consider weak. Through self-acceptance and inner peace, you can rediscover your strength.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Inner Strength","Gentle Resolve","Emotional Steadiness","Courage","Compassion"],"reversed":["Self-Doubt","Low Confidence","Excessive Force","Loss of Composure","Inner Conflict"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, Strength shows the wisdom of the woman who meets the lion without force, guiding it with patience and care. Its central message is that real strength integrates rather than suppresses. You can face your instincts and fears not by fighting them, but by understanding and accepting them. This is emotional maturity: remaining calm in anger and courageous in fear. Strength embodies the wisdom that gentleness can overcome force; the more gently and firmly you respond, the more resilient you become. The inner beast is not your enemy, but a part of you waiting to be met with love. When you treat your shadow with compassion, you find a strength that cannot be shaken.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, Strength suggests that you have lost touch with your inner resources. You may feel overwhelmed by fear and self-doubt, or use excessive force to hide your vulnerability, becoming controlling or domineering. The lion may be suppressed too deeply or allowed to roar unchecked. You may be harsh with yourself or others, replacing compassion with criticism. This card reminds you that real strength comes from inner balance, not outward domination. If you feel powerless, it may not be because you lack strength, but because you are using the wrong approach. Stop fighting yourself and begin making peace with who you are. True courage includes admitting vulnerability, and true strength can be gentle."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Integrated inward","type":"Balance and self-mastery","description":"Strength''s energy gathers inward, integrating instinct with conscious awareness. It is steady, sustained, gentle, and firm: not explosive, but enduring."},"timing":{"speed":"Steady over time","description":"Strength points to a process that calls for patience. Change may not happen overnight, but it can continue steadily. Building inner resilience and emotional steadiness may take two to three months."},"advice":{"upright":"Meet challenges with gentle resolve. Choose patience and care over force or pressure, and trust your inner strength to help you respond. Stay calm and treat yourself and others with compassion.","reversed":"Stop fighting yourself. Notice whether you are being too forceful or too hesitant, and look for a more balanced response. Accept your vulnerability and let care, rather than fear, guide you. Rebuild confidence in your inner resources."},"chakra":{"primary":"Heart Chakra and Solar Plexus Chakra","issue":"A wounded Heart Chakra may make it difficult to respond with love, while imbalance in the Solar Plexus Chakra may show up as low confidence or excessive control.","healingNote":"Strength calls for balance between the Heart Chakra, associated with love and compassion, and the Solar Plexus Chakra, associated with personal power. If you feel powerless or overly forceful, these centers may need harmony. Rose quartz and citrine can be included in personal reflection or grounding practices. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that you are stronger and gentler than you may realize. True strength is not about suppressing fear, but holding it with tenderness. When you stop fighting your instincts and learn to move with them, you discover a strength that cannot be shaken. Your gentleness is your strength.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that you do not need to prove how strong you are, or pretend that you feel no fear. Real courage means admitting that you are afraid and choosing to move forward anyway. Stop using harshness to protect your vulnerability; let care help you meet your fear. Your strength is still there, though mistaken beliefs may have obscured it."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '9-hermit', 'en', 'The Hermit', '隱士', '{"keywords":["Introspection","Wisdom","Solitude","Truth","Guidance"],"arcana":"major","number":9}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Hermit represents a period of introspection, solitude, and seeking inner truth. This card asks you to step back from the noise of daily life and give yourself quiet time to reflect and explore your inner world. The lantern in the Hermit''s hand symbolizes wisdom and guidance, illuminating the path toward truth. This can be a time for deep self-exploration, spiritual practice, or seeking a deeper sense of meaning. Solitude is not the same as loneliness; it can be an opportunity to reconnect with your authentic self. This period is well suited to study, reading, meditation, or other forms of inner work. The Hermit encourages you to trust your inner guidance and draw wisdom from your own experience. Through deep reflection, you can find answers to life''s questions and a direction for moving forward.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Hermit suggests that you may be isolating yourself too much and refusing help or support. You may feel lonely and disconnected, or avoid social contact until you become closed off. This card can also point to excessive inward focus that causes you to overlook the needs and opportunities of the outside world. You may have built walls out of fear of being hurt or disappointed, but those walls can also limit growth and connection. The reversed Hermit asks you to find balance between solitude and social contact. Reflection matters, but complete isolation can lead to stagnation and discouragement. Try opening up and receiving other people''s support and perspectives. Sharing your thoughts and feelings can sometimes bring fresh insight and understanding.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Inner Wisdom","Spiritual Search","Solitary Reflection","Guiding Light","Deep Exploration"],"reversed":["Isolation","Rejecting Guidance","Avoiding Connection","Excessive Loneliness","Feeling Lost"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Hermit represents a journey in search of wisdom deep within the soul. Standing on a mountaintop with a lantern, he symbolizes the insight that can come through reflection and solitude. This card calls you to step away from the noise of the outside world and enter a quieter inner sanctuary. The Hermit is not escaping; he is making space for a deeper connection. This can be an important period for seeking meaning and spiritual growth. You may need solitude to process past experiences, organize your thoughts, and listen to what matters within. The Hermit''s lantern first illuminates his own path, not someone else''s. When you find your own light, you may be able to offer guidance to others. The card reminds you that some answers are found not outside, but in the deepest part of yourself.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, the Hermit suggests that solitude may have turned into avoidance. You may have built walls because you fear being hurt, refusing connection with the outside world. The Hermit can become a recluse who hides from life rather than seeking wisdom. You may feel intensely lonely and still hesitate to open up. This card can also point to ignoring your inner guidance, becoming so focused on the outside that you lose contact with yourself. Sometimes the reversed Hermit means your inner search has reached a natural pause and it is time to return to the world and share what you have learned. Balance is key: neither complete isolation nor constant outward activity is likely to serve you."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Deeply inward","type":"Receiving and reflecting","description":"The Hermit''s energy moves inward, like diving into the depths of the unconscious to find a pearl. It is quiet, contemplative, and exploratory, calling for solitude and stillness."},"timing":{"speed":"Slow and deepening","description":"The Hermit points to a process that takes time. Genuine wisdom cannot be rushed; a period of inner exploration and reflection may take three to six months. Let insight emerge naturally."},"advice":{"upright":"Give yourself time and space alone. Reduce social activity and make room for meditation, reading, and reflection. Look inward for answers instead of seeking them everywhere else. Trust that your inner wisdom can emerge in quiet moments.","reversed":"Ask whether you are choosing solitude or becoming isolated. If you have closed yourself off, try opening up and accepting support. If you have been constantly outward-facing, make some quiet time for yourself. Seek a balance between being alone and connecting with others."},"chakra":{"primary":"Crown Chakra","issue":"Feeling disconnected from spiritual guidance or unable to receive insight, or becoming so absorbed in spiritual concerns that you lose touch with practical life.","healingNote":"The Hermit has a strong connection with the Crown Chakra, associated with spiritual awareness. If you feel lost or unable to hear your inner guidance, you may want to explore practices that help you feel centered and present. Clear quartz and amethyst can be included in personal reflection rituals. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that this may be a time to withdraw—not because you are weak, but because you need to recharge and find your direction. In stillness, you may hear a truth that has been overlooked. Your lantern is waiting for you to light it, and that calls for solitude and reflection. This is a part of the journey only you can walk.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that isolation is not strength; it can be fear. You may have hidden long enough, and it may be time to reconnect with the world. Or perhaps you have been out in the world for too long and need to return to yourself. Balance solitude with connection, and you can find a deeper wisdom."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '10-wheel', 'en', 'Wheel of Fortune', '命運之輪', '{"keywords":["Change","Fate","Cycles","Luck","Turning Point"],"arcana":"major","number":10}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Wheel of Fortune represents life''s cycles, change, and turning points. It reminds you that everything is in motion and nothing stays the same forever. When the Wheel appears, an important change may be approaching, bringing good fortune or a new opportunity. The card encourages you to accept life''s highs and lows as natural parts of a larger cycle. It also speaks to karma and cause and effect, reminding you that past actions can shape the present and future. This is a time to move with changing circumstances and make use of opportunities. Stay open and flexible, because change can bring growth and progress. Trust the unfolding of events, and keep faith through difficult moments: the Wheel continues to turn.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Wheel of Fortune suggests that you may be going through a difficult period or resisting a change that needs to happen. You may feel out of control, as though fate is directing your life without your input. This card can also point to bad luck or an unfavorable turn that leaves you discouraged or powerless. Even in difficulty, however, you can choose how to respond. Rather than becoming trapped in a victim mindset, look for ways to create change. This may be a time to reassess your circumstances and learn from what is challenging you. Remember that the Wheel does not stay at its lowest point forever; difficult periods pass. Be patient and resilient, and trust that circumstances can improve in time.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Turning Point","Karmic Cycle","Good Fortune","Timing for Change","Universal Order"],"reversed":["A Difficult Cycle","Resistance to Change","Bad Luck","Loss of Control","Karmic Reckoning"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Wheel of Fortune symbolizes life''s natural cycles and the arrival of a turning point. The Wheel keeps moving, reminding you that nothing lasts forever: highs pass, and so do lows. This card often signals good fortune and positive change, as circumstances may be turning in a more favorable direction. It can represent the results of past choices beginning to unfold. The Wheel encourages you to move with life''s flow rather than resist every change. When opportunity comes around, make use of it; when circumstances shift away, keep faith and allow another cycle to arrive. This card teaches you to accept life''s ups and downs as part of a larger pattern.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, the Wheel of Fortune suggests a low point or strong resistance to necessary change. The Wheel is still turning, but you may feel controlled by circumstances and unable to influence your life. This can be a period when past actions bring difficult consequences. Yet even at a low point, the Wheel will turn again. You are not powerless to choose your response. The reversed Wheel asks you to accept the circumstances you cannot immediately change and trust that they will also pass. Sometimes it is a prompt to create change actively instead of waiting passively."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Cyclical movement","type":"Transformation and change","description":"The Wheel of Fortune moves in cycles, like the changing seasons and rising and falling tides. This is the natural rhythm of the universe: you cannot control it entirely, but you can learn to understand and move with it. Energy shifts between highs and lows."},"timing":{"speed":"Sudden change","description":"The Wheel of Fortune points to an unexpected turning point. A change may occur suddenly within one to four weeks, often in a way that is difficult to predict. Timing may depend on circumstances beyond your control."},"advice":{"upright":"Move with changing circumstances and make use of the good fortune or opportunity available now. Stay open and flexible. Remember that every phase is temporary: appreciate what is here without clinging to it, and give thanks for what your past actions have made possible.","reversed":"Accept that a difficult period is temporary. Do not resist every change or become trapped in a victim mindset. Reflect on the results of your past choices and what you can learn from them. This is a time for learning and growth; keep faith that the Wheel will turn again."},"chakra":{"primary":"All Chakras, especially the Crown and Root Chakras","issue":"Difficulty accepting life''s cycles and changes, or feeling disconnected from a larger sense of order.","healingNote":"The Wheel of Fortune can be understood in relation to the whole energy system, especially the Crown Chakra, associated with connection to a larger order, and the Root Chakra, associated with grounding and surrender. If change feels impossible to accept or you feel out of control, grounding and balancing practices may help. Crystal practices can serve as a way to reconnect with a sense of rhythm. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that this turning point is part of a larger timing. The good you have done may be opening new possibilities. Enjoy this moment of change, while remembering that the Wheel will keep turning. Learn to stay centered as things move and steady within yourself as circumstances change.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that a low point is not a punishment; it is part of life''s natural cycles. You may be working through the consequences of past choices and learning from them. The Wheel does not remain at its lowest point forever, but it can take patience to keep faith through difficulty. This challenge may be one step on the way toward a new high point."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '11-justice', 'en', 'Justice', '正義', '{"keywords":["Fairness","Truth","Cause and Effect","Balance","Law"],"arcana":"major","number":11}', '{"uprightMeaning":"Justice represents fairness, truth, and karmic balance. It reminds you that actions have consequences. When this card appears, it may be time to make a fair decision, or to face the results of past actions. Justice encourages honesty and integrity, and choices that align with your conscience and ethics. It can also relate to legal matters, contracts, and agreements, reminding you to make sure that terms are fair and transparent. This is a time to take responsibility, face the facts, and seek balance. The figure of Justice holds scales and a sword, symbols of objective judgment and decisive action. She asks you to think clearly, view matters without bias, and make the fairest decision you can.","reversedMeaning":"Reversed, Justice may point to unfairness, bias, or dishonesty. You may be treated unjustly, or you may not be acting with integrity yourself. This card can also indicate avoiding responsibility, refusing to admit a mistake, or struggling to judge a situation fairly. Bias may be making it difficult to see the truth objectively. The reversed Justice asks you to be honest about your actions and motives. If you have caused harm, take responsibility and make amends. If you are being treated unfairly, do not stay silent; speak up for yourself. The card can also point to legal or contractual disputes where professional guidance may be helpful. Begin restoring balance and fairness with honesty and accountability.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Fair Judgment","Truth and Consequences","Accountability","Balance","Honesty and Integrity"],"reversed":["Unfairness","Avoiding Responsibility","Bias","Dishonesty","Imbalance"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, Justice represents balance and the principle of cause and effect. The scales and sword symbolize careful consideration followed by decisive action. This card reminds you that choices have consequences: what you set in motion can shape what follows. Justice asks you to look honestly at your decisions and behavior and accept your share of responsibility. It can also refer to legal matters, contracts, or important choices that call for objectivity and fairness. Justice is not revenge; it is the restoration of balance. Acting with honesty and integrity helps you make decisions you can stand behind. The card encourages you to trust that truth can come to light and fairness can be pursued.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, Justice points to unfairness, bias, or an unwillingness to take responsibility. You may be treated unfairly, or you may be reluctant to acknowledge where your own actions have lacked integrity. The scales are out of balance: facts may be obscured and responsibility shifted elsewhere. You may be judging yourself or others through bias rather than looking objectively at what happened. This card can indicate avoiding consequences or refusing to admit a mistake. Avoidance can make a problem harder to resolve. Face the facts honestly and take responsibility for your part to begin restoring balance. If you are being treated unfairly, speak up for yourself. Truth may be hidden for a time, but it can still come to light."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Symmetrical balance","type":"Evaluation and adjustment","description":"Justice seeks a point of balance, like the two sides of a scale. Its energy is rational, objective, and measured rather than driven by emotion. It looks for fairness and truth by finding a center between opposing positions."},"timing":{"speed":"Governed by due process","description":"Justice reflects cause and effect, and timing may depend on when circumstances are ready to resolve. A fair outcome may become visible within one to three months, though it can take longer. Justice is not rushed, but resolution can come in time."},"advice":{"upright":"Act honestly and with integrity. Make a fair decision without favoring one side unfairly. Accept your responsibilities and expect others to accept theirs. Trust careful fact-finding and fairness. If you have a legal matter, seek appropriate professional advice about your situation.","reversed":"Look honestly at your behavior: are you avoiding responsibility? If you are being treated unfairly, speak up for yourself. Set aside bias and judgment so you can see the facts clearly. Acknowledge mistakes, make amends where appropriate, and work toward restoring balance."},"chakra":{"primary":"Solar Plexus Chakra and Throat Chakra","issue":"Difficulty speaking up for yourself (Throat Chakra), or lacking the confidence to take responsibility (Solar Plexus Chakra).","healingNote":"Justice connects the Solar Plexus Chakra, associated with personal power and responsibility, and the Throat Chakra, associated with speaking truth. If it is difficult to tell the truth or take responsibility, these centers may need balance. Citrine and blue kyanite can be included in personal grounding or reflection practices. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that fairness begins with the choices you make. You are now in a position to see the results of acting with integrity. Continue treating yourself and others honestly and fairly, and let your actions reflect what you believe. Truth is one of your greatest strengths.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that consequences cannot be avoided forever. What you set in motion will eventually have results. Be honest about your actions and take responsibility for your part. If you are being treated unfairly, do not stay silent; speak up for yourself. Restoring inner integrity is part of creating greater fairness in your life."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '12-hanged', 'en', 'The Hanged Man', '倒吊者', '{"keywords":["Pause","New Perspective","Letting Go","Sacrifice","Waiting"],"arcana":"major","number":12}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Hanged Man represents a pause, letting go, and the wisdom of seeing things from a new perspective. It reminds you that sometimes stopping and changing your point of view is more valuable than pushing ahead. The Hanged Man willingly hangs from a tree, symbolizing a temporary sacrifice or devotion in service of a larger purpose. This is a period for reflection and waiting, not for forcing action. You may need to see a problem from a different angle to understand it. The Hanged Man encourages you to accept the present situation, even when it feels uncomfortable or counterintuitive. This period may suit spiritual practice, meditation, and inner exploration. By loosening your need for control and accepting uncertainty, you can gain new insight and wisdom. Sometimes letting go is the best way to move forward.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Hanged Man suggests that you may be resisting a necessary pause or a change in perspective. You may feel stuck while also being unwilling to make a change that could shift the situation. This card can point to procrastination, needless sacrifice, or feeling trapped and unable to move forward. You may be attached to old ways of thinking and unwilling to look at the problem from a new angle. The reversed Hanged Man asks you to consider taking action to break the stalemate. If you have been waiting indefinitely, it may be time to do something. At the same time, the card cautions against changing merely for the sake of change or making a rushed decision. Look at what you are resisting and why you may be reluctant to shift your perspective. Sometimes accepting the present and waiting patiently is the wiser choice.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Surrender and Wait","Shift in Perspective","Pause and Reflect","Devotion","Release of Control"],"reversed":["Resistance and Stagnation","Procrastination","Needless Sacrifice","Rigid Thinking","Unwillingness to Change"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Hanged Man represents a profound pause and a change in perspective. He hangs from a tree with a peaceful expression, symbolizing the wisdom that can come from surrendering and loosening control. This card asks you to stop struggling against circumstances you cannot change right now. This is not passive resignation, but an intentional choice to look at the situation differently. The Hanged Man reminds you that seeing the world upside down can reveal what you could not see before. This may be a time to set aside something smaller in service of a more meaningful insight. The waiting period has a purpose, and impatience may only prolong the process. The Hanged Man teaches growth in stillness and transformation through waiting.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, the Hanged Man suggests that you may be resisting a necessary pause or caught in an unproductive standstill. You may refuse to change your perspective and cling rigidly to old ways of thinking. The pause can become procrastination, and sacrifice can become needless suffering. You may feel trapped while being unwilling to make a change that could break the stalemate. This card can also mean that you have waited long enough and it is time to act. Waiting has value, but waiting indefinitely can become avoidance. Ask whether you are waiting patiently or postponing action out of fear. Sometimes meaningful change begins with being willing to consider another possibility."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Stillness and pause","type":"Internalization and transformation","description":"The Hanged Man''s energy pauses and turns inward, like a pupa transforming inside a cocoon. The surface may appear still while deep inner change is taking place. This is the energy of surrender, acceptance, and turning your perspective around."},"timing":{"speed":"A period of delay and waiting","description":"The Hanged Man points to a clear waiting period. Matters may not move quickly and can call for two to six months of pause and reflection. This is an opportunity to practice patience; rushing may not change what needs time."},"advice":{"upright":"Stop struggling against the situation for now. Accept what is present and try looking at the problem from a different angle. This pause may be necessary, and patient reflection can bring deeper insight. Ask yourself what you may need to release.","reversed":"Ask whether you are waiting or procrastinating. If fear is keeping you from acting, consider taking a practical next step. If you have been resisting a different perspective, try turning the problem around and looking again. Breaking a stalemate may require a willingness to change how you think."},"chakra":{"primary":"Crown Chakra and Root Chakra","issue":"Difficulty surrendering to a higher perspective (Crown Chakra), or an excessive need for control and security (Root Chakra).","healingNote":"The Hanged Man calls for balance between the Crown Chakra, associated with spiritual surrender, and the Root Chakra, associated with grounded security. If it is difficult to release control or tolerate waiting, grounding and reflective practices may help. Crystal practices can be used as personal reminders to build trust and patience. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that this pause is not a punishment; it can be a gift. During this period of waiting, deep inner change may be taking place. Look at things from a different angle and you may notice a truth you had overlooked. Surrender is not giving up; it can be a deeper kind of wisdom. Trust the process and allow transformation to unfold.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that you may have waited long enough, or may be unwilling to wait at all. If you have waited long enough, it may be time to act; if you are resisting the pause, practice surrender. Resistance can prolong discomfort. Sometimes the bravest step is to stop, become still, and look at everything with fresh eyes."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '13-death', 'en', 'Death', '死神', '{"keywords":["Transformation","Ending","Rebirth","Letting Go","Transition"],"arcana":"major","number":13}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Death card represents endings, transformation, and renewal, not literal death. It marks the close of an important phase and the beginning of another. When Death appears, it asks you to release the past and let what has run its course make room for new possibilities. This may involve ending a relationship, leaving a job, changing a belief, or releasing an old pattern of behavior. Change can feel unsettling, but Death points to necessary transformation and renewal. The card encourages you to accept life''s natural cycles and understand that endings make new beginnings possible. Death rides a white horse, symbolizing the purifying power of transformation. Rather than resist the process, meet change and trust that what follows can bring growth and evolution.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Death card suggests that you may be resisting a necessary ending or change. You may be clinging to people, situations, or things that no longer suit you because you fear that letting go means losing everything. This card can also point to stagnation and difficulty completing a transition. You may be caught between past and future, unable to release one or welcome the other. The reversed Death reminds you that refusing change can create more pain and difficulty. Some things have reached their end, and forcing them to continue can drain your energy. Be honest about what is happening and accept that something may need to end. Letting go is not failure; it creates room for something more fitting to enter your life. Allow yourself to grieve what you have lost, then find the courage to move forward.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Profound Transformation","Ending and Rebirth","Releasing the Past","Renewal","Necessary Endings"],"reversed":["Resisting an Ending","Unable to Let Go","Stagnation","Fear of Change","Slow Transition"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, Death represents deep and complete transformation: one cycle ends so another can begin. The white horse symbolizes a purifying force that carries away what is outdated or no longer serves you. This card asks you to accept the close of an important phase, whether it involves a relationship, work, a belief, or a way of living. It does not refer to literal death, but to symbolic ending and renewal. Death reminds you that something new can emerge when the old has ended. This transformation may be painful, but it can also be necessary, and resisting it may prolong the pain. Death teaches you to release attachment and trust the process of change. Beyond an ending, renewal remains possible.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, Death suggests strong resistance to a necessary ending or transition. You may be holding on to something that has run its course because you fear loss or the unknown. The ending may be delayed, but resisting it can create further pain and stagnation. You may feel suspended between past and future, unable to release one or welcome the other. This card can also point to such a strong fear of change that you will do almost anything to preserve the status quo. The reversed Death reminds you that some things have reached their end, and forcing them to continue can drain your life energy. Letting go is not failure; it can be an act of wisdom. When you allow an ending to happen, renewal becomes possible."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Clearing and release","type":"Transformation and rebirth","description":"Death''s energy clears and releases, like autumn leaves making room for spring growth. This is an irreversible kind of transformation: the old must end for something new to begin. Energy moves from an ending toward renewal."},"timing":{"speed":"An unavoidable ending","description":"Death points to an ending whose timing is shaped by life itself. A period of transition may take one to three months, while full renewal may take longer. What is ready to end cannot always be hastened or delayed."},"advice":{"upright":"Accept the ending instead of resisting it. Release people, situations, or habits that no longer fit your life. Trust the process of change, even if you cannot yet see what comes next. Give yourself room to grieve, then take a brave step forward.","reversed":"Be honest about what you are holding on to and why it is hard to release. Fear is natural, but it does not have to prevent necessary change. Some things must end; accepting that sooner can help you begin a new chapter sooner."},"chakra":{"primary":"Root Chakra and whole-system clearing","issue":"Fear of loss may unsettle your sense of security, or your overall energy may feel in need of deep clearing.","healingNote":"Death''s transformation can affect the whole energy system, especially the Root Chakra, associated with survival and security. If it is difficult to accept an ending or transition, rebuilding a sense of safety and trust may help. Obsidian and smoky quartz can be included in personal practices for reflection and release. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that this ending may be a necessary blessing. What you have been holding on to has fulfilled its purpose, and it may be time to let go. Death is not the end, but a doorway to transformation. As you release what is complete, new life can begin. Trust the process; renewal is waiting on the other side.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that you cannot remain between two worlds forever. What has reached its end must be allowed to end; resisting it can deepen the pain. Letting go does not mean losing everything; it can make room for what truly matters. Stop fighting life''s natural movement and allow change to take place. Renewal is waiting on the other side."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '14-temperance', 'en', 'Temperance', '節制', '{"keywords":["Balance","Adjustment","Patience","Harmony","Moderation"],"arcana":"major","number":14}', '{"uprightMeaning":"Temperance represents balance, harmony, and the wisdom of moderation. The image of an angel pouring water between two cups symbolizes energy moving and blending. When Temperance appears, it reminds you to seek balance and harmony in different areas of life. This may mean bringing opposing elements together, balancing work and personal life, or making room for both reason and emotion. Temperance encourages patience and self-restraint, and cautions against extremes and excess. This is a time for healing, adaptation, and integration, calling for gentle, gradual progress. Temperance also represents spiritual alchemy: different elements becoming a harmonious whole. It reminds you that moderation has wisdom and that enough can be enough. With patience and adjustment, you can cultivate inner peace and greater harmony around you.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Temperance card suggests imbalance, excess, or a lack of moderation. You may be putting too much energy into one area while neglecting other important parts of life. This card can also point to impatience and a desire for quick results that leads you to skip necessary steps. You may feel disharmony within yourself or in your surroundings, unable to bring opposing elements together. The reversed Temperance asks you to find your balance again. Review your life and notice where there may be too much or too little. Practice moderation and avoid swinging to extremes. This card may also caution against overindulgence in a habit or behavior that calls for greater self-control. Take time to adjust gently. Remember that balance is not a final destination, but an ongoing process.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Harmonious Balance","Moderation","Integration","Patient Progress","Alchemy"],"reversed":["Imbalance and Excess","Lack of Moderation","Extremes","Impatience","Difficulty Integrating"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, Temperance represents the art of integration and balance, like alchemy. An angel pours water between two cups, one associated with active energy and the other with receptive energy, symbolizing opposing elements blending in harmony. This card teaches the wisdom of moderation: avoid extremes and find a point of balance among different forces. Temperance is not suppression, but harmonizing what is present. This is a time for healing and integration, as seemingly conflicting parts of life are brought into a more coherent whole. Temperance asks you to be patient and make gradual progress. Real strength is not found in extremes, but in balance. When you find your center, you can work with change more skillfully.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, Temperance suggests imbalance and excess. You may be investing too much in one area and neglecting other important needs, or swinging sharply between extremes. The energy of integration is blocked, making it hard for opposing elements to coexist peacefully. You may be impatient for results and skip steps that matter. This card can also point to overindulgence in a habit or behavior and difficulty exercising self-control. The reversed Temperance reminds you that imbalance can cause distress. Look honestly at where there is too much and where there is not enough. Healing takes time and patience; it cannot be forced to happen all at once. Return to your center and find balance again."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Two-way flow and integration","type":"Harmonizing and balancing","description":"Temperance''s energy flows in both directions, building a bridge between opposing forces. It is gentle, gradual, and continually adjusting, seeking dynamic balance rather than rigid stillness. Energy transforms through integration."},"timing":{"speed":"Gradual and unhurried","description":"Temperance represents a gradual process that calls for time and patience. Genuine integration and balance cannot be rushed and may take two to four months of ongoing adjustment. Take your time; steady work matters."},"advice":{"upright":"Seek the middle path and avoid extremes. Find balance between work and personal life, reason and emotion, and giving and receiving. Be patient and make changes gently. Integrate opposing parts instead of forcing yourself to choose only one side.","reversed":"Look at where your life may be out of balance. What is receiving too much attention, and what is being neglected? Practice moderation and self-control. Do not rush results; give yourself time to adjust gradually. Return to your center and rebuild harmony."},"chakra":{"primary":"Heart Chakra","issue":"Heart Chakra imbalance may make it difficult to integrate opposing energies or may pull you too strongly toward one extreme.","healingNote":"Temperance is closely connected with the Heart Chakra''s role in balance and integration, bridging the upper and lower energy centers. If you feel out of balance or unable to reconcile conflicting needs, this center may benefit from care. Rose quartz and green aventurine can be included in personal reflection practices. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that the art of life is balance, not perfection. You are learning an alchemy that turns opposites into harmony. Be patient; the middle path can be a powerful one. You do not have to choose one side when you can integrate both. In balance, you may discover a truer sense of yourself.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that you may have lost your center. Excess and deprivation are both forms of imbalance. Pause and look honestly at your life; you cannot keep swinging between extremes. Healing comes through gentle adjustments rather than drastic changes. Return to your center and begin again from there."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '15-devil', 'en', 'The Devil', '惡魔', '{"keywords":["Bondage","Addiction","Materialism","Dependency","Limitations"],"arcana":"major","number":15}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Devil represents bondage, addiction, and the pull of material desire. The figures on the card are chained, but the chains are loose, suggesting that some constraints are self-imposed and may be possible to loosen. When this card appears, you may feel trapped by a habit, belief, or relationship. This could involve substance use, a harmful relationship, compulsive behavior, or a limiting pattern of thought. The Devil also represents the shadow self and suppressed desires, asking you to face deep fears and parts of yourself you have kept hidden. This card is not here to judge you; it is meant to bring awareness to what may be controlling you. Once you can recognize a bond, you can begin to consider your choices and seek support to loosen it. The Devil reminds you that change and greater freedom are possible.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Devil is often an encouraging sign of beginning to break free from constraints, move toward release, and see more clearly. You may be working to change an addictive pattern, leave a harmful relationship, or challenge a limiting belief. This card suggests that you are starting to see through an illusion. However, the reversed Devil can also point to denying that a problem exists or underestimating the hold a pattern has on you. You may tell yourself everything is fine while remaining caught in an unhealthy cycle. The reversed Devil reminds you that release is a process requiring courage and honesty. Do not be afraid to face your shadow; accepting and integrating it can help you move toward freedom. This can be a powerful time of change and an opportunity to take greater ownership of your life. If addiction or safety is involved, professional and trusted support can be an important part of that process.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Self-Imposed Bondage","Addiction and Dependency","Material Temptation","Shadow Self","False Security"],"reversed":["Breaking Free","Awakening and Release","Changing Addictive Patterns","Facing the Shadow","Breaking Limitations"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Devil reveals bonds and limitations that may have been created or reinforced by your own choices. The figures are held by loose chains, suggesting that a way out may exist even if it is not yet easy to see. This card asks you to notice what is controlling you: an addictive pattern, a harmful relationship, material desire, a limiting belief, or an excessive need for security. The Devil represents the shadow parts of yourself—the desires and fears you may not want to admit. It is not a judgment, but an invitation to become aware. Recognizing what binds you is the first step toward choosing what to do about it. The Devil reminds you that a prison can be built from your own beliefs, and that the possibility of freedom begins with seeing the key you already hold.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, the Devil often signals that you are beginning to break free and see clearly what has been controlling you. You may be loosening old chains, changing an addictive pattern, leaving a harmful relationship, or challenging limiting beliefs. Yet the reversed Devil can also indicate continued denial or the belief that you are free when the same pattern has simply taken another form. Genuine release takes courage and honesty about your vulnerabilities. The more clearly you can see the bond, the more consciously you can choose how to respond."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Heavy and downward","type":"Bondage and limitation","description":"The Devil''s energy feels dense and heavy, as though pulled downward by gravity. It can feel sticky and difficult to escape, leaving you trapped or powerless. Energy is confined to material concerns and struggles to rise."},"timing":{"speed":"Slow and stuck","description":"The Devil represents feeling trapped, where time itself may seem distorted. Breaking a pattern calls for awareness and sustained effort and may take three to six months or longer. Change will not happen automatically; it asks you to take active steps to interrupt the cycle."},"advice":{"upright":"Be honest about what is binding you. Stop telling yourself, “I can quit whenever I want,” without examining the pattern. Face your shadow, acknowledge your vulnerabilities and desires, and remember that a chain can sometimes be loosened. Ask yourself why you are choosing to stay. If addiction, abuse, or safety is involved, reach out to qualified and trusted support rather than facing it alone.","reversed":"If you are working to break free, keep going and seek support when you need it. If you are denying a problem, this is a time to face it honestly. Breaking an old pattern takes courage and persistence. You do not have to do it alone; acknowledging what is happening is a meaningful first step."},"chakra":{"primary":"Root Chakra and Sacral Chakra","issue":"Excessive attachment to material security (Root Chakra), or feeling controlled by desire and compulsive patterns (Sacral Chakra).","healingNote":"The Devil relates to imbalance in the lower energy centers, especially the Root Chakra, associated with fear and security, and the Sacral Chakra, associated with desire and pleasure. If you feel trapped or unable to change a pattern, grounding and reflective practices may help you explore what is happening. Obsidian and smoky quartz can be included in personal practices for reflection and release. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that you may be freer than you think. The chains that bind you may be loose, and a choice may be available—but first you have to acknowledge the chains are there. Do not be afraid to see your shadow; it is a part of you that needs care and acceptance. You still have the power to choose your next step.","reversed":"Your soul is celebrating your awakening: you are working to break free and reclaim your choices. This path may not be easy, but you have begun. Do not let old comforts pull you back into the same pattern. True freedom lies ahead. Or perhaps your soul is reminding you to stop denying the problem: you may not be fully free yet, but caught in a different form of the same cage. Be honest with yourself."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '16-tower', 'en', 'The Tower', '高塔', '{"keywords":["Sudden Change","Upheaval","Revelation","Destruction","Awakening"],"arcana":"major","number":16}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Tower represents sudden change, disruption, and moments of awakening. The lightning-struck tower symbolizes structures built on unstable foundations beginning to collapse. When this card appears, a dramatic shift may be approaching, perhaps through a startling revelation, an unexpected event, or problems that have been building over time finally surfacing. Although the change may be painful and unsettling, it can clear away what no longer serves you and make room for something more genuine and stable. The Tower reminds you that sometimes a system needs a complete reset before it can be rebuilt on firmer ground. This is a moment of awakening and truth coming to light. Even when the process is difficult, it can create room for release and growth. Accept what needs to be dismantled and remain open to new possibilities emerging from the ruins.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Tower suggests that you may be avoiding or delaying a necessary change or breakdown. You may sense a major shift coming and try to prevent or control it. Fear of change may be so strong that you would rather maintain an unhealthy status quo. The reversed Tower reminds you that resistance can make matters more difficult. When a foundation is unstable, continuing to build on it can make an eventual collapse more severe. This card can also represent recovering from upheaval or trauma: the process may be slow, but rebuilding has begun. The reversed Tower encourages you not to fear necessary change and to accept that some things need to end. Rather than resist what cannot be avoided, you may choose to make changes proactively and transform things in a more manageable way.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Sudden Collapse","Shocking Revelation","Destruction and Rebuilding","False Structures Falling","Liberation and Awakening"],"reversed":["Avoiding Upheaval","Slow Breakdown","Fear of Change","Recovery and Rebuilding","Resisting the Truth"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Tower represents sudden upheaval and a startling moment of awakening. Lightning strikes the tower, symbolizing a forceful break through false structures and illusions. Your world may be shaken as beliefs, relationships, or systems built on unstable foundations begin to fall apart. This can be painful, but it may also be necessary. The Tower does not destroy what is genuine; it exposes what is false or unstable. This can feel like a forced awakening when change has been resisted for too long. The Tower reminds you that sometimes an entire system needs to be dismantled and rebuilt. In the ruins, you may see truths that were hidden. The breakdown can be the beginning of release.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, the Tower suggests that you may be avoiding or delaying a necessary breakdown. You sense the foundations shaking, yet try to prevent or control what is happening. The disruption may unfold more slowly or less dramatically, or you may already be recovering from a painful upheaval. Fear of change may be keeping you attached to a status quo that is barely holding together. The reversed Tower reminds you that delay can make an eventual collapse more difficult. Continuing to build on an unstable foundation carries risks. Sometimes the braver choice is to dismantle what is not working before it falls on its own. This card can also mark gradual progress as you rebuild after a difficult experience."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Forceful downward impact","type":"Destruction and clearing","description":"The Tower''s energy is explosive and disruptive, like a sudden flash of lightning. It breaks down old structures and clears obstacles. Though startling, this energy can also bring release, striking forcefully from above."},"timing":{"speed":"Sudden and rapid","description":"The Tower points to a sudden event that may unfold within one to two weeks, though its timing cannot be predicted with certainty. The disruption may happen quickly, while rebuilding can take longer—often three to six months or more."},"advice":{"upright":"Do not cling to a structure that is no longer stable. Release your attachment to what is falling away and face the change. Look for truth and new possibilities amid the disruption. This is not necessarily the end; it can be the beginning of rebuilding. Give yourself time to recover without defining yourself only by what happened.","reversed":"If you sense a breakdown coming, consider facing the situation proactively instead of resisting it. Examine whether your foundations are sound; if they are not, making a deliberate change may be better than waiting for a collapse. If you are already rebuilding, keep moving one step at a time. Do not try to restore a structure that has already fallen if it no longer serves you."},"chakra":{"primary":"Whole-system reset","issue":"Your entire energy system may feel shaken and in need of rebuilding and realignment.","healingNote":"The Tower represents a deep reset that can affect the whole energy system. After upheaval, you may need time and support to regain your footing, starting with a sense of safety and grounding. Crystal practices can be used as personal reminders while rebuilding stability. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that this collapse may be a necessary blessing. The tower that held you back for so long may need to come down. In the ruins, you may discover a more authentic version of yourself. Do not assume that losing an old structure means losing everything; you can rebuild with greater honesty and stability. This can be a forceful release—meet it with courage.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that collapse cannot always be prevented, and delay can make it more difficult. If the foundation is unstable, it may be wiser to dismantle and rebuild intentionally. Or perhaps your soul is saying: you have been through upheaval, and you are still here. Now you can rebuild. Do not recreate the old tower; build something more honest and real."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '17-star', 'en', 'The Star', '星星', '{"keywords":["Hope","Faith","Inspiration","Serenity","Renewal"],"arcana":"major","number":17}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Star represents hope, faith, and spiritual renewal. Often appearing after the Tower, it symbolizes finding light and direction again after darkness and upheaval. When the Star appears, it brings an energy of calm, healing, and optimism. This can be a time to reconnect with your spirituality, restore confidence, and look toward the future. The Star encourages you to trust your sense of guidance and hold on to hope through difficult moments. It also represents inspiration, creativity, and connection with your higher self. Its energy is clear and peaceful, reminding you that quiet moments can hold strength. This may be a time to tend to old wounds, regain vitality, and become open to a brighter future. The Star illuminates the path ahead and reminds you not to give up hope; dawn can follow even a long night.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Star suggests that you may be going through a period of hopelessness, shaken faith, or lack of direction. You may feel discouraged and unable to see light ahead. This card can also point to feeling disconnected from your spirituality or losing a sense of meaning. Self-doubt and negative thoughts may be making it hard to recognize your potential and worth. The reversed Star reminds you that hope can still exist in dark moments. Do not let a temporary setback destroy your faith in yourself. This is a time to reconnect with your inner light. Seek out what inspires and uplifts you, whether that is nature, art, or spiritual practice. Losing hope can be temporary; you can take steps to rekindle it. Keep faith that light can return.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Renewed Hope","Spiritual Healing","Clear Faith","Guiding Inspiration","Peaceful Renewal"],"reversed":["Lost Hope","Shaken Faith","Spiritual Exhaustion","Self-Doubt","Feeling Directionless"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Star represents finding hope again after a period of darkness. Often following the Tower, it suggests that calm and healing may come after disruption and confusion. The Star brings clear hope, spiritual renewal, and renewed confidence in the future. This can be a time to reconnect with your spirituality and rebuild your faith. Its energy is gentle and restorative, like fresh water tending to a wound. The card reminds you that starlight can still be seen after the darkest night. The Star points to an authentic part of you that remains open, hopeful, and connected to a larger whole. It encourages you to keep faith and remain open to what may unfold. This may also be a period when inspiration and creativity begin to return. Your healing process can begin one small step at a time.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, the Star suggests hopelessness, shaken faith, or spiritual exhaustion. The darkness may feel so heavy that you cannot see any light. Hope can seem obscured, leaving you without direction or a sense of meaning. You may be overwhelmed by self-doubt and negative thoughts, unable to believe that things can improve. This card can also point to feeling spiritually disconnected, empty, or lost. The reversed Star reminds you that the light may be obscured without being gone. Even if you cannot see hope right now, it may still be there. This is a time to rebuild faith and look for meaning in small ways. Begin with simple steps that help you reconnect with your inner light. The reversed Star can also caution against optimism that is detached from practical reality."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Healing flow from above","type":"Receiving and renewal","description":"The Star''s energy is like healing water flowing down from the sky: gentle, nourishing, and renewing. It is clear, peaceful, and hopeful, soft yet enduring like starlight. Energy flows from the larger universe toward the earth, offering spiritual nourishment."},"timing":{"speed":"Slow healing","description":"The Star represents a period of healing and recovery that cannot be rushed. Renewal takes time and may unfold over two to six months. Allow yourself a quiet period to recover and let hope return gradually."},"advice":{"upright":"Keep room for hope and faith. This is a time for healing, so give yourself space to recover. Reconnect with your spirituality and seek out what inspires you. Remain open to a brighter future, and spend time in nature if it helps you feel restored.","reversed":"Do not let hopelessness consume you. Light may still be present even when you cannot see it. Rebuild faith through small things: a moment of gratitude or a beautiful experience. Seek support; you do not have to face the dark alone. Reconnect with your spirituality in ways that feel genuine to you."},"chakra":{"primary":"Crown Chakra and Throat Chakra","issue":"Feeling disconnected from a larger source of meaning (Crown Chakra), or unable to express your authentic self (Throat Chakra).","healingNote":"The Star relates to the Crown Chakra, associated with spiritual connection, and the Throat Chakra, associated with authentic expression. If you have lost hope or cannot express yourself, these centers may need care. Selenite and aquamarine can be included in personal reflective practices. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that the darkest part of the night may be behind you. Starlight can help illuminate your path, and healing may already be underway. You do not have to force anything; stay open and allow hope to return in its own time. Your essential nature can still be clear and full of light. Remember this when you feel lost.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that despair can pass and hope can return. Not feeling the starlight does not mean it is gone. Loosen your grip on doubt and make room to believe that good things are still possible. The darkness you are experiencing is not all that you are; there is light within you too. Take your time, let hope return gradually, and do not give up."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '18-moon', 'en', 'The Moon', '月亮', '{"keywords":["Illusion","Intuition","Subconscious","Fear","Mystery"],"arcana":"major","number":18}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Moon represents illusion, the subconscious, and the realm of inner fears. Its hazy moonlit scene suggests that things may not be as they appear. When this card appears, you may be in a period of uncertainty and confusion, with some truths hidden or distorted. The Moon encourages you to explore your subconscious and face fears and shadow parts within. It also represents intuition, dreams, and deeper layers of the mind. Its energy is mysterious and powerful, drawing attention to what is hidden or unknown. This is a time to listen to your intuition and find the courage to face inner fears. Do not be misled by appearances; look carefully for what is real. The Moon reminds you that some things need to develop in the dark before they can be revealed at the right time.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Moon suggests that illusions may be fading and the truth beginning to emerge. You may be moving out of confusion and gradually seeing what is really happening. This card can also indicate that you are releasing long-suppressed fears and anxiety and beginning to face your shadow. However, the reversed Moon may also mean that fear still has a hold on you or that you are avoiding messages from your subconscious. You may be suppressing emotions and intuition while trying to control everything with reason. The reversed Moon asks you not to ignore your inner voice and feelings. Give yourself time and space to process complicated emotions instead of demanding immediate clarity. Sometimes accepting uncertainty and ambiguity is necessary. As time passes, more may become clear. Trust your intuition as one source of guidance through the fog.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Fog of Illusion","Subconscious Exploration","Intuitive Guidance","Emerging Fears","Hidden Mysteries"],"reversed":["Truth Coming to Light","Finding a Way Through the Fog","Releasing Fear","Growing Clarity","Avoiding Intuition"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Moon leads into the mysterious realm of the subconscious, where illusion can obscure what is real. The moonlit scene is unclear, reflecting a period of uncertainty or confusion. This card reminds you that appearances may not tell the whole story and that deeper exploration may be needed. The Moon represents the subconscious, dreams, intuition, and also the fears and shadows within. This is a time to face the unknown and listen to your intuition. The Moon may not provide clear answers; it asks you to move carefully through ambiguity, using your felt sense as well as reason. It can also point to deception, illusion, or projections. The Moon reminds you that what is forming in darkness may need time to emerge. Do not force clarity before it is ready; allow some mystery to remain.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, the Moon often suggests that illusions are beginning to fade and the truth is becoming clearer. You may be finding your way out of confusion and releasing fears or anxiety that have been suppressed for a long time. This can be a constructive shift toward greater awareness. However, the reversed Moon can also point to avoiding or denying messages from your subconscious. You may use reason to suppress intuition or refuse to face your fears. The card reminds you that clarity can come from facing the darkness rather than avoiding it. Sometimes it is wiser to accept uncertainty than to force an answer. The Moon''s wisdom is not always about understanding everything; it can also be about learning to trust your perception while you wait for more to emerge."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Tidal ebb and flow","type":"Subconscious fluctuation","description":"The Moon''s energy fluctuates like tides responding to the lunar cycle. It is mysterious, ambiguous, and emotional, not easily grasped through reason alone. Energy moves between conscious and subconscious states, bringing dreams, feelings, and shifting perceptions."},"timing":{"speed":"Unclear and shifting","description":"The Moon represents uncertain timing, with matters still hidden or confusing. It may take one to three months for the fog to clear. Avoid rushing into a decision; allow more information and understanding to emerge over time."},"advice":{"upright":"Trust your intuition even when you cannot see the whole picture. Do not rush a decision; give yourself time to observe and feel. Write down your dreams if that helps you reflect on your subconscious. Face your fears rather than letting them grow unseen, and make room for uncertainty.","reversed":"If the truth is emerging, allow yourself to acknowledge it, even if it is uncomfortable. If you have been avoiding your intuition, pause and listen inwardly. Make room for fears and emotions you have been suppressing. As the fog lifts, rebuild trust in your own perceptions."},"chakra":{"primary":"Third Eye Chakra and Sacral Chakra","issue":"Fear may cloud intuition (Third Eye Chakra), or emotions may feel difficult to regulate (Sacral Chakra).","healingNote":"The Moon relates to the Third Eye Chakra, associated with intuition, and the Sacral Chakra, associated with emotion. If you feel confused or overwhelmed by fear, these centers may need balance. Moonstone and labradorite can be included in personal practices for reflection and grounding. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul wants you to know that not every truth can be understood immediately. Some things need to develop in darkness and take shape amid uncertainty. Your fear is not necessarily an enemy; it may be a message waiting to be understood. Trust your intuition, even when it leads you into unfamiliar territory. The Moon''s light may be faint, but it can still help you notice the next part of the path.","reversed":"Your soul is celebrating as the fog begins to lift and you start to see more clearly. Or your soul may be reminding you to stop avoiding what you already know. Your intuition may have been pointing toward the truth, even if you have not wanted to hear it. Face your fears and move beyond denial. Clarity can come from having the courage to see what is there, including what you would rather not see."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '19-sun', 'en', 'The Sun', '太陽', '{"keywords":["Joy","Success","Vitality","Positivity","Celebration"],"arcana":"major","number":19}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The Sun represents joy, success, and uncomplicated happiness. It is one of the most positive cards in the Tarot, symbolizing light, warmth, and vitality. When the Sun appears, it points toward a brighter period in which your efforts may be rewarded and success may be within reach. The Sun illuminates what was hidden, bringing clarity, truth, and insight. This can be a lively, confident, and optimistic time, well suited to expressing your authentic self and enjoying what life has to offer. The Sun also represents childlike openness, innocence, and simple happiness, reminding you to keep your heart sincere and receptive. It encourages you to celebrate accomplishments, share joy, and approach life with a positive attitude. The Sun''s energy is generous and nourishing, supporting growth. This is a time to appreciate what has come to fruition, give thanks for the good in your life, and look ahead with hope.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Sun is usually still positive, but may point to temporary clouds or joy that is delayed. You may feel low on energy, less confident, or unable to fully enjoy a success. This card can also caution against excessive optimism or overlooking a problem. You may be seeing a situation through rose-colored glasses instead of assessing it realistically. The reversed Sun reminds you that light can still be present during difficult moments, even when clouds temporarily obscure it. Do not let a setback diminish your confidence or optimism. Look for positive things in daily life, even if they seem small. Reconnect with your own sources of joy and vitality rather than letting outside circumstances determine your happiness. Remember that clouds can pass. Be patient and keep faith in the possibility of better days.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Pure Joy","Achievement","Vitality","Authentic Self","Radiant Clarity"],"reversed":["Temporary Clouds","Excessive Optimism","Delayed Joy","Low Confidence","Overlooking the Shadow"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the Sun represents life''s purest joy and the visible expression of success. It shines generously on all things, symbolizing abundance, warmth, and vitality at their height. This card brings clarity, truth, and strongly positive energy. It can mark a harvest period when your efforts are rewarded and progress is clear. The Sun represents your authentic self: open, lively, and unafraid to be seen. Its joy is simple and wholehearted. Under the Sun, things become easier to see and there is less room for concealment. The upright Sun encourages you to express yourself confidently, celebrate your achievements, and share your happiness. Enjoy this bright moment and remember that you deserve to appreciate what is good in your life.","reversedExplanation":"The reversed Sun is usually still positive, though its light may be temporarily obscured. You may feel less energetic or confident, or find it difficult to enjoy a success fully. There may be a delay, a temporary setback, or an inner cloud affecting your outlook. You may be overly optimistic and overlooking practical concerns, or seeing things through rose-colored glasses. This card can also point to fear of showing your authentic self or inner shadows that still need care. The reversed Sun reminds you that sunlight remains even when clouds cover it. Do not let temporary difficulties take all your joy away. Look for what is still bright, and rebuild your confidence and vitality. The clouds can part in time."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Radiating outward","type":"Expansion and generosity","description":"The Sun''s energy radiates outward, freely giving light and warmth. It is abundant, warm, and full of vitality, illuminating and nourishing what it touches. This energy is open, positive, and generous."},"timing":{"speed":"Rapid progress and clarity","description":"The Sun points to clear, relatively quick progress. Joy or a successful result may appear within one to four weeks. This can be a harvest period when the results of earlier effort are ready to be enjoyed."},"advice":{"upright":"Enjoy this positive period and celebrate what you have achieved. Share your happiness, express your authentic self with confidence, and do not hide your light. Give thanks for what you have. This can be a good time for creative and purposeful action.","reversed":"Look for what is still positive, even if it seems small. Do not let a temporary difficulty erase your optimism. Rebuild your confidence and remember your worth, while also checking whether excessive optimism is keeping you from seeing a real concern. Clouds can pass; keep perspective."},"chakra":{"primary":"Solar Plexus Chakra and Heart Chakra","issue":"Low personal power or confidence (Solar Plexus Chakra), or a closed heart that makes it difficult to feel joy (Heart Chakra).","healingNote":"The Sun relates to the Solar Plexus Chakra, associated with personal power, and the Heart Chakra, associated with joy and connection. If you feel low in energy or unable to enjoy things, gentle practices that support these centers may help. Citrine and orange calcite can be included in personal reflection rituals. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul is celebrating: you have come through darkness into the light. This joy is a result of your effort, and you deserve to enjoy it. Do not make yourself smaller; let yourself shine. Your light does not diminish others and may help illuminate the way for them too. Remember this moment if you face darkness again: light can return.","reversed":"Your soul is reminding you that the Sun is still there, even when temporarily obscured. Do not let a passing cloud make you forget your own light. You have an inner capacity for brightness and joy that difficulty cannot erase. Reconnect with your inner Sun; it is still there, waiting to be remembered. You deserve good things, and you can hold on to that belief."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '20-judgement', 'en', 'Judgement', '審判', '{"keywords":["Awakening","Reflection","Forgiveness","Decision","Rebirth"],"arcana":"major","number":20}', '{"uprightMeaning":"Judgement represents awakening, reflection, and an important moment of decision. The angel''s trumpet calls sleeping souls to rise, symbolizing an inner calling and a summons toward a higher purpose. When Judgement appears, it asks you to review past experiences, learn from them, and make an important choice. This is a time for honest self-reflection and looking carefully at your life, actions, and decisions. Judgement also represents forgiveness, atonement, and renewal, encouraging you to release past mistakes and regrets and offer yourself and others another chance. The card can bring clear insight and a broader understanding of patterns and meaning in your life. Judgement asks you to listen to your inner calling and respond to what feels purposeful and true. This is a time of transformation and growth, preparing you to welcome a new beginning.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed Judgement card suggests that you may be avoiding self-reflection or finding it difficult to forgive yourself or others. Guilt, shame, or self-criticism may be keeping you tied to past mistakes. This card can also indicate ignoring an inner calling or refusing to respond to a larger purpose. Fear of change or reluctance to take responsibility may cause you to miss an important opportunity. The reversed Judgement asks you to face yourself honestly rather than avoid necessary reflection and evaluation. Forgiveness can be a key to release, whether you are forgiving another person or yourself. Let go of harsh judgment and meet your past with compassion and understanding. Learn from experience without allowing it to define you. Listen to your inner voice and respond to what life is asking of you, even if you feel uncertain or afraid.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Spiritual Awakening","Self-Reflection","Forgiveness and Release","Answering a Calling","Renewal and Transformation"],"reversed":["Avoiding Evaluation","Difficulty Forgiving","Ignoring a Calling","Self-Criticism","Missed Opportunity"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, Judgement marks a moment of spiritual awakening and an inner call. The angel''s trumpet symbolizes a summons from a higher awareness, inviting you to respond to a purpose that feels true. This card asks you to review the past, reflect on experience, learn what you can, and make an important decision. It can be a time to reckon with past choices and awaken to what matters now. Judgement represents forgiveness: letting go of mistakes and regrets, and making room for a fresh start. This is a moment of renewal, when an old sense of self can give way to a new one. Judgement is not punishment; it is an opportunity for release and growth. It reminds you that you can answer your inner calling and prepare for a new chapter.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, Judgement suggests that you may be avoiding necessary self-reflection or evaluation. You may be unable to forgive yourself or others and feel caught in guilt, shame, or resentment. The inner call may be ignored or refused because you fear change or greater responsibility. This card can also point to harsh self-criticism and difficulty accepting that you have made mistakes. The reversed Judgement reminds you that forgiveness can be a key to release. You cannot change the past, but you can choose how to meet it now. Be honest about mistakes without allowing them to define you. Listen to your inner calling even if you feel afraid or uncertain. This may be a time to make an important decision instead of postponing it."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"Rising and elevating","type":"Awakening and renewal","description":"Judgement''s energy rises, like a soul waking from sleep and answering a higher call. It brings transformation, elevation, renewal, clear insight, and the possibility of a new beginning. Energy moves from an old sense of self toward a new one."},"timing":{"speed":"A decisive moment","description":"Judgement points to an important turning point that may unfold within one to three months. This can be a time for evaluation and decision-making. Circumstances may be ready for a choice and its consequences to be faced."},"advice":{"upright":"Review your past honestly and learn from it without becoming attached to regret. Forgive yourself and others where you can, and release what you are ready to put down. Listen to your inner calling and take responsibility for the purpose you choose. Meet a new beginning with courage.","reversed":"Stop avoiding yourself and look honestly at what is happening. Forgiveness is a form of release, not weakness. You may be judging yourself too harshly; accept that being human includes making mistakes. Listen for the inner call toward a more meaningful direction, and do not keep postponing a decision that is ready to be made."},"chakra":{"primary":"Crown Chakra and Throat Chakra","issue":"Difficulty receiving an inner or spiritual calling (Crown Chakra), or speaking up for what you believe is true (Throat Chakra).","healingNote":"Judgement relates to the Crown Chakra, associated with spiritual awareness, and the Throat Chakra, associated with authentic expression. If it is difficult to hear an inner calling or forgive, these centers may need care. Selenite and lapis lazuli can be included in personal reflective practices. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul is calling you: the time has come. You have learned from what you have been through, and now you can gather that wisdom and take responsibility for your purpose. Release the past, offer forgiveness, and move bravely toward what matters to you. You are being called to do something meaningful; do not underestimate yourself. A new beginning is already underway—meet it with openness.","reversed":"Your soul is asking you to stop avoiding and punishing yourself. You cannot change the past, but you can choose to forgive and release it. Your inner calling is growing louder; how long will you pretend not to hear it? Your purpose is waiting, but begin by accepting and forgiving yourself. It may be time to answer."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('tarot', '21-world', 'en', 'The World', '世界', '{"keywords":["Completion","Achievement","Fulfillment","Integration","Success"],"arcana":"major","number":21}', '{"uprightMeaning":"The World represents completion, achievement, and fulfillment. As the final card of the Major Arcana, it symbolizes the end of an important journey and the realization of a whole. When the World appears, you may have reached an important milestone, achieved a long-term goal, and integrated what you have learned. This is a time to celebrate success and enjoy the results of your efforts. The World also represents wholeness and unity: different parts of your life may be coming together in harmony. This card brings satisfaction, accomplishment, and inner peace. It encourages you to recognize your achievements and feel proud of how far you have come. At the same time, an ending can also be a beginning: one cycle is complete and another is about to open. Enjoy the present sense of fulfillment while staying open to new possibilities and adventures.","reversedMeaning":"The reversed World suggests that you may feel incomplete or not yet have reached a goal. You may be close to finishing but unable to cross the finish line for some reason. This card can point to a lack of closure, unresolved matters, or a delayed goal. You may have set unrealistic standards and feel dissatisfied, making it difficult to enjoy what you have already accomplished. The reversed World asks you to examine what is preventing you from completing this journey. Is it an outside obstacle or an inner fear? Sometimes fear of success or of the emptiness afterward can lead to self-sabotage. This card encourages you to overcome the final obstacle and finish what you started. It also asks you to appreciate the process, not only the outcome. Even if you have not reached your ultimate goal, you have already come a long way and deserve to recognize that effort.","detailedInterpretation":{"coreKeywords":{"upright":["Full Achievement","Integrated Wholeness","Journey Completed","A World of Possibilities","Fulfillment"],"reversed":["Unfinished Business","Lack of Closure","Stalled at the Threshold","Difficulty Celebrating","Unrealistic Standards"],"uprightExplanation":"Upright, the World represents the completion and fulfillment of the Major Arcana journey. After many experiences, the Fool reaches a moment of integration and wholeness. This card marks the close of an important journey, achievement of a goal, and a chance to celebrate success. The World symbolizes balance among the four elements and the integration of different parts of life into a harmonious whole. This is a time to gather the results of your effort and feel a deep sense of satisfaction and completion. The World encourages you to celebrate what you have achieved and recognize how far you have come. It also reminds you that every ending opens into a new beginning. One cycle is complete, and another is about to unfold. New possibilities and a larger journey may be waiting for you.","reversedExplanation":"Reversed, the World suggests that you may feel incomplete or have not yet reached a goal. You may be close to finishing but unable to cross the finish line. There may be unresolved matters, a lack of closure, or a delay. Unrealistic standards can leave you dissatisfied and unable to enjoy what you have already done. This card can also point to fear of the emptiness that may follow completion, leading to self-sabotage. The reversed World reminds you that completion does not require perfection. Ask what is holding you back: an outside obstacle or an inner fear? Recognize how far you have already come, even if the goal is not fully reached. Sometimes the process itself is an achievement. Let yourself pause, celebrate, and rest before beginning the next journey."},"energyFlow":{"direction":"A complete cycle","type":"Integration and completion","description":"The World''s energy is whole and complete, like a perfect circle. Its elements coexist in harmony and its many aspects are integrated. This is the energy of balance, completion, and realization, marking the close of one cycle and the beginning of another."},"timing":{"speed":"A moment of completion","description":"The World marks the end of a journey and suggests that circumstances may be ripe for completion. A milestone may arrive within one to three months. This is a time to gather results and celebrate as one important phase ends and another begins."},"advice":{"upright":"Celebrate what you have achieved and acknowledge the path you have taken. Enjoy this moment of fulfillment and be grateful for what you have learned and experienced. Stay open to what comes next; a new journey may be beginning. You have integrated a great deal, and you can take that experience into your next adventure.","reversed":"Look at what is keeping you from completing the journey. Are your standards too high, or are you afraid of the emptiness that may follow? Recognize what you have already accomplished instead of dismissing your effort because the goal is not fully complete. Sometimes the final step is letting go of perfectionism."},"chakra":{"primary":"Whole-system integration, especially the Crown and Root connection","issue":"Difficulty integrating spiritual and material life, or a lack of harmonious flow among the energy centers.","healingNote":"The World represents integration and balance throughout the energy system, connecting the Root Chakra with the Crown Chakra, earth with sky, and practical life with spiritual meaning. If you feel incomplete or out of balance, a whole-system approach to grounding and reflection may help. Crystal practices can be used as personal reminders of integration and balance. For chakra-related concerns, you may seek crystal-healing guidance from Teacher Wade."},"soulMessage":{"upright":"Your soul is celebrating: you did it. You completed this journey and learned what you came here to learn. You have integrated your experiences and become more whole. Enjoy this moment of fulfillment; you deserve joy and a sense of accomplishment. Remember, this is not the end, but a meaningful completion before a new beginning. A wider world is waiting to be explored.","reversed":"Your soul is gently asking: why can you not celebrate what you have achieved? You have come so far, so why does it still feel like not enough? Release perfectionism and recognize that you have completed an important part of the journey. Or perhaps your soul is encouraging you: you are at the final step, so do not give up. Whatever the case, you are already enough."}}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '1', 'en', 'Existence', '存在', '{"subtitle":"Existence"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You are in a state of complete ease and oneness with the universe. This is the energy of simply existing: you do not need to become anyone; you can just be. In this moment, you are experiencing a deep, essential joy, like a cloud drifting freely across the sky without a purpose or agenda. Your energy is expanding and resonating with everything around you. This is not an escape from reality, but a return to your most authentic state. When you stop chasing, you may discover that you are already home.","dailyGuidance":"Today''s message is to stop striving and simply be. You do not need to prove or accomplish anything. Let yourself settle into this moment and feel life''s natural flow. The universe is not asking you to do anything; it is inviting you to be. Each breath can be a celebration, and each moment can be complete in itself. Release plans and expectations for a while, and let life express itself through you. When you stop struggling, you may find that new possibilities arise naturally.","emotionalInsight":"Your anxiety may come from trying to become someone instead of accepting who you are now. Deep down, you may already be more whole than you realize. Loosening your attachment to the future can allow your emotions to settle. You have been looking outside yourself for approval and overlooking the abundance already within. Some fears and worries may be stories created by the mind. When you return to simple awareness, emotions can be experienced as passing visitors while you remain the steady center that notices them.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you are always doing and have forgotten how to simply be. The problem may not be outside you; you may have lost touch with the ease of existing without striving. Stop chasing, and an answer may arise on its own. The mind can keep creating problems and then trying to solve them in an endless cycle. A breakthrough may come not from finding one more answer, but from noticing that the problem itself may be less solid than it seems. When you relax into the present, some of the knots can begin to loosen because they were never as fixed as they appeared.","meditationEntry":"Close your eyes and notice the movement of your breath. You do not need to change anything; simply observe. Feel your body and its connection with the space around you. You are part of existence itself. Let awareness spread through your whole body and notice the life in each cell. Now allow that awareness to extend beyond the body''s boundaries and into the surrounding space. You are not separate from everything around you; you are part of the whole. In this space there is no problem to solve and no answer to chase, only stillness."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '2', 'en', 'Inner Voice', '內在聲音', '{"subtitle":"Inner Voice"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"Your inner world is asking for your attention. This is a time to listen inwardly; your intuition may be trying to share something important. Trust that quiet inner voice. Amid the noise of the world, your soul has been speaking softly, waiting for you to pause and listen. This energy invites you back to inner stillness, where the answers you have been seeking may already be waiting. Rather than searching outside yourself, remember that wisdom can be found within.","dailyGuidance":"Today, make some quiet space to listen to your inner wisdom. There is a lot of noise around you, so take a break from outside distractions and notice what your heart is saying. Give yourself time alone, away from social media, other people''s opinions, and outside expectations. In stillness, your intuition may become easier to hear. When making a decision today, do not ask everyone else first; check in with yourself. Your inner sense can help you discern what feels right for you, so give it room to speak.","emotionalInsight":"Emotional turbulence may arise when you ignore your inner voice. You may keep seeking outside advice and approval while forgetting that some of the truest answers are already within you. When you feel confused or anxious, it may be because your actions do not align with your inner guidance. Those uneasy feelings can be a reminder that you have moved away from your own path. Try listening for what your emotions are communicating; they can be guides to understanding what matters to you.","blockageAnalysis":"You may be unable to move forward because you are listening to other people instead of yourself. The block may be a lack of trust in your own intuition. As you learn to trust your inner guidance, your path may become clearer. You may fear making the wrong decision and keep looking for outside approval, but this can leave you feeling even more lost. The deeper block may not be a lack of information, but a lack of trust in yourself. When you begin to listen to your own wisdom, obstacles can look different and you may find a direction that feels like your own true north.","meditationEntry":"Find a quiet place and rest a hand over your heart. Ask yourself, “What is my heart trying to tell me?” Do not analyze; simply listen and allow an answer to emerge in its own way. Feel the rhythm of your heartbeat, the pulse of life. There is space between each breath, and in that space you can make room for inner wisdom. Do not rush to find an answer; stay open and receptive. When you become truly quiet, your inner voice may become clearer. It might arrive as a feeling, an image, or a simple knowing."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '3', 'en', 'Playfulness', '遊戲', '{"subtitle":"Playfulness"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"Your energy is calling for lightness and play. Life does not have to be so serious; this may be a moment to let your inner child come out and enjoy the simple joy of being alive. Perhaps it has been a long time since you truly laughed or felt carefree. This card reminds you that life can be a celebration, not only a list of tasks. Set down your responsibilities for a little while, even if only briefly, and reconnect with the part of you that knows how to play.","dailyGuidance":"Today''s reminder is not to take everything so seriously. Meet life with a playful spirit and you may discover more possibilities and creativity. Even work can sometimes be approached as a game. When you relax, inspiration may come more easily. Try doing something today without a goal, simply because it brings you joy: dance, sing, draw, or take a walk. Let a sense of lightness return, and you may find it easier to see new ways to approach a problem.","emotionalInsight":"Your heaviness may come from taking life too seriously. Loosen the frame of what you think you must do and allow yourself a little ease. Joy does not always need a reason. You may be carrying the weight of the world as though everything would fall apart if you stopped trying so hard. Yet life may flow more easily when you allow yourself to relax. Some things you treat as grave obligations may be mental cages. When you meet them with a playful perspective, they may lose some of their power over you.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you are treating life like an exam instead of an exploration. Loosen your attachment to outcomes and approach things with a spirit of play; new paths may open. Being preoccupied with right and wrong, winning and losing, can keep you from moving. Creativity and breakthroughs often need room to experiment. When you are less afraid of mistakes and imperfection, you may feel freer. The block may not be that you have not tried hard enough; you may be trying too hard. Relax and let yourself explore.","meditationEntry":"Remember a game you loved as a child and reconnect with the uncomplicated joy you felt. Let that energy move through your body. Feel the freedom of being fully present, with no past to revisit and no future to plan—only the joy of this moment. Let your body move without needing a reason, simply because it wants to. Allow a smile to arise naturally. In this space, you do not need to become anyone; you can simply enjoy being alive."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '4', 'en', 'The Rebel', '叛逆者', '{"subtitle":"The Rebel"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"Your rebellious spirit is awakening. This is a time to question old patterns and break out of limiting frames. You may no longer be willing to follow rules that do not belong to you. This energy is wild, free, and hard to contain. You are beginning to see through the supposed shoulds and musts that were never truly yours. This is not destruction for its own sake, but liberation. You are taking off masks that feel false and returning to a more original, untamed self. This can be a powerful moment of change.","dailyGuidance":"Today''s message is to have the courage to be yourself. Do not compromise what is true for you just to please others. Real freedom comes from living honestly. If something feels uncomfortable or false today, it is all right to say no. If there is something you have wanted to do but held back for fear of judgment, consider taking a step toward it. You do not need to wait for permission to be your own authority. The world needs your authenticity, not your compliance. Stand up for yourself, even if doing so feels lonely for a while.","emotionalInsight":"Anger and unease may come from suppressing your authentic self. You may have been playing a role others expect while something in you pushes back. Listen to that resistance. Relationships, work, or ways of living that make you feel stifled may be telling you that this path does not fit. Your emotions are not necessarily the problem; they can be signals. Anger may point to strength, and restlessness may reflect a desire for change. Rather than suppressing these feelings, explore what they are asking of you; they may help you return to what is genuine.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you fear breaking rules or being rejected. Yet the deeper block may be that you have not allowed yourself to be free. When you give yourself permission to question the rules, new paths may appear. You may be too concerned with others'' opinions and afraid of losing love or belonging. But when you distort yourself to gain acceptance, you risk losing touch with who you are. A breakthrough may ask you to tolerate some loneliness, misunderstanding, or discomfort in order to live more truthfully. When you make that choice, you may find support in unexpected places.","meditationEntry":"Imagine a wall in front of you representing the rules and limits that hold you back. Now picture yourself walking through it. Feel the energy of freedom moving through you. The wall may represent your parents'' expectations, social standards, or limits you have absorbed. Look at it and ask: do you want to remain confined by it, or are you ready to move beyond it? Take a deep breath and feel the strength within you. You may be stronger than you think. Walk through the wall and into a life that feels more truly yours, where no one else can dictate how you must live."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '5', 'en', 'Aloneness', '孤獨', '{"subtitle":"Aloneness"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You are in a moment of deep solitude. This is not the same as loneliness; it can be an opportunity to connect deeply with yourself. In solitude, you may discover the richness within. This is a sacred space where you do not need to play a role or meet anyone else''s expectations. You can simply be yourself, fully. This energy invites you to stop looking outward for everything and return to your inner sanctuary. There, you may meet your most authentic self, the part of you that is not defined by being alone. Solitude can be a gift rather than a punishment.","dailyGuidance":"Make some time to be alone today. Do not fear your own company; solitude may help you discover what feels most true to you. This can be a nourishing moment for your inner life. Cancel a social plan if you need to, turn off your phone, and give yourself time that belongs only to you. Do not fill every moment with activity; spend some quiet time in your own company. In that space, you may hear an inner voice that is usually covered by noise. Practice enjoying time by yourself; it can be a deep form of self-care.","emotionalInsight":"A feeling of emptiness may come from looking outside yourself to fill it. Lasting contentment begins with your relationship with yourself. Learn to be with solitude rather than always escaping it. You may fear facing yourself, so you keep filling life with relationships, work, or entertainment. Yet these external things cannot always fill an inner space. When you are willing to sit with what feels empty, you may discover that it is not a void but a space full of possibility. Aloneness is not necessarily a lack; it can also be a sense of wholeness.","blockageAnalysis":"You may have difficulty moving forward because you fear being alone and rely heavily on outside connections. The block may be that you have not yet learned to be your own good companion. Embrace solitude and your strength may return. You may be spending a lot of energy maintaining relationships, pleasing others, and seeking connection while forgetting your relationship with yourself. Fear of being alone can keep you in unhealthy relationships. As you learn to enjoy your own company, you may feel stronger and less dependent on others to define you. This can be a form of freedom.","meditationEntry":"Sit in a quiet space and notice what it is like to be here on your own. You do not need anyone''s company; simply be with yourself. Feel the wholeness of this moment. Close your eyes and breathe deeply. Notice your existence, not as someone''s partner, friend, child, or parent, but simply as yourself. In this moment, you are whole; nothing is missing. Let the feeling of aloneness be present without resisting it. Within solitude there can be deep quiet and freedom. You can set down your masks and return to your essential self."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '6', 'en', 'The Lovers', '愛人', '{"subtitle":"The Lovers"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You are in a moment of deep connection, whether with another person, with life, or with the receptive and active energies within yourself. This is the energy of love in motion—not possession, but meeting and blending. Your heart may be opening, allowing you to feel and give more fully. This energy invites you to lower your defenses and allow vulnerability, because genuine intimacy needs room for it. Love is not about finding perfection; it is about recognizing wholeness within imperfection. This can be a time of healing, as old hurts begin to soften in the light of love.","dailyGuidance":"Today is about connection. Whether you are deepening a relationship or bringing the receptive and active energies within yourself into greater harmony, be present and involved. Do not be afraid to show who you really are, including your vulnerability and imperfections. Real love does not require perfection; it asks for authenticity. Practice giving without expecting something in return. When you give from a sense of abundance rather than lack, love can flow more naturally. Remember that caring for yourself is part of being able to care for others.","emotionalInsight":"Your emotions may be telling you that it is time to open your heart. Past hurts may have led you to build high walls, but those walls can also keep love from entering. Allow yourself to risk feeling again. Even though being open can involve the possibility of hurt, it is also part of being alive. Your heart may long for connection and to be seen, understood, and accepted. Do not deny that need; it is not weakness. When you allow yourself to give and receive love, you reconnect with an essential part of life. Healing may be taking place; give the process time.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you fear being hurt again, so you have closed your heart. But a closed heart also has difficulty receiving love. A breakthrough may begin with a willingness to be vulnerable and take an emotional risk. You may be waiting for perfectly safe love, but intimacy involves letting go of some control. It is difficult to experience closeness while remaining completely guarded. The block may not be that you have not found the right person, but that you are still learning how to show up authentically. When you accept and care for all parts of yourself, including those you think are unworthy of love, some barriers may begin to fall.","meditationEntry":"Rest a hand over your heart and feel its rhythm. Imagine your heart as a lotus slowly opening, one petal with each breath. Do not force it; simply allow it. Notice past hurts without running away from them. You might thank them for what they have taught you about the depth of love. Now imagine a warm light rising from your heart and filling your chest. This is the energy of love; it has been here all along. Let this love flow toward yourself first, embracing every part of you. Then allow it to move outward naturally, toward the people and beings in your life."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '7', 'en', 'Patience', '耐心', '{"subtitle":"Patience"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"This is a time of waiting, but not passive waiting; it is an opportunity to be fully aware and present. The seed has been planted, and now it needs time to sprout. You cannot hurry a rose into bloom; you can offer sunlight and water, then trust the process. This energy teaches you that life has its own rhythm and forcing it can interfere with its natural unfolding. You are learning a deep lesson in trust. When you stop pushing, you may notice that life has its own way of moving forward. This is not giving up, but participating with greater awareness.","dailyGuidance":"Today''s message is to slow down. Do not rush to see the result or reach the destination; the process itself has value. You may be hurrying so much that you forget to notice what is along the way. Practice waiting without anxiety and trusting without trying to control everything. When impatience arises, take a deep breath and remind yourself that things unfold in their own time. The universe may not follow your schedule, so stay open to the timing that is actually available. Finding calm while you wait can be a source of strength.","emotionalInsight":"Your anxiety may come from wanting results immediately. Life is not a microwave; it is more like a slow process of ripening. Impatience can reflect a lack of trust in the future or in yourself. Take a deep breath and return to the present. What you need may arrive in its own time, neither too early nor too late. The things that ask you to wait may be helping you prepare. If they arrived now, you might not yet be ready to receive them. Let waiting be an opportunity rather than a punishment.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you are so eager for results that you interfere with the natural process. The deeper block may be pushing too hard instead of allowing things to unfold. When you learn to loosen your grip and trust life''s wisdom, a path may open more naturally. Trying to control the timing and outcome can create more resistance. A breakthrough may call for surrender—not giving up your effort, but releasing your attachment to a specific result. When you stop struggling against life and begin moving with it, new possibilities may emerge. Patience is not passive waiting; it is an active form of trust.","meditationEntry":"Imagine that you are a tree. Feel your roots extending deep into the earth and drawing nourishment. Feel your branches reaching toward the sky and receiving sunlight. You do not need to hurry your growth; it happens in its own way. When spring arrives, flowers bloom without being forced. Now bring this awareness to your life. The things you are eager to see may be like seeds growing beneath the ground. You cannot see them, but growth may already be underway. Trust the process. With each breath, practice yielding to life''s rhythm. As you wait, you are also becoming more deeply yourself."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '8', 'en', 'Courage', '勇氣', '{"subtitle":"Courage"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You are at a moment that may call for courage—not reckless bravery, but meeting fear with awareness. Real courage does not mean feeling no fear; it means continuing even when fear is present. An inner fire may be urging you beyond your comfort zone and into the unknown. This energy is raw, untamed, and difficult to suppress. It does not begin with a guaranteed outcome; it responds to a call for growth. You may be stronger than you think, and this can be a time to discover that for yourself. Step into the unknown with care and trust in your capacity to meet what comes.","dailyGuidance":"Today may call for a brave step. The thing you have been afraid of or the decision you have been postponing may need your attention. Do not wait for a perfect moment; it may never arrive. Courage is not waiting until fear disappears, but moving forward while acknowledging it. Do one thing that feels challenging: have a conversation, make a decision, or try something new. As you move through fear, you may discover greater freedom on the other side. Remember that you have already faced difficult things, and you have resources to meet this too.","emotionalInsight":"Your fears are real feelings, but they are not always facts. Fear is the mind''s response to the unknown, and the unknown is not automatically dangerous. You may be avoiding certain emotions, conversations, or truths, but avoidance can make fear grow. Face what you can, and you may find it less frightening than expected. Emotional turbulence may come from being caught between a familiar path that feels constricting and a new path that feels uncertain but freeing. Your heart may have a sense of direction while your mind resists. Listen inwardly and let courage grow alongside the fear.","blockageAnalysis":"Fear may be freezing you while you wait for guarantees that life cannot provide. A breakthrough may begin by acknowledging fear and taking a thoughtful step anyway. You may believe you have to overcome fear before acting, but sometimes confidence grows through action. The block may be less about ability than trust in yourself. You may already have resources you have not recognized. As you move through uncertainty without a perfect map, you may discover the next part of the path as you go. Courage is not the absence of fear; it is fear being present without having the final say.","meditationEntry":"Stand up and feel both feet firmly on the ground. Notice the earth supporting you. Imagine a door in front of you, with the unknown on the other side. Your fear may say, “Do not open it,” while another part of you may be ready to cross the threshold. Take a deep breath and feel your own strength. You are larger than this moment of fear. Reach out and open the door in your imagination. As you step across, notice any sense of freedom or possibility. Each time you face a fear, you can learn more about your strength. Carry that awareness into daily life, one step at a time."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '9', 'en', 'Completion', '完成', '{"subtitle":"Completion"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"A cycle is coming to a close, and this may be a time to gather what you have learned. You have traveled a long way; now there may be room to celebrate, integrate, and let go. Completion is not only an ending; it also creates space for a new beginning. This energy invites you to look back with gratitude and then release what is finished. Do not cling to what has already served its purpose and given you what you needed to learn. Empty your hands and make room to receive what comes next. Completion is an art: it asks you to let go with grace and trust that another chapter can unfold in its own time.","dailyGuidance":"Today is about endings and new beginnings. Look at your life and ask what has reached completion and what may need to be released. It could be a relationship, a job, a belief, or a habit. Consider giving it a clear ending instead of leaving it unresolved and draining your energy. You might write a letter, create a small ritual, or simply say goodbye inwardly. Be grateful for what it gave you, then let it go. This is also a day to celebrate how far you have come. You have done meaningful work. Clear some space for what may come next.","emotionalInsight":"You may feel some sadness, and that is natural. Endings often include a sense of loss, even when the ending is chosen. Allow the sadness; it is part of transition. At the same time, notice any relief or lightness as you put down a burden. Your emotions may include gratitude, grief, anticipation, and uncertainty; all of these can be natural responses to completion. Do not suppress them—let them move. An ending can feel like a small death, while also making room for renewal. Trust yourself to move through the transition at your own pace.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you cannot release something that has already ended. You may be attached to the past even though it no longer serves you. The deeper block may be fear of emptiness or of not knowing who you are without it. Yet letting go can make room for something new. You may be lingering in a relationship, job, or pattern because it is familiar, not because it is right for you. A breakthrough may begin with acknowledging that it has ended. Grieve it, appreciate what it gave you, and then release it. When you do, you may notice new doors opening.","meditationEntry":"Sit down and close your eyes. Look back on the journey you have taken, as if watching a film. Notice its highs and lows and how you have grown. Now offer a quiet thank-you for the experience. Feel whatever gratitude is present. Imagine placing the whole experience in a beautiful box and gently closing the lid. This is not forgetting; it is completion. Notice your hands empty and your heart spacious. This emptiness is not only loss; it can also be possibility. Take a deep breath, open your eyes, and meet the world in front of you with fresh attention."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '10', 'en', 'Change', '改變', '{"subtitle":"Change"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"Life is moving, and everything is changing. Resisting this movement may not help; you can choose to move with it. This is a dynamic, fluid moment in which nothing is fixed forever. The energy invites you to loosen your attachment to stability and make room for impermanence. Change is not a threat; it is part of life''s nature. You may be shedding an old skin and growing into something new. The process can feel uncomfortable, but it may also be necessary. Instead of trying to hold on to what is leaving, open yourself to what is arriving. You are becoming someone new through this process.","dailyGuidance":"Today''s message is to yield to change. Rather than trying to control or predict everything, stay responsive to what is unfolding. Life may be rearranging things, sometimes clearing away the old before something new can take shape. Trust the process even when you cannot yet see the direction. Practice flexibility today. When plans change, instead of only complaining, ask what the change might be showing you. A different possibility may be opening. Loosen your grip on control and allow life to surprise you. Change can be a companion rather than an enemy.","emotionalInsight":"You may feel uneasy because change can take away your sense of control. You want to know what will happen next, but life does not provide the whole script in advance. Uncertainty can stir fear. Look a little deeper: perhaps what you fear is not change itself, but losing an identity you have built around a role, a job, or a relationship. You are more than any one of those things. Change may be removing a mask and helping you see yourself more clearly. This can be frightening, but it may also bring freedom. Allow yourself to discover who you are becoming.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you are resisting change that cannot be avoided. You want everything to stay as it was, but life keeps moving. The block may be that you are fighting the river instead of learning how to move with it. The more you resist, the more painful the struggle can become. A breakthrough may begin with accepting that change is already happening. You cannot prevent it, but you can choose how to respond. When you stop resisting and begin to cooperate with what is real, change may bring release rather than only loss. Let the old end so the new can take shape.","meditationEntry":"Imagine yourself standing beside a river. Its water keeps moving and is never exactly the same; this is one way to see life. Now imagine stepping into the river. At first, you try to hold your position and resist the current. Notice the struggle. Then relax and let the water carry you for a moment. Notice any sense of release. You do not need to know exactly where the river will take you; practice trust. Now notice your body and your life. Cells renew, thoughts move, and emotions change. Change is already part of being alive. As you accept this, fear may begin to loosen. You are part of the river too."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '11', 'en', 'Breakthrough', '突破', '{"subtitle":"Breakthrough"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You may be on the edge of a significant breakthrough. Your preparation and struggles may have been leading to this moment. This is a point where gradual change can become a different way of seeing or being. The energy can feel explosive, liberating, and difficult to reverse. You may not be able to return to the old state because you have begun to see a new possibility. This is not always a gradual shift; it can feel like a leap. Fear and excitement may be present together as you step into unfamiliar territory. A deeper part of you may recognize that this is the moment you have been waiting for.","dailyGuidance":"Today may be a day for action. The thing you have prepared for or the decision you have thought about for a long time may be ready for a next step. Instead of endlessly analyzing, consider what you can do now. A breakthrough can ask for courage and a willingness to change an old pattern, even before you know exactly what comes next. Allow yourself to take a reasonable risk and accept that success and failure are both possible. Sometimes a leap becomes possible when you stop trying to control every detail and take the next step. If you are ready, take it.","emotionalInsight":"You may feel a strong energy building inside you, as if a breakthrough is near. Excitement, fear, anticipation, and unease can all be present at once. That can be normal when moving from one state into another. Do not suppress these feelings; notice how they may be giving you energy to move. You may have been waiting for a perfect moment, but progress often begins when you are willing to move imperfectly. Your emotions may be telling you that something is ready to change; take time to listen and choose a grounded next step.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck at the threshold of a breakthrough, seeing a possibility but fearing the loss of familiar security. The block may be waiting for a guarantee, even though a breakthrough often involves uncertainty. You may need to take a first step before you know exactly how everything will unfold. You might think you are not ready, but readiness does not always arrive as certainty. As you move forward without knowing every detail, you can learn what the next step needs to be. Stop preparing endlessly and begin with one practical action. That can be the path through the threshold.","meditationEntry":"Stand up and notice the energy in you that wants to move beyond an old limit. You may feel it in your chest, abdomen, or limbs. Do not suppress it; allow yourself to notice it fully. Imagine a thin membrane in front of you, representing an old limitation. Look at it and feel what it brings up. Take a deep breath and imagine moving through it with your whole presence. Notice any feeling of release or openness on the other side. Carry that awareness into your life. You do not need to be perfect to begin; willingness is enough for one next step."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '12', 'en', 'Acceptance', '接受', '{"subtitle":"Acceptance"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"This is the energy of deep surrender—not giving up, but accepting reality as it is. You are learning a difficult lesson: not everything needs to be changed; some things first need to be acknowledged. Acceptance can bring peace because struggle eases when you stop resisting what is already true. It is not the same as approving of everything or giving in; it is seeing clearly. You cannot change the past or control other people, and life may not follow your script. But you can choose how to respond. As you accept what is real, you may find more freedom in deciding what to do next.","dailyGuidance":"Today''s practice is acceptance. Notice what in your life you have been resisting: a person, a situation, a fact, or a part of yourself. For today, stop fighting its present reality. This does not mean you have to like it or give up on taking action to change it; first, acknowledge that this is how things are right now. When you accept the facts, new energy may become available—energy that was tied up in resistance. For what you cannot change today, try saying, “I accept this as it is.” Then notice what choices remain open to you.","emotionalInsight":"Much of your pain may come from resisting reality. You want things to be different, the past not to have happened, other people to change, or yourself to be someone else. But reality is what it is. When you stop arguing with what has already happened, pain may shift toward greater calm. Acceptance is not surrendering your ability to act; it is acknowledging the facts. You can accept the present while still working toward a different future. Without accepting where you are now, you may remain caught in resistance and find it harder to move forward. Your emotions may be inviting you to put down the burden of how things should be and meet what is.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you refuse to accept some part of reality. A great deal of energy may be going into resistance rather than creation. The deeper block may be believing that acceptance means defeat, when it can be the beginning of effective action. When you see the current situation clearly, you can decide what can be changed and what cannot. Fighting an unchangeable fact can exhaust you. When you can say, “Yes, this is the situation right now,” a path forward may become easier to see. Acceptance does not have to keep you stuck; it can help you move with what is real. This is a paradox and a deep kind of wisdom.","meditationEntry":"Sit quietly and bring to mind something you have been resisting. Look at it without turning away. Notice the tension that resistance creates in your body. Take a deep breath, and as you exhale, say inwardly, “I accept this as it is.” Notice whether anything softens: your shoulders, your breath, or your heart. Say it again, not because you approve of everything, but because you are willing to see what is true now. Let a little calm move through you. This is the strength of surrender. In acceptance, you may find more freedom to choose your next step."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '13', 'en', 'Transformation', '轉化', '{"subtitle":"Transformation"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You are in the midst of a deep transformation. This is not a surface change but a shift in your very nature: an old version of you is ending while a new one is taking shape. The process may feel like being divided between two states—you are no longer who you were, but not yet fully who you will become. This is a moment of alchemy, in which pain, challenges, and confusion can become material for change. Do not try to hurry the process; it has its own timing. You are becoming something new.","dailyGuidance":"Today, allow transformation to happen. Do not cling to an old identity just because it feels safe. You are shedding an old skin; the process may be uncomfortable, but it can be necessary. Notice what may be ending: old beliefs, habits, or relationship patterns. Rather than trying to revive them, let them leave quietly. Also notice what is beginning to emerge: new perceptions, desires, and possibilities. Give them care even if you do not yet understand them completely. This is a day of transition; remain open.","emotionalInsight":"Feeling lost and confused can be a natural part of transformation. You may not know who you are or what you want, and that uncertainty can be part of the process. Old structures are dissolving before new ones have formed. Being in this open space can feel frightening, but it also holds possibilities. Do not force yourself to find a new identity immediately; give yourself time. Your emotions may fluctuate as you release what is old and make room for what is new. Trust the confusion as part of a process of renewal.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you are holding on to an old identity while wanting a new life. It can be difficult to carry both at once. The block may be the fear that something in you has to end before you can be reborn. You may be afraid to release the person you think you are, though that identity may be only one role you have played. You are larger than that role. When you allow the old to end without clinging to it, transformation can continue. You may discover that what you lose is a limitation, while new possibilities open. First, be willing to step into the unknown.","meditationEntry":"Imagine that you are a caterpillar forming a cocoon. Inside, your old shape dissolves and you no longer know what you are. This can feel frightening, but it is part of the passage. Notice the dissolving and the feeling of solid things becoming fluid. Do not resist; stay present with the transformation. Then imagine a new form beginning to take shape, entirely different from before. Wings emerge, and you become a butterfly. When you leave the cocoon, you are changed. Let yourself imagine flight as a natural expression of what you have become."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '14', 'en', 'Integration', '整合', '{"subtitle":"Integration"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"This is an energy of integration and balance. You have been through many experiences and learned a great deal; now it may be time to bring the pieces together. You do not have to choose one extreme when you can hold two opposites at once. This is a sign of maturity: being able to contain contradictions without feeling split apart. Your yin and yang, light and shadow, reason and emotion can each find a place. Integration does not erase differences; it allows them to coexist in harmony. You are becoming more whole.","dailyGuidance":"Today is a day for integration. Notice parts of your life that seem opposed: work and rest, giving and receiving, strength and softness, independence and connection. Rather than choosing one side, look for a point of balance. You can be both strong and gentle, both independent and close to others. Practice including rather than excluding. When you feel an inner conflict, do not suppress either side; let them have a conversation. You may discover that they are not enemies, but two aspects of a larger whole. Integrating them can help you feel more complete.","emotionalInsight":"You may have felt that you must choose: reason or emotion, strength or vulnerability. But life is not always an either-or question. You can contain many qualities at once. Emotional turbulence may arise when you suppress some parts of yourself and permit only others to be expressed. Now may be a time to let every part come home: your anger and compassion, your fear and courage, your shadow and your light. They are all part of you. As you integrate these parts, inner conflict may soften and a greater sense of peace can emerge.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you are divided against yourself, fighting certain parts while trying to become a “better” version of yourself. You may not realize that the parts you reject can hold strength and wisdom too. The deeper block may be difficulty integrating opposites. When you stop dividing yourself into good and bad or right and wrong and begin accepting more of your whole experience, your energy may return. You may not need to become a different person; you may need to become more fully yourself. Integration can be a path back home.","meditationEntry":"Close your eyes and imagine two parts of yourself that have been pulling in different directions: perhaps your head and heart, your masculine and feminine energies, or your inner child and adult self. See them standing opposite one another. Invite them to move closer. There may be resistance, and that is all right; keep making room for them to meet. Imagine them joining into one whole presence. Feel any sense of completeness or coming home. This is you, with all your parts. Breathe deeply and let that wholeness settle through your body. You do not have to be divided; you can be one."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '15', 'en', 'Slowness', '緩慢', '{"subtitle":"Slowness"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"Life is inviting you to slow down—not because you are lazy, but because depth matters more than speed. In a fast-moving world, choosing slowness can be a way to return to what is essential. When you slow down, you may feel, see, and experience life more fully. This energy reminds you that what matters is not how fast you move, but whether you are truly traveling your own path. Slowness can help you savor life and make each moment more meaningful. You are not running away; you are arriving.","dailyGuidance":"Today, slow down intentionally. Walk a little more slowly, speak a little more slowly, and take your time eating. Notice what changes when you slow down: you may see more detail, feel your body, and hear your inner voice. This does not need to be a day for doing the most things, but it can be a day for doing each thing with greater care. Quality matters more than quantity. When you feel an urge to rush, pause and breathe. Ask yourself what you are hurrying toward and whether it is truly urgent. Give yourself permission to move at a gentler pace.","emotionalInsight":"Anxiety and haste may come from a belief that you must keep running to deserve your place in the world. That is not the measure of your worth. Your value is not only in your productivity; it is also in your existence. When you slow down, you may feel panic because you have learned to equate slowness with laziness. But beneath that fear may be a deep desire for rest, quiet, and permission to simply be without proving anything. Listen to that desire; it may come from a wise part of you.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you are always running but never feel that you have arrived. You may think speed will take you to your destination, while missing what is around you. The deeper block may be avoiding the present by filling every space with activity because inner quiet feels uncomfortable. Yet that quiet may be what you need. When you slow down and become more present in each moment, you may discover that arrival is not somewhere in the future. The destination can be found in the present. Slow down and come home to this moment.","meditationEntry":"Find a comfortable place to sit. Now slow your breathing, very gently. Breathe in for a count of six and out for a count of six, adjusting to what feels comfortable. Notice the details of each breath. Then move your hand slowly, as if it were moving through water. Feel the texture of the air and the movement of your muscles. Let everything slow down. In this slower pace, time may feel more spacious and each moment more expansive. You do not have to be chased by time. Let yourself rest in the present, one breath at a time."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '16', 'en', 'Thunderbolt', '打雷', '{"subtitle":"Thunderbolt"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"This is an energy of shock and awakening. Life may be using a sudden event to wake you and break through a state of sleep. It could be a crisis, a loss, or an unexpected event that arrives before you feel ready. Its force can break through defenses and bring something directly into view. The Thunderbolt is destructive, but it can also illuminate. It burns away old structures and clears a path for new light. This may be a chaotic but necessary moment. Rather than trying to understand everything immediately, allow yourself to notice how the experience is changing you.","dailyGuidance":"If something shocking or unsettling happens today, try not to react or defend yourself immediately. Pause, breathe, and ask what the disruption may be showing you and what old pattern it may be breaking open. When a thunderbolt strikes, the first impulse can be to regain control, repair everything, and return to the way things were. Notice that impulse before acting on it. Allow the shock to reveal what may already have ended but still occupies space in your life. Trust that clearing space can make room for new life.","emotionalInsight":"You may feel shocked, helpless, or even angry. You may wonder why this is happening and why now. The Thunderbolt is not a punishment; in this reading, it represents a forceful awakening. You may have been living within a comfortable structure that no longer feels true, and now it is breaking apart. This can hurt because your sense of security has been shaken. Look gently at whether that security was as solid as it seemed. This experience may be bringing you face to face with something you have avoided. Your emotions are understandable; let yourself feel them without becoming trapped in them. This is a transition, and clarity may come after the turmoil settles.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you are trying to recover the old normal after a thunderbolt. But the old normal may no longer exist; something new may need to be built. The deeper block may be resisting a fundamental change and trying to rebuild from the same fragments. The Thunderbolt suggests that the old structure is no longer working. When you are ready to release it, new possibilities can begin to appear. The disruption may have cleared a path for a life that feels more genuinely yours, rather than one shaped by what you thought it should be.","meditationEntry":"Imagine a clear sky, then a sudden flash of lightning. Notice the shock and the unexpectedness. Everything is illuminated, then darkness returns. Yet in that flash you saw something clearly. Now think of a moment in your life that brought sudden clarity. It may have disrupted things, but it may also have shown you something important. Notice the energy of that moment without resisting it. Imagine it burning away what feels false or no longer useful. In the ashes, new possibilities may take shape. You have been changed by what you have seen."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '17', 'en', 'Silence', '沉默', '{"subtitle":"Silence"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"This is an energy of deep inner quiet. It is not simply the absence of sound, but a pause in the inner conversation. You are being invited into a space where you do not need to speak, think, or act—only to be. In this silence, you may hear something unfamiliar: the voice of your own soul. Silence is not empty; it can be full of possibility, answers, and wisdom. You can touch it only in stillness. This is a moment of returning to your source.","dailyGuidance":"Create moments of silence today. Turn off outside stimulation—music, news, social media, and conversation—and give yourself at least thirty minutes of quiet if you can. At first, you may feel uncomfortable because the mind is used to noise. It may try to fill the space with thoughts. Do not fight them; simply observe. Gradually, thoughts may settle and a deeper quiet may emerge. Listen without searching for anything in particular. Stay open. An answer may come in a way you did not expect.","emotionalInsight":"You may use noise to avoid being with yourself. Music, conversation, work, and entertainment can fill the space so you do not have to meet what is inside. In silence, you may notice emotions you have suppressed, questions you have avoided, or truths you have denied. That can feel frightening, but silence can also offer room for healing. You may finally hear your own voice—not society''s, your parents'', or your friends'', but yours. Your feelings need space to be heard, and quiet may help you listen to them.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because your mind is too noisy. It keeps planning, analyzing, worrying, and remembering, making it hard to hear your inner guidance. The deeper block may be believing that answers are outside you, in more information, advice, or activity. Yet some answers may already be within, in the center of stillness. When you stop searching outward for a moment and turn toward inner quiet, you may notice what you have been seeking. Silence is not giving up; it is returning inward. From there, things may become clearer.","meditationEntry":"Find a place where you will not be interrupted. Sit down and close your eyes. You do not need to meditate in a special way or accomplish anything; simply sit. Let sounds come and go, whether they are cars outside, the wind, or thoughts within. Do not hold on to them or push them away. Gradually, a gap may appear between one thought ending and the next beginning. Notice that gap. This is silence. It may last only a second, but it can feel expansive. Each time you notice it, allow yourself to rest there. In that quiet, you are already whole."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '18', 'en', 'Past Lives', '過去世', '{"subtitle":"Past Lives"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You are being invited to consider a wider picture. The issue you face now may feel as though it has deeper roots than your current circumstances alone can explain. This card uses the language of past patterns, unresolved karma, and past-life wounds to explore how old themes may influence the present. It is not asking you to become attached to the past, but to consider that healing can reach beyond one chapter of life. This perspective may help you see meaning in your struggle and recognize that you are working to break an old cycle. This is soul work.","dailyGuidance":"When a familiar pattern appears today, ask yourself how long this feeling has been with you. Does it seem connected to childhood, or does it feel older? Some fears, attractions, or aversions can feel stronger than your present experience alone would explain. Rather than addressing only the surface, make room to feel into the deeper layer. Set an intention: I am willing to work with this pattern, wherever it began. The intention itself can be meaningful.","emotionalInsight":"You may sometimes feel an inexplicable sadness, an unclear fear, or a strong sense of familiarity. In the language of this card, these can be understood as memories of the soul. You do not need to remember specific past-life details to work with the feelings; you can simply acknowledge that the pain may feel larger than your personal story. That recognition can be a beginning. Your emotions can be a doorway to deeper understanding; rather than closing it, approach them with care. There may be a sense of release in what you find there.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you are struggling with a pattern whose full history is not visible to you. Trying to solve a deeply rooted pattern with only the tools you have used in this lifetime can feel discouraging. The block may be the assumption that the issue is simple or shallow. Recognizing that it may have deeper roots is not weakness; it can invite wisdom and compassion. When you consider the larger picture, you may see this not as a personal failure but as work you are ready to do. Be patient with yourself; old wounds can take time to understand and tend.","meditationEntry":"Close your eyes and imagine standing in a long hallway. Each door represents a possible past life. You do not need to open any of them; simply notice them. Now feel your life as it is today and imagine a thread connecting the present with the past. Some patterns may feel as though they have followed you for a long time: a fear, a longing, or a gift. Notice what comes up. Then say to the hallway, “Thank you for bringing me here. I am ready to work through this cycle.” Feel the strength in not having to face it alone."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '19', 'en', 'No-Mind', '無心', '{"subtitle":"No-Mind"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"This is a state of going beyond the mind—not having no thoughts, but not being controlled by them. You are being invited into a space where you are not your thoughts, but the awareness that notices them. This can be the beginning of freedom: when you see a thought as a thought, it may lose some of its power over you. No-Mind is spontaneous, fresh, and rooted in the present. It does not depend on the past or the future; it is here now. This is a Zen-like state of simple presence. In this space, there may be no problem that needs an explanation.","dailyGuidance":"Today, practice noticing your thoughts without identifying with them. When a thought appears—for example, “I am anxious”—try reframing it as “There is an anxious thought here.” Can you notice the difference? You are not the anxiety; you are the awareness noticing it. Whenever you get caught in thinking, gently ask yourself: who is observing this thought? The observer is quiet and still, and it has been here all along. The more you rest in the position of observer, the less you may be pulled around by each thought.","emotionalInsight":"Your suffering may come less from an emotion itself and more from the thoughts you attach to it. You feel sadness, and then the mind says, “This should not be happening,” “This will last forever,” or “This proves I have failed.” Those thoughts can add another layer of pain. If you simply feel the sadness without building a story around it, it may be experienced as energy moving through you. Today, practice feeling an emotion without analyzing it. Let sadness be sadness and joy be joy. In a state of greater awareness, emotions can be seen as expressions of life passing through you.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you are overthinking. You try to find a path by analyzing every possibility and predicting every outcome. But life is not only a puzzle to solve; it is also an experience to live. The deeper block may be believing that the mind will provide the final answer, when more thinking can sometimes create more questions. When you loosen your grip on analysis and become present, action may arise more naturally—not as a perfect plan, but as a responsive next step. Trust the wisdom that can come from a quieter awareness.","meditationEntry":"Sit down and begin noticing your thoughts as they arise. Watch them pass like clouds crossing the sky. Do not follow them or judge them; simply observe. One thought comes, another goes. Gradually, notice the space between one thought and the next. Rest your attention there for a moment. You do not need to do anything; simply be aware. In that open space there may be no problem to solve and no answer to chase, only the experience of being present."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '20', 'en', 'Beyond Illusion', '超越幻象', '{"subtitle":"Beyond Illusion"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You are beginning to look through appearances and consider things as they are. You may have been living within a world shaped by beliefs, expectations, and fears, and its walls may now be coming down. This can leave you feeling disoriented as familiar reference points shift. Yet it can also offer a gift: seeing more clearly. You may begin to question whether some things you considered important truly matter, or whether some things you assumed were real were partly shaped by an illusion. This can be the beginning of waking from a dream and seeing life with fresh eyes.","dailyGuidance":"Question your assumptions today. Are the things you take for granted really the only way to see them? Do you truly need a particular thing in order to be happy? Is a person or situation definitely limiting you, or could there be another way to understand it? Look closely at these stories. Are they facts, or do they feel real because you believe them? Asking these questions can loosen the hold of an illusion. You may discover more freedom than you expected. Your happiness may not depend entirely on outside conditions, and your inner strength may still be available to you. You may already be more whole than you remember.","emotionalInsight":"You may feel a strange mixture of loss and liberation. There can be grief as an old worldview falls away and the beliefs you held on to no longer seem to fit. There can also be relief as you recognize that some of those beliefs felt more like a cage than a truth. Your emotions can help you move through this transition. Allow sadness for what you are leaving and joy for what you are beginning to see. This can be a delicate moment between two ways of seeing. Do not rush to build a new belief system; take time to appreciate the open space. Truth does not need to be believed into existence; it needs to be seen clearly.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you are attached to an illusion, such as a perfect relationship, a perfect life, or a perfect version of yourself. That perfection may be an image created by the mind rather than something real. The deeper block may be chasing a mirage that keeps moving farther away. When you stop and see it for what it is, you may notice the beauty already present in imperfect reality. Real relationships, real life, and your real self can be richer and more alive than an idealized image. Stop chasing an illusion long enough to notice what is here. That is one way toward freedom.","meditationEntry":"Imagine watching a movie and becoming completely absorbed in it. You cry, laugh, and feel afraid alongside the characters. Then suddenly the lights come on. You see the screen and the seats and remember: it was a movie. Notice the relief and the moment of recognition—“Oh, I see.” Now look at your life. What if some things you assume are completely real are only part of the picture? This does not mean they are unimportant; it means they are not all there is. You are also the one observing the story, not only a character in it. Remembering that perspective can change how you meet what happens."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '21', 'en', 'Creativity', '創造力', '{"subtitle":"Creativity"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"This is a moment when creative energy may be moving through you. It is not only about skill or talent; it is about allowing life to express itself through you. You can be a channel through which energy takes a new form. That form might be art, a project, or a new way of living. The point is not only the result, but the act of creating itself. When you are creating, you may feel more connected with life and less like a bystander. This can be a deep source of joy: you are participating in the unfolding of life.","dailyGuidance":"Give yourself time to create something today, whatever it may be. Draw, write, dance, cook, rearrange a room, or do anything that lets you express an inner impulse. The point is not to do it well, but to do it. Do not judge the process or compare the result. Let yourself be a channel for something to move through. If you feel stuck, do not force it; step away and do something completely different for a while. Let your unconscious mind work. Creativity often needs room to relax, not more tension.","emotionalInsight":"There may be a creator within you who has been held back and longs to express something. Perhaps you were told you had no talent, or that creating was a waste of time and you should do something useful instead. Those messages can suppress your vitality. Creativity is not merely a luxury; it can be a meaningful way for your soul to speak. When you suppress it, you may feel dull, bored, or disconnected from meaning. When you express it—even through something small—you may feel more alive. Give that inner creator a voice. It does not need to be perfect; it needs to be genuine.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you are waiting for the right moment or a great idea. Creativity is not always something you wait for; it can emerge through making and exploring. The deeper block may be attachment to the result and fear that it will not be good, useful, or special enough. Many meaningful creations begin with play and experimentation. When you allow yourself to make something imperfect or messy, creative energy can begin to move. It is not only about the product, but also about the process. Start creating, and some answers may appear along the way.","meditationEntry":"Imagine that you are an open riverbed. Now feel water beginning to flow from its source. It does not ask where it is going or why; it simply moves. Notice that flow within you. It might appear as color, sound, movement, or words. Do not try to control it or give it a particular shape; let it flow. Your part is to stay open and allow expression. In this process, you are not forcing creation; you are allowing it to happen. This is one way to experience creativity: surrendering to a larger source of inspiration and letting it find expression through you."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '25', 'en', 'Projection', '投射', '{"subtitle":"Projection"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"What you are seeing may not be the whole truth; your own projections may be shaping how you interpret it. You may be placing inner fears, desires, or unresolved concerns onto people and situations around you. You may think the problem is out there, while some of what is troubling you may also be within. Projection is a natural human process, not a personal failing, but it can keep you caught in an illusion—fighting a shadow in a mirror instead of looking at the source. This card invites you to turn the projector inward. What disturbs you most may have something to teach you about yourself.","dailyGuidance":"When you have a strong reaction to someone or something today, pause and ask what it has stirred in you. If someone''s behavior makes you angry, ask whether there is a similar behavior in yourself that you have not acknowledged. If you feel drawn to someone, ask what quality you see in them that you would like to develop in yourself. The outside world can act like a mirror, reflecting your inner life. Use that reflection to understand yourself rather than judge someone else. This shift can turn blame into insight and helplessness into learning.","emotionalInsight":"Some emotional pain may be intensified by projection. You may feel hurt because you believe someone is targeting you, when they may simply be living their own life and dealing with their own struggles. Your own wounds can shape how you interpret their actions. This does not mean your pain is unreal; it means its source may be different from where you first thought. When you look at your projections and reduce blame, you may discover a source of agency: you can tend to your own wounds without requiring another person to change. That can be a step toward freedom.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck while waiting for the outside world to change so you can feel better. But what if some of what you see outside is being shaped by your own projection? The deeper block may be giving people and situations power over your feelings that they do not entirely hold. The intensity of your reaction may show that the situation connects with past experiences or an unhealed part of you. When you are willing to look at that inner wound and care for it directly, the outside may look different because you are no longer seeing it through the same filter. Sometimes the problem changes when your perspective changes.","meditationEntry":"Imagine that you are in a dark room holding a flashlight. You point it at other people: they did something wrong, they hurt you, they should be different. Each time, you see a monster. Now slowly turn the flashlight toward yourself. Illuminate your fears, wounds, and shadow. At first it may feel frightening. But as you keep looking, you may find that these are not monsters, but parts of you waiting to be seen and cared for. As you bring light to your own inner world, the monsters outside may disappear. The room has not changed; you are seeing more clearly."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '26', 'en', 'Intensity', '強烈', '{"subtitle":"Intensity"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"Life may feel very intense right now: emotions and experiences can seem amplified. This may not be a calm or balanced period; it can feel like everything is burning brightly. You may feel overwhelmed, yet intensity can also bring energy and wake you from numbness. It may burn through what no longer serves you. This energy deserves to be acknowledged rather than automatically suppressed. Allow it to move in a safe way, and it may find its own balance. For now, notice the fire without denying it or letting it consume you.","dailyGuidance":"Do not force yourself to feel calm or “normal” today. If you feel intense, acknowledge that energy. Find a safe way to express it: exercise, create something, laugh, or cry. Let the energy move rather than trapping it. At the same time, care for your body; intensity can be tiring, so eat, rest, and ground yourself. Avoid major decisions if you feel overwhelmed, because your perspective may be affected. But do not suppress yourself either. This can be a time to feel deeply while taking care of your limits.","emotionalInsight":"Your emotions may feel like waves arriving one after another. That can be frightening, but it may also be part of processing feelings that have been held back. Do not try to control or explain every feeling; let it move through you while staying grounded and safe. In an intense moment, you may discover that feelings can be strong without destroying you. You may be more resilient than you thought. This process can clear emotional space for a new beginning. Trust the process while seeking support if it feels too difficult to manage alone.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you are trying to control intense energy and make it manageable. Some energy may be too large to suppress; it needs direction and a safe outlet. The deeper block may be fear that if you let go, you will lose control or hurt yourself or someone else. Yet suppressing everything can make pressure build. When you find healthy channels—movement, art, or time in nature—the energy may become motivation rather than danger. Do not trap the fire; give it a safe direction. If you feel unable to stay safe, reach out to a trusted person or qualified support.","meditationEntry":"Imagine a volcano within you. It is alive, with molten energy moving inside. You could try to cover it and pretend it is not there, but that may increase pressure. Or you can acknowledge it and imagine a safe, contained channel for release. Look at the volcano and feel its power. It is not your enemy; it is energy. Imagine giving it a path, like a stream of lava flowing safely toward the sea. The volcano is still there and its power remains, but now the energy has somewhere to go. This is one way to work with intensity."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '27', 'en', 'Falling in Love', '陷入愛中', '{"subtitle":"Falling in Love"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You may be experiencing the magic of love, the moment when the world seems brighter. This could be love for a person, for life, or for yourself. Whatever its focus, you may be feeling the beauty of opening up, along with the vulnerability and courage it involves. Falling in love can mean surrendering some defenses and allowing something larger than your usual routines to enter. It can be a blessing, while still being important to stay connected to yourself. Genuine love does not require you to lose yourself; it can help you find yourself more deeply.","dailyGuidance":"Enjoy the feeling of opening up and saying yes to life. Let yourself feel joy, excitement, and hope, while remembering to breathe and stay grounded. In the intoxication of love, it can be easy to lose perspective, idealize someone, or overlook warning signs. Feel the love, but keep a little awareness too. Ask yourself: am I seeing this person or situation as it is, or am I in love with my own fantasy? Real love can look at what is true and still care.","emotionalInsight":"Your heart may be wide open, like a flower turning toward the sun. This can be beautiful and also leave you feeling vulnerable. Your emotions may rise and fall dramatically; that can happen during the intensity of falling in love. Enjoy the passion while remembering that this stage can change over time. Love that remains after the first intensity may grow through respect, trust, and commitment. Let yourself enjoy what you feel now while also making room for a deeper, steadier connection to develop.","blockageAnalysis":"If you long for love but feel stuck, ask whether you allow yourself to receive it. Many people say they want love, but retreat when it appears because they doubt their worth or fear being hurt. The deeper block may be that your heart wants to open while old wounds have built a wall. Begin to lower that wall carefully, one small step at a time. Allow small risks and moments of vulnerability. Love may not wait until you feel completely ready, but you can choose to try when it feels right for you.","meditationEntry":"Remember a moment when you were completely open—perhaps in nature, holding a child, or listening to music. In that moment your heart had no defenses; you were simply there, fully alive. Feel that memory and let it come alive in you again. That openness, that yes, is part of the nature of love. It is not only about another person, but also about your own state of being. You can choose to return to that openness, whatever the outside circumstances. This is one way to fall in love with life itself."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '28', 'en', 'Laziness', '懶惰', '{"subtitle":"Laziness"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You may feel a deep reluctance to move—not necessarily because you are tired, but as if you do not want to strive, change, or grow. You may simply want to stay where you are and do nothing. This could be resistance, or it could be wisdom. This card asks: is this stillness serving you, or harming you? If you need rest and integration, honor that need. If laziness is disguising fear or helping you avoid something you know matters, meet it gently and honestly.","dailyGuidance":"Look honestly at what you are calling laziness today. List the things you have been putting off and ask of each one: why do I not want to do this? The answer may tell you something. Perhaps the task is not important to you and comes from someone else''s expectations; if so, consider releasing it. Or perhaps it matters to you, but you fear failure or success. Acknowledge the fear and consider beginning anyway. Sometimes the remedy is action: start, and motivation may follow. Sometimes it is permission: allow yourself to rest without guilt. Today, notice which one you need.","emotionalInsight":"What you call laziness may be emotional exhaustion. You may have spent a long time striving, pushing, and proving yourself, and now something in you is asking for a pause. That is not necessarily weakness; it may be a wise signal. If this state lasts a long time, it can also be connected with depression or hopelessness, and support may be helpful. You may have lost a sense of meaning or wonder why effort matters. If so, reconnect with what you genuinely care about, not only what others say you should do. When you find a reason that is truly yours, energy may begin to return.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you are waiting for motivation before taking action. But motivation often follows action rather than preceding it. The deeper block may be wanting a guarantee that effort will pay off, so you wait for the perfect moment or plan. That moment may never arrive. To move through inertia, try the smallest first step, whatever you feel. Often, once you begin, the task may feel less difficult and you may even find some enjoyment in it. Action can create clarity, and clarity can create momentum. Do not wait indefinitely; begin small.","meditationEntry":"Imagine that you are lying in a very comfortable bed. It is so comfortable that you do not want to get up. Outside the window, a beautiful day is waiting: sunlight, fresh air, and adventure. You sense that you may enjoy it if you rise, but the bed is comfortable and getting up takes effort. Now imagine your future self, already up and outside, returning to tell you it was worth it. That small effort, that moment of moving through resistance, opened a whole day of possibility. Listen to that voice and let it help you take one step."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '29', 'en', 'Trust', '信任', '{"subtitle":"Trust"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"This is a time to practice trust, especially when things are uncertain. You may be facing the unknown without a map or a clear idea of what will happen. This card invites you to loosen your grip and take a step while trusting that support may be available, even when you cannot yet see how. This is not blind certainty; it is a willingness to meet what is unfolding. Trust is not something you can force, but you can practice it. Each time you release some control and say, “I do not know, but I am willing to trust,” you strengthen that capacity.","dailyGuidance":"Practice a small act of trust today. Perhaps it means not overplanning and allowing the day to unfold naturally. Perhaps it means giving someone room to keep a promise without checking or reminding them. Or perhaps it means listening to your body and its signals. Each time you notice yourself trying to control or worrying, pause, breathe, and say, “I trust.” Observe what happens. Sometimes things work themselves out in a way that is different from what you could have forced. Trust is not passivity; it is doing your part and then releasing your grip on the result.","emotionalInsight":"Your trust may have been hurt in the past, by a person or by life not unfolding as you expected. That hurt may have made you vigilant and ready to be disappointed. This protective stance can also cut you off from the flow of life, leaving you tired and alone. Rebuilding trust does not mean forgetting the past or becoming naive. It means recognizing that one betrayal is an experience, not the whole of experience. You can learn to discern who and what is worthy of trust while allowing room for new evidence. Begin with small steps and show yourself that trust can still be possible.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you want guarantees and control before you are willing to trust. But certainty is not the same as trust. The deeper block may be believing that everything will fall apart if you do not manage every detail. Constant control can exhaust you and sometimes push away opportunities or help. When you loosen your grip, you may discover that things can unfold in ways you could not have planned. This does not mean abandoning responsibility; it means allowing room for life and other people to participate too.","meditationEntry":"Remember learning to swim, or imagine what it might be like. At first, you may have held tightly to the edge, afraid of the water. Then perhaps there was a moment when you let yourself float. You did not know exactly how the water would support you, but you tried. Notice the feeling of discovering that it could hold you. Your body relaxed and began to float. That moment can be an image of trust. Imagine life as water that can support you when you soften and stop struggling. Remember this feeling and return to it when you need to."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '30', 'en', 'Understanding', '理解', '{"subtitle":"Understanding"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"Light is reaching places that were once dark. You may be beginning to understand something that has confused you for a long time: why a relationship unfolded as it did, why a pattern repeats, or why a particular hurt goes so deep. This understanding is not only intellectual; your heart and body may recognize it too. Such insight can bring release because when you truly understand something, some attachments may naturally fall away. You may no longer need to force forgiveness or let go; the issue may simply matter differently. This can be a moment of deep healing.","dailyGuidance":"Give yourself time to integrate a new understanding today. You may want to write it down, speak it aloud, or sit quietly with it. This insight may change how you see many things, so allow your perspective to reorganize. Do not rush into action or a decision; let the new view settle first. Look gently at your past through this understanding. Some things you thought were mistakes or failures may also have been steps that brought you to where you are now. Treat this new perspective as a gift and give it time.","emotionalInsight":"Your emotions may be gaining context. Before, you may have felt pain, anger, or sadness without knowing why it was so intense. Now you may see a connection: a current situation stirred an older wound, someone reminded you of an earlier relationship, or a fear connects with a childhood experience. This insight may not immediately remove the pain, but it can change your relationship to it. You may feel less confused or controlled by it as you see its logic and origins. That recognition can itself be healing. Gradually, understanding may help transform how you carry the pain.","blockageAnalysis":"You may be overanalyzing, trying to understand every detail, while deeper understanding may not come from analysis alone. The block may be trying to use the mind to solve an issue that also needs the heart. Some things cannot be thought through; they need to be felt through. If you are caught in analysis, try setting aside the question of why and notice what is here. Allow your body and heart to have their own wisdom. Sometimes insight appears when you stop trying so hard to understand, like an “aha” moment that arrives in quiet and openness.","meditationEntry":"Imagine looking at a painting from very close up. You can see colors and brushstrokes but cannot tell what the picture is, which may feel confusing. Now slowly step back. With more distance, an image begins to emerge. Step back a little farther and suddenly you see a face, a landscape, or a story. That moment of recognition is understanding. Your life can be like that too: when you are very close to an experience, you may see only confusion. With a little distance and a wider view, meaning may become visible. Your experiences may be part of a larger tapestry."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '31', 'en', 'Control', '控制', '{"subtitle":"Control"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You may be holding on very tightly, trying to control every detail: how people see you, how events unfold, and what the future will bring. This urge can come from fear that if you let go, everything will fall apart. Yet holding so tightly may leave you more anxious, tired, and alone. Life cannot be controlled in every detail; it has to be lived. This card invites you to notice that control can offer an illusion of certainty. You may never have had complete control, and pretending otherwise can be exhausting. It may be time to loosen your grip.","dailyGuidance":"Notice moments when you want to control something today: directing a conversation, making every plan go your way, or preventing surprises. When you notice the urge, ask what you fear would happen if you loosened your control. Often, the worst case may not be as bad as you imagine. Practice letting go in small ways: allow someone else to decide, accept a change of plan, or let something unfold naturally. Notice what happens in your body when you release control. There may be anxiety, but there may also be relief.","emotionalInsight":"A deep sense of insecurity may be hidden beneath your need for control. Perhaps life felt chaotic or unpredictable when you were young, and taking charge became a way to feel safe. That strategy may no longer be serving you and may have become a prison. A sense of safety does not have to come only from controlling the outside world; it can also come from trusting your ability to respond. You have already made it through things you once thought you could not. You may be stronger than your need to control suggests. Begin building trust in that inner strength and gradually loosen your grip on what is outside your control.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you equate control with safety and letting go with danger. The deeper block may be overlooking the cost of control. It can create an illusion of safety while limiting spontaneity, surprise, flow, and connection. Other people may pull away when they feel controlled, and opportunities may pass when rigidity leaves no room for them. As you loosen your grip and trust life more, you may find a different kind of security in being flexible and able to adapt. Control can be brittle; trust can be resilient.","meditationEntry":"Imagine holding a handful of sand. The tighter you squeeze, the more sand slips between your fingers. Your hand becomes tired and sore, but you are afraid to relax because you might lose all the sand. Now imagine slowly opening your palm. Some grains remain there, and your hand is relaxed and free. It can receive something new. This can be an image of releasing control. You do not necessarily lose everything when you loosen your grip; you may gain room to breathe and choose."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '32', 'en', 'Politics', '政治', '{"subtitle":"Politics"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You may be caught in power games, manipulation, or strategy—perhaps at work, in family dynamics, or in a social circle. You may notice yourself calculating, defending, or trying to gain the upper hand. This can drain your energy and pull you away from what feels genuine. This card is not here to condemn you, but to show what can happen when you live through political maneuvering: sincerity can get lost. You may begin to act like a player in a game rather than a real person. Ask yourself why you are playing and whether the cost is worth it.","dailyGuidance":"Notice moments when you make a strategic choice that does not feel genuine: saying something you do not believe to please someone, hiding your real thoughts to avoid conflict, or manipulating a situation to get what you want. When you notice this, ask what might happen if you responded honestly. There may be consequences, but there may also be freedom. Choose at least one moment today to respond sincerely rather than strategically. Notice the difference. You may lose an advantage in a game, but gain a stronger sense of yourself.","emotionalInsight":"Living through politics and maneuvering can leave you emotionally tired and cynical. You may begin to distrust everyone because you assume they are all manipulating something. That can protect you, but it can also isolate you. Genuine connection is difficult when no one sees the real you and you do not see the real person in front of you. If you want more authentic relationships, consider stepping out of the game where it is possible and safe to do so. This can take courage because it involves vulnerability, but vulnerability can also make real closeness possible.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you believe you will lose if you do not play politics. But what would you be losing? If “winning” means betraying yourself, living in fear, and constantly wearing a mask, that victory may come at a high cost. The deeper block may be overlooking another option: neither manipulating others nor accepting victimhood, but stepping away from the game where possible. Seek or create an environment where sincerity is welcome. When you stop engaging in political maneuvering, you may find more room for relationships and situations built on mutual honesty.","meditationEntry":"Imagine being at a ball where everyone wears a mask and follows carefully rehearsed steps. You are wearing a mask too, following the rules. It feels tiring and false, but you are afraid to take off the mask because you might be rejected. Now imagine pausing and slowly removing it. Some people may be surprised or uncomfortable. Then one person removes their mask too, followed by another. Gradually, the gathering changes. The dance becomes less rehearsed and more genuine. Imagine that change beginning with one person''s courage: yours."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '33', 'en', 'Celebration', '慶祝', '{"subtitle":"Celebration"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"This may be a moment to celebrate—not because you are waiting for a special reason, but because existence itself can be celebrated. You are alive, breathing, and here in this moment; that can be enough. This card invites you out of a serious, heavy mode in which you are always striving, and toward joy and play. Life is not only a list of tasks to complete; it can also be a party to enjoy. You can choose to smile, dance, and laugh along the way. Celebration is not selfish or irresponsible; it is a way of honoring the gift of being alive.","dailyGuidance":"Find a reason to celebrate today, even if it is small: the sun came out, your coffee tasted good, you read a lovely book, or you laughed with a friend. Notice small joys and let yourself appreciate them. Play music you like and dance, give yourself a small treat, or spend time doing something that makes you happy. Today, give joy some priority alongside productivity. Notice how your energy shifts when you give yourself permission to enjoy life. Celebration is not wasted time; it can replenish you.","emotionalInsight":"You may live under a strict inner voice that says you can be happy only after you have finished everything and proved yourself. But “afterward” may never arrive because there is always more to do. This card says you can be happy now without needing a special reason. Your inner child may be longing for play, spontaneity, and joy without a goal. Give yourself permission. It may help soften old messages that you must always be serious, work hard, or postpone satisfaction. Celebration can be a quiet rebellion against those internalized demands.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you feel guilty or unworthy when you are happy. Perhaps you think there is too much suffering in the world for you to celebrate, or that you have not earned the right to feel joy. The deeper block may be believing that happiness is a reward you must earn rather than a natural part of being alive. Your joy does not take joy away from others; it can be shared and contagious. When you celebrate, you may give others permission to do so too. Your happiness need not be selfish; it can be a contribution to the world.","meditationEntry":"Remember a moment from childhood when you were completely absorbed in play—perhaps at the beach, in the snow, or at a playground. You were not thinking about tomorrow or yesterday; you were fully in the present and happy without needing a reason. Feel that memory in your body. The capacity to play and celebrate life has not left you; it may simply be buried beneath duties and expectations. It is still there, waiting to be awakened. Play is not only for children; it is for everyone who is alive."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '37', 'en', 'Ordinariness', '平凡時刻', '{"subtitle":"Ordinariness"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"This is an ordinary moment, without drama, a peak, or a crisis—just the simple flow of daily life. You may feel bored or disappointed, waiting for more excitement or meaning. This card invites you to look again at the ordinary: it is not necessarily missing something; it can be a deep presence in the here and now. In ordinary moments, you can breathe, rest, and notice small things. Morning coffee, sunlight through a window, or a friend''s laughter can be life itself. You do not have to wait for real life to begin; this is it.","dailyGuidance":"Give your ordinary tasks your full attention today. When you wash dishes, notice the water''s temperature, the texture of the soap, and the clean dish. When you walk, feel your feet touching the ground, the air on your skin, and the sounds around you. Do not rush toward the next thing or spend the moment planning and replaying thoughts. Simply be here. You may find that when you are truly present, nothing is entirely ordinary. Each moment has its own texture and richness. The ordinary can become sacred when you meet it with awareness.","emotionalInsight":"You may have been pursuing the extraordinary: extraordinary achievements, relationships, or experiences. That pursuit can keep you elsewhere, never satisfied with what is here. Paradoxically, deep satisfaction may come not from extraordinary events but from appreciating ordinary life. When you can find beauty and meaning in a quiet evening, a simple meal, or an everyday conversation, you may feel freer. You become less dependent on outside stimulation or validation. Happiness can become steadier and more internally grounded.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you dismiss the ordinary while chasing the extraordinary. The deeper block may be idealizing exceptional moments and believing they contain something you cannot find here. But extraordinary moments are rare; if you live only for them, you may miss much of life. Ironically, meaningful insight, deep connection, and creative breakthroughs often grow in ordinary moments when you are relaxed and present. When you learn to appreciate the ordinary, the extraordinary can arrive in its own time as an unexpected gift rather than something you have to chase.","meditationEntry":"Imagine yourself in an art gallery searching for the “greatest” painting. You hurry past each one, judging and comparing, looking for the one that will make you say “wow.” In your search, you have not really looked at any painting. Now stop and truly look at the one in front of you. It may not be famous or precious; it is simply this painting. Notice its colors, brushstrokes, and composition. Give it time. Slowly, you may begin to see its beauty, depth, and story. It does not have to be the greatest to deserve your attention. Life can be like that too."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '38', 'en', 'Stress', '壓力', '{"subtitle":"Stress"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You may be under pressure, feeling overwhelmed, unable to catch your breath, or close to your limit. There may be too much to do, too many responsibilities, and too many expectations. Your body may be tense, your mind racing, and your emotions at the edge. This card is a warning that the current state may not be sustainable. Pause, breathe, and reassess. What is truly necessary? What are you placing on yourself? What can you set down, and where could you ask for help? Stress is not simply something to push through; it can be a signal that something needs to change.","dailyGuidance":"Today, your first priority may not be getting more done, but lowering your stress. That could mean saying no, canceling or postponing something, or asking for help. Look at your to-do list and ask what would really happen if you did not do each item. The consequences may be less severe than you imagine. Prioritize caring for your body: breathing, stretching, walking, or sleeping. Your performance may improve when you are rested, rather than when you push harder. Give yourself permission to slow down, even if only for today.","emotionalInsight":"Your stress may come not only from outside demands, but also from inner drives and beliefs. Perhaps you believe your worth depends on productivity, that you must prove yourself, that rest is laziness, or that failure is unacceptable. These beliefs can act like an inner taskmaster, pushing you forward. Notice and question those voices. Your worth is not only in what you do; it is also in who you are. You have a right to rest, make mistakes, and be imperfect. As you change these inner beliefs, outside pressure may feel more manageable too.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck in a trap of doing more. You feel pressure, so you try to work harder, faster, or more efficiently in the hope of catching up. But there is always more to do. The deeper block may be needing to change the game rather than play it better. That could mean setting boundaries, redefining success, or accepting that you cannot do everything. This takes courage because someone may be disappointed or you may fear looking inadequate. But the cost of living under constant pressure—your health, relationships, and joy—can be high. Consider choosing a different way.","meditationEntry":"Imagine carrying a backpack full of stones. Each stone represents a responsibility, expectation, or commitment. It is heavy and presses on your shoulders, making you bend. You keep walking because you think you must, but each step becomes harder. Now stop and set the backpack down. Look at it. Ask each stone: do I truly need to carry you? Some may not belong to you at all. Some may have served their purpose, and some can wait. Slowly remove what you do not need. Feel your body grow lighter. You do not have to carry everything."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '39', 'en', 'Exhaustion', '精疲力盡', '{"subtitle":"Exhaustion"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You may have reached your limit—not simply feeling tired, but exhausted emotionally, physically, or mentally. You may have given too much, gone too far, or held on for too long. Right now, there may be nothing left to give. This card does not mean failure; it can mark a necessary stop. Your body and being may be saying, “Enough.” That can be wisdom, not weakness. When you reach this point, a wise response may be to stop, rest, and recover. Give yourself the time you genuinely need, not just a day or a week if that is not enough. This is an invitation to deep replenishment.","dailyGuidance":"If possible, do very little today. Cancel plans, turn off notifications, and let people know you are unavailable if you can. If you must do something, do only what is essential, then rest. Sleep, lie down, or sit in the sunlight. Do not try to be productive or even to relax in a particular way; simply stop. Your system may need a pause to recover. Do not feel guilty. This is not selfish; it is necessary care. Give your body what it is asking for: a stop and a chance to replenish. Trust that energy can return when you truly rest, but do not force it.","emotionalInsight":"Exhaustion often comes after you have ignored your needs and limits for a long time. You may have kept saying, “I can do a little more,” “I will rest later,” or “Other people need me.” Now your system may be forcing you to stop. You may feel failure, guilt, fear, or shame. Meet those feelings and yourself with compassion. You are not weak; you are human. Everyone has limits, and honoring them is strength. Ask what this exhaustion may be teaching you about a more sustainable way to live.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you believe you cannot stop or something bad will happen if you do. The deeper block may be overestimating how indispensable you are and underestimating other people''s capacity. The world will not collapse if you rest. People can wait, handle things themselves, or find other resources. When you keep pushing through exhaustion, your decisions, emotional balance, creativity, and effectiveness may suffer. You may think you are helping, but you could be harming yourself. Caring for yourself can help you support others from a more replenished place.","meditationEntry":"Imagine a phone battery in the red zone at one percent. You keep trying to use it, but it shuts down. You feel frustrated and press the buttons, but nothing happens. What it needs is clear: to be plugged in, allowed to charge, and left unused for a while. You would not be angry at the phone or tell it to try harder. You would give it what it needs. Your body and being are similar. When your battery is in the red, the answer may be to recharge—not push harder, use more willpower, or rely on more caffeine. Stop, rest, and recover. Give yourself that basic respect."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '34', 'en', 'Sharing', '分享', '{"subtitle":"Sharing"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You may have abundance to share—not only materially, but also in emotion, wisdom, and experience. This card invites you to share not because you should or because you expect something in return, but because sharing can be a joyful expression of what you have. Giving can enrich you too. This is not necessarily sacrifice or loss, but a cycle: you have received, and now you can pass something on. This movement keeps energy alive and allows abundance to circulate. Holding on too tightly can make energy feel stuck, while sharing can help it flourish.","dailyGuidance":"Look for an opportunity to share today. It could be your time, a smile, your knowledge, or a resource. Notice how sharing feels. Genuine sharing is light and not driven by expectation or resentment. If you feel resentful, it may be an obligation rather than a gift; pause and reconsider. Share only what you truly want to give. Practice receiving too. Sharing moves in both directions, and allowing others to give to you is part of the cycle. Some people are comfortable giving but not receiving, which can interrupt that flow. Today, practice being both a giver and a receiver.","emotionalInsight":"Your relationship with sharing may reflect what you believe about worthiness. If it is difficult to give, you may be acting from scarcity and believing there is not enough. If it is difficult to receive, you may doubt that you deserve to. Genuine sharing can come from a sense of abundance: I have enough to give, and I am worthy of receiving. You can cultivate that inner sense even when material resources are limited. Abundance can begin as an inner state and shape how you relate to what is around you. When you feel more resourced, sharing may become more natural and joyful.","blockageAnalysis":"You may be stuck in a pattern of giving too much or too little. Overgiving can be an attempt to buy love or avoid rejection; withholding can be an attempt to protect yourself from loss or being used. The deeper block may be that you are not in a balanced flow of giving and receiving. Examine your motives. Are you giving because you genuinely want to, or because of fear or expectation? Are you holding back because you truly have nothing to give, or because of fear? Balanced sharing comes from a cup that is full: give from what overflows rather than depleting yourself. Care for your own needs, then share freely when you choose.","meditationEntry":"Imagine standing beside a river. Water keeps flowing from upstream to downstream; it does not hoard itself. Because it moves, the river stays fresh, alive, and abundant. If it built a dam, the water would become stagnant. You are also like a river, with energy and resources moving through your life. When you allow them to flow—receiving as well as giving—you can stay connected and alive. When you hoard or close yourself off, things may feel stuck. Flow is part of life. You are not only a container waiting to be filled; you can also be a channel through which abundance passes."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '35', 'en', 'Compromise', '妥協', '{"subtitle":"Compromise"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You may be facing a choice between holding your position and compromising. This card does not say that compromise is always right or wrong; it invites you to examine why you are considering it. If you are seeking peace and understanding or can recognize value in another perspective, compromise may be wise. But if you are acting from fear of conflict, a desire to please, or a loss of your center, it may feel like betraying yourself. The key question is whether you can keep your integrity while compromising, or whether you are giving up something true to you.","dailyGuidance":"When you face a situation that calls for compromise today, slow down and notice how your body responds. A genuine compromise may feel open, like being willing to see the other side and find a middle way. An unhealthy concession may feel constricted, like “I do not want this, but I have no choice.” If it is the latter, you may need to set a boundary, even if that feels uncomfortable. Remember the difference: compromise seeks a solution that can work for both sides; submission leaves one side feeling they have lost. Do not confuse the two.","emotionalInsight":"You may have a pattern of always compromising, giving way, and putting other people''s needs ahead of your own. This can come from believing that conflict is dangerous and pleasing others is safer, but it may leave you resentful and disconnected from yourself. Or you may have the opposite pattern: never compromising and seeing any concession as weakness. That can come from believing that yielding is failure and control is strength, but it may leave you isolated and rigid. Wisdom can lie between these extremes: knowing when to bend and when to stand firm.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck in all-or-nothing thinking: either I win or you win. The deeper block may be not believing that a solution can benefit both sides. If you see relationships as zero-sum, every compromise can feel like a loss. Yet there may be a third option that neither of you has considered—one that respects both people''s needs. Finding it takes creativity, communication, and a willingness to set aside the need to be right. When you shift from who is right to how both of you can get what you need, a breakthrough may become possible.","meditationEntry":"Imagine two people pulling on opposite ends of a rope. Each is using all their strength and neither wants to yield. They are tired and frustrated, but letting go feels like losing. Now imagine one person suggesting: what if we put down the rope and look for a direction we both want to go? At first the other person may be unsure, but then they try. They discover that when they stop fighting and start cooperating, they can travel much farther. Compromise does not have to weaken your strength; it can bring strengths together."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '36', 'en', 'Conservativeness', '保守', '{"subtitle":"Conservativeness"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You may be holding tightly to what is known, familiar, and safe. Change is knocking, but you may be answering, “No, thank you. I am fine.” This conservativeness can come from fear: fear of losing what you have, fear of the unknown, or fear of making a mistake. Yet holding on so tightly can leave you stagnant. Life moves, and trying to freeze it can feel more like a prison than safety. This card is not telling you to be reckless or irresponsible. It asks you to examine whether your caution is protecting you or limiting you.","dailyGuidance":"Notice moments today when you say no out of habit rather than genuine preference. It may be a new suggestion, a different approach, or a small change. Ask yourself: am I refusing because this truly does not suit me, or because it is unfamiliar? Try saying yes to one small change today. It could be taking a different route home, tasting a new food, or doing a familiar task in a new way. Notice the freshness, even if it feels a little uncomfortable. Discomfort does not always mean danger.","emotionalInsight":"Your conservativeness may have roots in past loss or betrayal. Perhaps you trusted, opened up, or took a risk and were hurt. You learned to withdraw and build a wall, telling yourself it would never happen again. That protection is understandable, but it may also cost you vitality and possibility. Healing is not necessarily about staying guarded forever; it can involve rebuilding your capacity to trust: trusting yourself to respond and recognizing that life can hold both hurt and beauty. When you feel ready, open a small window in the wall and let in some fresh air.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you confuse safety with keeping everything unchanged. The deeper block may be believing that if you preserve the status quo, you can avoid pain. But change can happen whether you resist it or accept it. The difference may be that resistance adds struggle, while acceptance lets you move with what is happening. Trying to keep everything the same takes a great deal of energy, like trying to hold back a river. When you relax that effort and allow a more natural flow, you may have more energy to create, enjoy, and live.","meditationEntry":"Imagine that you are a tree in autumn. Your leaves are changing color and preparing to fall, but you hold on to them, saying, “No, I need these leaves; they are part of me, and I will die without them.” But trees do not work that way. To make room for new growth, the old leaves must be released. When the leaves fall, the tree is not lost; it is preparing for renewal. Winter brings rest, and spring can bring new growth. This is a natural cycle. You have cycles too. What you are holding on to because it must stay the same may be keeping new growth from beginning."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '22', 'en', 'Mind', '頭腦', '{"subtitle":"Mind"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"Your mind is very active right now, perhaps overly so. It may be analyzing, planning, worrying, and solving problems. This is not necessarily bad; the mind can be a useful tool, but it can be a poor master. This card reminds you that you are not your mind, but the awareness that uses and notices it. It may be time to create some distance and observe your thinking without being controlled by it. The mind can serve you, but when it takes over, it can create endless problems. Learn when to use it and when to let it rest.","dailyGuidance":"Notice what your mind is doing today. Is it worrying about the future, replaying the past, or judging yourself or someone else? When you catch it doing this, gently label it: “The mind is worrying,” or “The mind is judging.” This simple label can create some distance. You may begin to see that the mind is following a familiar habit, but you do not have to believe every thought. Give your mind a break too. Do something that does not require much thinking, such as walking, washing dishes, or petting an animal. Let the mind relax for a while.","emotionalInsight":"Some of your emotional distress may come from thinking too much about what you feel. You do not only experience an emotion; you may also think about it, analyze it, and worry about it. That can add a second layer of suffering. An initial feeling may pass, while the mind can keep a story about it going much longer. Today, practice separating the two: this is an emotion, a sensation in the body; that is a thought or story about the emotion. Let the feeling move through you without being swept away by the story. Emotions can pass; stories can keep going. Choose to feel rather than endlessly analyze.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you are trying to use the mind to solve a problem that thinking alone cannot resolve. Some situations call for intuition, some need time, and some may not be problems at all, but constructions of the mind. The deeper block may be believing that if you think long enough, an answer must appear. Sometimes an answer becomes easier to notice when you stop thinking for a while. When the mind gets quiet, a deeper kind of wisdom may have room to speak—not logical analysis, but the intelligence of being present. Give it a chance.","meditationEntry":"Close your eyes and imagine that your mind is a noisy marketplace. Vendors call out: you should do this, you should do that, remember this, worry about that. Now imagine slowly walking out of the marketplace. The noise grows more distant. You arrive somewhere quiet, perhaps a forest, a beach, or a mountaintop. The marketplace is still a faint hum in the distance, but you can hear other things: the wind, your breath, the quiet. This place has always been available to you; it is your center. You can return whenever you need to."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '23', 'en', 'Ice-olation', '冰期', '{"subtitle":"Ice-olation"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You may feel frozen, numb, or disconnected from the world and from yourself. This is an emotional winter, when things can seem to have stopped. Perhaps you built this wall of ice to protect yourself because feeling became too painful, or perhaps you are simply exhausted and need rest. This card acknowledges that you may be in a cold and difficult period. Yet winter has a purpose too: seeds can rest safely underground until spring. This is not necessarily permanent, but a season. Allow yourself to be dormant for a while. Do not force growth; make room for healing.","dailyGuidance":"Do not force yourself to feel or do more than you can today. If you feel numb, notice that. If you need to withdraw, allow yourself some space. This is not giving up; it is respecting your current state. Your mind and body may be telling you that they need rest. Do what is necessary and let other things wait. Today''s goal may not be improvement or progress, but simply getting through gently. Treat yourself as you would a friend who is unwell. An icy season does not last forever, but it needs time to thaw. Do not hurry it; allow your own pace.","emotionalInsight":"Numbness is not necessarily indifference; it can be a form of protection. You may have felt deeply and been hurt, so your system has closed an emotional channel to protect you. That can help you feel safe, though it can also feel costly. Behind the ice wall, you may be safe but lonely. Your emotions may be waiting until it feels safe enough for them to return. Do not force them, but do not assume you must stay behind the wall forever. When you feel ready, begin to thaw gently: with a little warmth, connection, or vulnerability. Take your time; your timing matters.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you are trying to plant seeds in frozen ground. But perhaps this is winter, not spring. The deeper block may be believing that you should feel more, do more, or be more. Nature has seasons, and so do you. Winter is not failure; it can be a necessary period of rest. When you accept that you are in a winter season and stop fighting it, you may find an unexpected calm. You do not have to thaw immediately; you may need rest and time. Spring can come in its own time. Trust the cycle.","meditationEntry":"Imagine that you are a tree in winter. Your leaves have fallen and your branches are bare. From the outside, you may look lifeless. But within, where no one can see, life is still present. The sap moves slowly, and the roots quietly prepare for spring. You are not dead; you are resting. Feel that inner life, even if the outside seems barren. It is still there, waiting for the right conditions to bloom again. Do not rush. Trust the cycle. You may blossom again in your own time."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '24', 'en', 'Participation', '參與', '{"subtitle":"Participation"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"Life is inviting you to participate rather than remain on the sidelines. You may have been watching others dance, take risks, and live while holding back yourself. Perhaps fear, shyness, or a sense of not being good enough has kept you there. This may be a time to step in. Participation is not about doing everything correctly or perfectly; it is about being present and wholeheartedly involved. When you participate, life can feel more real. You are no longer only a spectator; you become part of the story. This takes courage because it means risking being seen, making mistakes, or getting hurt. It can also mean feeling more fully alive.","dailyGuidance":"Practice saying yes to an opportunity today when it feels right for you. When someone invites you, or your heart says “maybe,” notice whether you are retreating into safety. You do not have to wait until you feel perfectly ready. Try participating in something that stretches you a little: speak up, share something, or try something new. Notice your resistance, but do not automatically let it stop you. Each time you participate, you may discover that it is less frightening than you imagined and can even be enjoyable. Life becomes more vivid when you take part.","emotionalInsight":"Feelings of loneliness and disconnection may come from holding yourself back. You may be protecting yourself from hurt, but that can also keep out joy, connection, and belonging. You may watch other people enjoy closeness and vitality without seeing the willingness to participate that helped create those experiences. Yes, participation can make you vulnerable and you may get hurt. But never participating can bring its own deeper pain: a chronic sense of emptiness. Your emotions may be longing for connection, to be seen and understood, and to belong somewhere. Consider giving yourself the gift of stepping in, at a pace that feels manageable.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you are waiting for guarantees: that you will not fail, be rejected, or look foolish. Life cannot offer those guarantees. The deeper block may be wanting an outcome without taking any risk. But participation always involves some uncertainty. When you release complete control of the result and give yourself to the process, you may discover a different kind of freedom. You are not participating only to succeed; you are participating in order to live. Success and failure are both parts of the story. Being present is meaningful in itself.","meditationEntry":"Imagine that life is a huge dance and everyone is moving in their own way. Now notice yourself. Where are you: at the edge, in a corner, or in the middle of the dance? If you are at the edge, feel any impulse to join in. There may be fear, but perhaps there is longing too. Imagine stepping onto the dance floor. No one is judging you; everyone is busy with their own movement. Begin to move, awkwardly or gracefully. What matters is that you are moving and participating. Notice any feeling of release. This is one way of feeling alive."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '40', 'en', 'The Golden Flower', '金色的花', '{"subtitle":"The Golden Flower"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"Something within you may be opening into a deep spiritual flowering. This is not something you can force or hurry; it unfolds naturally when the conditions are right. You may notice a new awareness, a more expansive consciousness, or a sense of connection with something larger. This card suggests that the flowering reveals your true nature. You are not becoming something entirely new so much as uncovering what has been within you all along. Like a bud opening to show petals that were already there, this can be a sacred and beautiful moment. Honor it without trying to possess it.","dailyGuidance":"Give attention to your inner life today. You might meditate, reflect, or simply allow a quiet moment. Do not expect a particular experience; just be present. This flowering happens in its own time and in its own way. Your role is not to push or control it, but to create space for it. This may mean stepping back from the world a little, reducing stimulation, and allowing room for emptiness and silence. In that space, something subtle and deep may arise. Trust the process even if you cannot see an immediate result. Inner work can be meaningful even when its results are not obvious.","emotionalInsight":"This flowering may bring deep joy and peace, but it may also stir fear or resistance. As you touch what feels most authentic, you may also encounter layers that have covered it: conditioning, hurt, beliefs, and identities. Those layers can be stirred before they are released, so the process may feel confusing or emotional. Allow what arises without judging it. Joy and pain, light and shadow, can all be part of this unfolding. You are loosening what is not essential so you can live more fully as yourself.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck trying to hold on to or possess a beautiful spiritual experience. When you have a meaningful moment, you may want to preserve it, repeat it, or define it. But flowering is fluid, alive, and always changing. Trying to freeze it can keep you from experiencing what is here now. You can continue creating conditions that allow it: presence, openness, and surrender. Each moment is new. Yesterday''s flowering will not be exactly like today''s, and that is part of its beauty. Rather than grasping at an experience, rest in awareness and allow experiences to come and go.","meditationEntry":"Imagine yourself in a garden, watching a flower bud. You are excited to see it bloom, so you try to help: pulling at the petals, pouring on too much water, checking constantly for progress. But the interference may delay or harm its opening. The flower knows how to bloom; it needs suitable conditions—soil, water, sunlight, and time. Then, in its own moment, it opens. Your inner flowering can be similar. Create supportive conditions, then step back. Trust the wisdom of nature. The opening happens not because you force it, but because you allow it."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '41', 'en', 'Participation', '參與', '{"subtitle":"Participation"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"Life is inviting you to participate—not only to observe or analyze, but to step in and engage. You may have been standing at the edge, thinking, planning, and waiting for the perfect moment or perfect preparation. This card suggests that the moment available now is the one to meet, and you can begin as you are. Participation is not about doing something perfectly; it is about being fully present and involved. When you participate, you are no longer a separate observer but part of the dance. In that immersion, you may feel more alive.","dailyGuidance":"Choose one thing today that you have been watching from a distance instead of participating in. It might be a conversation where you have stayed on the surface, an activity you have done halfheartedly, or an opportunity you have hesitated to take. Decide to be more fully present. Do not hold back just to keep yourself safe or judge yourself while you are doing it. Give yourself wholeheartedly to the experience. Yes, it may feel vulnerable or risky, but it can also help you feel truly alive. Notice the difference between participating and withdrawing. Life happens through participation, not only through observation.","emotionalInsight":"You may fear participating because you could lose control, get hurt, or look foolish. Staying at the edge can feel safer: you can leave at any time, avoid getting too involved, and limit how much you might be hurt if something goes wrong. But that safety can have a cost: less connection, joy, and meaning. Life often happens in the center, not only at the edges. When you take the risk of participating, you also open yourself to beauty and depth. This is not recklessness; it is choosing experience while staying aware of your own limits.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you are waiting for something to change before you participate. Perhaps you are waiting to feel ready, for fear to disappear, or for a guarantee. Those things may never arrive exactly as you hope. Fear may ease through participation rather than before it. Readiness can grow while you act. Waiting gives doubt more time to grow, while one small step can break the cycle. You can learn to swim by entering the water gradually and safely, to dance by moving, and to love by practicing connection.","meditationEntry":"Imagine a swimming pool. Some people are standing at the edge, testing the water with their toes and thinking, “Maybe it is too cold,” “I am not a good enough swimmer,” or “I will wait until I am fitter.” They never get in, or they enter so cautiously that they cannot enjoy it. Then someone jumps in. At first it is a shock, then laughter, freedom, and play. They were not necessarily more prepared or braver; they simply chose to participate instead of hesitating. Life is like that pool. You can think about it from the edge, or enter at a pace that feels right."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '42', 'en', 'Uniqueness', '獨特性', '{"subtitle":"Uniqueness"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You are unique, like a fingerprint that cannot be copied. Yet you may have been trying to fit in, adapt, or become what others expect. This card calls you back to yourself: your quirks, differences, and the parts of you that do not fit a mold. What you consider a flaw or problem may also be a gift or strength. When you stop trying to be like everyone else and embrace what is distinctive about you, you may feel freer and more able to contribute what only you can offer. No one else can be you.","dailyGuidance":"Celebrate something distinctive about yourself today. It might be how you think, express yourself, what interests you, or a quirk you usually hide. Rather than concealing or normalizing it, let it be seen in a way that feels safe for you. Wear something that feels like you, share a joke that reflects your humor, or explore an interest others may not understand. Some people may not appreciate it, and that is all right. What matters is honoring what feels true. You may be surprised to find that authenticity attracts people who appreciate it. Genuine connection grows through being real, not performing.","emotionalInsight":"You may carry an old pain of feeling different, excluded, or not good enough. Perhaps you were criticized, mocked, or left out because of your differences while growing up. You may have learned to hide, adjust, or pretend. But hiding can create a deep loneliness: even in a crowd, no one sees the real you. Healing can begin by slowly showing parts you have hidden, first with people you trust and then more broadly if you choose. Each time you show more of yourself and are met with acceptance, an old wound may soften. Not everyone will understand, but some people will.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you believe you have to choose between being unique and being loved, or between being yourself and being accepted. The deeper block may be treating those as opposites. Trying to fit in may bring tolerance without the feeling of being truly known. People can accept a mask without seeing who is behind it. When you are more authentic, you may lose some connections while deepening others with people who genuinely see and appreciate you. Those genuine connections may matter more than broad but superficial approval. Allowing the risk of some rejection can make room for being loved as you are.","meditationEntry":"Imagine a garden where every flower is trying to look the same. Roses try to look like lilies; sunflowers try to look like tulips. The garden feels confused and lifeless because each flower is twisting itself into another shape. Now imagine another garden where every flower is fully itself: the rose is proudly red, the lily is graceful and white, and the sunflower is boldly yellow. This garden feels alive and beautiful because each flower honors its own nature. You are like that too. When you stop trying to be another flower, your own beauty can unfold."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '43', 'en', 'Friendship', '友誼', '{"subtitle":"Friendship"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"A genuine friendship may be appearing in your life or asking for your attention. This is not only a surface connection or convenient company, but a deeper meeting. A true friend sees you, accepts you, and can challenge you to grow. They celebrate your successes, support you through setbacks, and remind you who you are when you lose your way. This card says that such friendship is rare and precious. If you have it, honor it. If you are looking for it, become the kind of friend you hope to find. Friendship is not about finding a perfect person, but about being imperfect together with care.","dailyGuidance":"Connect with a friend who matters to you today. Go beyond a surface-level “How are you?” and reach out sincerely. You might call, meet, or send a heartfelt message saying what you appreciate about them and the friendship. Do not wait for a perfect occasion; connection does not need a reason. If you feel that deep friendship is missing, ask yourself whether you offer what you hope to receive: are you vulnerable, genuine, and present? Friendship goes both ways. To have a deep connection, you need to be willing to show up deeply too.","emotionalInsight":"You may carry hurts from friendship: betrayal, disappointment, or a gradual drifting apart. Those experiences may make you cautious, guarded, or inclined to keep relationships on the surface. Or you may have one-sided friendships where you are always giving and supporting but do not feel equally met. Both patterns can be tended with care. Real friendship needs vulnerability and reciprocity. You need to be willing to be seen and to receive support, not only give it. You can also choose people who are willing and able to invest in the friendship. Not everyone can be a close friend, and that is all right. Quality matters more than quantity.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because of unspoken expectations or unmet needs in a friendship. The deeper block may be expecting people to know what you need or how you want to be treated without telling them. Or you may notice an imbalance but never bring it up. Silence can create resentment and distance. Real friendship needs communication: say what you need, how you feel, and what is or is not working for you. This can feel uncomfortable, but it is part of a healthy relationship. Some friendships may deepen through honest conversation; others may end. Either outcome can bring greater truth.","meditationEntry":"Imagine two trees growing close together. At first, each grows independently, with its own roots and branches. Over time, their roots intertwine beneath the ground and their branches touch in the air. They do not become one tree; each keeps its own identity while supporting the other. One shelters the other from the wind, and they share nourishment. If one is struggling, the other''s roots may help. This is a picture of friendship: two independent beings choosing to support, honor, and grow alongside one another without losing their uniqueness."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '44', 'en', 'Turning Point', '轉折點', '{"subtitle":"Turning Point"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You are at a turning point, an important crossroads. Old ways, patterns, or identities may be ending while the new direction is not yet clear. This can be a powerful and vulnerable moment. You can return to what is familiar, even if it no longer serves you, or move toward the unknown. This card suggests that a turning point can be a gift, even when it feels uncomfortable: an opportunity to choose again, redefine yourself, and begin anew. Trust the significance of this moment. Having a choice can be a source of power, even when things feel unstable.","dailyGuidance":"Take time today to look honestly at this turning point. What is ending, and what wants to begin? Do not rush into a decision, but do not postpone it indefinitely either. Make space to feel fear, excitement, grief, and hope; all of these feelings are valid. Then ask yourself deeply: which choice feels aligned with what is true for me? Not simply the easiest, safest, or most pleasing to others, but the most authentic. Notice how your body responds when you imagine each choice. Does it feel expansive or constricted? Let that response inform you, alongside practical judgment.","emotionalInsight":"Turning points often bring emotional swings: one day you may feel excited and clear, and the next doubtful and afraid. This is normal. You are letting go of what is known and facing what is not, one of life''s harder transitions. Allow the emotional process without judging your fear or forcing yourself to think positively. Fear can be understandable when you are taking a risk. At the same time, do not let fear make the entire decision for you. Feel it, honor it, and then ask what you genuinely want beyond the fear. Courage means choosing growth while fear is present.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you want guarantees. You want to know what will happen if you choose one path, whether it will succeed, or whether you will regret it. The deeper block may be expecting certainty at a turning point. Often, you have to choose without knowing the outcome. That is what makes it a real choice rather than a calculation. If you wait for guarantees, the opportunity may pass and circumstances may choose by default. Instead, acknowledge the uncertainty and make the choice that feels most aligned with your values and practical needs. Even if you later adjust, you are actively shaping your life rather than only reacting.","meditationEntry":"Imagine walking along a familiar path through a forest. It is safe and predictable, though perhaps narrow and dim. Then you reach a fork. One path continues as before; another turns in a different direction, through denser trees, but you can see light in the distance. You do not know where the new path leads or what is there. Part of you wants the familiar road, while another part is drawn to the light. This is a turning point. There may be no perfect choice—only a choice you make, and the life you create as you walk it."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('osho', '45', 'en', 'The Journey', '旅程', '{"subtitle":"The Journey"}', '{"meanings":{"currentEnergy":"You are on a journey, not only a physical one but an unfolding within. It may not have a fixed destination or timetable. The journey is also about what you learn along the way, who you become, and what you experience. This card reminds you not to focus so much on arriving that you miss the journey itself. Destinations can change and goals can evolve, but the step you take now, the view you see now, and who you are now are real. Live the journey rather than postponing life until you reach a destination.","dailyGuidance":"Instead of asking “When will I arrive?” ask “What am I experiencing now?” Whatever you are pursuing—a goal, a dream, or a change—give some attention to the journey happening today. What are you learning, experiencing, and noticing? Celebrate small progress and the beauty of this moment rather than waiting only for a big result. Each step has value when you are present to receive it. Allow your route to change too. The best journeys can include surprises, detours, and unexpected discoveries. Rigidity can limit the adventure.","emotionalInsight":"You may feel impatient, frustrated, or tired along the way. You want to be there already; you are tired of moving, striving, and waiting. These feelings are normal, but they may signal that you are treating the journey as an obstacle to overcome instead of an experience to live. Shifting from an arrival mindset to a present mindset can change how the journey feels. When you enjoy the process, the destination can become an added joy rather than the condition for your happiness. You may also discover that what you thought was the destination is only the beginning of another journey.","blockageAnalysis":"You may feel stuck because you are attached to one particular outcome or route. You have a clear picture of how it should look, when it should happen, and how you will get there. But life may have other plans, and rigidity can create suffering. The deeper block may be trying to control what cannot be fully controlled. A journey has its own rhythm and direction. When you loosen your grip and allow it to unfold, it may take you somewhere different from—and perhaps richer than—what you planned. This is not about abandoning your intention, but staying flexible about how and when you get there. Trust the process while remaining engaged in your choices.","meditationEntry":"Imagine climbing a mountain. You have a map and a goal: the summit. As you walk, you discover a beautiful waterfall, a hidden cave, and a breathtaking view. If you focus only on the goal, you may miss them. Or the weather may change and your original route may become unsafe, so you need another way. If you rigidly insist on your plan, you may have difficulty adapting. But if you stay open, a new route may hold its own beauty and lessons. A journey is not a straight line from A to B. It is exploration, discovery, and adaptation. The summit can be wonderful, but there is also magic in the climb."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '1', 'en', 'Spiritual Awakening', '靈性覺醒', '{"keywords":["Awakening","Transformation","Growth","Expanded Awareness"],"nameEn":"Spiritual Awakening"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"A profound shift in awareness is unfolding through you. Your soul may be ready to move beyond old limitations and explore a higher level of consciousness. This need not be random; it may feel like a significant moment in your personal spiritual path. Cosmic energies are described here as recalibrating your light body, helping you become more receptive to wisdom and guidance from higher dimensions.","currentSituation":"You may be experiencing major changes in your life or deep inner upheaval. Truths you once believed may be breaking down, and the belief system that felt stable may be shifting. You may feel confused, lost, or even question everything. These feelings can accompany a period of awakening. Your awareness may be expanding beyond old containers that no longer fit. People around you may not understand your changes, but this is a personal spiritual journey that unfolds in its own way.","deeperMeaning":"This card''s appearance may mark an important threshold in your spiritual journey. You are no longer exactly who you were, and you may not yet feel fully settled into who you are becoming. This sacred in-between space can hold powerful transformation. Your higher self may be guiding you to release what no longer serves you, including identities, relationships, work, or even your previous understanding of yourself. The process of symbolic death and rebirth can be part of your soul''s evolution.","actionGuidance":"Create a daily spiritual practice, whether that means meditation, journaling, or spending time in nature. Give yourself enough solitude to integrate these changes. Do not rush to explain your experience to others; some experiences are felt more easily than they can be put into words. Read spiritual books, attend workshops, or seek a community that resonates with you. Record your dreams and intuitive impressions as ways to reflect on your inner life. Most importantly, practice patience and compassion toward yourself.","energyHealing":"You may choose to work with amethyst and selenite as part of a personal Crown and Third Eye Chakra practice. Try a light-body meditation, imagining white or golden light entering at the crown of your head and bringing clarity and a sense of renewal. Palo santo or frankincense may be used to mark a reflective ritual in your living space. A chakra-balancing practice may focus especially on the upper energy centers. Listen to high-frequency music or explore tuning-fork sound practices if they feel supportive. Stay grounded by walking barefoot outdoors when it is safe, and balance spiritual exploration with ordinary routines.","soulQuestion":"Am I ready to release an old version of myself and welcome a truer expression of my soul? Can I trust this transformation, even when it feels confusing?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '2', 'en', 'Inner Strength', '內在力量', '{"keywords":["Strength","Courage","Resilience","Confidence"],"nameEn":"Inner Strength"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"There may be more strength within you than you recognize. This is not outward force or control, but resilience and wisdom that come from deep within. The universe reminds you that you have already faced many challenges, and each one may have refined your spirit. You carry the courage of the dragon, the phoenix''s power of renewal, and the wisdom of an ancient warrior. Now may be a time to own and embody that strength more fully.","currentSituation":"You may be facing a challenge that seems difficult, and feel that you do not have enough strength to meet it. Your surroundings may leave you feeling powerless or restricted, but this may also be a moment to look inward for a more grounded source of strength. You may have been seeking approval, support, or rescue from the outside while overlooking resources within yourself. This card can be a reminder to remember the strength you already carry.","deeperMeaning":"True strength is not about conquering the outer world, but about meeting yourself with awareness. Remaining centered in a storm, calm amid confusion, and authentic while feeling vulnerable can all be expressions of strength. This card teaches that gentleness and strength are not opposites; compassion can coexist with firmness. Your strength may grow from understanding yourself, trusting life, and feeling connected to a sacred source. You do not have to prove anything. You can simply be.","actionGuidance":"Build a daily ritual that helps you feel strong, such as exercise, martial arts, yoga, or energy work. Practice saying no and setting healthy boundaries; these can be expressions of strength. Reflect on challenges you have already overcome and write down what they taught you. Stand before a mirror, look into your own eyes, and speak an affirmation of strength if that feels supportive. Connect with the fire element by lighting a candle or reflecting near a campfire, while observing appropriate safety.","energyHealing":"Focus on practices that support balance in the Solar Plexus Chakra, often associated with personal power. Tiger''s eye, citrine, or amber may be included in a personal ritual. You might try Warrior poses in yoga and notice strength and steadiness in your body. Cinnamon or ginger essential oils may be used as part of a sensory ritual if suitable for you. A sound practice with the “RAM” mantra may help you focus on the Solar Plexus area. Visualize golden light at your core, gently expanding through your body.","soulQuestion":"In what areas am I giving my power away to people or circumstances outside me? Am I willing to take responsibility for the strength I already have?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '3', 'en', 'Light Bringer', '光之使者', '{"keywords":["Light","Hope","Healing","Purpose"],"nameEn":"Light Bringer"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"Your soul carries a sacred code of light, and your purpose on Earth may be to offer a light in dark places. You are not only searching for light; you can also embody it. Through your eyes, the universe sees the world; through your heart, you can offer love; through your hands, you can bring care. Your presence itself can be a form of service, and your light may influence what is around you. This can be a time to let yourself shine more fully instead of hiding or making yourself smaller.","currentSituation":"You may have been questioning your worth or influence and feeling insignificant. People around you may be going through a dark period, while you feel called to help but are unsure how. Perhaps you have held back your light because you fear that being too visible could make others uncomfortable or envious. This card reminds you that hiding what you can offer does not necessarily help others; the world may need the gifts you are ready to share.","deeperMeaning":"As a Light Bringer, your soul''s commitment is described as bringing higher-dimensional light into the material world. This is not only a role but part of your essence. You may identify with ideas such as being a Starseed, Indigo soul, or Crystal Child, carrying a distinctive frequency to help the Earth''s ascension. Your light does not need to be announced loudly or displayed deliberately; it can flow naturally from your presence. A smile, a warm word, or a compassionate action can express it. Remember that light does not have to fight darkness; it can illuminate it.","actionGuidance":"Begin the morning with a light meditation if it feels right, imagining yourself as a channel for light moving into the world. In daily interactions, consciously offer kindness, hope, or encouragement. Do not be afraid to share your gifts and talents; they are part of what you can contribute. Create art, music, writing, or another form that expresses something within you. Join or create a supportive community. Remember that you do not need to rescue anyone; you can help illuminate the light they already carry.","energyHealing":"Try a light-body visualization, imagining your body filled with radiant white or golden light. Clear quartz, opal, or moonstone may be used as personal ritual objects to focus on your light-body imagery. At sunrise or sunset, you may reflect on natural light without looking directly at the sun. Rose or jasmine essential oil may be part of a Heart Chakra ritual if suitable for you. Listen to high-frequency music if it feels calming. Imagine your light extending compassionately to people and places that may need care, without taking responsibility for fixing them.","soulQuestion":"Am I ready to let my light shine without making myself smaller out of fear? How can I consciously bring light into my everyday life?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '4', 'en', 'Divine Timing', '神聖時機', '{"keywords":["Timing","Patience","Trust","Surrender"],"nameEn":"Divine Timing"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"The universe''s clock and the human clock move on different scales. This card suggests that your prayers have been heard and your wishes may already be taking shape on a higher plane, now moving toward material reality in their own time. The universe is arranging a complex and beautiful symphony, bringing together many elements, people, and circumstances so you may be ready to receive what you have been hoping for. A delay is not necessarily a rejection; it may be a form of protection and preparation.","currentSituation":"You may feel impatient or frustrated because a dream or goal has not yet come to fruition. You have done what you believe you should, but the result has not appeared. You may begin to wonder whether your approach is wrong or whether this is a goal you should release. People around you may have achieved something similar, making you feel behind or anxious. This card reminds you that every soul follows a different timeline, so comparison may not be useful.","deeperMeaning":"The idea of divine timing challenges the desire for control and immediate gratification. It invites you to see life as an organic process rather than a machine that can be forced or manipulated. When something is delayed, there may be inner growth, healing, or preparation still unfolding. The universe may see a wider picture than you can see right now, and circumstances may need time to come together. Surrendering to divine timing is not passive resignation; it is an active practice of trust and wisdom.","actionGuidance":"Loosen your attachment to a specific result or schedule, and bring your attention to the journey you are on now. Practice gratitude for what you already have; this can help you become more receptive. Continue taking actions that feel inspired while releasing your attachment to the outcome. Build trust through a daily practice such as affirmations, prayer, or meditation. Reflect on times when something happened at a fitting moment and let that strengthen your trust. Use this waiting period to know yourself more deeply, develop skills, or tend to old wounds.","energyHealing":"Blue lace agate or celestite may be used as personal ritual objects while practicing patience and calm. Try breathing exercises to settle anxiety or impatience. A moon-themed meditation may help you reflect on natural cycles and timing. Lavender or chamomile essential oils can be part of a relaxing practice if suitable for you. Grounding exercises may help balance an overactive mind. You could create a small altar with objects that symbolize surrender and trust, or write down worries as a letting-go ritual. These are reflective practices, not substitutes for professional care.","soulQuestion":"Can I trust that things may be unfolding for my highest good even when I do not understand the delay? Am I willing to release some control over the timing?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '5', 'en', 'Heart Healing', '心輪療癒', '{"keywords":["Healing","Love","Release","Emotion"],"nameEn":"Heart Healing"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"Your heart may be moving through a deep process of transformation. Old hurt, betrayal, disappointment, or loss may be coming up to be met with care. Your capacity for love may be expanding as you make room for greater openness. This healing is not only about past pain; it can also be about remembering the heart''s capacity for unconditional love. The universe is gently recalibrating your heart toward a sense of openness and innocence.","currentSituation":"You may be in an emotionally vulnerable period, with old hurts rising to the surface. You may feel heartbroken, sad, or afraid of love. These feelings may relate to what is happening now, or they may feel connected to earlier experiences. Your defenses may be trying to protect your heart from being hurt again, while also making it harder to let love in. This card suggests that it may be a safe time to explore heart healing at your own pace and with appropriate support.","deeperMeaning":"Heart healing can be an important part of a spiritual journey. Our hearts carry many memories—from our own lives, family histories, and the wider human experience. When you choose to care for your heart, the effects may reach beyond you into your relationships and community. A closed heart can make it difficult to receive love and abundance. Healing means being willing to feel emotions, including painful ones, rather than suppressing or avoiding them. It does not mean having no scars; it can mean learning to love fully while carrying your history with compassion.","actionGuidance":"Give yourself permission to feel and express emotions without judging them. You might write a letter to someone who hurt you without sending it, simply to express and release your feelings. Inner-child practices may help you comfort a younger, wounded part of yourself. Explore forgiveness as a path toward your own freedom, not as an obligation to anyone else. Create a soothing space with gentle music, candlelight, or comfortable surroundings. Consider seeking qualified support, such as psychotherapy or other healing practices that feel right for you. Treat yourself with extraordinary gentleness and compassion.","energyHealing":"Rose quartz, green aventurine, or pink quartz may be used in a personal Heart Chakra practice, such as resting them near the heart while reflecting. Try a heart meditation that imagines green or pink light moving gently through the center of your chest. Rose or ylang-ylang essential oil may be included in a ritual if suitable for you. Practice breathing gently toward the heart area and imagining each breath bringing kindness. You could also explore sound practices with the “YAM” mantra. A bath with rose petals and sea salt can be a soothing ritual. These practices are for reflection and relaxation, not medical treatment.","soulQuestion":"Am I ready to soften the walls around my heart and feel and offer love again? Can I trust my heart to heal and grow stronger?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '6', 'en', 'Intuitive Wisdom', '直覺智慧', '{"keywords":["Intuition","Wisdom","Guidance","Inner Voice"],"nameEn":"Intuitive Wisdom"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"Your inner knowing may be awakening. The Third Eye is described in this tradition as opening, allowing you to perceive truths beyond the material. Intuition can be a language of the soul and a way of connecting with your higher self, guides, or universal wisdom. You may have been looking outside yourself for answers and validation, while this card reminds you that important wisdom can also be found within. Learning to listen to and discern your inner voice can be part of spiritual growth.","currentSituation":"You may be facing an important decision, with rational thinking and outside advice pointing in different directions. Your intuition may have been offering signals, but fear, doubt, or external pressure could make it difficult to hear. You may also be noticing more synchronicities, vivid dreams, or a strong inner sense without knowing how to interpret them. This card affirms that you can give these experiences thoughtful attention and learn how to discern what they mean for you.","deeperMeaning":"Intuitive wisdom is described as an innate capacity, though a society that emphasizes reason and logic can teach people to suppress or ignore it. Intuition does not have to oppose reason; it can offer another kind of information. Developing it may require quiet, inner space, and practice. It can appear subtly: as a bodily sensation, a sudden knowing, a recurring symbol, or an unexplained sense of attraction or aversion. Learning to distinguish intuition from fear, desire, or conditioned responses takes time and reflection.","actionGuidance":"Create quiet time each day to listen inwardly, through meditation, walking, or sitting in stillness. Keep a record of intuitive impressions, dreams, and synchronicities, and reflect on them over time. Practice following intuition with small decisions to build self-trust. Notice how your body responds when something feels like a yes or a no; intuition may speak through physical sensations. Reduce outside noise and excessive information so there is room to hear yourself. You may explore card reading, a pendulum, or energy awareness as reflective exercises. Do not demand immediate results; the meaning of an intuitive impression may become clearer later.","energyHealing":"You may choose practices focused on the Third Eye Chakra, using amethyst, lapis lazuli, or sugilite as ritual objects. Try a Third Eye meditation that imagines indigo light gently turning at the space between the eyebrows. Frankincense or sage essential oil may be part of a cleansing ritual if suitable for you. Practice visualization and inner imagery as exercises in attention. If you explore pineal-gland or breathing practices, choose gentle, evidence-informed approaches and avoid unsafe techniques. Reduce overstimulation, such as long periods of screen use, when it affects your well-being. Sound practices with “OM” or “SHAM” may help you focus. Treat impressions as reflections to consider rather than unquestionable facts.","soulQuestion":"Am I truly listening to my inner voice, or only looking for the answer I want to hear? Am I willing to trust my intuition even when it differs from outside advice?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '13', 'en', 'Starseed', '星際種子', '{"keywords":["Starseed","Purpose","Connection","Cosmos"],"nameEn":"Starseed"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"You may identify as more than human—as a Starseed whose soul originates in a distant star system. In this spiritual framework, your essence carries light codes from the Pleiades, Sirius, Arcturus, or other systems. You may feel that you chose to be born on Earth at this pivotal moment to support the evolution of human consciousness and the transformation of the planet. Perhaps you have often felt out of place or longed for home. This card suggests that you may be here to bring your unique wisdom and perspective into your life on Earth.","currentSituation":"You may have long felt lonely or misunderstood, as though you do not belong in this world. You may have a natural interest in technology, the cosmos, or spirituality. Perhaps you have had experiences you interpret as contact with extraterrestrial life or craft, or you often dream of starscapes. Violence, injustice, and destruction on Earth may affect you deeply. This card invites you to remember what gives your life meaning and consider how your sense of purpose can be expressed here.","deeperMeaning":"In this spiritual belief system, Starseeds are souls said to come from highly evolved civilizations, bringing frequencies of love, peace, and expanded awareness. You may feel that your soul carries memories of advanced knowledge, healing traditions, or cosmic truths. Awakening to a Starseed identity can mean integrating your human experience on Earth with a sense of cosmic belonging, becoming a bridge between worlds. Your purpose is not to escape Earth, but to bring what you value into your life here.","actionGuidance":"Try a meditation in which you reflect on your connection to the stars, your sense of belonging, and what feels meaningful to you. Explore different star-system traditions and notice which ideas resonate without feeling pressured to adopt an identity. Spend time under the night sky if it feels grounding. Seek communities where you can share these experiences thoughtfully and support one another. Stay connected to ordinary life on Earth as well; grounding can help you serve your values effectively. Develop your distinctive gifts and use them in ways that feel helpful and responsible. Remember that you can choose how to express your sense of purpose.","energyHealing":"Moldavite or Libyan desert glass may be used as symbolic ritual objects associated with star origins in some traditions. Labradorite can be included in reflective practices about identity and purpose. You might try a meditation beneath the night sky, imagining a thread of light connecting you with the stars. Frankincense essential oil may be part of a ritual if suitable for you. Listen to space-themed or ambient music if it supports relaxation. Visualize light connecting with the Crown Chakra as an imaginative exercise. Balance any cosmic exploration with grounding practices and everyday routines. Treat these as spiritual practices, not literal proof of extraterrestrial origin.","soulQuestion":"Am I ready to explore my sense of cosmic origin and live out a meaningful purpose on Earth? How can I become a bridge between the perspectives that matter to me?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '14', 'en', 'Sacred Shadow', '神聖陰影', '{"keywords":["Shadow","Integration","Acceptance","Wholeness"],"nameEn":"Sacred Shadow"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"Your shadow is not your enemy. It can include parts of yourself that have been denied or suppressed and are waiting to be seen, accepted, and integrated. Everyone has aspects they consider unacceptable, unspiritual, or difficult. Yet a fuller sense of light can come from embracing the whole self, including the shadow. As you integrate these parts, you may feel more whole and spend less energy fighting yourself.","currentSituation":"You may be trying hard to become a perfect spiritual person by suppressing anger, jealousy, desire, or other emotions you consider negative. Or your shadow may be appearing through projection: traits that trigger a strong reaction in someone else may also reflect something you have not acknowledged in yourself. Emotional outbursts, self-sabotaging behavior, or repeated negative patterns may be signals asking for your attention. Approach them with curiosity and care rather than judgment.","deeperMeaning":"Jungian psychology describes the shadow as including suppressed aspects of the self, as well as undeveloped potential and strength. Rejecting the shadow can mean rejecting a part of your own wholeness and power. Shadow work is not about becoming darker; it is about becoming more honest and complete. Light and shadow are two sides of experience, and accepting the shadow can strengthen your capacity to live authentically. Some people find that spiritual growth stalls when they focus only on light and love while avoiding difficult inner material. Transformation can ask for the courage to explore what has been hidden.","actionGuidance":"Begin a shadow journal, noting parts of yourself you dislike, feelings or thoughts you try to hide, and situations that trigger strong reactions. Ask what these reactions may reflect within you. You might write a dialogue with a shadow part, asking why it is present, what it needs, and what it is trying to protect. Do not judge or try to eliminate it; seek to understand it with curiosity and compassion. Inner-child reflection may help when a pattern connects with experiences from childhood. Consider qualified psychotherapy or a trusted shadow-work practitioner if you want support. Give yourself permission to feel uncomfortable emotions without acting harmfully on them.","energyHealing":"Obsidian or black tourmaline may be used as grounding objects during reflective shadow work. Smoky quartz can serve as a symbol of transformation and integration. In a guided visualization, imagine entering a cave or basement within yourself and meeting a shadow aspect with care, inviting it into awareness rather than forcing it away. Myrrh or cedar essential oils may be part of a ritual if suitable for you. A new-moon ritual can be a symbolic time to reflect on patterns you want to change. Shadow work is best done in a supportive and safe setting. Practice grounding and seek professional support if difficult feelings become overwhelming.","soulQuestion":"Am I ready to face and embrace parts of myself that I have tried to hide or deny? Can I meet my shadow with compassion instead of criticism?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '15', 'en', 'Divine Connection', '神聖連結', '{"keywords":["Connection","Oneness","Presence","Divinity"],"nameEn":"Divine Connection"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"Your connection with the divine source has never been broken; perhaps you have simply lost sight of it. You do not have to search outside yourself for the divine, because this card invites you to recognize the sacred within. You do not need to become spiritual to connect with the divine; the card suggests that divinity is already part of your essence. Your connection with all things can be understood as enduring and inseparable. Each breath and heartbeat can remind you of the sacred moving through life. One simple way to return to this connection is presence: being fully here in this moment.","currentSituation":"You may feel disconnected from the sacred, and spiritual practices may have become mechanical or empty. Perhaps you are looking for the divine through complicated rituals or doctrines while overlooking the simple possibility of presence here and now. Or you may have had a brief experience of sacred connection and now long to feel it again. This card invites you to stop searching for a better future state and begin by being present. Connection need not wait until you become a better version of yourself; it can be explored in this moment.","deeperMeaning":"Divine connection does not have to be a special mystical experience, though such experiences can occur. More deeply, it can mean being aware of sacred presence in all things. When you are fully present and not pulled away by regret about the past or worry about the future, you may feel this connection. When you look at a flower, listen to rain, or notice your breath, being fully with the experience can feel sacred. Many spiritual seekers make connection complicated, but this card points to a simple truth: the sacred may be found here, in the ordinary wonders of daily life.","actionGuidance":"Practice present-moment awareness, not to achieve a special state but simply to notice what is here. Begin with simple activities: drink tea attentively, feel each step while walking, or listen to birdsong. Create a sacred space if that helps, such as an altar, a place in nature, or a quiet inner refuge. Remember that the sacred can also be encountered in ordinary places. Loosen fixed ideas about what the divine must look like and allow for different experiences. Washing dishes, driving, or working can also become mindful activities. Gratitude may help you notice the blessings already present in your life. Spend time in nature if it helps you feel connected.","energyHealing":"Clear quartz or selenite may be included as symbolic objects in a personal ritual. Try an oneness meditation, imagining your connection with trees, stars, and living beings while remaining grounded in your own body. Palo santo or frankincense can be used to create a reflective atmosphere if suitable for you. Practice breathing gently into the heart and imagining love extending outward. Listen to sacred music or repeat a sound that is meaningful to you, such as Om or Amitabha Buddha. A light meditation may help you reflect on connection. Above all, keep the practice simple: it may call for an open and present heart rather than elaborate techniques.","soulQuestion":"Am I looking for the divine only in my thoughts and missing the sacred presence of this moment? Can I recognize something sacred in ordinary life?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '7', 'en', 'Abundance Manifestation', '豐盛顯化', '{"keywords":["Abundance","Manifestation","Creation","Attraction"],"nameEn":"Abundance Manifestation"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"You may be at a powerful threshold for bringing intentions into form. Your frequency may feel elevated, helping you notice opportunities and possibilities more quickly. The universe is responding not only to your thoughts, but also to your overall energy and choices. You are a creator, and your thoughts, emotions, and beliefs can shape how you meet reality. This may be a time to use that creative power consciously and move toward a life that feels abundant to your soul. Remember that true abundance is not only material; it can include richness and flow in many areas of life.","currentSituation":"You may be noticing a quicker connection between your thoughts and what happens around you. Things you think about may seem to appear soon afterward, whether positive or negative. This can feel exciting and also unsettling, because it asks you to be aware of your thoughts and energy. You may be trying different manifestation techniques, some of which seem to work and others not. This card reminds you that manifestation is not only about technique; your inner state and beliefs matter too.","deeperMeaning":"Manifestation is not about manipulating the universe into giving you everything you want; it can be understood as aligning with the creative flow of life. When a desire feels connected to your authentic nature and purpose, pursuing it may feel more natural. Obstacles can come from limiting beliefs, feelings of unworthiness, or conflicted attitudes about abundance. Some people may say they want abundance while holding deeper beliefs that money is bad, spiritual people should be poor, or they do not deserve good things. Manifestation work can begin internally by examining those beliefs and developing a greater capacity for gratitude and receiving.","actionGuidance":"Each day, visualize the kind of life you hope to create and notice what feelings arise, such as joy or gratitude. You may make a vision board or an abundance altar as a way to give your intentions form. Write down what you want, including how you hope to feel, not only the objects or outcomes. Examine limiting beliefs about money and abundance through journaling or other reflective practices. Practice gratitude for what you already have. Take inspired, practical actions; creation involves both intention and your participation. Practice receiving help and gifts when they are freely offered. Keep choosing activities that support your well-being rather than trying to maintain a constant high mood.","energyHealing":"Citrine, green phantom quartz, or gold may be included in a personal abundance ritual. Try grounding practices that bring attention to the Solar Plexus and Root Chakras. In an abundance meditation, imagine golden light moving through different areas of your life. Cinnamon, orange, or patchouli essential oils may be used in a personal ritual if suitable for you. You could reflect on your relationship with money and release beliefs that no longer serve you. Visualize details of a life with sufficient resources, using all your senses. An affirmation such as “I am open to abundance” or “I deserve good things” may help you focus your reflection.","soulQuestion":"Do I truly believe I deserve abundance? Am I ready to receive more than I currently know? What hidden beliefs do I hold about money and material abundance?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '8', 'en', 'Soul Family', '靈魂家族', '{"keywords":["Connection","Community","Support","Soul"],"nameEn":"Soul Family"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"Your soul family may be finding you through a sense of resonance. These souls may feel connected to you through an old bond, as though you have learned and grown together across many lifetimes. You may share similar light codes and a sense of purpose. The universe may be bringing about meaningful meetings and reunions because this is a time when you can serve the Earth together. You do not have to walk your path alone; a community of kindred spirits may be gathering around you.","currentSituation":"You may have felt lonely or misunderstood, even when surrounded by people. Family members and old friends may not understand your current path or the changes you are going through. You may long for deeper spiritual connection and a community where you can be yourself. Or you may recently have met people whose connection feels unusually deep and familiar, as though you already know them. This card invites you to remain open to new soul connections and notice which relationships feel supportive and genuine.","deeperMeaning":"A soul family does not have to be a family by blood. It can mean beings with whom you feel a deep soul agreement and resonance. You may imagine that you agreed to meet in this life to support one another''s growth and purpose. Soul-family connections can bring a sense of recognition, deep understanding, and acceptance. These people may see your essence beyond your personality or social role. Such connections are not always easy; sometimes people mirror your shadow or encourage you to grow. The card frames this as a relationship grounded in care and commitment to one another''s development. Your soul family may include people, animals, spiritual guides, or beings from other dimensions within this belief system.","actionGuidance":"Set an intention to welcome meaningful, resonant connections. Attend spiritual workshops, gatherings, or online communities to create opportunities to meet people. When you meet someone with whom you resonate, consider deepening the connection rather than withdrawing out of fear. Join or create a learning circle or support group. Share your spiritual journey on social media or a blog if that feels right, so kindred people can find you. Trust your discernment about who belongs in your close circle. Soul family is about quality, not quantity: a few deep connections can matter more than many surface relationships. Stay open to unconventional forms of community, including online groups or friendships across generations.","energyHealing":"Rose quartz or rhodonite may be included in a personal practice focused on openness and connection. Practices that balance the Heart and Throat Chakras can support expressing yourself authentically and building resonant relationships. You could create a simple ritual to welcome supportive connections using candles, crystals, or written intentions. Visualize being surrounded by people who care about and understand you. Lavender or rose essential oil may be part of a heart-opening ritual if suitable for you. A chakra-alignment meditation may help you reflect on how you show up in relationships. A full-moon ritual can be used as a symbolic moment to set intentions for connection.","soulQuestion":"Am I truly open to deep soul connections, or are fear and defenses keeping them at a distance? Am I ready to show my authentic self to the people I hope to meet?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '9', 'en', 'Divine Feminine', '神聖陰性', '{"keywords":["Receptivity","Acceptance","Intuition","Creativity"],"nameEn":"Divine Feminine"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"The Divine Feminine is described as a rising energy on Earth, and you may be one channel through which this ancient force returns. This energy is not about gender; it represents qualities such as receptivity, flow, intuition, nourishment, and creativity. It is associated with the moon, the wisdom of water, and the creative womb. After long periods of suppression, the Divine Feminine is being invited to be seen, honored, and embodied. The goddess within you may be awakening, inviting deeper self-acceptance and a freer creative flow.","currentSituation":"You may have been relying heavily on active, goal-directed energy—constantly acting, pushing, controlling, and achieving. You may feel tired, depleted, or disconnected from your body and emotions. Your receptive side may be asking for attention through physical sensations, emotional shifts, or a deep desire for rest and nourishment. Or perhaps you are just beginning to explore goddess energy, lunar cycles, or feminine spiritual practices. This card encourages you to honor and embody receptive qualities within yourself, regardless of your biological sex.","deeperMeaning":"The Divine Feminine teaches the power of being, not only doing. It reminds you that receiving matters as much as giving, rest has value alongside work, and feeling can be as wise as thinking. Feminine energy is cyclical, spiral, and inclusive, complementing the linear and goal-directed qualities often called masculine energy. In a world that can overvalue constant action, restoring balance can support personal and collective healing. This may include honoring the body, emotions, and intuitive wisdom; learning to receive help; allowing things to unfold organically; and aligning with natural cycles. The Divine Feminine can also symbolize deep creativity, giving form to something new from a space of possibility.","actionGuidance":"Build a relationship with lunar cycles by noticing how your energy and emotions shift through the month. Give yourself permission to rest, receive, and do nothing without guilt. Explore feminine spiritual practices such as goddess meditation, womb-centered reflection, or sacred dance if they resonate with you. Nourish your body with food, touch, and attention that feel caring. Create art, music, or another form of expression. You could create an altar honoring different aspects of the Divine Feminine. Meditate or bathe in water as a symbolic way to connect with its wisdom. Practice receiving support from others. Reflect on your relationship with your mother, female ancestors, and the wider community of women.","energyHealing":"You may choose practices that focus on balancing the Sacral and Heart Chakras, which some traditions associate with receptive and creative energy. Moonstone, rose quartz, or pearls may be used as personal ritual objects. A womb-centered meditation can be practiced regardless of whether you have a physical womb, as an image of a creative inner space. Rose, ylang-ylang, or jasmine essential oils may be part of a ritual if suitable for you. Try gentle, flowing movement such as Yin Yoga if it feels supportive. A full-moon ritual can be a symbolic time for reflection and renewal. Visualize soft pink or silver moonlight surrounding you, and explore sound practices such as goddess mantras or womb-drum rhythms if they resonate.","soulQuestion":"Where in my life am I overusing active, goal-driven energy and neglecting receptivity? Am I ready to receive, surrender, and trust the flow of life?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '10', 'en', 'Divine Masculine', '神聖陽性', '{"keywords":["Masculine Energy","Action","Protection","Manifestation"],"nameEn":"Divine Masculine"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"A healthy Divine Masculine energy may be awakening within you. This is not toxic masculinity or control, but qualities such as protection, action, structure, and conscious leadership. It is the energy of the sun, the transformative power of fire, and the steadiness of a mountain. In this tradition, the Divine Masculine offers a container in which the creativity of the Divine Feminine can safely take form. It can embody a warrior''s courage, a wise leader''s discernment, and a father''s protective love. This may be a time to embody these qualities, take action, and create a solid structure for your dreams.","currentSituation":"You may have been planning, dreaming, and feeling, but finding it difficult to put ideas into practice. Perhaps you have relied heavily on receptive, flowing energy and waiting, and now need more focused action. Or you may have lost touch with healthy masculine energy because of painful experiences with toxic masculinity. You may need clearer boundaries, ways to protect your energy, or the courage to stand up in certain situations. This card calls on your inner warrior and wise leader.","deeperMeaning":"The Divine Masculine is very different from cultural ideas of masculinity. It is not about domination, suppressing emotion, or opposing feminine energy. A healthy Divine Masculine is conscious, responsible, and oriented toward service. It knows how to use strength without abusing it, protect without controlling, and lead without dominating. It offers direction, structure, and action while staying connected to the wisdom of the heart and soul. It can be an inner father archetype that offers support, encouragement, and confidence in your abilities. Balanced masculine energy can help you bring a spiritual vision into the world effectively.","actionGuidance":"Set clear goals and an action plan that breaks your vision into practical steps. Build daily structure and discipline that support your growth and goals. Practice setting and maintaining healthy boundaries, including saying no to things that do not align with your well-being. Develop discernment so you can make decisions when needed. Try physical training, martial arts, or another embodied practice to connect with strength and agency. Speak up for yourself and others when appropriate. Take on leadership or mentoring roles if they suit you, and complete projects you have begun. You might also reflect on your relationship with your father, male ancestors, and the wider community of men.","energyHealing":"You may focus on practices associated with the Solar Plexus Chakra, often linked with willpower and personal agency. Tiger''s eye, red jasper, or citrine can be included in a personal ritual. Try a sun meditation, imagining golden sunlight warming your whole being and gently activating your inner fire. Cedar, sandalwood, or frankincense essential oils may be used as part of a ritual if suitable for you. Dynamic yoga or qigong can help you explore movement and strength. Spend time in sunlight safely, and visualize a protective golden or red light if that feels grounding. Warrior breathing or fire-breathing practices should be gentle and appropriate to your health; stop if uncomfortable.","soulQuestion":"Am I avoiding an action or responsibility that matters to me? Am I ready to embody healthy strength to protect and bring my dreams into reality?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '11', 'en', 'Angel Guidance', '天使指引', '{"keywords":["Angels","Guidance","Protection","Support"],"nameEn":"Angel Guidance"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"This card describes a strengthening connection with the angelic realm. In this spiritual belief, these beings of light are nearby and await your invitation to offer help. They do not override free will, but are said to respond when asked. You are not alone: angels, archangels, and beings of light may be imagined as watching over you and guiding you toward your highest path. This may be a time to consciously invite support and remain open to love, wisdom, and encouragement.","currentSituation":"You may feel lonely, overwhelmed, or unsure of your direction. Life''s challenges may feel heavy, and you may wonder whether you can handle them alone. Or you may have begun noticing angel numbers, feathers, or other signs that feel meaningful to you. You may receive impressions in dreams or meditation without being sure where they come from or what they mean. This card invites you to notice what feels supportive and explore your own interpretation of these experiences.","deeperMeaning":"Angels are described in this tradition as beings of pure love whose existence extends beyond the three-dimensional world. Many people believe everyone has at least one guardian angel and that some may have more. You may also choose to call on archangels, ascended masters, or other beings of light for support. In this belief system, angels may communicate through synchronicities, intuition, dreams, bodily sensations, or recurring symbols. Learning to notice and interpret these signs is part of developing a relationship with angelic guidance. Guidance rooted in love should feel supportive and encouraging; if a message brings fear or negativity, pause and use your discernment rather than assuming its source.","actionGuidance":"You may speak to your guardian angel each day, aloud or silently. If you ask for help, be clear about what you need. Notice synchronicities, repeating numbers such as 111, 222, or 444, and other signs that feel meaningful to you. Create an altar with objects that represent angels, such as a feather or a white candle. Learn about different archangels if that interests you and consider calling on them symbolically. Keep a journal of impressions and responses. Express gratitude when you feel supported. Stay open to unexpected forms of guidance while also using your judgment.","energyHealing":"Clear quartz, angelite, or moonstone may be included in a personal ritual focused on connection. Practices that balance the Crown and Heart Chakras may support reflection on spiritual messages. Create an angel-connection meditation by inviting your guardian angel into your awareness, if that is meaningful to you. Frankincense or rose essential oil may be part of a ritual if suitable for you. Visualize yourself surrounded by protective wings as a symbol of care and support. Listen to music that feels uplifting. Before sleep, you may set an intention to remember dreams, then write down what you recall in the morning. Interpret these experiences thoughtfully and in a way that feels grounded.","soulQuestion":"Am I willing to receive support and trust that I am not alone? Am I ready to open my heart to guidance and encouragement?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '12', 'en', 'Chakra Balance', '脈輪平衡', '{"keywords":["Chakras","Energy","Balance","Healing"],"nameEn":"Chakra Balance"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"Your energy system may need attention and recalibration. In this tradition, chakras are described as centers in the energy body. When they feel balanced and aligned, life energy—sometimes called qi or prana—is thought to flow freely, supporting vitality and clarity. A blockage or imbalance may be associated with physical, emotional, or spiritual concerns, though chakra concepts are not medical diagnoses. This card invites you to care for your energy and physical well-being together. It may be a good time for reflection and practices that help you feel balanced.","currentSituation":"You may notice areas of life that feel out of balance. In chakra traditions, Root Chakra concerns are associated with anxiety, finances, or safety; Sacral Chakra concerns with creativity or emotion; Solar Plexus concerns with confidence or digestion; Heart Chakra concerns with giving or receiving love; Throat Chakra concerns with communication or self-expression; Third Eye concerns with intuition or vision; and Crown Chakra concerns with spiritual connection. These associations are reflective frameworks, not diagnostic tools. This card invites you to notice which areas may need care and to seek qualified support for health concerns.","deeperMeaning":"The seven main chakras are understood in some traditions as bridges between the physical and energy bodies. Each is associated with parts of the body, emotional themes, and spiritual questions. Chakra work appears in many older spiritual traditions, including Indian yoga and Tibetan Buddhism, and is also used in some modern energy-healing practices. Balancing chakras is not only an energy exercise; it can also involve attending to life themes connected with each center. For example, heart-centered reflection may include forgiveness, openness to love, and self-compassion. These practices can complement, but do not replace, medical or mental-health care.","actionGuidance":"Learn about the location, color, element, and themes associated with each chakra in the tradition you follow. Scan your body and notice where you feel tension, openness, or disconnection without treating the sensation as a diagnosis. You may use color-associated stones as reflective objects, try a chakra meditation, or explore yoga poses associated with different centers. Essential oils, tuning forks, or chanting can be part of a personal ritual if suitable for you. Notice whether recurring life patterns connect with themes you associate with a chakra. Reiki or other energy practices may be options if they feel right, but consult qualified professionals for medical or mental-health concerns.","energyHealing":"A seven-color crystal set may be used as a symbolic focus in a whole-chakra meditation: red jasper at the Root, carnelian at the Sacral, citrine at the Solar Plexus, green aventurine or rose quartz at the Heart, blue kyanite at the Throat, lapis lazuli at the Third Eye, and amethyst or clear quartz at the Crown. You may also explore chakra sound practices using a tone or mantra associated with each center. Imagine rainbow light moving upward from the base of the body, bringing attention and care to each area. These are optional contemplative practices, not treatments.","soulQuestion":"Where in my life do I feel blocked or out of balance? Am I willing to make time to care for and rebalance my energy system?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '16', 'en', 'Energy Protection', '能量保護', '{"keywords":["Protection","Boundaries","Cleansing","Shielding"],"nameEn":"Energy Protection"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"As a sensitive lightworker, you may be especially receptive to the energy around you. This can be a gift, and it can also call for learning how to care for your own energy. Protection does not have to mean fear or opposition; it can mean setting wise boundaries. Just as locking your front door can be ordinary common sense rather than an act of fear, energy boundaries can be part of spiritual self-care. When you feel clear and grounded, you may be better able to serve without becoming depleted or overly affected by others.","currentSituation":"You may often feel drained, especially in crowds or after spending time with certain people. You may absorb other people''s emotions, leading to mood changes or physical discomfort. Perhaps it is difficult to set healthy boundaries or say no, and you take on other people''s problems. You may feel targeted by what some spiritual traditions call “energy vampires,” or sense that your space is affected by negative energy. This card reminds you that caring for your energy can be an act of self-respect and discernment.","deeperMeaning":"Energy protection is treated in this spiritual framework as a basic skill for lightworkers. If your energy feels depleted or scattered, it can be harder to feel clear and serve others in the way you intend. Protection does not have to mean building a cold wall; the card describes it as creating a permeable boundary that allows love in and out while limiting what feels harmful. Some traditions connect this with maintaining a steady personal energy. Practical and symbolic tools can both matter. You have the right to protect your time and energy, say no, and set boundaries; this is not selfishness, but taking responsibility for yourself.","actionGuidance":"Create a morning boundary-setting ritual, perhaps imagining a sphere of white or golden light around you. Practice saying no without overexplaining or feeling guilty. Limit contact with people who consistently leave you depleted, or decide what boundaries you need before interacting with them. Cleanse your space in a way that is meaningful to you, using sage, palo santo, or sound if suitable. Notice where your energy seems to go—certain people, places, or activities—and consider limiting or changing those situations. You may visualize releasing unhelpful ties while keeping appropriate relationships intact. Pay attention to your boundaries, especially when you feel vulnerable. Trust your instincts while also checking them against the facts of a situation.","energyHealing":"Black tourmaline, obsidian, or hematite may be carried or placed in your home as symbolic grounding objects. Try a protective-bubble visualization, imagining yourself surrounded by light while remembering that practical boundaries matter too. A sea-salt bath can be a personal cleansing ritual if suitable for you. You could create a symbolic energy grid in your home with black tourmaline and clear quartz. Cedar or juniper essential oils may be used if suitable. In a visualization, imagine a layer of light around each chakra. Ask trusted people or spiritual guides for support if that is meaningful to you. Regularly check in with yourself and use grounding practices; you do not need to assume that every difficult feeling comes from outside energy.","soulQuestion":"Am I allowing others to cross my boundaries without noticing? Am I willing to set healthy limits to protect my time and energy?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '17', 'en', 'Ascension Symptoms', '揚升症狀', '{"keywords":["Ascension","Transformation","Symptoms","Adjustment"],"nameEn":"Ascension Symptoms"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"This card''s spiritual framework describes your body as moving through a deep transformation, sometimes called ascension, accompanied by physical, emotional, or mental symptoms. These experiences may feel uncomfortable. Some spiritual interpretations view them as part of personal evolution and adjustment, but they are not a medical diagnosis. Be patient and compassionate with yourself while also caring for your physical health.","currentSituation":"You may be experiencing physical symptoms such as fatigue, headaches, ringing in the ears, joint pain, digestive problems, or sleep disruption. You may also notice emotional fluctuations, difficulty concentrating, or feeling disconnected from reality. Sensitivity to light or sound, or unusual bodily sensations, may also be part of your experience. This card offers a spiritual lens for reflection, but it cannot determine the cause of symptoms. Please seek medical advice for new, persistent, severe, or concerning symptoms, even if you also find spiritual meaning in them.","deeperMeaning":"In this spiritual tradition, ascension refers not to leaving Earth for another place, but to a shift in consciousness and a process of bodily change. Some people understand changes in energy as part of adapting to a higher frequency. Experiences and symptoms vary from person to person. This belief should not be used to dismiss illness or delay care. A computer-upgrade metaphor may help describe the feeling of needing time to adjust, but physical symptoms can have many causes. Listen to your body and seek qualified medical advice when needed.","actionGuidance":"Listen to your body and give it the rest it needs; do not force yourself to keep the same pace. Stay hydrated and choose nourishing food that suits your health. Gentle movement such as yoga, walking, or swimming may feel supportive; avoid strenuous exercise if it worsens symptoms. Ground yourself by spending time in nature. A salt bath may be soothing if appropriate for you. Try not to panic about symptoms, but do consult a medical professional—especially if they persist, are severe, or interfere with daily life. Connect with supportive people, and keep spiritual practices gentle and optional. Meditation or energy work should not replace medical care.","energyHealing":"Clear quartz or amethyst may be used as symbolic objects in a reflective practice. Try a gentle visualization of light while allowing your body to rest and adjust at its own pace. Lavender or chamomile essential oils may be soothing if suitable for you. Grounding practices can include time in nature, gentle stretching, or feeling your feet on the floor. A salt bath or calming music may help you relax. Imagine warm golden light as a comforting image, not as a treatment. Affirmations such as “I will care for my body with patience” can support self-compassion. Seek medical advice for physical or mental-health symptoms.","soulQuestion":"Can I meet changes in my body with patience and trust while also taking its needs seriously? Am I willing to slow down and seek the support I need?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '19', 'en', 'Earth Guardian', '地球守護者', '{"keywords":["Earth","Protection","Environment","Responsibility"],"nameEn":"Earth Guardian"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"You may feel a deep soul connection with Mother Earth and a desire to help care for and protect the planet. Earth is not only a resource or backdrop; many spiritual traditions regard it as a living presence that nourishes and supports life. As a lightworker, you may feel called to protect the Earth through your choices, awareness, and way of living. Small actions matter, because collective change can begin with individual choices. The card frames the Earth''s transition as something to which you can contribute through caring action.","currentSituation":"You may feel deep pain or helplessness about environmental destruction. You may try to make environmentally conscious choices but feel that your efforts are too small. Perhaps you feel called to participate more actively in conservation or ecological movements. Or this card may invite you to review your lifestyle and consider where you can show more respect and care for the Earth. You may also want to spend more time in nature and tend to your relationship with it.","deeperMeaning":"Humanity has been disconnected from the Earth for a long time, treating her as a resource to be endlessly extracted. This card asks you to remember that the planet is our home and that human well-being is connected to the health of the Earth. Caring for the planet can begin with healing our relationship with nature—recognizing that we are part of it, not separate from or above it. Anyone can be an Earth Guardian without becoming an environmental activist; it begins with living consciously. Consumption, food, energy use, and attitudes toward nature are all ways to care for the planet. The card also frames raising awareness as a way to serve the Earth.","actionGuidance":"Spend regular time in nature, not only to relax but to connect and listen. Walk barefoot outdoors if it is safe and comfortable for you. Review your lifestyle and make environmentally conscious choices where possible: reduce plastic, recycle, conserve water and electricity, and support sustainable products. You could reduce meat consumption or choose sustainably sourced food if that suits you. Plant or care for a tree, garden, or other living things. Participate in environmental activities or support organizations doing this work. Learn about environmental issues and share what you learn. Try a meditation that imagines the Earth surrounded by light and care. Practice gratitude for what the Earth provides and cultivate a respectful relationship with nature.","energyHealing":"Moss agate or green jasper may be used as symbolic objects for grounding and connection with the Earth. You could create a simple outdoor ritual or offer care through practical service, such as picking up litter where safe or helping care for a local green space. Grounding meditation may involve imagining roots extending from your feet into the earth while remaining aware of your body and surroundings. Cedar or pine essential oils may be part of a reflective practice if suitable. Mark seasonal changes with a small ritual honoring the Earth''s cycles. Create an altar with stones, plants, or soil as a reminder of your connection. You might say, “I see you, I care for you, and I will do my part to protect you.”","soulQuestion":"Am I living in a way that respects my relationship with the Earth? How can I care for and protect the planet more consciously?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '20', 'en', 'Spiritual Teacher', '靈性導師', '{"keywords":["Mentor","Teaching","Sharing","Wisdom"],"nameEn":"Spiritual Teacher"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"You may have traveled a deep spiritual path and gathered wisdom and insight along the way. This may be a time to share what you have learned and offer light to others. You do not have to be perfect or all-knowing to teach; you can share your experiences honestly. A spiritual teacher need not be a distant master, but can be a humble fellow traveler who has walked a little farther and offers a hand. Your story, healing, and awakening may inspire or help someone else.","currentSituation":"You may feel called to share your spiritual knowledge and experience but be unsure how to begin or doubt whether you are qualified. Or people may naturally come to you for guidance and advice, which could be an invitation to notice your mentoring abilities. You may be considering teaching, writing, healing work, or another form of spiritual service. This card encourages you to take a thoughtful first step and trust that your particular experience has value, while staying honest about what you do and do not know.","deeperMeaning":"People who have moved through healing and awakening can choose to share what they have learned. This is not about believing you are better than others; it can be a natural exchange. Wisdom shared with care may benefit both the giver and receiver. A spiritual teacher remains a lifelong student; teaching and learning are two sides of the same process. What you teach may also be something you are still learning, and serving others can deepen your own understanding. Do not wait until you feel completely ready. Begin where you are and share what you can responsibly offer.","actionGuidance":"Start sharing your perspective in small ways, such as writing a blog post, making a social media post, or having a thoughtful conversation with a friend. Consider your distinctive gifts and experiences and what you can responsibly teach. You might offer a low-cost or introductory service to build experience, while respecting your training and boundaries. It is all right to say “I don''t know.” Stay humble and keep learning. Develop a teacher identity without letting it define your whole self. Set healthy boundaries: you are a guide, not a rescuer. Seek mentors or a peer community to support your growth. Most importantly, try to live by the values you teach.","energyHealing":"Lapis lazuli or blue kyanite may be used as symbolic objects in a Throat Chakra practice focused on clear, authentic expression. Labradorite can be included in reflection about intuition and insight. Try a meditation in which you ask what you can responsibly share and what is not yours to carry. Frankincense or sage may be used to prepare a teaching space if suitable. Consider grounding and setting boundaries before and after teaching so you can remain present without taking responsibility for students'' energy. Create an altar with objects representing wisdom and learning. Visualize light flowing from your heart and voice as a symbol of care. An affirmation such as “I share what I know with humility” may help you focus.","soulQuestion":"Am I ready to step beyond my comfort zone and share what I have learned? Can I be a light for others with humility and honesty?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '21', 'en', 'Soul Contract', '靈魂契約', '{"keywords":["Contract","Agreement","Release","Freedom"],"nameEn":"Soul Contract"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"In some spiritual traditions, the soul is described as making agreements with other souls, guides, or the universe before incarnation. These agreements are understood as opportunities for learning and growth. Some may feel complete or no longer aligned with your present well-being. This card invites you to reflect on patterns you may want to update or release, and to make conscious agreements that support the path you choose now. You have the power to reconsider the meaning you give these spiritual ideas and to choose how you move forward.","currentSituation":"You may feel caught in a pattern, relationship, or situation, as though an invisible force is preventing you from moving forward. Perhaps you experience recurring lessons or relationships that seem difficult to change. You may feel an unexplained sense of obligation toward certain people or roles. In the language of this card, these experiences might be interpreted through the idea of a soul contract. If a pattern no longer serves you, you can reflect on what keeps it going and consider what choices are available now.","deeperMeaning":"Soul contracts are spiritual agreements, distinct from legal contracts, and are understood in some traditions as flexible and open to reconsideration. They may be used symbolically to reflect on relationships, life experiences, or roles a person feels drawn into. Such interpretations can help people make meaning of experience, but they are matters of belief rather than established fact. A past-life or soul-contract explanation should not be used to excuse harm, blame someone for illness or hardship, or avoid present responsibilities. Releasing a contract can be understood as a spiritual expression of maturity: recognizing your agency and choosing your path now.","actionGuidance":"Try a reflective meditation and ask your higher self what patterns no longer support you. Notice recurring themes in your life and consider what they may be teaching you without assuming a supernatural cause. Write down an agreement you are ready to release, such as “I must suffer in order to grow” or “I must sacrifice myself to save others.” If you choose, create a symbolic ritual by reading the statement aloud and safely disposing of the paper. You can also write a new intention, such as choosing growth through joy or relationships built on mutual care. Releasing a belief does not harm anyone else. Consider a qualified, grounded practitioner if you seek support, and keep your focus on choices you can make in this life.","energyHealing":"Obsidian or smoky quartz may be used as symbolic objects in a personal letting-go ritual. An Akashic-records meditation may be meaningful within your spiritual beliefs, but treat what arises as reflection rather than verified history. Sage or palo santo may be used to mark a transition if suitable for you. You could state aloud what you are choosing to release and what values you want to follow now. Visualize setting down an old agreement and making room for a new intention. A new moon can serve as a symbolic time for reflection. Notice any sense of freedom or lightness afterward, and allow new possibilities to develop at a grounded pace.","soulQuestion":"Am I ready to release beliefs or agreements that no longer support me? Am I willing to take ownership of the choices that shape my path now?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '18', 'en', 'Past Life Memory', '前世記憶', '{"keywords":["Past Lives","Karma","Memory","Healing"],"nameEn":"Past Life Memory"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"Many spiritual traditions describe the soul as moving through multiple lifetimes, each offering opportunities for learning and growth. Within this belief, memories, wounds, and gifts from past lives may be carried deep in the soul and influence present experience. Some fears, talents, relationship patterns, or physical concerns may feel connected to experiences beyond this lifetime. This card suggests exploring whether such a perspective offers insight or a sense of healing. Remembering the past is not about becoming absorbed in it, but about releasing old patterns and living more freely now.","currentSituation":"You may experience déjà vu, a strong attraction or aversion to a particular era or place, or fears and talents that seem difficult to explain. Images or feelings may arise in dreams or meditation. You may feel an immediate, deep connection with someone or an unexplained aversion, which some people interpret through the idea of past-life relationships. You may be curious about past lives, or find that old stories influence how you understand your present. This card invites you to explore these impressions for reflection and insight while keeping your attention on your life today.","deeperMeaning":"Belief in past lives is part of many spiritual traditions, though it is not established historical fact. Reincarnation teachings suggest that souls may learn and grow through different roles, cultures, and circumstances over multiple lifetimes. In this framework, past-life wounds may be used to interpret present fears or relationship difficulties, while past-life gifts may be viewed as continuing strengths. Exploring past lives should not become an excuse to avoid present responsibilities or a reason to treat an impression as proven fact. It may instead be used as a reflective tool for gaining insight and compassion. When you understand a pattern through this lens, you can still choose how to work with it now.","actionGuidance":"If you are curious about past-life ideas, you may explore them with a qualified practitioner, while remembering that imagery and impressions are not proof of historical events. Try a gentle meditation and notice what arises without forcing a story. Strong resonance with a particular era, culture, or place may be a prompt for reflection or historical learning. Keep a dream journal, since dreams can reveal themes from your inner life. Notice recurring patterns in your present and ask what they may be teaching you. Stay open without becoming attached to a specific explanation; your life now remains the focus. Forgiveness and letting go can be meaningful without assuming a karmic cause.","energyHealing":"Ruby or garnet may be used as symbolic grounding objects during reflection on strength and courage. In a guided visualization, you may revisit an imagined scene connected to a present concern and offer your current self compassion. Myrrh or sandalwood essential oils may be included in a reflective ritual if suitable. You could write down a pattern you are ready to release and safely dispose of the paper as a symbolic gesture. If imagery of death or trauma arises, pause and seek support from a qualified mental-health professional if distressed. A sea-salt bath with rose petals may be a calming ritual. Let any altar or remembrance practice honor your present life and choices.","soulQuestion":"Am I ready to explore old stories and patterns that may shape my present without letting them define me? Can I learn from the past while staying grounded in this life?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '34', 'en', 'Divine Masculine', '神聖男性', '{"keywords":["Masculine Energy","Strength","Protection","Action"],"nameEn":"Divine Masculine"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"The Divine Masculine represents qualities such as direction, protection, action, logic, and strength. It is not toxic masculinity—domination, control, or aggression—but a healthy expression of active energy, including protection, provision, structure, and wise action. Regardless of gender, you can explore these qualities within yourself. This card invites you to honor and integrate the Divine Masculine, especially if you have suppressed it or expressed it in a distorted way. Healthy active energy can offer direction and structure, bring a vision into action, and protect what is precious.","currentSituation":"You may need more active energy: clearer direction, action, structure, or boundaries. Or you may be expressing it in an unhealthy way through excessive control, aggression, or domination. Some men may be healing their relationship with masculinity and seeking a balance between toxic patterns and suppression. Some women may be learning to integrate inner masculine qualities without giving up their feminine strength. This card invites you to explore your relationship with masculine energy, both personally and collectively.","deeperMeaning":"Healthy Divine Masculine qualities can include clear purpose, considered action, protection without control, balance between logic and intuition, offering structure and support, courage, responsibility, and reliability. Collectively, people have experienced harmful forms of masculinity associated with war, domination, oppression, and environmental exploitation. In reaction, some have suppressed all masculine energy. Healing does not have to mean suppression; it can mean transforming harmful patterns into a healthier expression. We need active energy that can give direction, protect what is new and vulnerable, create structure amid uncertainty, and bridge vision with action. In balance with receptive energy, it can support a more integrated whole.","actionGuidance":"Assess how active energy is showing up in your life: is it excessive, absent, or distorted? If you need more of it, practice taking action before conditions are perfect, setting clear goals, building supportive structure, maintaining boundaries, and protecting your values. If you need balance, loosen control, trust receptivity as well as action, and let strength coexist with gentleness. Explore and heal relationships with your father or other masculine figures if that feels useful. Notice healthy masculine role models and archetypes, such as the king, warrior, magician, or mature lover. If you are a man, you can honor masculinity as a gift without adopting toxic extremes. Connect with images of mountains, the sun, deer, or eagles if they resonate. Try a meditation on the inner warrior or wise king.","energyHealing":"Tiger''s eye or red jasper may be used as grounding objects in a personal practice. Practices focusing on the Solar Plexus and Root Chakras may help you reflect on agency and stability. A midday sun meditation can be a symbolic way to connect with vitality. Visualize a healthy inner masculine figure—perhaps a wise king, warrior, or sage—with strength, compassion, and responsibility. Cedar or sandalwood essential oils may be part of a ritual if suitable. Create an altar with symbols such as a sword for discernment, a staff for action, a mountain for steadiness, or the sun for vitality. Try strength poses or Warrior yoga poses if safe and comfortable. Explore healing paternal wounds with appropriate support. Visualize your inner masculine and feminine qualities working together in harmony.","soulQuestion":"Am I ready to embrace and integrate healthy masculine qualities? Can I release harmful patterns and express strength with care?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '35', 'en', 'Cosmic Abundance', '宇宙豐盛', '{"keywords":["Abundance","Prosperity","Flow","Receiving"],"nameEn":"Cosmic Abundance"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"Many spiritual traditions describe the universe as abundant, like the countless stars, seeds, flowers, and forms of life in nature. Creation can feel generous and full of possibility. This card reminds you that abundance is not only money, but can include love, health, opportunity, joy, beauty, connection, and creativity. When you shift from a sense of scarcity toward a more abundant outlook, you may become more open to noticing and receiving what is available. This is an invitation to explore your relationship with abundance, not a guarantee of material wealth.","currentSituation":"You may be experiencing a sense of scarcity in one or more areas of life—finances, love, health, opportunity, or support. This may be a practical shortage or a deeper scarcity mindset, even when some resources are present. You may find it difficult to receive and be more accustomed to giving. Limiting beliefs about money, prosperity, or worthiness may be involved. Or perhaps you are beginning to notice ways life supports you. This card invites you to reconsider your relationship with abundance and explore ways to move from struggle toward a healthier flow.","deeperMeaning":"Abundance and scarcity mindsets offer very different ways of viewing life. A scarcity mindset assumes resources are limited, competition is necessary, and there is not enough for everyone. An abundance mindset emphasizes possibility, cooperation, circulation, and the ability to receive. These perspectives can shape your experience and choices. Healing a scarcity mindset may involve noticing beliefs learned in childhood, family, or society, and addressing guilt, shame, or fear around money and worthiness. It also involves balancing giving with receiving; some spiritually minded people give too much and have difficulty accepting support. Abundance here means allowing yourself to receive care and resources while also acting responsibly.","actionGuidance":"Notice beliefs you hold about scarcity and abundance. Complete the sentence “When it comes to money or abundance, I believe…” and observe any limiting ideas. Reflect on your relationship with money, acknowledge what it helps you do, and allow yourself to want and enjoy material well-being without judgment. Practice receiving compliments, help, or gifts without immediately feeling obligated to repay them. Notice whether you give beyond your means, refuse to receive, feel unworthy, or try to control everything. Appreciate what you already have. Visualize a life with more resources while taking practical steps toward it, such as learning, planning, or creating sustainable opportunities. Give generously when you can, without depleting yourself. Align work with your values and strengths where possible. Trust is helpful, but pair it with grounded choices.","energyHealing":"Citrine is often associated with abundance and success, and green aventurine with openness and the Heart Chakra; they may be used as symbolic objects. Try an abundance meditation in which golden light represents possibilities across different areas of life. Cinnamon or orange essential oils may be part of a personal ritual if suitable. Reflect on and release beliefs about money that no longer serve you. Visualize the details of a life with sufficient resources, using your imagination without treating it as a guarantee. You might write an affirmation such as “I am open to abundance” or “I deserve good things.” Practice both giving and receiving, and notice how resources flow in your life.","soulQuestion":"Am I ready to release a scarcity mindset and become more open to abundance? Can I allow myself to receive different forms of support and prosperity?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '36', 'en', 'Soul Family Reunion', '靈魂家族重聚', '{"keywords":["Soul Family","Connection","Reunion","Support"],"nameEn":"Soul Family Reunion"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"A soul family is described as beings with a deep connection at the soul level, not necessarily through blood. You may imagine that you have traveled through many lifetimes together, supporting one another''s growth and purpose. At different times in your life, you may meet people who feel like members of your soul family—some connections brief, others lasting, and each meaningful in its own way. This card celebrates the possibility of meeting or reconnecting with people who understand you, share your values or vision, and resonate with you.","currentSituation":"You may have long felt lonely or out of place, even in a crowd. You may long for deep connection and understanding beyond surface relationships. Perhaps you have recently lost some friendships or relationships, creating space for new connections. Or you may already have met people with whom you feel immediate recognition and a deep bond. This card invites you to remain open to finding people with whom you can share mutual understanding, care, and purpose.","deeperMeaning":"Soul family does not have to mean a family related by blood. In some spiritual traditions, it refers to a group of souls believed to travel, learn, or serve together. You may feel a sense of belonging with one or more communities because of shared values or resonance. A connection can feel immediate and hard to explain, as though you have known one another for a long time. Conversation may feel deep and understanding natural. Soul-family relationships can offer support, reflection, challenge, and celebration. In this time of awakening, spiritual communities may be gathering to work toward shared goals. Feeling part of a community may require tending past hurt, fear, or defensiveness and allowing yourself to be seen. Connection develops through mutual care and respect.","actionGuidance":"Tend wounds from past relationships and release what you can from betrayal, rejection, or abandonment, so you can be open to new connections. Clarify your values, purpose, and authentic self; these can help you recognize people with whom you resonate. Spend time in communities that feel welcoming, such as workshops, classes, online groups, or spiritual events. When you meet someone you connect with, consider taking a small step toward a deeper friendship. You can share authentically while respecting your boundaries. Not everyone will be a close friend, and that is all right. Trust takes time. Appreciate each meaningful connection, whether brief or lasting. Community can also include animals, nature, or spiritual practices that help you feel connected.","energyHealing":"Rose quartz may be used as a symbolic object in a practice focused on openness and care. Celestite may be included in a reflection on spiritual connection. Try a meditation in which you set an intention to welcome supportive community while remaining discerning. Create an altar with space for people you value and connections you hope to build. Lavender or jasmine essential oils may be part of a ritual if suitable. Heart-centered practices can help you reflect on old relational defenses. Write a letter to a future friend or community describing the kind of mutual connection you hope to cultivate. Notice people with whom you feel safe, respected, and able to be yourself. Give thanks for the connections already in your life.","soulQuestion":"Am I ready to open my heart to supportive community? Can I release the belief that I must walk alone and allow mutual connection into my life?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '22', 'en', 'Divine Masculine-Feminine Integration', '神聖陽性與陰性整合', '{"keywords":["Balance","Integration","Wholeness","Harmony"],"nameEn":"Divine Masculine-Feminine Integration"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"You carry both receptive and active energies within you, regardless of your biological sex. Yin and yang, moon and sun, receiving and giving, action and surrender are complementary forces that can seek harmony within you. When you integrate these energies, you may feel more whole and less dependent on someone outside you to complete you. This inner union can create a foundation for healthier relationships with others.","currentSituation":"You may be leaning too heavily toward one kind of energy. An excess of active energy may appear as constant action, control, and pushing; an excess of receptive energy may appear as passivity, waiting, or difficulty taking action. This imbalance can affect different areas of life, such as work, relationships, well-being, or creativity. Or you may be healing a painful relationship with gendered expectations because of personal or collective experiences. This card invites you to explore the receptive and active qualities within you and seek a balance that feels authentic.","deeperMeaning":"We all carry a range of qualities that traditions describe as feminine and masculine. Receptive energy can mean listening, intuition, flow, nourishment, and being; active energy can mean giving, logic, structure, protection, and action. Society may overvalue action and suppress receptivity, or express these qualities through restrictive stereotypes. A sacred balance is not about gender roles, but about complementary forces working together. When these qualities are in balance, you may better sense when to act or wait, speak or listen, give or receive. The yin-yang symbol offers one image of two energies moving in harmony.","actionGuidance":"Notice which qualities are most present in your life right now. If you are overextended in action, you might practice receiving, resting, feeling, and trusting a process. If you are waiting indefinitely, you might practice taking action, making a decision, setting boundaries, or expressing your strength. Try a meditation in which the receptive and active parts of you meet and communicate. Reflect on relationships with parents or caregivers if that feels useful, and explore any biases or hurt connected with gender. Create a small altar representing balance if you wish. Practices such as tai chi or yoga can help you explore balance in the body. Bring feeling and action together in daily choices.","energyHealing":"Moonstone may symbolize receptive energy and tiger''s eye active energy in a personal reflection practice. You may explore balance between the Heart and Solar Plexus Chakras, which some traditions associate with connection and personal agency. At the full moon, you could reflect on receptivity; at midday, you could reflect on action and vitality. A ritual imagining two inner figures meeting can be a way to explore integration. Rose and sandalwood essential oils may be paired in a ritual if suitable for you. Create art or a mandala that represents integration. Notice any sense of wholeness, while remembering that these are symbolic practices rather than biological changes.","soulQuestion":"Where am I overusing active or receptive energy? Am I ready to bring these qualities into greater harmony within myself?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '23', 'en', 'Universal Laws', '宇宙法則', '{"keywords":["Laws","Principles","Alignment","Wisdom"],"nameEn":"Universal Laws"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"Many spiritual and esoteric traditions describe the universe as operating according to underlying principles, such as attraction, cause and effect, vibration, and correspondence. These are not human-made rules within those traditions, but ways of describing how existence is understood to work. When you study such principles and bring them into your life, they may help you reflect on your choices and intentions. When your actions conflict with your values or circumstances, you may experience resistance and struggle. This card invites you to explore these ideas and consider how this ancient wisdom might inform modern life.","currentSituation":"You may feel that life is full of resistance, as though you are swimming upstream. Perhaps you have tried manifestation techniques without seeing the results you hoped for, or you are awakening to deeper questions about how life works. You may notice synchronicities or experiences that feel like meaningful coincidences. This card encourages you to remain a student of spiritual principles and turn what you learn into thoughtful, grounded choices.","deeperMeaning":"Universal laws are central to many ancient esoteric schools, from Hermetic philosophy to Buddhist teachings. These traditions discuss principles such as attraction, cause and effect, vibration, polarity, rhythm, gender, and correspondence—often summarized as “as above, so below.” Understanding these ideas can be more than intellectual study; they can change how you reflect on and experience reality. The card invites you to see yourself as participating in your life rather than only being acted upon. You can learn to move with circumstances instead of always fighting them. These are spiritual and philosophical frameworks, not established scientific laws.","actionGuidance":"Study spiritual teachings about universal laws through sources such as The Kybalion, books on the law of attraction, or spiritual interpretations of quantum physics. Read critically and treat these ideas as frameworks for reflection rather than guaranteed mechanisms. Experiment thoughtfully in daily life: notice how gratitude affects your outlook, how habits shape consequences, and how cycles influence your energy. Use intention to guide choices without assuming it controls external events. Share what you learn with others if appropriate. Remember that principles do not reward or punish; they are ways people describe patterns. Rather than complain or resist automatically, learn from what happens and respond wisely.","energyHealing":"Labradorite or amethyst may be used as symbolic objects while reflecting on universal principles. Try an alignment meditation, imagining your values and actions in harmony. Create a learning altar with symbols that remind you of the principles you are studying. Frankincense essential oil may be included in a contemplative ritual if suitable. Music, dance, chanting, or laughter can help you shift your mood and reconnect with your body. Reflect on cycles in your life and how polarity or rhythm appear in your experience. Keep notes on observations, questions, and insights, distinguishing personal meaning from claims about objective laws.","soulQuestion":"Am I working with the principles I believe in, or struggling against them? Am I ready to bring spiritual wisdom into my everyday choices?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '24', 'en', 'Crystalline Lightbody', '水晶光體', '{"keywords":["Light Body","Upgrade","Crystal","Activation"],"nameEn":"Crystalline Lightbody"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"In this spiritual framework, the lightbody is described as shifting from a carbon-based form toward a crystalline structure. The crystalline lightbody is imagined as able to hold higher frequencies of light and support interaction with higher dimensions, faster manifestation, and deeper healing. This is presented as part of an ascension process, a symbolic upgrade of your whole being. Crystals are used as images of light, information, and energy; becoming a walking crystal or living channel of light is a spiritual metaphor, not a literal biological transformation.","currentSituation":"You may be noticing changes in your body or awareness, such as feeling more sensitive to light and sound, or noticing shifts in energy. You may feel drawn to crystals as symbols of qualities you are exploring. You may also notice changes in your sense of time, expanded awareness, or new interests in healing and energy work. This card frames such experiences as recalibration and integration of light codes. It can feel beautiful and intense, so be gentle with yourself. Do not assume physical symptoms are spiritual upgrades; consult a healthcare professional about new, persistent, or concerning symptoms.","deeperMeaning":"The crystalline lightbody is a spiritual idea about human evolution and expanded consciousness. Some traditions describe the physical body as suited to dense, material experience and imagine crystalline structure as a way to hold higher frequencies of light. In that metaphor, when your lightbody becomes more crystalline, you can receive spiritual guidance more clearly, manifest more quickly, and deepen healing for yourself and others. You become a living example of light. This process is not an overnight change, but a gradual spiritual integration. Caring for your physical, emotional, mental, and spiritual well-being can support a balanced approach. These ideas are not established biological science.","actionGuidance":"Work with crystals as symbolic tools for reflection and support. Clear quartz can represent clarity and the crystalline qualities you are exploring. Try a lightbody meditation, imagining light moving gently through your system; treat it as visualization, not a literal DNA upgrade. Drink water and eat nourishing foods that suit your body. Prioritize adequate sleep, since rest supports overall well-being. Spend time in sunlight safely and use sound or calming music if it helps you relax. Be patient with yourself; personal change takes time. Respect your body''s needs and seek medical care for health concerns.","energyHealing":"Clear quartz and other crystals may be used as ritual objects while you reflect on lightbody imagery. You could create a crystal grid and lie nearby for a meditation if comfortable. Imagine rainbow light moving through your body, bringing attention to each part without expecting a physical transformation. A bath with clear quartz nearby may be a soothing ritual; do not ingest crystals or place unsafe materials in bathwater. Visualize your body as bright and whole. DNA-activation language can be used as a spiritual metaphor, not a biological claim. If visiting an energy center or sacred site, follow practical safety and accessibility needs. Ask for spiritual support in whatever way aligns with your beliefs, while staying grounded in daily life.","soulQuestion":"Am I open to personal transformation while respecting my body''s real needs? How can I be a grounded, compassionate channel for the light and values I believe in?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '25', 'en', 'Sacred Service', '神聖服務', '{"keywords":["Service","Devotion","Purpose","Contribution"],"nameEn":"Sacred Service"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"This card invites you to see service not as sacrifice or obligation, but as a joyful expression of your soul. When you are aligned with what feels true, service may flow naturally, without force or struggle. Service does not have to be grand; it can be a smile, a kind word, or the way you show up. Living by your deepest values can itself be a form of service. This card calls you to consider how you might offer your life in service to a purpose larger than yourself, while honoring your own limits and well-being.","currentSituation":"You may feel an inner call to serve in a more meaningful way but be unsure what form it should take. Perhaps you are already serving but feel burned out or disconnected. Or you may resist a call to serve because of fear or a sense of unworthiness. This card reminds you that service is not only something you do; it is also the spirit in which you live. When you act from care and authenticity, everyday actions can be service. Look at how you give: does it come from joy or obligation, and does it honor you or deplete you? Sustainable service can nourish both giver and receiver.","deeperMeaning":"Service is central to many spiritual paths, but it can be misunderstood. Sacred service is not self-sacrifice, giving from superiority, or seeking recognition or spiritual merit. It can come from recognizing our connection with others: caring for another person can also be a way of caring for the wider human community. Service that comes from love is more sustainable when you also care for yourself. A depleted cup cannot keep pouring. True service also respects each person''s journey and freedom; it is not about rescuing or fixing others, but supporting their agency.","actionGuidance":"Explore what forms of service make your heart feel engaged and how your distinctive gifts could contribute. Start small; everyday kindness and a mindful presence can matter. Examine your motives: are you acting from genuine care, or from obligation, guilt, or a wish for approval? Adjust toward an intention that feels honest. Learn to say no; service does not mean saying yes to everyone, but responding to what you can genuinely offer. Care for yourself so your cup is not depleted. Before and after serving, take time to ground and reset. Do not cling to results or gratitude; offer service because it reflects your values, not because you expect repayment. Connect with other service-oriented people for mutual support. Remember, you do not have to earn your worth by doing more.","energyHealing":"Rose quartz or green aventurine may be used as symbolic reminders of an open heart and compassionate service. Try a meditation in which you dedicate your actions to the well-being of yourself and others. Create an altar with objects that represent service and compassion. Frankincense or lotus essential oil may be part of a ritual if suitable. Visualize care flowing from your heart while maintaining clear boundaries. Practice compassion meditation, wishing well-being and freedom for all beings. Before serving, set an intention to act with care and respect. Feel gratitude for the opportunity to contribute, while remembering that you also deserve rest and support. A guiding phrase might be: “I serve from love, not depletion.”","soulQuestion":"Does my service come from love and joy, or from obligation and guilt? Am I ready to offer my life more deeply in service while honoring my own needs?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '26', 'en', 'Starseed Activation', '星際種子啟動', '{"keywords":["Starseed","Origin","Purpose","Remembering"],"nameEn":"Starseed Activation"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"This card draws on the Starseed belief: that a soul may originate in another star system, dimension, or universe and choose to come to Earth with a special purpose. In this framework, activation means remembering a sense of cosmic origin, connecting with a star family, or exploring a feeling of universal belonging. You may feel drawn to the Pleiades, Sirius, Arcturus, Andromeda, or another constellation, each associated in spiritual traditions with different gifts and purposes. Consider what these ideas mean to you without needing to prove a literal origin. This can be a time to reflect on who you are and why you are here.","currentSituation":"You may have long felt out of place in the world or yearned for “home” without knowing where that is. You may feel a deep connection with the night sky and a sense of nostalgia or sadness when looking at the stars. You may feel confused or discouraged by collective human behavior. Perhaps unusual memories, dreams, or experiences with nonhuman beings have arisen, or you sense an important purpose without knowing what it is. This card validates the feelings you are having and invites you to explore them while staying grounded in your life here.","deeperMeaning":"In Starseed spirituality, Starseeds are described as souls from other star systems or dimensions who incarnate on Earth. They are believed to carry high-frequency light codes and help anchor higher-dimensional energy. Starseeds may feel out of place because their idea of “home” comes from a different way of being—one they imagine as more harmonious, conscious, or spiritual. Their purposes vary, but may include embodying light, teaching, healing, modeling new ways of being, or supporting transformation. Activation in this context means consciously exploring these beliefs and choosing how to express a sense of purpose. You do not need to accept a specific cosmic identity to live meaningfully on Earth.","actionGuidance":"Try a meditation under the night sky and ask yourself what feels meaningful about your connection to the stars, your sense of belonging, or your purpose. Stay open to images, feelings, or insights without treating them as proof. You can read about different Starseed traditions and notice what resonates, while holding these ideas lightly. Join a supportive community if that feels helpful. A symbolic activation ritual may include setting an intention to live your values. Do not become so absorbed in a cosmic identity that you neglect daily life; staying grounded can help you act on what matters. Focus on purpose rather than labels, whether that means healing, teaching, art, energy work, or simply being present.","energyHealing":"Moldavite or Libyan desert glass may be used as symbolic objects in Starseed rituals; they are meteorite-related glasses associated with cosmic themes in some spiritual communities. Labradorite can be included in reflection on identity and purpose. Try a guided visualization beneath the night sky, imagining connection with a place in the universe that feels meaningful to you. Before sleep, you may set an intention to remember dreams and write them down upon waking. Visualize light as a symbol of the qualities you want to embody. Visit sacred or energetic places only with practical care and respect for the site. Keep notes on dreams and insights, and remember that imagination and spiritual meaning are not evidence of a literal extraterrestrial origin.","soulQuestion":"Am I ready to explore my sense of cosmic origin and purpose while remaining grounded in this life? Am I willing to be a bridge between the perspectives I value?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '27', 'en', 'Inner Child Healing', '內在孩童療癒', '{"keywords":["Healing","Childhood","Innocence","Wholeness"],"nameEn":"Inner Child Healing"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"Your inner child can hold both old hurt and qualities such as innocence and wonder. Caring for younger parts of yourself may help you feel more whole as an adult, because unhealed wounds can influence present reactions. At the same time, the inner-child idea can be a way to reconnect with joy, creativity, play, and curiosity. This card invites you to imagine meeting a younger version of yourself and offering the love, recognition, and protection they may have needed. As you care for that part, energy that has been tied up in the past may become available to you now.","currentSituation":"You may be having an emotional reaction that feels larger than the current situation, which could mean an older wound has been touched. You may feel capable and adult in some areas of life and young or vulnerable in others. Perhaps you feel disconnected from joy, play, or spontaneity, and life feels heavy or serious. Or you may find yourself avoiding adult responsibilities. This card invites you to explore inner-child work with care. Current difficulties may connect with needs that were unmet in childhood, but you are the adult now and can seek resources and support to tend to them.","deeperMeaning":"The inner-child idea describes younger parts of ourselves, especially those shaped by difficult or emotionally significant experiences. Those parts can feel frozen in time and may react when present situations resemble past ones. This can help explain why some reactions feel stronger than expected: a younger part may be responding alongside your adult self. Inner-child work can involve revisiting those memories with compassion and offering the care, protection, reassurance, or love that was missing. This may help you integrate rather than reject those parts. The inner child can also represent innocence, wonder, creativity, and play. Healing can mean tending to old hurts and restoring these valuable qualities.","actionGuidance":"Try a gentle inner-child meditation: imagine meeting a younger version of yourself and ask what they need, then offer comfort and reassurance. Look at childhood photos if that feels supportive and practice compassion for the child you were. You might write a letter to your inner child, then write a response from that younger perspective. Make time for playful or creative activities without focusing on a product or goal: drawing, dancing, or swinging at a park. Notice your triggers and ask how old you feel in that moment. Consider professional support from a qualified therapist, especially if trauma comes up. Set boundaries with people or situations that feel unsafe. Practice reparenting yourself by offering care and support now.","energyHealing":"Rose quartz may serve as a symbolic reminder of unconditional love and gentleness. Mangano calcite is sometimes associated with inner-child reflection. Create a safe, comfortable space for a ritual with a childhood object, toy, or photograph. A lullaby or gentle sound practice may help you feel soothed. Visualize holding and comforting a younger version of yourself, saying words you needed to hear. Visit an important childhood place only if it feels safe and supportive. Create new joyful memories by offering yourself experiences you longed for. A Heart Chakra meditation may help you reflect on compassion. Let the adult and younger parts of yourself meet with care and respect.","soulQuestion":"Am I ready to meet and care for childhood wounds with compassion? Can I become a loving, supportive adult for the younger parts of myself?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '28', 'en', 'Cosmic Mother', '宇宙母親', '{"keywords":["Mothering","Nourishment","Creation","Protection"],"nameEn":"Cosmic Mother"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"The Cosmic Mother represents the creative and nurturing principle of the universe, expressed through images such as the Earth Goddess, the Holy Mother, and the Divine Feminine. She symbolizes unconditional love, compassion, and welcome. Every soul is imagined as her child, never judged or abandoned and always welcome home. This card brings a mothering energy of care, whatever your relationship with your biological mother. It invites you to embody nurturing energy by caring for yourself and others, creating beauty and life, and protecting what is vulnerable.","currentSituation":"You may need mothering care and support, and feel tired, lonely, or helpless. You may be healing your relationship with your mother or another mothering figure. You may also feel called to express nurturing energy more fully through caring, nourishing, creating, or protecting, regardless of your gender or whether you have children. Perhaps you need to let yourself be cared for and receive nourishment, which can be difficult if you are used to caring for everyone else. This card reminds you that you are not alone and invites you to seek comfort and support.","deeperMeaning":"The mothering principle is one way spiritual traditions describe a fundamental creative force, complementary to the fathering principle. If the father archetype is associated with structure, order, and protection, the mother archetype is associated with flow, nourishment, and life. A mother''s love is often imagined as unconditional, offered because you exist rather than because of achievement. The Cosmic Mother appears in many forms and names—Gaia, Mary, Guanyin, Isis, or Pachamama—across different traditions. She can represent both tenderness and fierce protection, like a mother lion guarding her cubs. This archetype teaches receiving, surrender, and trust in life''s processes. You can embody its qualities by connecting with nature, nourishing yourself and others, creating beauty, and protecting what is vulnerable.","actionGuidance":"Connect with a sacred mother figure from a tradition that resonates with you, such as Mary, Guanyin, or Mother Earth. You may build a daily reflective practice and ask what care or guidance you need. If your relationship with your biological mother is difficult, consider support for healing while recognizing that a spiritual mother archetype is different from a human relationship. Nourish yourself as a loving caregiver would: with healthy food, rest, comfort, and encouragement. Spend time on the Earth and notice the support nature offers. Create something that brings beauty or life, whether a plant, artwork, meal, community, love, or peace. Protect what is vulnerable and speak for those without a voice. If you are a mother, honor that role while also caring for yourself. If you wish to become a mother, remember that mothering can take many forms, not only biological ones. Practice unconditional love, compassion, nourishment, protection, and creativity.","energyHealing":"Moonstone may be used as a symbolic object in reflection on the Cosmic Mother and the Divine Feminine. Rose quartz can represent unconditional love. Try a womb-centered meditation as a symbol of creative space, whether or not you have a physical womb. Imagine the Cosmic Mother holding and comforting you, and notice what feelings arise. A full moon can be a symbolic time for a mothering ritual. Rose or jasmine essential oil may be included if suitable. Create an altar with objects that represent nourishment and creation, such as seeds, flowers, water, or soil. In a grounding meditation, imagine the Earth supporting you. Practice saying caring words to yourself, such as “I am enough, I am loved, and I deserve care.” Visualize a connection of light as a symbol of ongoing support.","soulQuestion":"Am I allowing myself to receive care and nourishment? Am I ready to embody nurturing, protective, and creative energy in my life?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '29', 'en', 'Soul Contract Rewrite', '靈魂契約重寫', '{"keywords":["Contract","Freedom","Choice","Rewrite"],"nameEn":"Soul Contract Rewrite"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"In some spiritual traditions, the soul is believed to form agreements with other souls, a soul family, or the universe before incarnation. These agreements are understood as opportunities for learning and growth. Some may feel complete or no longer aligned with your well-being; others may have been formed from fear or obligation. This card invites you to reconsider spiritual agreements that no longer fit and consciously choose new intentions that support your present path. You can take ownership of your choices without treating these spiritual ideas as binding facts.","currentSituation":"You may feel caught in patterns, relationships, or situations, as though an invisible force keeps repeating an experience. You may feel tied to someone or something by a karmic connection that is difficult to loosen. You may also be repeating family or ancestral patterns without realizing it. Or perhaps you are becoming aware that you have more choice and agency than you once believed, and no longer want old agreements to limit you. This card invites you to explore what may be keeping a pattern in place and consider what you can change now.","deeperMeaning":"Soul contracts are spiritual agreements described in some traditions as being formed between souls, often before incarnation. For example, a person may interpret a difficult relationship as a mutual lesson. Family contracts may be used to understand repeated roles or patterns, while karmic contracts may be used to make sense of cause and effect across lifetimes. These are spiritual frameworks, not verifiable legal agreements or established facts. They should not be used to excuse harm, blame someone for suffering, or avoid present responsibilities. As you grow, beliefs that once felt meaningful can be reconsidered. Rewriting a soul contract can symbolize choosing intentions that better reflect who you are now.","actionGuidance":"Notice recurring patterns, difficult relationships, or limiting beliefs and reflect on what you want to change. In meditation or journaling, ask what agreement you may be carrying, while staying open to ordinary explanations and choices in the present. Write down a belief you are ready to release, such as “I must suffer in order to grow” or “I must sacrifice myself to save others.” If you wish, create a symbolic ritual by stating your intention and safely disposing of the paper. Write a new intention, such as choosing growth through joy or relationships built on mutual care. You can do this without claiming that a supernatural contract is objectively real. Consider grounded, qualified support when working through difficult patterns.","energyHealing":"Obsidian or smoky quartz may be used as symbolic objects in a personal reflection ritual. You might explore an Akashic-records meditation as part of your spiritual beliefs, while treating what arises as imagination or reflection rather than verified history. Sage or palo santo can mark a transition if suitable. State what you are choosing to release and what values you want to follow now. Visualize setting down an old agreement and making room for a new intention. A new moon can be a symbolic time for a fresh start. Ground yourself afterward and notice what choices are available in your present life. Give thanks for what you have learned, then move forward freely.","soulQuestion":"Am I ready to release beliefs or agreements that no longer serve me? Am I willing to create new intentions from a place of freedom and clarity?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '30', 'en', 'Divine Timing', '神聖時機', '{"keywords":["Timing","Patience","Trust","Perfection"],"nameEn":"Divine Timing"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"This card invites you to consider that events may unfold in their own timing. Your wishes may not be rejected simply because they have not happened yet; some things need time to mature, like fruit that cannot be hurried. The card asks you to trust the process and release the demand to control every detail. When circumstances are ready, things may come together with less force. Your part is to prepare, stay aligned with your values, and remain open.","currentSituation":"You may feel impatient, frustrated, or worried because something you hoped for has not yet happened. You may wonder whether your wish will come true or whether you are on the right path. Life may feel stalled. This card offers the spiritual perspective that unseen preparation or alignment may be happening. A delay does not necessarily mean rejection; it may be a chance to prepare or grow. At the same time, look honestly at what is within your control and what practical steps remain available to you.","deeperMeaning":"The idea of divine timing asks you to consider that life may be wider than your immediate perspective. You may see events in linear time and want immediate results, while spiritual traditions may frame them as part of a broader unfolding. A goal may involve other people, events, or learning that takes time to coordinate. Forcing something before circumstances are ready may lead to an incomplete or misaligned result. Imagine planting a seed: you water it, give it sunlight, and allow it time to grow rather than digging it up each day. Likewise, you can nurture a wish while staying open about when and how it may take shape.","actionGuidance":"Practice patience and trust when impatience arises. Focus on what you can influence—your attitude, actions, and preparation—and release what you cannot control, such as exact timing. Use the waiting period to learn, grow, address obstacles, and prepare for opportunities. Stay connected to your hopes without becoming attached to exactly when they must happen. Notice small steps and signs of progress, but do not treat coincidences as guarantees. Spend time in nature and observe its seasons and cycles. Practice being present rather than living only in an anticipated future. Remember past occasions when timing worked out differently than expected, while keeping practical judgment in view.","energyHealing":"Celestite may be used as a symbolic object in a patience or guidance ritual. Red jasper can represent grounding while you wait. Try a surrender meditation in which you imagine offering a wish to the universe and holding it with care rather than control. Lavender or cedar essential oils may be part of a calming ritual if suitable. Create a small altar with symbols of timing, such as a clock, seed, or butterfly. Reflect on cycles and timing through the moon or seasons. Place a hand over your heart and breathe when you feel impatient. An affirmation such as “I can be patient while I take the steps available to me” may help you stay grounded.","soulQuestion":"Can I trust the unfolding of life even when I do not understand a delay? Am I willing to release some control over timing while continuing to prepare and act?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '31', 'en', 'Quantum Leap', '量子飛躍', '{"keywords":["Leap","Transformation","Breakthrough","Quantum"],"nameEn":"Quantum Leap"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"In spiritual language, a quantum leap describes a sudden, nonlinear shift into a different level of experience rather than gradual growth. Like an electron changing orbit in a scientific model, you may be approaching a major change in awareness or life experience. It could feel like a sudden insight, a significant change in circumstances, the discovery of a new ability, or a shift in perspective. This card suggests preparing for change while remembering that “quantum leap” is being used here as a spiritual metaphor, not a prediction or scientific explanation.","currentSituation":"You may sense that a major change is approaching, like the stillness before a storm. You may already be noticing unusual changes in how you experience reality, such as more coincidences, a different sense of time, or vivid dreams. Or you may feel stuck in an old way of living and long for a breakthrough without knowing how it will happen. This card suggests that forcing or struggling may not help. You can loosen your attachment to an old identity, stay open to change, and take grounded steps into new possibilities.","deeperMeaning":"Quantum physics is sometimes used in spiritual writing as a metaphor for possibility, but its scientific findings do not establish claims about manifestation or spiritual timelines. In this card''s spiritual framework, a “quantum leap” means a sudden change in awareness that lets you see new possibilities. It may come through releasing an old identity, belief, or story and choosing to align with a different way of living. Such a shift can feel dramatic, but it can also be approached through practical decisions and gradual integration. Examples include moving from a victim mindset toward greater agency, from scarcity toward gratitude, or from fear toward care. The key is being willing to release what no longer fits while taking responsibility for how you live now.","actionGuidance":"Notice where you are ready for a significant change, whether in awareness, relationships, work, health habits, or spirituality. Clarify the direction you hope to move in without becoming rigid about exactly how it must happen. Try perspective-shifting exercises and imagine how you would approach the situation from the life you want to build. Release attachments that keep you in an old pattern when doing so is safe and appropriate. Stay open to possibilities while remaining grounded in practical reality. If fear or doubt appears, acknowledge it and choose a small, thoughtful next step. Prepare for change by reviewing your support, responsibilities, and resources.","energyHealing":"Moldavite may be used as a symbolic object for reflecting on rapid change, and clear quartz as a focus for intentions. Try a visualization in which you consider several possible futures and choose actions aligned with your values; this is an imaginative practice, not a way to control quantum physics. DNA-activation language can be used symbolically, not as a literal biological process. You might create a transition ritual by physically moving from one space to another while naming what you are releasing and what you are welcoming. Eucalyptus or sandalwood essential oils may be part of a ritual if suitable. Use objects, images, or words as reminders of the direction you want to take. Major changes still benefit from planning and support.","soulQuestion":"Am I ready to release what no longer fits and take a grounded step toward a new possibility? Can I remain open without needing certainty about the outcome?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '32', 'en', 'Sacred Rebellion', '神聖叛逆', '{"keywords":["Rebellion","Breakthrough","Freedom","Authenticity"],"nameEn":"Sacred Rebellion"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"Some forms of rebellion come not from anger or opposition, but from deep loyalty to what feels true. When society, culture, or group expectations try to shape you into someone you are not, Sacred Rebellion can mean having the courage to say no. This is not rebellion for its own sake; it is refusing what feels false in order to live more truthfully. This card invites you to question norms that no longer serve you, challenge limiting rules, and express yourself even when that is not popular. Your rebellion can serve love and truth, creating new possibilities rather than simply destroying.","currentSituation":"You may feel stifled by social expectations, family traditions, or collective beliefs. A voice within you may be saying, “This is not right,” or “There must be another way.” You may fear expressing your beliefs, choices, or way of living because you worry about judgment or rejection. Or you may already have rebelled in some way and now feel guilty or unsure whether it was right. This card affirms your right to question what does not fit, and invites you to act with love and clarity rather than anger or reactivity.","deeperMeaning":"Many important changes in history have involved people who questioned the status quo, challenged authority, or lived according to a different vision. This card evokes figures such as Jesus, Buddha, prophets, mystics, and reformers as examples of people who followed a higher truth as they understood it. Sacred Rebellion differs from reactive opposition: it stands for something rather than only against something. It can come from love and vision instead of fear and anger. It respects that others have their own paths while remaining committed to yours. In times of change, people who live a new possibility can help others imagine it too. This may not be easy, but it can be an authentic path.","actionGuidance":"Notice where you may be following a rule or expectation that does not align with your values. Begin with clarity rather than anger: understand why you are choosing a different path. Let your core values guide your choices. Prepare for some people to misunderstand or disagree; not everyone will celebrate your authenticity. Seek out people who value honesty and support one another. Your life can demonstrate another possibility more powerfully than argument alone. Set boundaries with people or situations that try to control you. Remember what you stand for—truth, freedom, love, or justice—and stay open-hearted even while holding your position. Respect others'' paths as you follow your own.","energyHealing":"Red jasper may be used as a symbolic object for grounding and courage, and lapis lazuli as a reminder to speak truthfully. A liberation ritual might involve safely breaking or discarding an object that represents a limiting rule. Visualize yourself as a sacred warrior standing for truth and love, not violence. Obsidian may be included as a personal symbol of boundaries. Try a meditation that reconnects you with your untamed, authentic nature. Cedar or juniper essential oils may be part of a ritual if suitable. You could write a personal declaration such as “I choose authenticity over approval and freedom over comfort.” Safely burn a written intention if that is meaningful to you. Let your rebellion be guided by love for what is true, including care for yourself and others.","soulQuestion":"Am I ready to stand for what feels true even when it is unpopular? Can I help make room for a new way of living with courage and care?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '33', 'en', 'Past Life Wisdom', '前世智慧', '{"keywords":["Past Lives","Karma","Wisdom","Integration"],"nameEn":"Past Life Wisdom"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"Many spiritual traditions describe the soul as having lived through many lifetimes, each offering opportunities for learning, experience, and growth. In this belief system, past-life memories, wounds, and gifts may influence the present through unresolved patterns, talents, fears, or strong connections. This card invites you to reflect on what wisdom you can draw from these ideas, tend to wounds that feel unresolved, and integrate gifts you value. The point is not to become absorbed in the past, but to live with greater understanding now.","currentSituation":"You may feel a strong attraction or aversion to a particular time, place, or culture that is difficult to explain through your current experience. You may have a natural talent or knowledge you do not remember learning. Some relationships may feel deeply familiar, as though you have known the person before. Or you may have unexplained fears, physical symptoms, or repeated patterns that make you curious about past-life explanations. This card invites exploration for reflection and healing while keeping present-day causes and support in view.","deeperMeaning":"Reincarnation is taught in many spiritual traditions, but past lives are not established historical facts. These teachings describe each lifetime as an opportunity to learn, develop qualities, and work through karma. Souls may be imagined as meeting repeatedly in different roles—parent, child, partner, friend, or adversary—to teach one another. Some traditions understand karma as a chance for learning and growth, not punishment. Talents and wisdom from past lives are also believed to remain in the soul''s memory. Past-life ideas can be used as reflective frameworks for understanding fears or relationship patterns, but they should not replace present-day explanations or care. Exploring them may help you consider your experience with more insight and compassion.","actionGuidance":"If you feel drawn to past-life exploration, you may try a gentle meditation or consult a qualified practitioner. Hold images and impressions lightly; they are not proof of historical events. Notice recurring relationship dynamics, fears, physical symptoms, or natural talents and consider several possible explanations. Keep a dream journal and explore any attraction to particular eras, cultures, or places through historical learning as well as spiritual reflection. If a memory or image of trauma arises, pause and seek qualified support rather than trying to process it alone. You may use forgiveness and release practices without assuming a karmic cause. Let your present life remain the focus.","energyHealing":"Amethyst or labradorite may be used as symbolic objects for reflection on memory and personal history. An Akashic-records meditation may be meaningful within your spiritual beliefs; treat any impressions as reflection rather than verified records. Visualize golden light as a symbol of compassion across time. Myrrh essential oil may be included in a personal ritual if suitable. If you revisit an imagined past-life scene, bring your present-day perspective and offer yourself care. Let go of any interpretation that feels frightening or disempowering. A ritual with a candle can honor the experiences that shaped you, while remembering you are more than any story about a past life.","soulQuestion":"Am I ready to explore old stories with curiosity while staying grounded in the present? Can I integrate wisdom without letting past-life beliefs define me?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '37', 'en', 'Earth Guardian', '地球守護者', '{"keywords":["Earth","Protection","Healing","Responsibility"],"nameEn":"Earth Guardian"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"This card invites you to feel your relationship with the Earth as a home deserving of care, rather than merely a backdrop or a source of resources. In some spiritual traditions, Earth is understood as a conscious being who nourishes life. As a lightworker, you may feel a special responsibility or connection to the planet. The card calls you to be an Earth Guardian by caring for nature, supporting healing, and bringing light into the world around you. This is not a burden but a meaningful form of service. Caring for the Earth can also help you feel more connected to yourself and the natural world.","currentSituation":"You may feel deep sadness or anger about environmental problems, as though the Earth''s pain resonates within you. Perhaps you feel called to take part in conservation or ecological work. Or you may already be caring for the planet in some way, and this card recognizes that service. You may want to connect more deeply with nature, feel grounded, or tend to your relationship with the Earth. It reminds you that humans are part of nature, not its owners, and that human well-being is connected to the planet''s well-being.","deeperMeaning":"Many Indigenous cultures have long taught that humans are part of the Earth, not separate from it, and that the planet is more than a resource for human use. When ecosystems suffer, people and other living beings are affected too. The Earth faces serious pressures, including climate change, species loss, deforestation, and pollution. This card frames you as a guardian with several possible roles: in spiritual practice, offering care and attention; in practical life, taking actions to protect the environment, however small; in community, teaching and modeling ways to live in greater harmony with nature; and spiritually, honoring Earth as sacred. Every action can matter, even if it seems small.","actionGuidance":"Spend regular time in nature to connect and listen, not only to relax. Walk barefoot if safe and comfortable, or simply notice the ground beneath you. In meditation, imagine sending care to the Earth while staying grounded yourself. Make practical environmental choices where possible: consume less, recycle, support ecological businesses, clean a beach or forest, or plant a tree or garden. Learn about environmental issues and solutions, use your voice, and participate in community efforts or policy work if that suits you. Reconnect with the idea that you are part of nature. Appreciate the Earth''s beauty and abundance, support Indigenous communities and knowledge, and honor seasonal cycles. You do not have to save the planet alone; seek ways to cooperate with others and with nature.","energyHealing":"Green aventurine, emerald, or moss agate may be used as symbolic objects in a grounding practice. Imagine roots extending from your body into the Earth, exchanging light and steadiness. In a visualization, picture a network of care surrounding the planet and extending to places that need restoration. Cedar or pine essential oils may be part of a nature-focused ritual if suitable. Work with the elements—earth, water, fire, and air—as reminders of the living systems that support life. Create an altar with stones, leaves, seeds, or water as a focus for gratitude. Celebrate seasonal changes and imagine a healthy planet where life can flourish. Pair visualization with practical care for the environment.","soulQuestion":"Am I living in a way that respects my relationship with the Earth? How can I care for and protect the planet in my everyday life?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '38', 'en', 'Spiritual Alchemy', '靈性煉金術', '{"keywords":["Transformation","Alchemy","Metamorphosis","Mastery"],"nameEn":"Spiritual Alchemy"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"Alchemy is traditionally described as the art of turning lead into gold, while spiritual alchemy uses that image for inner transformation: pain becoming wisdom, trauma becoming a source of insight, and darkness making room for light. This is not about suppressing or avoiding difficult feelings, but meeting them consciously. This card suggests that you may be developing the ability to work with what life gives you, however difficult, and transform it into growth, wisdom, compassion, strength, or beauty. You are the alchemist of your life, and your experiences are the material you work with.","currentSituation":"You may be going through or recovering from a difficult experience—pain, challenge, loss, or a dark period. Unlike in the past, you may now be beginning to ask what you can learn from it rather than only “Why me?” You may be developing the ability to draw wisdom from experiences, even painful ones. Or perhaps you have already transformed some past pain and are using what you learned to support others. This card recognizes your path of transformation and invites you to continue it at a pace that feels manageable.","deeperMeaning":"Some alchemical traditions describe a process in stages: nigredo, or darkening and breaking down an old form; albedo, or purification; and rubedo, or renewal in a new form. This can be an image for a hero''s journey, death and rebirth, or a phoenix rising from ashes. Spiritual alchemy is about conscious participation rather than passively enduring life. When challenges arise, you might ask what the experience is teaching you, what you are ready to release, and who you are becoming. This is not toxic positivity or denying pain; it is finding meaning and growth while acknowledging that pain is real. The deepest wounds can sometimes lead to deep wisdom, and difficult nights can be followed by light. Mastery here means learning how to work with experience, not becoming invulnerable.","actionGuidance":"Look back on experiences you have transformed and recognize the wisdom, strength, or compassion you gained. Celebrate the work you have done. For a current challenge, ask reflective questions: what is this teaching me, what may I need to release, what is it asking me to become, and how can I care for myself through it? Keep an alchemy journal of your process and insights. Shadow work may help you meet difficult parts of yourself consciously; consider qualified support if it feels overwhelming. Look for meaning without forcing yourself to find a positive lesson in every painful event. You can share your story to support others when you are ready. Study alchemical symbols or philosophy as a map for reflection. Do not seek hardship; work with it carefully when it comes.","energyHealing":"Amethyst may be used as a symbolic focus for transformation, and obsidian as a grounding object while reflecting on shadow material. Try a meditation in which you imagine placing an experience in an alchemical vessel and allowing it to change into wisdom over time. A violet-flame visualization can symbolize releasing old patterns. Create an altar with symbols of transformation, such as a butterfly, phoenix, gold, or a vessel. Myrrh or frankincense essential oils may be used in a reflective ritual if suitable. A fire ritual can symbolize releasing what you are ready to let go of; follow fire safety and do not burn unsafe materials. Visualize a phoenix as an image of renewal. Keep notes on what you are learning and acknowledge each completed stage of change.","soulQuestion":"Am I ready to work consciously with my experiences and transform what I can into wisdom? Can I find light in darkness without denying the pain?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '39', 'en', 'Rainbow Bridge', '彩虹橋', '{"keywords":["Connection","Bridge","Integration","Oneness"],"nameEn":"Rainbow Bridge"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"The Rainbow Bridge symbolizes a connection between heaven and earth, spirituality and material life, or the sacred and the human. In many traditions, a rainbow represents promise, hope, and connection. This card invites you to see yourself as a living bridge: bringing spiritual insight into everyday life and embodying a sense of unity. You do not have to choose between spirituality and material life; you can explore how both belong in a whole and colorful life.","currentSituation":"You may feel split between spiritual practice and material life: uplifted during meditation but struggling when you return to daily responsibilities. Or you may lean too far in one direction—so focused on spirituality that practical needs are neglected, or so focused on material concerns that you long for spiritual connection. You may be trying to bring spiritual values into work, relationships, and daily tasks. This card reminds you that these parts of life do not have to be opposites. You can become an example of integrating them in a way that works for you.","deeperMeaning":"Some spiritual paths teach transcendence or escape from the material world, but this card offers a different image: not leaving Earth, but bringing sacred meaning into everyday life. Integration can mean balancing spiritual experiences with daily responsibilities, meditation with action, and heaven with earth. The rainbow is a useful symbol because it contains many colors without excluding any of them. In the same way, you can hold different aspects of yourself—spiritual and practical, sacred and human, light and shadow. When you integrate rather than divide them, you may express a fuller spectrum of who you are. A master need not live on a mountaintop; wisdom can also be practiced among people, without losing connection to what matters.","actionGuidance":"Notice where you feel split: spirituality and material life, work and reflection, meditation and action. Explore ways to integrate them rather than choosing one side. Bring mindfulness into ordinary tasks, such as washing dishes attentively or treating work as a chance to practice your values. Let your spirituality be practical and grounded in daily life. Balance time and energy between spiritual practice and worldly responsibilities. Live your values at work and in relationships, not only on a meditation cushion. Share your gifts in the world in sustainable ways, without guilt about earning a living. Honor both your humanity and your spirituality. Practice being fully present in whatever you do, so the sacred can meet the everyday. Show that integrated living is possible through your own example.","energyHealing":"Rainbow obsidian, aura quartz, or any naturally iridescent crystal may serve as symbolic reminders of integration. Try a rainbow meditation, imagining colored light moving down from the sky through you and into the Earth, then rising back through you. Visualize the colors of the chakras as an image of your whole spectrum. Create an altar with objects in seven colors to represent integration. When you see a rainbow after rain, use it as a reminder of connection between earth and sky. Try a grounding exercise with one hand reaching upward and the other resting toward the ground, noticing your body as the meeting place. Use a blend of scents or sounds that feels balanced to you. Celebrate both your practical life and your spiritual values without needing to choose between them.","soulQuestion":"Am I ready to be a bridge between my spiritual values and everyday life? Can I integrate both into a whole, grounded way of living?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '40', 'en', 'New Earth Anchoring', '新地球錨定', '{"keywords":["New Earth","Grounding","Vision","Creation"],"nameEn":"New Earth Anchoring"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"The New Earth need not be a place in the future; it can be a vision of consciousness and community taking shape now. It represents a way of living guided by love, connection, cooperation, abundance, and peace. In contrast, familiar systems shaped by fear, separation, competition, or scarcity may feel as if they are breaking down. This card suggests that a more humane world begins wherever people choose to live by different values. Through your awareness, choices, actions, and presence, you can help bring that vision into everyday life. You are invited to be one of its builders, without needing to carry the whole mission alone.","currentSituation":"You may feel out of alignment with old systems, values, or ways of operating. You carry a vision of a different world, even if you cannot fully describe it yet. Perhaps you are already living parts of that vision by building loving relationships, cooperative communities, conscious businesses, or more compassionate approaches to healing and education. Or you long to live this way more fully but are unsure where to begin. This card invites you to take an intentional role in shaping the world around you, choosing the values you want to embody in each moment.","deeperMeaning":"The idea of an old Earth and a New Earth existing at once can be read as a metaphor for different ways of seeing and organizing life, not as two physical planets. One outlook emphasizes separation, fear, competition, control, scarcity, and human dominance over nature. Another emphasizes connection, love, cooperation, freedom, enoughness, shared power, and humanity as part of nature. Change does not have to arrive on a predicted date; it happens through choices people make together. When you choose connection over separation, generosity over hoarding, or authenticity over pretense, you help anchor the world you hope to see. You can contribute to new ways of living before institutions change, while recognizing that collective transformation takes cooperation and time.","actionGuidance":"Clarify your vision: what values, relationships, and systems would you like to see in the world? Write them down, then look for ways to practice them now rather than waiting for circumstances to change. Create small pockets of the world you want in your home, relationships, work, and community. At a decision point, ask which choice better reflects your values and choose accordingly when you can. Join or create a community project; collective work can reach further than individual effort. Support businesses, artists, teachers, and practitioners whose work aligns with your vision. Release habits or beliefs that no longer serve you, at a realistic pace. Meditation and ritual can help you hold a hopeful vision, while practical action gives it form. Keep hope without mistaking upheaval for proof of a guaranteed transformation.","energyHealing":"Moldavite, selenite, or labradorite may be used as symbolic objects while reflecting on the world you hope to help create. Try a New Earth meditation: picture the details of a world guided by your values and notice how you might live differently in it. Create an altar with images or objects that represent your vision. Myrrh or palo santo may be included in a ritual if suitable and used with respect for their cultural context. A visualization of a web of light can symbolize connection among people working toward a kinder world. You might mark equinoxes or solstices with a ritual to renew your intentions. Connect with others who share your hopes. Imagine a healthy, peaceful, flourishing Earth, then identify one grounded action that can support that vision. Treat this as inspiration, not a promise that visualization alone changes material conditions.","soulQuestion":"Am I ready to help build the world I long for through my choices? Will I choose connection, care, and cooperation in the moments available to me?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '41', 'en', 'Sacred Solitude', '神聖孤獨', '{"keywords":["Solitude","Inner Life","Renewal","Depth"],"nameEn":"Sacred Solitude"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"Sacred solitude is not the same as loneliness; it is time spent in close relationship with your inner life. It can mean intentionally stepping back from the noise of the outer world to enter a quieter space for reflection. Many spiritual teachers are remembered for periods of solitude, such as Jesus in the desert, the Buddha beneath the Bodhi tree, or prophets in caves. In quiet, distractions may ease and new truths may become easier to hear. Away from familiar roles and expectations, you can meet yourself more honestly. This card invites or affirms a period of solitude for reflection and reconnection, not because something is wrong with you, but because stillness may be useful now.","currentSituation":"You may have entered a period of solitude by choice or circumstance, whether physically alone or more withdrawn emotionally. Friends may have moved away, a relationship may have ended, or your desire to socialize may have changed. Perhaps you want more time alone than before. Or you may resist solitude because you feel lonely or abandoned. This card offers a different way to view time alone: it can create room for rest, reflection, and change. In a busy life, it may be difficult to hear your own thoughts. Still, solitude is not a punishment, and it does not require you to refuse connection or support.","deeperMeaning":"Loneliness is often a painful sense of disconnection and a longing for contact; chosen solitude can be a nourishing time alone, with room for a closer relationship to yourself or your spiritual beliefs. Modern life can fill every moment with communication, entertainment, and stimulation, while many spiritual traditions recognize the value of quiet. Solitude can be a cocoon in which you reflect, tend to feelings, explore your sense of purpose, and integrate experience. It may help you notice who you are beyond your roles and expectations. Your time alone need not transform you or produce a revelation to be worthwhile. After a period of solitude, you may return to relationships with greater clarity, but there is no need to rush or to follow a prescribed timeline. If solitude becomes distressing or isolating, reaching out is a valid and caring choice.","actionGuidance":"If you feel drawn to time alone, make gentle room for it: reduce optional commitments, limit social media, or protect an uninterrupted hour. Establish a simple practice such as meditation, journaling, a walk in nature, or creative expression. Use quiet for reflection, healing, or shadow work only as far as feels manageable. Solitude is not always comfortable, and difficult feelings may arise; consider qualified support if they feel overwhelming. Keep a record of thoughts, dreams, emotions, or changes you notice. If you feel lonely, ask what kind of connection you need and consider reaching out to someone you trust. Practice enjoying your own company without requiring yourself to be endlessly self-sufficient. Trust that you can reconnect with others when you are ready, while honoring your need for both solitude and support.","energyHealing":"Amethyst or selenite may be used as symbolic objects for reflection on solitude and spiritual connection. Try sitting quietly for a few minutes, without needing to do anything, and notice your inner experience. Create a personal space for reflection in a corner of a room or outdoors, somewhere that feels safe and private. Lavender or sandalwood scents may be part of a calming ritual if suitable. Instead of sensory deprivation, choose a comfortable, low-stimulation setting and remain free to stop whenever you wish. You might write to yourself with kindness or ask what you need today. A meditation on meeting your inner self can support reflection; avoid ungrounded regression practices, especially if they bring up distress. Give yourself permission to end the practice and reconnect with someone supportive. Let solitude have a natural duration rather than treating it as a test you must complete.","soulQuestion":"Can I welcome some quiet as a gift without confusing solitude with isolation? What would help me feel both connected to myself and supported by others?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '42', 'en', 'Karma Completion', '業力完成', '{"keywords":["Karma","Completion","Release","Freedom"],"nameEn":"Karma Completion"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"In many spiritual traditions, karma is understood not as punishment but as a framework for learning from the consequences of actions. Repeated patterns may offer opportunities to reflect, make different choices, and grow. This card invites you to notice whether a familiar cycle is beginning to change and to acknowledge the work you have done. Completion may involve forgiveness, release, closure, or acceptance, but it does not require you to reconcile with someone who harmed you or to ignore practical consequences. Let this be a reflection on growth and freedom, rather than a guarantee that every difficulty has ended.","currentSituation":"You may notice that a long-standing pattern is no longer repeating: perhaps you no longer seek the same kinds of painful relationships, react in familiar ways, or struggle with an issue as you once did. Or an old pattern may be surfacing intensely, giving you a chance to respond differently. You may feel called to address something unresolved by offering forgiveness, releasing an attachment, or finding closure. This card recognizes the effort you have made and encourages you to take any remaining steps that feel safe and appropriate, without assuming that every recurring problem is karmic in origin.","deeperMeaning":"Karma is understood in different ways across religious and spiritual traditions, including as cause and effect, ethical consequence, or a cycle of learning across lifetimes. Some people also use the word to describe family or collective patterns. These beliefs are not a single universal doctrine, and they do not establish that suffering is deserved or that events are fated. In a reflective reading, a recurring pattern may invite awareness, learning, healing, and a different response. Signs of change might include noticing a trigger before reacting, choosing differently, setting boundaries, or feeling less controlled by an old story. This kind of completion is not passive or guaranteed: it can involve recognizing patterns, addressing wounds, making amends where appropriate, and releasing what you can. You can be grateful for what you learned without being grateful for harm.","actionGuidance":"Notice patterns that have changed and acknowledge your progress. If a cycle still troubles you, ask what you have learned and what choice might interrupt it. Practice responding from your present awareness rather than an automatic old reaction. Consider forgiveness if it is meaningful to you, including self-forgiveness, but do not force it or equate it with excusing harm. You can release resentment, guilt, or regret gradually and still maintain boundaries. Seek closure through a conversation, an unsent letter, or a personal ritual if that feels useful and safe. You do not need to contact someone to find closure. If a pattern is affecting your well-being, practical help from a trusted person or qualified professional may be more useful than a spiritual explanation. Let gratitude for your learning coexist with honest acknowledgment of pain, and make room to enjoy the freedom you have gained.","energyHealing":"Black tourmaline, obsidian, or smoky quartz may serve as symbolic grounding objects while reflecting on a pattern you are ready to release. Try a forgiveness meditation focused on your own well-being, without requiring reconciliation or contact. Visualize a violet flame as an image of change and release. If you make a ritual of writing down a pattern, dispose of the paper safely; there is no need to burn it or release anything into waterways. A new moon can be a personal symbol of endings and beginnings. You might journal about what you learned and what you choose now. Let visualization and ritual support reflection rather than substitute for practical steps, boundaries, or care. Mark the changes you have made and celebrate them without declaring that every cycle is permanently closed.","soulQuestion":"What pattern am I ready to meet with greater awareness and a different choice? Can I release what is no longer mine to carry while keeping the boundaries and support I need?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('lightworker', '43', 'en', 'Infinite Possibilities', '無限可能', '{"keywords":["Possibility","Openness","Creation","Potential"],"nameEn":"Infinite Possibilities"}', '{"cosmicMessage":"This card uses the image of an infinite field of possibilities to invite you to imagine more than what you can currently see. Your future is not fully determined by your present circumstances: your beliefs, choices, and actions can shape what happens next, though they cannot control every outcome. You are not limited to the options that first come to mind. In this moment, ask what you would like to create, who you hope to become, and what you want to experience. Stay open to possibilities while recognizing that some paths also depend on circumstances, resources, and other people.","currentSituation":"You may feel stuck or constrained, unable to see a way forward. Or you may be at the threshold of a new beginning, with many possibilities that feel exciting or overwhelming. Perhaps an ending or release has made space for a fresh start. This card reminds you that you can explore options even when none is obvious yet. Your task is not to force a particular outcome, but to clarify what matters to you, question assumptions that may be narrowing your view, and take a grounded step toward a possibility you value.","deeperMeaning":"Quantum physics is sometimes used in spiritual writing as a metaphor for possibility, but it does not show that human consciousness selects personal futures or makes every outcome possible. In this card''s spiritual framework, the “field of possibilities” represents the many directions life might take. Your expectations, feelings, beliefs, choices, and actions can influence your experience, but they do not determine everything. You are not fixed, and your future is not entirely settled; at each moment, you can sometimes choose a different response and open a new path. This does not mean that nothing is impossible or that constraints are only beliefs. It means you can question self-limiting assumptions while accounting for real circumstances. Let the idea of possibility invite curiosity, not pressure to manifest a perfect future.","actionGuidance":"Notice limiting phrases you tell yourself, such as “I can''t,” “It''s impossible,” or “It''s too late,” and ask whether they are always true. If you had more room to choose, what would you want? Try “what if” questions: What if I asked for help? What if I took one small step? What if I explored another route? Write or sketch a vision that gives your imagination room, then identify actions, resources, and support that could move you toward it. Stay curious and willing to revise your plan when you learn more. Take an inspired but practical step in a new direction. You can welcome opportunities while checking whether they fit your needs and values. Let go of needing to know every detail of how things will unfold, but do not rely on fate or visualization in place of planning and action.","energyHealing":"Clear quartz or labradorite may be used as symbolic reminders of openness and possibility. In a visualization, imagine several paths before you and consider which one best reflects your values; this is a reflective exercise, not a way to choose a quantum reality. A DNA-activation image may serve as a metaphor for exploring untapped potential, not a biological process. Create an altar with objects that symbolize openness, such as a key, feather, star, or open doorway. Mint or lemon scents may be part of a fresh-start ritual if suitable. You might imagine speaking with a future version of yourself and reflect on what practical wisdom they might offer. Celebrate possibilities you have already explored and steps you have taken. Let excitement support your effort while making room for uncertainty and realistic constraints.","soulQuestion":"What possibility would I like to explore if I questioned one limiting assumption? Am I willing to imagine a wider future and take a grounded step toward it?"}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '1', 'en', 'Unicorn of New Beginnings', '新開始獨角獸', '{"keywords":["New Beginnings","Renewal","Purity","Hope","Possibility"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of New Beginnings"}', '{"point1":"This card symbolizes the infancy of life and the first light of dawn, like a unicorn emerging from morning mist with a sense of fresh possibility. Its message is that an ending can make room for a beginning. A chapter of your life may have run its course, and you now stand at a threshold, looking toward a world of new options. Treat this moment as an invitation to choose again, create again, and shape who you want to become.","point2":"Dear soul, you are being invited to enter a new season of life. A beginning may reflect the growth you have already done; you do not need to see it as a sign that everything is destined or perfectly arranged. You can release old limits, identities, or stories that no longer fit. At this starting point, you have room to choose who you want to be and what you want to build. Let past experiences become sources of insight rather than burdens you must carry unchanged.","point3":"The energy of a new beginning can feel fresh, light, and hopeful, like the first flower opening in spring. It can bring creativity and renewal, helping you set down some of the weight of the past and make room for new vitality. When you connect with this feeling, you may find a quiet sense of “I can begin.” It is a reminder that possibilities can open when you are willing to take a first step.","point4":"Your current lesson may be learning to let go and find the courage to begin again. You may be holding on to a relationship, job, belief, or identity because the unknown feels frightening. Growth can require releasing a chapter that is complete and making space for what comes next. An ending is not necessarily a failure; it can be part of change. When you are ready, saying goodbye can help you welcome something new.","point5":"Take one small action today. You might write down what you are ready to release and dispose of the paper safely, or sketch a vision for what you hope to create. Clear a small area in your home if that feels helpful. Set a simple, specific goal and take its first step. You do not need perfect timing or a complete plan to begin, but you can choose a step that is safe and realistic.","point6":"Treat yourself gently as you move through change. A new beginning can bring insecurity or fear, and that is understandable. Give yourself time to adjust instead of expecting immediate perfection. Write down past transitions you have navigated to remember your capacity to adapt. When doubt arises, pause, breathe, and remind yourself that you can take this one step at a time. Seek out people and environments that support your growth, and notice one thing you appreciate today.","point7":"Spiritually, a new beginning can be a meaningful moment in your personal growth. Each time you begin again, you may loosen an old pattern and live with greater awareness. This card is not only about changing your outer circumstances; it also invites you to reshape how you meet life. Bring a beginner''s mind, as if seeing the world with fresh curiosity. Trust your own reflection and judgment as you step into this next chapter; you do not need to assume that every event follows a perfect plan."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '2', 'en', 'Unicorn of Trust', '信任獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Trust","Surrender","Calm","Flow","Confidence"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Trust"}', '{"point1":"This card symbolizes deep trust and surrender, like a unicorn running freely through a forest. It reminds you that control has limits and that strength can also come from allowing life to unfold. When you grip too tightly, you may find it difficult to adapt; when you allow some uncertainty, new options can become visible. Trust is not weakness. It can mean having the courage to take a thoughtful step even when you cannot see the whole path.","point2":"Dear soul, you are gently invited to loosen your grip. Life may not follow the route you planned, and you do not have to control every turn. Your mind may want certainty, while another part of you may be ready to practice trust. Even in a difficult or unclear period, you can move forward one decision at a time. Let trust be a compass, not a guarantee that everything will go as hoped; pair it with your own discernment.","point3":"The energy of trust can feel deep, calm, and steady, like resting in warm water and letting yourself float. This softness can help you meet anxiety or fear with less resistance. When you connect with this feeling, you may find more calm inside even when things outside remain uncertain. A calmer state can help you stay open to support and possibility, without promising that every difficulty will disappear.","point4":"Your current lesson may be learning to release the need to control every outcome. You may plan carefully and try to prevent surprises, but constant tension can exhaust you. Some things are beyond your control; recognizing this can help you focus on what is yours to do. You can learn to live with uncertainty while continuing to make practical choices. Trust is a capacity you can develop gradually, and it may help you meet challenges with more steadiness.","point5":"Practice trust in small, low-stakes moments. Notice how you feel when a plan changes or you have to wait, and take a few slow breaths before responding. Write down times when listening to your judgment helped you, as well as times when you adapted after uncertainty. You may place a worry on paper and set it aside for now, then identify one useful action you can take. Observe whether practicing trust changes your feelings, without treating coincidences as proof that events are arranged for you.","point6":"Healing around trust begins with treating your distrust gently. If trusting is difficult, past hurt may have taught you to protect yourself. Acknowledge that fear and consider what boundaries or support would help you feel safer now. You might imagine warm light around your heart as a calming reflection practice. An affirmation such as “I can build trust at my own pace” may feel more honest than asking yourself to trust everything. Give yourself time; trust is often built gradually through experience.","point7":"On a spiritual path, trust can mean feeling connected to something larger than yourself, according to your own beliefs. This card invites you to consider whether surrender means giving up or cooperating with what you cannot control. You can stay open to guidance while checking it against your values, evidence, and needs. Each time you choose a considered response over an automatic attempt to control everything, you may feel more freedom. Let trust be a practice, not a demand for certainty or a reason to ignore warning signs."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '3', 'en', 'Unicorn of Miracles', '奇蹟獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Miracles","Magic","Surprise","Possibility","Blessings"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Miracles"}', '{"point1":"This card celebrates the possibility of being surprised by life and finding meaning in what exceeds your expectations. The unicorn is a mythical creature, and here it represents wonder: something extraordinary to imagine, even if it cannot be proven. The card invites you to remain open to outcomes you had not considered. When you believe a new possibility is worth exploring, what once seemed out of reach may become something you can approach through real choices and effort.","point2":"Dear soul, you may be longing for a beautiful change, even if you cannot yet see how it could happen. Some things may be coming together in ways you did not expect, but no one can promise a particular result. You can prepare to notice opportunities, accept support, and remain open to pleasant surprises. Your hopes and gratitude can shape how you meet the present, while your actions and circumstances also matter.","point3":"The energy of wonder can feel bright, joyful, and expansive, like starlight scattered across the night sky. It may help you notice beauty in the ordinary and experience moments of delight as meaningful. When you make room for joy and gratitude, you may feel more present and receptive. You do not have to be joyful all the time or treat difficult feelings as a failure; wonder can exist alongside uncertainty and hardship.","point4":"Your current lesson may be expanding your sense of what is possible. Past experience, practical reasoning, and social expectations can sometimes narrow your imagination, but they can also help you make sound decisions. This card invites you to question assumptions that are holding you back while staying realistic about what you can influence. Let yourself hope and explore without believing that faith alone guarantees an outcome.","point5":"Make room for experiences that bring you joy: meditation, time in nature, music, creativity, or a conversation with someone you care about. Notice coincidences or small unexpected moments if they feel meaningful to you, but do not treat them as reliable predictions. In the morning, you might set an intention to stay open to what the day brings. Release the expectation that a good surprise must arrive in a particular form, and appreciate small moments of kindness or delight.","point6":"If you want to make space for possibility, write down something you assume cannot happen and ask, “What would I need to learn or try to explore this?” You can loosen attachment to one exact outcome while still taking practical steps toward what matters to you. Celebrate progress, even when it is modest. If doubt arises, let it help you examine your expectations rather than treating it as a sign that you have blocked a miracle. Keep your sense of wonder and allow yourself to be surprised.","point7":"Spiritually, a miracle can be a way of describing an experience of awe, grace, or unexpected support. This card invites you to feel connected and cared for, if that meaning resonates with you, while remembering that needing help does not mean you have failed. You can receive support and also offer it to others. Let a sense of wonder enrich your life without requiring extraordinary events as proof of your worth or of a divine plan."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '4', 'en', 'Unicorn of Love', '愛的獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Love","Compassion","Healing","Connection","Gentleness"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Love"}', '{"point1":"This card embodies love as a powerful, fundamental force in life. The unicorn''s pure heart represents love offered without judgment or conditions. Its message is that love is more than a feeling or relationship status; it can be a way of meeting yourself and the world. When you act from care and compassion, situations may change, and you may find a gentler way to tend to hurt. Love can be an answer, though it does not replace boundaries, accountability, or practical support.","point2":"Dear soul, you are worthy of care not because of your achievements, appearance, or good deeds, but because you are a person. Today, the unicorn invites you to return to a loving way of relating: include the parts of yourself you find imperfect, offer care to others where it is safe, and remain open to life even after disappointment. Choosing love over fear can shape the way you treat people and the choices you make. It does not require you to excuse harm or remain in an unsafe relationship.","point3":"The energy of love can feel warm, accepting, and restorative, like a gentle embrace offered to someone who is hurting. Compassion may soften harsh self-judgment and help you feel safer and more accepted. When you practice this kind of care, you may find more room to believe you are worthy of love. In some spiritual traditions, the heart chakra symbolizes connection and compassion. Love is not a resource you must earn, but expressing care still works best with honesty, respect, and healthy limits.","point4":"Your life lesson may be learning self-love. You may be used to caring for others while withholding the same gentleness from yourself, or holding yourself to standards you would not apply to someone else. You cannot give sustainably when you are ignoring your own needs. Caring for yourself is not selfish; it can help you show up for others in a healthier way. Begin by offering yourself the respect and compassion you would give someone you love.","point5":"Begin a small practice of love today. You might look in the mirror and offer yourself a kind, believable phrase, such as “I am learning to care for myself.” Before a decision, ask what a loving response would look like for you and for anyone affected. List a few qualities you appreciate in yourself. Tell someone you care about them when the moment feels right. Most importantly, be gentle with yourself when you make a mistake, feel vulnerable, or fall short of your expectations.","point6":"Healing around self-love can begin by accepting the part of you that struggles to feel worthy. Past experiences may have left you believing you are not deserving of care, but those messages do not define your value. Try a mirror reflection: “I see you. I accept you as you are today. I am willing to care for you.” You might write a compassionate letter to your younger self. When self-criticism appears, pause and imagine responding with warmth. If old wounds feel difficult to work through alone, a trusted person or qualified therapist can offer support.","point7":"Spiritually, love is not only something to search for; it can also be a quality you practice and embody. This card invites you to reconnect with the care and tenderness already available in your life. When you act from love, you may feel closer to your deepest values or spiritual beliefs. Each kind choice toward yourself or others can contribute to a more compassionate world. You do not have to be love all the time or heal everyone around you; you are allowed to be human and to receive care too."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '5', 'en', 'Unicorn of Light', '光之獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Light","Illumination","Sacred","Inspiration","Clarity"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Light"}', '{"point1":"This card points to the light you may find within yourself: your values, insight, creativity, and capacity to encourage others. The unicorn''s shining horn symbolizes the ability to bring clarity to confusion, hope to discouragement, and care to difficult moments. Your light can help illuminate your own way and offer inspiration to people around you. You do not need to be perfect or take responsibility for rescuing everyone; being genuine can be meaningful on its own.","point2":"Radiant soul, this card invites you not to hide the qualities that make you who you are. The world can benefit from your particular perspective and presence. Letting yourself be seen does not have to mean boasting or seeking attention; it can simply mean expressing your gifts honestly. When you show up as yourself, you may encourage others to do the same. You do not have to prove that your presence heals the world. Your worth is not measured by how much you give.","point3":"The energy of light can feel bright, uplifting, and clarifying, like morning sun appearing through fog. It may bring hope and help you see what had been difficult to notice. A visualization of light can be a calming reminder of connection to what you value or consider sacred. It cannot remove every shadow or transform every circumstance, but it may help you approach a challenge with more clarity, courage, and care.","point4":"Your current lesson may be moving through the fear of taking up space. You might hide a talent or downplay your ideas because you fear criticism, envy, or conflict. Your strengths need not threaten others; sharing them with humility and generosity may inspire people. Making yourself smaller does not serve you or the people who could benefit from your contribution. Consider one safe, authentic way to let yourself be seen, while respecting your own limits and the context around you.","point5":"You might begin the day with a brief visualization of warm light surrounding you, if that feels grounding. Spend a few minutes outside in daylight when practical and safe. Write down a few strengths, talents, or qualities you value in yourself. In a room or conversation, consider what you can contribute without taking responsibility for everyone''s feelings. Do one thing today that expresses who you are, even if it is a small step. Let other people''s opinions matter without making them the only measure of your worth.","point6":"If you learned to hide your abilities, reflect on when that became necessary and what you needed at the time. You can acknowledge the hurt without judging yourself for adapting. Try affirmations that feel true enough to practice, such as “It is safe to share some of who I am” or “I deserve to be treated with respect.” When you notice yourself shrinking, pause and consider what would help you feel secure. Celebrate moments when you express yourself honestly, whether or not others respond as you hoped.","point7":"On a spiritual path, recognizing your inner light may mean honoring your conscience, compassion, and capacity for hope. You are more than your physical appearance or any single role, while still being a human being with needs and limits. This card invites you to let what you value guide how you live and how you treat others. Your presence can make a difference in ordinary ways, but you are not responsible for changing the world''s energy. Share your light in ways that are sustainable and true to you."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '6', 'en', 'Unicorn of Healing', '療癒獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Healing","Recovery","Release","Nourishment","Wholeness"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Healing"}', '{"point1":"This card represents a process of healing unfolding in your life, like the unicorn''s legendary healing horn. Whether you are facing physical illness, emotional hurt, grief, or spiritual disconnection, what you are carrying deserves care and attention. Healing is not an instant magic trick; it often takes time, patience, and self-compassion. Each wound has its own story, and with support you may find new ways to understand and live with what happened.","point2":"Dear soul, you may be moving through a courageous healing journey. What happened to you was not necessarily your fault, and you do not need to feel ashamed for being hurt. Let yourself experience emotions such as grief, anger, sadness, or vulnerability at a pace that feels manageable. You do not have to carry everything alone: trusted people and qualified professionals can support you. Spiritual practices may offer comfort if they resonate, but they are not a substitute for medical or mental-health care when you need it.","point3":"The energy of healing can feel gentle, nourishing, and restorative, like warm water soothing a tender place. Giving difficult feelings space to be noticed may help you understand what you need. When you feel safe and supported, you may begin to reconnect different parts of your experience. Healing is not guaranteed to remove pain or restore things exactly as they were, but care, time, and appropriate support can help you find ways forward. A reassuring phrase can be comforting, but you do not have to promise yourself that everything will be fine.","point4":"Your current lesson may be allowing yourself to receive care. You may be used to staying strong, suppressing pain, or moving on quickly, but it can help to pause and acknowledge when you are hurt or need support. Asking for help is not weakness. Healing does not mean returning to who you were before; it can mean integrating your experiences and finding a way to feel more whole. Give yourself permission to rest, feel, and reach out.","point5":"Choose one healing action that fits your needs today. You might contact a doctor, therapist, support worker, or trusted friend; rest; write in a journal; or take a warm bath if that feels soothing. Do not pressure yourself to function as usual if you need recovery time. Let emotions move without forcing yourself to share more than you want. Try a kind affirmation such as “I deserve support and care.” Healing has no universal timetable, and some forms of pain benefit from professional attention.","point6":"Self-compassion matters throughout healing. If you feel vulnerable, have a setback, or experience strong emotions, respond with care rather than criticism. Healing is rarely a straight line; better and harder days can both be part of the process. Create a supportive space with a quiet corner, comforting music, or a personal ritual. When pain comes up, you might acknowledge it: “I notice this is here, and I can seek the support I need.” You do not have to rely on your body or spirit to heal without outside help; use the resources available to you.","point7":"Spiritually, healing can be an important part of growth and meaning-making. Caring for yourself may also help you relate to others with more understanding, but your healing is not a duty to repair family or collective pain. You are allowed to focus on your own needs. The goal is not to erase every scar, but to keep the past from defining all of who you are. Let healing include practical care, supportive relationships, and the freedom to decide what your experience means to you."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '7', 'en', 'Unicorn of Wisdom', '智慧獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Wisdom","Insight","Knowing","Understanding","Enlightenment"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Wisdom"}', '{"point1":"This card suggests that you may be reconnecting with a deep source of wisdom: the insight you have gained from experience, reflection, and what you have learned. Your understanding is not limited to books or logical analysis; it also includes what you have observed and lived through. The card invites you to quiet the noise around you and listen inwardly. Answers may become clearer when you make space to reflect, while remaining open to learning from other people and reliable sources.","point2":"Wise soul, this card asks you to remember that you may already have some of the insight you need. You do not have to look only to books, teachers, or authorities for every answer; your own experience and values matter too. When you step back from anxiety and other people''s expectations, you may hear your own thoughts more clearly. Inner reflection can be a helpful guide, but it does not mean you know everything or should dismiss outside expertise. Let your own judgment work alongside thoughtful counsel.","point3":"The energy of wisdom can feel deep, steady, and rooted, like an old tree reaching into the earth. It can bring discernment and help you look beyond appearances to understand a situation more fully. When you connect with this quality, you may experience a quiet sense of knowing. Some spiritual traditions describe a universal source of wisdom or the Akashic Records; these are matters of belief rather than verified sources of information. Stay curious and distinguish personal insight from facts that need to be checked.","point4":"Your current lesson may be learning to trust your own judgment while staying open to other perspectives. You might often seek advice from people, experts, or books and overlook what you have already noticed. No one else knows your life exactly as you do, though people with relevant expertise may know things you do not. Practice distinguishing fear from considered insight: fear may feel urgent or constricting, while reflection can help you see options more clearly. You can take responsibility for your choices without treating yourself as infallible.","point5":"Make time for quiet each day, even if it is only ten minutes of meditation, a walk, or sitting without distractions. Before an important decision, pause and ask what matters to you and what you already know about the situation. Write down dreams or intuitive impressions if that interests you, then reflect on them rather than assuming they predict events. Read books that inspire you, while remembering that learning can come from both outside sources and your own experience. Explaining an idea to someone else may help deepen your understanding.","point6":"Developing wisdom takes patience and practice. At first, it may be hard to tell insight from fear or wishful thinking. Notice the tone and evidence behind each thought, and give yourself time before acting on high-stakes decisions. A calm feeling is not always proof that something is true, just as anxiety does not always mean something is wrong. You might create a small reflection ritual with a candle and a few slow breaths. Look back on choices that worked well and those that taught you something. Trust yourself as a learner, not as someone who must always have the right answer.","point7":"On a spiritual journey, listening inwardly can be an important turning point: you become an active participant in your own search for truth rather than relying only on external authority. This card invites you to bring forward the wisdom you have gathered and live by it. You may inspire others through how you act, not only by teaching. You do not need to carry ancient or cosmic knowledge to be wise; humility, careful listening, and a willingness to keep learning are also forms of wisdom."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '10', 'en', 'Unicorn of Courage', '勇氣獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Courage","Strength","Bravery","Breakthrough","Resolve"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Courage"}', '{"point1":"This card calls on your inner courage, like a gentle unicorn with the strength to face what is difficult and protect what matters. Courage is not the absence of fear; it is choosing a thoughtful next step while fear is present. It is not never falling, but finding a way to rise again when you can. You may have more resilience than you recognize, built through the challenges you have already met. This is an invitation to meet the current challenge with care, not a demand to take reckless risks.","point2":"Brave soul, remember the times you have shown courage: beginning again after heartbreak, trying after a setback, being honest when it felt vulnerable, or facing the unknown. Now you may be asked to act courageously once more. The challenge may look large, but fear does not prove you are weak. It may simply signal that something matters or feels uncertain. Each time you choose a considered, values-aligned action, you can reshape your story, whatever the outcome.","point3":"The energy of courage can feel strong, encouraging, and empowering, like a steady mountain or a bright flame. It may help you stand a little taller and remember the ways you have endured, adapted, and learned. When you connect with this quality, self-doubt may ease enough for you to act. Courage does not guarantee success or remove fear; it helps you take a step while staying aware of your limits and the support available to you.","point4":"Your current lesson may be practicing courageous action. You may know you need to have a conversation, begin a project, share a feeling, or set a boundary, but fear can leave you stuck. You do not have to wait until you feel no fear. Break the situation into manageable steps and consider the risks before you act. Courage can include leaving an unhealthy situation, but it can also mean planning carefully and seeking support. Each safe, small act of honesty or self-advocacy can build confidence.","point5":"Choose one courageous action that is important and appropriate for you. Name what it is, then break the challenge into steps and focus on the first one. Write down times you have acted bravely before to remind yourself of what you can do. Ask a trusted person to support you or keep you accountable. You might practice a slightly uncomfortable but safe action, such as expressing a preference or asking a question. Let the goal be acting with intention, not controlling how others respond.","point6":"Courage grows through practice and self-kindness. Do not judge yourself for feeling afraid; fear is a normal human response and can sometimes point to a risk worth considering. Notice it, then ask, “What can I do while this fear is here?” A few slow breaths or a hand over your heart may help you pause before choosing. Courage is often a series of decisions, not one grand gesture. Recognize each effort, regardless of whether the result was what you hoped for.","point7":"Spiritually, courage can support growth by helping you move beyond familiar habits and live closer to your values. This card reminds you that you are not defined only by fear or past setbacks. Your honest efforts may encourage someone else, though you do not need to become a symbol or catalyst for everyone. Let courage include care for yourself and others. You can be brave and still ask for help, take time, or change direction when you learn something new."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '11', 'en', 'Unicorn of Grace', '優雅獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Grace","Composure","Balance","Harmony","Dignity"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Grace"}', '{"point1":"This card invites you to meet life''s changes with grace, like a unicorn keeping its poise in a storm. Grace is not polished manners or pretending to be perfect; it can mean staying connected to yourself under pressure. How you respond to a challenge may matter as much as the challenge itself. Consider choosing a response guided by care and wisdom rather than fear or impulse, while still allowing yourself to feel what you feel.","point2":"Dear soul, grace can express inner strength; it is not a mask of weakness. When difficulties arise, someone triggers an emotion, or events do not go as planned, you have choices about what to do next. You might react quickly, or pause, reconnect with yourself, and choose a response that reflects your values. This is not suppressing emotion or pretending everything is fine. It is making room for your feelings without letting them dictate every action. That can be grace: steadiness in a storm and dignity in uncertainty.","point3":"The energy of grace can feel fluid, gentle, and firm, like a willow bending without breaking or water finding a way around an obstacle. It may support balance when circumstances are unsettled. When you connect with this quality, you may feel less pressure to prove, control, or fight everything. Grace does not require passivity or going along with what is wrong; it can help you move with awareness and dignity while holding clear boundaries.","point4":"Your current lesson may be staying grounded during a challenge. You might shut down under pressure, lash out in conflict, or lose perspective when things are hard. Practice pausing when you notice you are triggered, taking a breath, and checking what you need before responding. You do not have to answer every provocation immediately. Grace is not perfection; it can include getting back up, acknowledging a mistake, and making repair when needed.","point5":"Begin cultivating grace with a brief pause when you feel activated. Take three slow breaths, if that feels comfortable, and give yourself room to choose a response. Before a difficult conversation, set an intention to be clear and respectful. Notice people you admire for how they handle pressure, while finding your own way to define grace. Write down what dignity and composure mean to you. You can feel anger or grief without losing your right to express yourself. At the end of the day, reflect on one moment you handled with care.","point6":"Practicing grace takes time; do not expect yourself to respond perfectly right away. If you act impulsively or lose your balance, treat yourself with compassion and reflect afterward on what you might try next time. A simple anchor—one breath, a grounding phrase, or a familiar gesture—can remind you to pause. Practice it when life is calm so it is easier to remember under pressure. Grace is a choice you can return to, not a standard you must meet in every moment.","point7":"Spiritually, grace may look like emotional awareness paired with dignity and honesty. Maturity is not escaping emotion or appearing flawless; it can mean feeling fully while taking responsibility for your actions. Your way of meeting difficulty may encourage others, but you do not have to maintain peace at the expense of your needs. You can be compassionate and assertive. Let grace be a gift you offer yourself as well as the people around you."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '12', 'en', 'Unicorn of Freedom', '自由獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Freedom","Liberation","Release","Independence","Flight"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Freedom"}', '{"point1":"This card is a call toward greater freedom, like a unicorn running across an open field. It invites you to examine what limits or constrains you, including inner beliefs as well as external circumstances. Freedom is not simply doing anything you want; it can mean being more fully yourself without shame or fear. Notice the chains you may have placed on yourself and consider which ones you are ready to loosen, while recognizing that some limits are real and require practical solutions.","point2":"Dear soul, some constraints may come from internalized beliefs, other people''s expectations, social standards, or past experiences. You can feel restricted even when parts of your life look free from the outside. This card gives you permission to question the rules you have accepted and commitments that no longer fit. You are not here only to meet everyone else''s expectations. You can seek a life that reflects your values, while honoring responsibilities and considering the effects of major decisions.","point3":"The energy of freedom can feel expansive, light, and full of options, like a wide sky or an open breeze. It may help you breathe more easily, widen your perspective, and remember that you have choices. This is not necessarily rebellion or escape; it can be a deeper sense of self-ownership. You have a right to consider your path, truth, and way of living. Freedom also includes making choices with awareness of their consequences and respect for others'' autonomy.","point4":"Your current lesson may be recognizing and loosening what constrains you. Ask honestly what is limiting you: a job, an unhealthy relationship, an outdated self-image, a belief about what you “should” do, or a promise you no longer know how to honor. Sometimes fear of change, disappointing someone, or facing the unknown can keep us in place. You do not need to label every obligation a cage. This card invites you to assess what still serves you and plan carefully for changes that affect your safety, livelihood, or loved ones.","point5":"Start a freedom inquiry by listing areas where you feel restricted. For each one, ask whether it still fits your values and whether you would choose it freely today. Be honest without demanding that you change everything immediately. Make a realistic plan for any changes you decide to pursue, and consider talking with someone trustworthy. A symbolic act—saying no, deleting an app, changing your routine, or dancing in the rain—may help you mark a choice. Your freedom can begin with one small, deliberate step.","point6":"The process of change can bring discomfort, guilt, fear, or grief. Those feelings are understandable, especially when a familiar situation once provided security. Remind yourself that seeking more freedom is not automatically selfish, while also taking seriously the needs and commitments involved. If fear asks what you might lose, consider both sides: what could staying cost you, and what resources would change require? Seek support from people who respect your autonomy. Celebrate small steps, and allow time for new routines or relationships to take shape.","point7":"Spiritually, freedom can mean releasing identities and expectations that no longer reflect you. You are more than your roles, relationships, achievements, or past, even as these may be meaningful parts of your life. This card invites you to explore who you are beneath old labels and to choose your next steps with care. Your example may encourage others, but you do not need to persuade anyone else to change. Let freedom include responsibility, connection, and the ability to revise your path."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '8', 'en', 'Unicorn of Joy', '喜悅獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Joy","Happiness","Play","Lightness","Laughter"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Joy"}', '{"point1":"This card celebrates pure joy, like a unicorn leaping in the sunlight. Its message is that you are allowed to feel happiness without earning it through achievement or having a reason to justify it. You are invited to set down some of life''s heaviness and reconnect with the part of you that enjoys play and being present. Joy is not only a destination; it can be found in moments along the way, even while other parts of life remain difficult.","point2":"Dear soul, do you remember small moments that once made you happy: seeing a butterfly, blowing bubbles, running in the rain, or hearing a favorite song? That capacity for joy may still be there, though adult responsibilities, expectations, and worries can make it harder to notice. Give yourself permission to do something enjoyable simply because you like it, whether that means laughing, playing, or listening to music. Joy is not selfish, and you do not have to feel it on demand or at the expense of anyone else.","point3":"The energy of joy can feel light, bright, and lively, like sunshine dancing across a lake or wind chimes in a breeze. It may ease a heavy moment and help you notice what is good around you. Enjoyment can support connection and creativity, but it does not guarantee that more good events will follow or cure anxiety or sadness. Being joyful is not a requirement. You can appreciate a happy moment while also making room for more complicated feelings.","point4":"Your current lesson may be allowing yourself to feel happy. You may have absorbed beliefs such as “I must suffer before I deserve joy,” “happiness is shallow,” or “I should not be happy while problems remain.” But your happiness does not add to other people''s suffering. Play and laughter are not automatically a waste of time or an escape; they can give you rest and renewed energy. You can care about serious issues while still enjoying parts of your life.","point5":"Make a list of simple things that bring you joy and choose one to do today. Play, draw, dance, or sing without judging the result. Watch something funny, listen to music you love, or spend time with a child or pet if that is part of your life. Notice small pleasures such as a good meal, warm sunlight, or a kind conversation. Before bed, you might write down three moments you appreciated, not to force positivity but to remember that good moments can coexist with challenges.","point6":"If joy feels hard to access, past hurt, stress, or other experiences may be affecting you. Begin gently: notice a small pleasant detail or allow yourself a brief smile without demanding more. When happiness arises, you do not need to immediately dismiss it because of tomorrow''s problems. Let it be present for a moment, even if other feelings remain. You might say to your inner critic, “I hear you, and I can allow myself this moment.” If low mood or loss of interest persists and troubles you, consider reaching out to a qualified professional.","point7":"Spiritually, joy can be a way of feeling connected to what you consider sacred or meaningful. A spiritual path need not be serious every moment; play and laughter can belong too. Your joy may encourage others, but you are not responsible for raising the world''s energy or proving that life is good. This card reminds you that even in an imperfect world, you are allowed to experience pleasure and delight. Let joy be one part of a whole life, not a demand to stay positive."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '9', 'en', 'Unicorn of Dreams', '夢想獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Dreams","Vision","Possibility","Manifestation","Desire"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Dreams"}', '{"point1":"This card represents a dream or aspiration calling for your attention, like the unicorn as an image of the seemingly impossible made vivid in imagination. The desires that excite you or make your eyes light up may point toward things you value. They need not be a fixed soul blueprint or a guaranteed message from the universe to be worth exploring. Take your dreams seriously enough to ask what they mean to you and whether you want to begin working toward one now.","point2":"Dear dreamer, your hopes matter and need not stay indefinitely behind “when I have more time, money, or ideal conditions.” The ideas that excite you or move you emotionally may help you find direction. Do not let fear, other people''s doubt, or a narrow idea of what is realistic silence them before you have explored them. At the same time, inspiration does not guarantee success. You can honor a dream by learning what it would take, making a plan, and deciding whether its costs and rewards fit your life.","point3":"The energy of a dream can feel expansive, inspiring, and full of possibility, like stars across a night sky. It can widen your imagination beyond your current circumstances and help you picture a larger direction. When you connect with a meaningful vision, you may feel more motivated and alive. Imagining a future version of yourself can help you clarify what you want, but it cannot guarantee that a particular future will occur. Let hope and creativity support thoughtful action.","point4":"Your current lesson may be learning to take your dreams seriously enough to explore them. You may suppress an aspiration because you fear disappointment, ridicule, or discovering how difficult it will be. Calling a dream unrealistic can sometimes protect you from risk, but it can also keep you from finding out what is possible. Pursuing something meaningful is not selfish or childish, and your worth does not depend on achieving it. You can make a brave choice while still being practical and flexible.","point5":"Write down your dreams without editing them at first, then choose one that feels important to explore. Make a sketch, a short description, or a vision board if that helps you clarify it. Turn the idea into doable steps and take one today. Look for people who have tried something similar and learn from their experience. Visualization may help you stay focused, but pair it with planning, practice, and support. Remind yourself that your dream deserves consideration, whether or not the final outcome matches your first picture.","point6":"Doubt may come from other people and from your own inner critic. When you hear “This is impossible,” “I''m not good enough,” or “It''s too late,” ask what evidence you have and what you might learn by trying a small step. Seek a support system: people who can encourage you while giving honest feedback, along with notes or stories that inspire you. Progress can be slow and difficult to see, so notice incremental effort. Keep your self-worth separate from whether a particular dream succeeds; a changed goal is not a personal failure.","point7":"Spiritually, a dream can feel like an invitation to create, grow, or contribute something meaningful. You may understand it as a gift or calling within your beliefs, while remembering that no one can know that the universe guarantees its fulfillment. Your efforts may inspire or support others, but your dream is yours to shape and revise. Take it out of your heart and into the world in a way that respects your needs and limits."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '13', 'en', 'Unicorn of Hope', '希望獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Hope","Confidence","Optimism","Dawn","Faith"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Hope"}', '{"point1":"This card is a small light in the dark, like a unicorn''s horn glowing at night. However difficult the tunnel you are in may feel, it offers a reminder that circumstances can change and this moment is not necessarily the end of your story. Hope is not blind optimism or an escape from reality; it is the courage to believe that other possibilities may exist even when you cannot see them yet. Let this card help you find a little hope again, without requiring you to deny what is hard.","point2":"Dear soul, if you feel despair, exhaustion, or unable to imagine a future, please hear this: your pain deserves care, and you do not have to face it alone. You have lived through difficult moments before, but that does not mean you must manage this one without help. Hope does not require certainty that everything will work out; sometimes it is simply the choice to get through today or to reach out to someone. If you cannot feel hopeful right now, let a trusted person hold hope with you. Support is available, and asking for it is a brave step.","point3":"The energy of hope can feel warm, gently rising, and open to possibility, like the first green of spring or the first light on the horizon. It may bring a small sense of “maybe” into a hard moment: perhaps you can take one more step, or perhaps something can change. Hope need not be excitement; it may be the quiet thought “I can continue for now.” That feeling can support another attempt, while still allowing you to acknowledge pain and uncertainty.","point4":"Your current lesson may be finding a way to hold hope alongside difficulty. When evidence feels discouraging, it can be hard to imagine a different outcome. Hope is not foolish, and neither is recognizing real obstacles. You can be honest about what is difficult while staying open to options you cannot yet see. Look for small sources of support and moments of kindness—not as proof that everything is guaranteed, but as reminders that care and possibility still exist.","point5":"Begin by acknowledging your exhaustion or despair rather than pushing it away. Then look for three small things that offer comfort or possibility: a person who cares, the fact that you made it through today, or the chance to ask for help. You might write a kind note to your future self about what you hope for, or collect meaningful reminders in a box. Read or listen to stories that encourage you, while remembering that your path is your own. A phrase such as “I can take one step at a time” may feel more supportive than promising yourself that better days are certain.","point6":"It can be hard to stay hopeful when setbacks repeat, change is slow, or you feel alone. You do not have to be hopeful every moment. Rest when you are low instead of forcing positivity. Reach out to a trusted person who can sit with you when hope feels out of reach. When a discouraging thought overwhelms you, try naming it as a thought rather than a final verdict. Remembering past difficulties you have navigated may help, but you do not have to minimize what you are facing now. You can choose a small next step and seek support one day at a time.","point7":"Spiritually, hope may express a belief that love, meaning, or possibility remains even during hardship. This card invites you to connect with that belief if it supports you, without assuming that suffering is part of a perfect plan or that everything happens for a reason. Your hope may help you care for yourself and connect with others. You do not need to carry hope for the whole world. For now, it may be enough to keep going with support and remain open to a next moment."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '14', 'en', 'Unicorn of Transformation', '轉化獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Transformation","Metamorphosis","Evolution","Renewal","Growth"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Transformation"}', '{"point1":"This card marks a period of significant change, like the unicorn as an image of metamorphosis from the ordinary to the extraordinary. Transformation can reach deeper than a change in appearances: an old way of seeing yourself may be giving way to something new. The process may feel uncomfortable, confusing, or painful, like a caterpillar changing inside a chrysalis. You do not have to call the upheaval sacred or assume it is happening for a reason. This card invites patience and care while you adjust to what is changing.","point2":"Dear soul, a period of transition can feel uncomfortable because you are no longer who you were, yet the next version of life has not taken shape. An old identity, belief, relationship, or job may no longer fit, while what comes next remains unclear. Feeling lost or vulnerable can be part of uncertainty; it does not mean you are doing something wrong. You do not have to cling to what is ending, but you also do not need to force a change faster than feels safe. Focus on what you can care for today and let clarity develop over time.","point3":"The energy of transformation can feel intense, as if something is breaking down while something else begins to form. You may notice emotional shifts, changes in your routines or relationships, or a major life event. Not every strong feeling or physical change is evidence of spiritual transformation; seek appropriate help if you have concerns. This card offers an image of change that includes both endings and beginnings. It can take courage to release what no longer fits and patience to discover what may replace it.","point4":"Your current lesson may be learning how to work with change rather than resist every part of it. You might try to control the process, hold on to the past, or prevent an ending, but some changes are outside your control. Where you do have choices, you can decide what to release and what to carry forward. Letting go is not always the right choice, and uncertainty does not have to be resolved all at once. You are not necessarily losing yourself; you may be learning which parts of you remain meaningful through change.","point5":"Support yourself during transition by naming what is changing and what you need. Rest, quiet, or time alone may help, as may journaling about what you are letting go of and what you hope to grow into. If symbolic rituals are meaningful, write down an old story and dispose of the paper safely, or make a small change to your space. Make room for new experiences gradually: learn a skill, meet someone, or revisit an interest. Remind yourself, “I can take this step without understanding the whole process.” Seek support from people who are also navigating change or who can offer steady perspective.","point6":"During transition, grief, fear, excitement, and uncertainty may appear together. Let yourself feel them without assuming you need to fix yourself. Hard days can happen, and missing the past does not mean you should return to it. Instead of using a metaphor of metamorphosis to dismiss distress, reach out when you need care or help. Do not compare your timeline with another person''s. Keep track of small changes and the things that help you feel grounded; give yourself time to adapt.","point7":"Spiritually, transformation can be a meaningful path of growth, but you do not have to believe that your soul chose hardship or that every painful event was necessary. This card invites you to notice what you are learning, what you want to leave behind, and what feels more authentic now. Your changes may affect how you relate to other people, though you are not responsible for raising collective consciousness. Trust yourself to move through change with support, and remember that growth can include pausing, seeking help, or changing direction."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '15', 'en', 'Unicorn of Protection', '保護獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Protection","Safety","Guardianship","Boundaries","Shield"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Protection"}', '{"point1":"This card offers an image of protection, like a unicorn creating a safe field with its horn. It reminds you that you can seek care, connection, and support while facing a challenge or fear. Spiritual beliefs about angels, guides, ancestors, or unicorn energy may bring comfort, but they cannot guarantee physical safety. You do not have to carry everything alone: consider the real people, resources, and practical steps that could help protect your well-being.","point2":"Dear soul, if you feel vulnerable or exposed to danger, your feelings deserve to be taken seriously. You are worthy of protection and care. A spiritual belief that your inner self remains sacred may be comforting, but it does not mean that you cannot be harmed or should ignore an unsafe situation. Reach out to someone you trust or to appropriate local support. You are allowed to ask for help, make a safety plan, and take concrete steps to protect yourself.","point3":"The energy of protection can feel sturdy, warm, and containing, like a cloak, a strong wall, or a caring embrace. A visualization of a light shield may help you feel centered before a difficult interaction. In practical life, boundaries can help you decide what you will accept and what you need to step away from. Protection is not isolation; it can make it safer to stay open to caring relationships while limiting access to people or situations that cause harm.","point4":"Your current lesson may be building healthy boundaries and asking for protection when needed. You may be used to overextending yourself, absorbing other people''s moods, giving too much, or letting others cross your limits. Boundaries are not coldness; they can be a form of care for yourself and your relationships. Practice saying no, leaving draining situations, or protecting your time and privacy. Asking for help is also a strength; you do not have to face everything alone.","point5":"Choose practical ways to feel safer today. You might visualize a light around you as a calming ritual, carry a meaningful object, or say a prayer if those practices comfort you. You can also identify which people and situations feel supportive, set a clear boundary, or make a plan for where to go if you feel unsafe. A phrase such as “I can let care in and say no when needed” may help. Treat spiritual practices as sources of comfort, not proof that you are protected from harm.","point6":"Creating boundaries is a wise act of self-care, not necessarily a sign of fear. If a person or place feels unsafe, take that concern seriously and seek help; you have the right to leave, say no, and protect yourself. At the same time, avoid letting a desire for protection isolate you from all connection. Boundaries can be firm while your heart remains open to safe, respectful relationships. Consider what support would help you feel both protected and connected.","point7":"Spiritually, protection may mean feeling accompanied by a sacred presence, according to your beliefs. This card invites you to ask for support and to notice the care available around you. It also reminds you that your own judgment, boundaries, and practical decisions are important forms of protection. You are not alone simply because you cannot see every source of help, but do not rely on unseen guardians instead of addressing real-world risks. Let faith and practical care work together."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '16', 'en', 'Unicorn of Abundance', '豐盛獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Abundance","Plenty","Prosperity","Receiving","Gratitude"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Abundance"}', '{"point1":"This card opens a reflection on abundance, like the unicorn bringing a treasure from myth. It asks you to consider that life may hold more sources of nourishment, opportunity, love, and joy than you currently notice. You deserve care and good things simply because you are a person, not because you have earned them through achievement. This card invites you to loosen a scarcity mindset where possible and become more open to receiving, while recognizing that real resources can be limited and unevenly shared.","point2":"Dear soul, you may have learned messages such as “money is hard to earn,” “resources are scarce,” or “I do not deserve much.” Those beliefs can shape how you approach opportunities, but they do not explain every financial or material constraint. Nature offers images of generosity and renewal, yet people also face real limitations. You can practice believing that you are worthy of support and explore ways to receive it. Abundance does not have to be something you win from the universe; it can include recognizing what is available, asking for help, and building resources over time.","point3":"The energy of abundance can feel expansive, flowing, and generous, like a spring or a river. It may encourage you to see where there is enough, share what you can, and accept help without shame. When you connect with this quality, you may feel more spacious and secure. Giving and receiving can both be part of healthy relationships, but abundance is not proof that the universe always provides or that scarcity is only an illusion. Let gratitude coexist with a clear view of your needs and circumstances.","point4":"Your current lesson may be examining beliefs about money, success, and what you deserve. You might think “I''m not good enough,” “I have to struggle for everything,” or “If I receive, someone else will have less.” Question these assumptions without blaming yourself for financial hardship. Consider whether you can make room for receiving support, fair compensation, opportunities, or kindness. Gratitude can help you notice what you value, but it cannot guarantee that more will arrive. It is also okay to advocate for yourself and seek material security.","point5":"Start an abundance practice by noting five things you appreciate each day, including small sources of support such as clean water, sunlight, or a friend''s kindness. Clear or donate items you no longer need if that is useful and affordable for you. Practice generosity in a way that fits your means, whether by sharing time, attention, or money. You might use an affirmation such as “I am worthy of support, and I can make thoughtful choices with what I have.” Visualization can help you clarify a goal; pair it with practical steps toward that goal.","point6":"Changing scarcity beliefs takes time. When you think “I can''t afford this” or “there isn''t enough,” do not deny your actual finances or pressure yourself to spend. You might instead name the situation clearly and decide what resources or alternatives are available. Replace harsh self-labels with language that recognizes your efforts, such as “I am working toward greater stability.” Celebrate small gains when they happen, without treating them as a promise of more. Abundance includes time, relationships, health, opportunity, and care, but none of these cancels the need for support in areas where you lack them.","point7":"Spiritually, abundance may represent connection to a source of generosity or gratitude within your beliefs. This card invites you to recognize the value you already hold and the good you can receive or offer. Your well-being need not come at someone else''s expense, and shared resources and mutual care can create more security for a community. Let an abundance mindset encourage generosity and self-respect, not shame about needing help or blame for circumstances beyond your control."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '17', 'en', 'Unicorn of Balance', '平衡獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Balance","Harmony","Middle Way","Stability","Integration"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Balance"}', '{"point1":"This card invites you to create a more harmonious life, like a unicorn standing steadily on all four feet. Life includes many parts: work and rest, giving and receiving, action and stillness, material needs and spiritual meaning, time alone and time with others. If one part takes up nearly all your energy, you may feel depleted or disconnected. Take an honest look at how life feels and consider a small adjustment toward a more sustainable rhythm.","point2":"Dear soul, you may be leaning heavily toward one area: working without enough rest, giving without receiving, caring for others while neglecting yourself, focusing on material concerns while longing for meaning, or using spirituality to avoid practical responsibilities. Balance is not equal time for everything every day. Life shifts and needs change, like breathing in and out or the tides moving. You do not have to sacrifice one important part of yourself to honor another. Consider what deserves more attention in this season.","point3":"The energy of balance can feel steady, integrated, and harmonious, like a chord in music or finding your center on a narrow path. It is not about always being moderate; it is about responding to what the moment requires. When you connect with this quality, you may find a sense of “enough” and notice when it is time to move forward, rest, give, receive, say yes, or say no. Balance can be a continuing practice of adjustment rather than a fixed state.","point4":"Your current lesson may be creating balance across different parts of your life. Look honestly at where you give too much or too little. Imbalance can sometimes be a response to fear or an attempt to compensate: overwork may leave little room for personal needs, while overgiving may make it hard to ask for care. Be curious rather than judgmental about the reasons. Notice an extreme pattern and consider one gentle change that could bring you closer to the center. Balance usually needs regular adjustments.","point5":"Try a simple life-wheel exercise: rate areas such as work, health, relationships, rest, spirituality, creativity, finances, and social life. Notice one area that needs attention and choose a manageable action. If work is taking over, set a realistic stopping time; if you need movement, take a short walk if that is accessible; if you miss someone, send a message. Practice receiving after giving and resting after effort. Review your schedule occasionally to see whether it reflects what matters to you.","point6":"As you make changes, you may encounter inner resistance or pressure from other people. Setting a work boundary can bring guilt or disagreement; be clear and kind while considering your responsibilities. Balance does not mean every day must be divided perfectly. One week may require more work, with more rest afterward. What matters is noticing when an imbalance becomes a pattern and adjusting where possible. Use a transition ritual, such as a few slow breaths after work, to mark the shift. Acknowledge each choice that helps you create a more sustainable rhythm.","point7":"Spiritually, balance can mean making room for different parts of human experience: light and shadow, feminine and masculine symbolism, spirituality and material life. No part of life has to be treated as inherently more worthy than another. A spiritual practice can help you engage more consciously with ordinary responsibilities, rather than escape them. When your life feels more integrated, you may experience greater harmony. Let balance be personal and responsive to your needs, not a standard imposed by someone else."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '18', 'en', 'Unicorn of Magic', '魔法獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Magic","Creation","Manifestation","Power","Alchemy"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Magic"}', '{"point1":"This card awakens the inner magician as a symbol of creativity and intentional action. Its message is that you are not powerless: your thoughts, words, beliefs, and intentions can influence how you see and shape your life. Repeating a harsh belief may affect your confidence and choices, but thoughts do not magically cause every event. You can use awareness to choose how you respond and what you create, becoming a more active participant in your life.","point2":"Dear magician, the words you repeat to yourself can affect your expectations and behavior. If you keep thinking “I''m not good enough,” you may be less likely to take a chance; if you tell yourself “I always have bad luck,” you may overlook opportunities. This is not a universal law or punishment, and positive thoughts do not guarantee positive outcomes. Magic here can be a metaphor for the influence of attention, language, and action. Choose thoughts and words that support you, while leaving room for reality to be more complex than your mindset.","point3":"The energy of magic can feel creative and focused, like bringing an idea into form. When you connect with this quality, you may remember that you can influence some parts of your experience. A vision or ritual can help you focus on what you want, but it cannot make circumstances fully controllable or turn thoughts directly into matter. You are not only acted upon by your environment, and you are not solely responsible for everything that happens to you. You can be a co-creator by making choices within the opportunities and limits you have.","point4":"Your current lesson may be creating more consciously. Notice your self-talk, the language you use, and the assumptions you bring to a situation. Ask whether these help you respond in ways that fit your values. You have influence over some outcomes, and accepting that can be empowering; it does not mean every circumstance is the result of your past thoughts or feelings. Avoid blaming yourself for hardship. Focus instead on the choices and supports available to you now, and make one change that could lead toward a different experience.","point5":"Practice being intentional today. When a discouraging thought appears, notice it and consider a more balanced alternative, rather than forcing yourself to think positively. Use affirmations that feel credible, such as “I can take one step toward what matters.” Spend a few minutes visualizing a goal, then write down a concrete action that would support it. A candle or written intention can mark the beginning of a project. Express gratitude for what is genuinely present. Doubt does not cancel your effort, and rituals work best as reminders to act rather than guarantees of an outcome.","point6":"Working toward a goal often requires patience, and results may not appear on your preferred timeline. If you are not seeing progress, review your plan, seek feedback, adjust your approach, or rest. You do not have to maintain a particular emotional frequency or believe without question. Let go of trying to control every detail, but do not assume the universe will arrange the perfect path. A helpful combination is a clear intention, realistic effort, openness to changing course, and acceptance of what lies outside your control.","point7":"Spiritually, magic can symbolize the creativity and agency you bring to your life. This card invites you to use those qualities with care, knowing that your influence has limits and that other people have their own choices. Your actions may affect more than just you, but you do not need to take responsibility for all collective outcomes. You are not required to believe you are an unlimited consciousness in order to create, grow, or make meaningful change. Remember your capacity, and put it into practice in grounded ways."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '19', 'en', 'Unicorn of Clarity', '清晰獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Clarity","Insight","Truth","Understanding","Discernment"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Clarity"}', '{"point1":"This card represents a moment when the fog may begin to lift, like a unicorn''s horn revealing a path through confusion. You may be moving toward a clearer understanding of a question that has troubled you. Perhaps you have been hesitating, weighing options, or circling around a problem. This card invites you to create space to see what matters and what direction feels right. Clarity may come gradually, and it may not provide every answer at once.","point2":"Dear soul, confusion can come not only from a lack of information but also from too many voices: other people''s opinions, social expectations, fears, and competing desires. When you take a quiet moment, you may hear your own perspective more clearly. Insight can rise from reflection, but it is not always separate from analysis or outside information. This card reminds you to listen inwardly while checking facts and considering advice from people with relevant knowledge. Be open to clarity without assuming an answer is already decided.","point3":"The energy of clarity can feel bright, clear, and focused, like a sky after rain or a calm pool reflecting what is there. It may quiet your mind enough to notice the core of a situation. When you connect with this quality, you might experience an “Ah, now I understand” moment. Clarity is not always about gathering more information; sometimes it comes from simplifying the question or recognizing what you do not know yet. You do not need to solve everything before taking a reasonable next step.","point4":"Your current lesson may be seeking clarity without becoming trapped in overanalysis. When confused, you may collect more information, ask more people, and imagine every possible outcome until the choices feel even less clear. Try pausing and giving yourself room to reflect. For a major decision, do not rush while overwhelmed, but do not assume that waiting will reveal a perfect answer. Identify what is known, what remains uncertain, and when you need to decide. Sometimes clarity means “I do not know yet” or “this is not the right time.”","point5":"Create some space for clear thinking today. You might step away from more advice or information if you already have enough to consider. Spend ten quiet minutes without your phone, sitting or walking, and gently bring your question to mind without forcing an answer. Write down your thoughts to clear mental clutter. Ask what matters most in this situation, then listen to your own response alongside relevant evidence. The first thought that arises is not automatically the truth; give important insights time and check them against your values and circumstances.","point6":"Clarity may arrive suddenly or emerge over time. Avoid forcing an answer, and allow yourself to revise your view as you learn more. A sense of relief can accompany insight, but ease alone does not prove that an answer is correct. If a conclusion leaves you more confused, you may need more information or a different perspective. Sometimes the clearest answer is “I need more time.” Notice moments when you think clearly and what helped—quiet, conversation, rest, or writing—and use that knowledge to support future decisions.","point7":"Spiritually, clarity may feel like connection with a higher self or inner guidance. If that belief resonates, you can use it as a reflective practice while remaining your own decision-maker. You are not always lost when you feel uncertain, and you do not need to reject outside expertise to trust yourself. Inner knowing and evidence can work together. Let clarity illuminate your path without demanding certainty about every step or treating your perspective as infallible."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '20', 'en', 'Unicorn of Purity', '純淨獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Purity","Cleansing","Clearing","Sacred","Renewal"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Purity"}', '{"point1":"This card is a call to clear space and reconnect with what feels essential, like the unicorn as an image of unspoiled nature. Consider what is weighing on your attention, mood, routines, or surroundings, and whether a change could help. Purity does not mean perfection, sterility, or being free from ordinary human feelings. It can mean letting go of what no longer supports your well-being and returning to a clearer sense of your own values. Choose a gentle reset that respects your body, relationships, and circumstances.","point2":"Dear soul, you may take in a lot each day: other people''s emotions, distressing news, unhelpful thoughts, food that does not suit you, or a cluttered environment. These things can leave you tired or overwhelmed, though not every difficult feeling is caused by “energy” you have absorbed. This card gently reminds you that regular care and rest can help. Like washing your body, you can make time to tidy your surroundings, take a break from media, or reflect on what helps you feel lighter and more focused.","point3":"The energy of renewal can feel fresh, bright, and clear, like mountain water, morning air, or clean linen. A reset may help you feel less weighed down and more at ease. This is not about judging yourself or striving for perfection; it is a way of respecting your needs and space. You might think of your body as deserving care and your home as a place where you can rest. Let this idea encourage practical choices that feel restorative, rather than a fear that anything imperfect is contaminating you.","point4":"Your current lesson may be noticing what is affecting your well-being and adjusting your boundaries. This might include a habit of consuming distressing news, a cluttered room, self-critical thoughts, or a relationship dynamic that leaves you drained. Instead of labeling people or things as toxic energy, describe what is happening and how it affects you. You can limit exposure, ask for a change, or seek support. Cleansing is ongoing care, not a one-time ritual that makes you permanently immune to stress.","point5":"Start with one practical reset: tidy a small area, open a window if appropriate, take a shower, or unfollow an account that consistently leaves you distressed. A bath, salt, music, or a personal prayer can be part of a ritual if you enjoy it and it is safe for you. Be mindful of smoke, plants, and cultural traditions if you choose to use a cleansing practice. When a negative thought appears, notice it without judging yourself and consider whether another perspective is available. You might say, “I can let go of what is not helping me right now.”","point6":"Build small habits that help you reset: take a quiet moment in the morning, reflect on the day in the evening, and notice which routines, media, or social settings affect you. Adjust gradually rather than trying to make every choice perfectly pure. Distance from someone may be appropriate when a relationship is harmful, but you can also set boundaries or seek support; you are not required to cut people off to protect your energy. Avoid cleanliness rituals that increase fear or become hard to control. A healthy reset should help you feel more grounded, not more isolated or anxious.","point7":"Spiritually, purity can represent returning to your values and what feels authentic beneath distraction. You are not a being of pure light who must remove every fear, critical thought, or human feeling; those experiences are part of being human. A ritual may help you mark a fresh start, but it cannot make you immune to difficulty or guarantee spiritual guidance. Let this card encourage clarity, care, and renewal while honoring the complexity of your life."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '21', 'en', 'Unicorn of Compassion', '慈悲獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Compassion","Kindness","Understanding","Gentleness","Acceptance"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Compassion"}', '{"point1":"This card invites compassion for yourself and others, like the unicorn''s gentle gaze recognizing the vulnerability in every person. Compassion is not weakness or excusing harmful behavior; it can be the strength to notice pain beneath appearances and respond with understanding when possible. It allows you to acknowledge hurt without reducing a person to their worst moment. Begin with yourself, then extend care to others in ways that remain honest and safe. Compassion can support healing, though it cannot fix every situation on its own.","point2":"Dear soul, you may be very hard on yourself, criticizing mistakes, imperfections, or setbacks. You may also find it difficult to stay patient with other people''s flaws or choices. Compassion invites a wider view: you have done the best you could with what you understood and had available at the time, and other people''s histories and limits may shape their actions too. This does not make every choice acceptable. You can understand what may be behind behavior while still naming harm and protecting yourself. Offer yourself some of the gentleness you have wanted from others.","point3":"The energy of compassion can feel warm, accepting, and soothing, like a caring embrace or gentle rain on dry ground. It may soften defensiveness and help you acknowledge pain without turning away. When you connect with this quality, you might feel your heart soften or become more present with someone. Compassion is not pity; it can mean “I see that you are hurting, and I can be with you.” It recognizes that pain is real while leaving room for healing, accountability, and change.","point4":"Your current lesson may be developing compassion for yourself and others. Start with self-compassion: when you make a mistake or feel imperfect, how do you speak to yourself? This card invites you to become a supportive presence in your own life. You may also consider compassion toward someone who hurt you, but this is not required and does not mean saying “it''s fine,” forgiving on demand, or allowing further harm. You can understand someone''s pain and still maintain distance, boundaries, or accountability.","point5":"Practice compassion by looking in the mirror and saying, “I see how hard you are trying, and I care about what you are feeling.” When self-criticism appears, try responding as you would to a close friend. Write yourself a kind letter from a more understanding perspective. Before judging someone, pause and consider what you do not know about their situation, without assuming an excuse. If someone has harmed you, a private practice of releasing resentment may help, but you do not need to contact or reconcile with them. Compassion includes protecting yourself.","point6":"Compassion takes practice, especially toward yourself. If gentleness feels unfamiliar or undeserved, begin with a small, neutral step. When you notice judgment, try not to judge yourself for judging; simply observe it and choose what to do next. Compassion does not remove the need for boundaries. You can recognize another person''s humanity and still say no, leave, or ask for help. It is not self-sacrifice or passivity; it is a way of responding from care and strength. A loving-kindness reflection might begin, “May I be safe and well,” and extend to others only as feels right.","point7":"Spiritually, compassion is central to many paths of awakening. Some traditions describe an underlying unity among beings; you can explore that idea without assuming every person is doing their best or that all harm comes from a lack of love. This card invites you to reduce shame and judgment where you can, while remaining honest about injustice and pain. Your compassion can make a difference in your relationships and community. Offer it freely, including to yourself, without making yourself responsible for healing the world."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '22', 'en', 'Unicorn of the Inner Child', '內在小孩獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Inner Child","Healing","Innocence","Play","Nurturing"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of the Inner Child"}', '{"point1":"This card connects you with the idea of an inner child, like the unicorn as a guardian of innocence. It invites you to notice younger parts of yourself that may still long to be seen, heard, comforted, or free to play. You might be carrying feelings from childhood that were not fully acknowledged, or simply miss the curiosity and spontaneity you once felt. Consider meeting those parts with care. You do not need to revisit painful memories alone or assume every current difficulty comes from childhood.","point2":"Dear soul, you may carry memories and feelings from different ages: fear of being left, a longing for approval, or sadness about something that happened. Past experiences can influence present reactions, though they are not the only explanation for them. This card offers a gentle image: the adult you can now offer care, reassurance, and protection to younger parts of yourself. Ask what you need today and what support might help. Inner-child work is one reflective approach, not a substitute for therapy or other care when old pain feels overwhelming.","point3":"The inner child''s energy can suggest innocence, curiosity, play, and vulnerability, like a child''s laughter or a carefree run. Reconnecting with it may bring up emotion, sadness, or a desire to play. Those feelings do not necessarily prove that a particular memory is accurate or that you are healing in a prescribed way. The image can also help you remember creativity, wonder, and vitality. Approach whatever arises with gentleness and let yourself choose what feels safe.","point4":"Your current lesson may be caring for younger parts of yourself while making room for play. Reflect on whether a present reaction connects with an old experience, without assuming every fear or relationship pattern has one childhood cause. You might imagine listening to a younger version of yourself and asking what they need. Offer yourself the care you can provide now, and seek help from a qualified professional if trauma or distress comes up. You can also reconnect with simple pleasures and curiosity.","point5":"Try a gentle inner-child reflection: look at a childhood photo if that feels comfortable, or imagine meeting a younger version of yourself. Ask what they might need and listen without forcing an answer. You could write a kind letter to your younger self or do an activity you enjoyed as a child, such as drawing, dancing, playing with clay, or watching a favorite show. Give yourself permission to enjoy something without a reason. Start with just a few minutes and stop if the exercise feels upsetting.","point6":"Inner-child reflection can bring up strong emotions or painful memories. Go slowly, and pause if you feel overwhelmed. If a younger part feels afraid, you might remind yourself of your present age and surroundings, then identify a safe person or professional you can contact. Notice when an old reaction may be present, but let your adult self make decisions using the information available now. Consider professional support for trauma. Reparenting yourself can be a long process; you do not have to do it perfectly or alone.","point7":"Spiritually, the inner child may represent qualities that feel close to your core: curiosity, wonder, and openness before you learned certain defenses. This card invites you to reconnect with what feels genuine, not to strip away every protection or deny what you have lived through. Caring for younger parts can help you feel more creative or compassionate, but it is not a duty to heal family or collective trauma. Offer yourself patience and choose what meaning this practice holds for you."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '23', 'en', 'Unicorn of Divine Timing', '神聖時機獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Timing","Patience","Trust","Readiness","Flow"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Divine Timing"}', '{"point1":"This card invites patience with the timing of change, like a unicorn following the seasons. Life has rhythms that may not match your urgency or expectations. A hope may take time, a path may still be unfolding, or circumstances may need to align. If it fits your beliefs, you can think of this as divine timing; you can also simply recognize that not everything is under your control. The card invites you to wait, prepare, and trust where you can without assuming that every wish is guaranteed or delayed for a reason.","point2":"Dear soul, you may be frustrated and asking, “Why hasn''t it happened?” or “Why does someone else have what I want?” It is understandable to want to push, speed things up, or control the timeline. This card gently suggests that some outcomes depend on readiness, circumstances, and other people. A delay does not always mean rejection or protection, and there may not be a hidden plan. Release the idea that something “should have happened already” if that helps, while allowing yourself to make choices and seek opportunities now.","point3":"The energy of patience can feel steady and receptive, like a seed growing underground or tides moving in their own cycles. It can help you act without fighting every delay. When you connect with this quality, you may feel less anxious and more able to focus on what is available today. Patience is not passivity: do what you can, then accept that some results and timing are beyond your control. You can trust yourself to adjust as circumstances change.","point4":"Your current lesson may be practicing patience without trying to control time. You may be used to pushing for quick results and feeling anxious about delays. Focus on what you can influence—your preparation, effort, and choices—rather than assuming you can control the result or when it arrives. Waiting can offer time to learn, rest, or reconsider, but it is not always a test or proof that a better outcome is coming. Look for ways to find peace in the “not yet” while still making plans.","point5":"For something you are waiting for, write down what is within your control and what is not. Ask, “How can I use this time to prepare or care for myself?” Take a useful step, learn something, or rest if needed. When anxiety rises, breathe slowly and remind yourself that you can respond to the situation as it develops. Reflect on past delays that led somewhere unexpected, but do not treat those memories as proof that every delay will be a blessing. Let them remind you that outcomes can be unpredictable.","point6":"Trusting timing can be difficult when you see others receive what you want, worry that time is running out, or feel afraid it may be too late. Acknowledge those feelings rather than shaming yourself for them. Your path is different from other people''s, but that does not mean a specific outcome is promised. If an opportunity is available, consider acting; if you need to wait, use active patience to prepare and seek support. You can change course if new information appears. Sometimes action is appropriate, and sometimes pausing is wise.","point7":"Spiritually, divine timing is one way to describe trust in an unfolding larger than your immediate view. You may find comfort in that belief, but it is not possible to know that every event is perfectly arranged or for the highest good. This card invites humility about what you cannot control and care for what you can. Your waiting is not necessarily serving a hidden plan. Let go of the demand to know exactly when something will happen, while staying engaged with your life and choices."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '24', 'en', 'Unicorn of Forgiveness', '寬恕獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Forgiveness","Release","Freedom","Peace","Healing"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Forgiveness"}', '{"point1":"This card raises the possibility of forgiveness, like a unicorn''s horn cleansing poison from a wound. Forgiveness may be a way to release some hold that anger or resentment has on you, but it is not a gift you owe to the person who hurt you. It does not mean what happened was acceptable or that you must forget, reconcile, or trust again. You can choose freedom and peace while maintaining distance and accountability. If you are not ready to forgive, you can begin by caring for yourself.","point2":"Dear soul, you may have carried anger or hurt for a long time—from neglect, betrayal, a friend''s actions, or a mistake of your own. Those feelings can keep an experience close, and they may also alert you to harm that needs attention. This card asks what holding the pain is doing for you and what it may be making harder. Forgiveness is not a requirement, and letting go may take time. You deserve support and the chance to live beyond what happened, at a pace you choose.","point3":"The energy of forgiveness may feel like setting down a heavy object, breathing more deeply, or opening a cage. It can mean choosing not to let an old injury define every part of your present. This does not erase what happened, excuse the person responsible, or guarantee that resentment disappears. You may need to revisit your feelings or keep firm boundaries. Forgiveness can be a personal process of reclaiming attention and peace, not a promise to restore a relationship.","point4":"Your current lesson may be exploring whether forgiveness could serve your well-being. Begin by acknowledging the harm honestly and noticing what you need now. If you choose to work toward forgiveness, it may be a gradual process with many returns to the decision. Self-forgiveness can also involve taking responsibility, making amends where possible, and learning from a mistake—not denying its impact. You can release some bitterness without absolving someone, and you are not obligated to forgive before you are ready.","point5":"If you want to explore forgiveness, write honestly about what happened and what you feel. Let anger and sadness exist without rushing to resolve them. You might write a private letter that you do not send, describing what you are ready to release and what boundaries you still need. A meditation can help you imagine setting down a burden, but you do not need to picture the other person or say “I forgive you.” Do not burn paper unless you can do so safely. Choose a practice that supports your freedom without pressuring you to reconnect.","point6":"Forgiveness is a process, and you do not have to feel different immediately. If anger returns, treat it as information about what you need rather than proof that you have failed. Some harm takes a long time to process, and professional support may help. You can begin with “I am willing to consider what release might mean for me.” Forgiving someone does not mean inviting them back into your life; boundaries can remain. Remember to offer yourself patience for your own mistakes and regrets while taking responsibility where appropriate.","point7":"Spiritually, forgiveness is central to many traditions, but no single spiritual perspective should be used to minimize harm. You do not have to believe that every painful experience was a lesson, or that a person who hurt you was doing their best. This card invites you to consider what peace and freedom mean to you. Let compassion coexist with justice, accountability, and self-protection. Your choice to forgive or not forgive belongs to you; you are not responsible for breaking a karmic cycle on behalf of others."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '25', 'en', 'Unicorn of Gratitude', '感恩獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Gratitude","Appreciation","Recognition","Abundance","Joy"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Gratitude"}', '{"point1":"This card is a strong reminder to notice and appreciate life''s blessings, like a unicorn receiving the world with grace. Gratitude is more than politeness or forced positive thinking; it is a way to pay attention to what you value. It may shift your perspective and help you notice sources of care, beauty, or support. Gratitude does not guarantee that the universe will send more or make hardship disappear. Today, you are invited to count what matters to you, even if it seems small.","point2":"Dear soul, it is easy to focus on what is missing—money, a relationship, work, or health—and overlook what you do have. The mind often searches for problems, but that does not mean you have caused hardship by focusing on it. This card gently invites you to widen your attention: perhaps to a breath, a place to rest, a meal, someone who cares, or simply making it through today. Noticing what you appreciate may create a more balanced view. Your difficulties remain real, and they deserve care too.","point3":"The energy of gratitude can feel warm, open, and appreciative, like sunlight reaching everything around you. It may bring a sense of fullness, a natural smile, or even tears of appreciation. When you connect with this quality, you may feel more present and recognize what is already meaningful. Gratitude does not require believing you have enough in every area, nor does it guarantee more abundance. It can offer a moment of joy in the present while leaving room for unmet needs and difficult feelings.","point4":"Your current lesson may be making gratitude a regular practice rather than an occasional gesture. You can train your attention to notice good things without ignoring problems. Ask what you appreciate even in a difficult season, but do not force yourself to call pain a blessing or a lesson. You might be grateful for clean water, a safe place, or people who support you, while still working toward better circumstances. Gratitude can help shift perspective; it is not a replacement for action, support, or change.","point5":"Try a simple gratitude practice: each morning, name three things you appreciate, and at night write down a few specific moments. Instead of “my family,” you might note a hug or a laugh you shared. Notice small things too: a cup of coffee, sunlight, a smile, or a deep breath. Tell someone what you value about them. In a difficult situation, ask whether anything deserves appreciation, without demanding that you find something. Let gratitude be honest and specific.","point6":"Gratitude takes practice, especially during hard times. When you feel caught in complaints or negativity, gently ask whether one small thing feels supportive or meaningful. Sometimes “at least” is all you can find, and that is enough; sometimes nothing comes to mind, and you do not need to force it. Avoid comparing your life to someone else''s. Gratitude is not denial or suppression, but a wider view that can include both difficulty and appreciation. A note or reminder may help you pause, and you can celebrate the practice without making it another obligation.","point7":"Spiritually, gratitude can be a way of acknowledging what feels sacred, generous, or miraculous in existence. You may experience it as prayer or appreciation from within your own beliefs. This card invites you to notice what is already here rather than treating gratitude as a way to manifest more. Your appreciation may encourage kindness and connection, but you are not responsible for raising the collective frequency. Let gratitude be one honest way of relating to your life, not a requirement to feel thankful for everything."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '26', 'en', 'Unicorn of Connection', '連結獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Connection","Relationships","Community","Belonging","Authenticity"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Connection"}', '{"point1":"This card is a call toward genuine connection, like the unicorn bridging the human and the celestial in myth. People need relationships and community, and feeling seen, understood, and accepted can be deeply nourishing. This is different from having many contacts or functional relationships. The card invites you to look for and care for connections where you can be more fully yourself. You are not an island, and belonging can grow through mutual respect, shared interests, and time.","point2":"Dear soul, you may feel lonely even when surrounded by people because connection depends on depth and authenticity, not numbers. Perhaps you have many acquaintances but few people who know you well, or you wear a mask in social situations. Past hurt may also lead you to keep distance for protection. You deserve relationships in which you can be respected and seen. Letting yourself be known can take courage, so choose someone who has earned your trust and share at a pace that feels safe.","point3":"The energy of connection can feel warm, open, and resonant, like two people meeting each other with attention. It can soften isolation and create a sense of belonging. When you connect with this quality, conversations may become more honest and eye contact more present. Authenticity does not mean sharing everything or dropping all defenses; healthy connection includes privacy and boundaries. The aim is mutual recognition: “I see you, and you see me,” with room for difference.","point4":"Your current lesson may be building and maintaining nourishing relationships. Notice which connections feel mutual and respectful, which feel superficial, and which leave you depleted. You can let go of relationships that no longer serve you, but consider context and communicate where it is safe and useful. Practice sharing a real feeling, challenge, or hope rather than showing only a polished image. Listen to understand, not only to prepare your reply. Genuine connection takes courage, vulnerability, and continued care from both people.","point5":"Think of people who make you feel seen or supported, and invest in one of those relationships with a call, a visit, or a meaningful conversation. If you trust someone, share something honest but not more than you are ready to share. Join a community centered on an interest or value, such as a book group, class, or volunteer project. Try asking a thoughtful question, like “What matters most to you right now?” Be present and listen. Small, consistent exchanges often build more trust than a single intense disclosure.","point6":"Building genuine connection takes time and involves some risk. Fear of rejection or being misunderstood is normal, but you can take small steps and notice how the other person responds. Not everyone will become a close friend, and you do not need everyone''s approval. Some relationships may require boundaries or distance, especially when you feel pressured to pretend or your limits are ignored. If you feel isolated, begin with a low-pressure online group or shared activity and let trust grow gradually. Appreciate each moment of mutual honesty.","point7":"Spiritually, connection can feel like souls recognizing one another, or it may simply mean shared humanity and care. This card invites you to be authentic with yourself and to seek people who respect that authenticity. You cannot guarantee who you will attract, and no one owes you a particular kind of connection. Each genuine relationship can challenge isolation and remind you that belonging is possible. Your openness may make it easier for others to be honest too. You are not alone in wanting connection, and you can build it one relationship at a time."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '27', 'en', 'Unicorn of Creativity', '創造力獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Creativity","Expression","Inspiration","Art","Talent"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Creativity"}', '{"point1":"This card is a powerful invitation to creativity, like the unicorn as an image of imagination and magic. You are capable of creating, whether or not you identify as an artist, musician, or writer. Creativity can be the language of your inner world, a way to express feelings, solve problems, or connect with what matters to you. You may have a perspective or skill waiting to be explored. Let yourself create without suppressing the impulse just because the result may not be perfect.","point2":"Dear soul, you may believe “I''m not creative” or “I have no talent,” but creativity has many forms beyond painting or writing. Cooking, gardening, decorating, problem-solving, caring for a child, or finding a new way to do something can all involve creativity. You may hold back because you fear criticism, feel your work is not good enough, or have little time. This card reminds you that creating can be for your own expression and enjoyment, not only for achievement or approval. Give yourself permission to experiment.","point3":"The energy of creativity can feel fluid, free, and full of ideas, like a river moving or a child immersed in play. You may feel excited, lose track of time, or want to move your hands. These experiences can come and go; you do not need to wait for a perfect state of inspiration. Creativity can involve both intuition and deliberate practice. Let ideas flow, then use reflection and revision to shape them. Making something can help you express emotion, though it is not a substitute for support when you need it.","point4":"Your current lesson may be allowing creativity to flow and expressing your distinctive ideas. You might need to quiet the inner critic, loosen perfectionism, or work through fear of judgment. Explore different mediums to find what you enjoy—writing, painting, dance, music, crafts, or something else entirely. Try creating for the process rather than the outcome. Make time and space for practice, even in small amounts. Your creative work can be meaningful without needing to become a career or a gift for others.","point5":"Choose one creative activity you have wanted to try and begin today without waiting to feel ready. Protect a small amount of time for it, even fifteen minutes. Doodle, free-write, dance, sing, cook, or build something just to see what happens. When you hear “This is terrible,” remind yourself that you are experimenting, not judging. Collect images or ideas that inspire you and connect with other people who enjoy making things. Celebrate the act of creating, however small.","point6":"Creating can mean meeting obstacles such as perfectionism or fear of criticism. Early attempts are often awkward; that is a normal part of learning. Give yourself permission to make something unfinished or imperfect, then decide later whether you want to revise or share it. You can protect your work while it is developing without hiding it forever. If you feel blocked, change the medium, place, or task, or take a break. Creativity benefits from nourishment—reading, nature, art, conversation, and rest. Notice each time you make something, no matter its size.","point7":"Spiritually, creativity may feel like participation in a sacred act of bringing an idea into form. You can hold that meaning while recognizing your own effort, influences, and practice. Your work can add beauty or perspective to the world, but creating is not an obligation or proof of your destiny. Let this card invite expression that feels authentic to you. Making something can be a form of reflection or meditation, and it can be valuable even if only you ever see it."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '28', 'en', 'Unicorn of Surrender', '臣服獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Surrender","Trust","Release","Flow","Peace"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Surrender"}', '{"point1":"This card offers a deep lesson in surrender, like a unicorn trusting the forest that shelters it. Its paradox is that strength can sometimes come from loosening control. Surrender is not giving up, weakness, or passivity; it can mean trusting yourself to meet what comes without needing to control every detail. When you grip too tightly, you may block your ability to adapt. This card invites you to release what is beyond your control and stay engaged with what you can do.","point2":"Dear soul, you may feel you need to plan everything, know the outcome, and manage every variable. That urge can come from fear of being hurt, failing, or facing pain. Yet no one can control every part of life, and trying to do so can exhaust you. Ask what you are afraid might happen if you loosen your grip, and whether there is a way to prepare for that possibility. Surrender can mean “I will do what I can, and accept that the rest is not entirely mine to decide.” It is a way to distinguish your choices from what belongs to others or to circumstance.","point3":"The energy of surrender can feel relaxed, fluid, and trusting, like floating in water or a branch moving with the wind. It may help release tension and soften resistance. When you connect with this quality, you might breathe more deeply and feel your shoulders drop. This is not helplessness or indifference; it is allowing yourself to stop fighting what you cannot change right now. You can let go while continuing to act where action is useful.","point4":"Your current lesson may be distinguishing what you can influence from what you cannot. You can often choose your actions and attitudes, but you cannot control other people''s choices, every outcome, or the past. Notice the cost of trying to manage everything, then experiment with releasing one part of it. Surrender to an emotion by allowing yourself to feel it, or to your body''s need for rest by taking a break. Trust need not mean believing in a higher plan; it can mean staying present and responding to reality as it is.","point5":"List what you are trying to control and separate it into what you can influence and what you cannot. Choose one useful action from the first list, then consider setting aside the rest for now. When anxiety rises, take a breath and ask, “What can I do in this moment?” Do that, then pause before taking on more. A body relaxation practice may help you notice tension. If you have resisted a situation, try saying, “This is where things stand right now,” without deciding that you must like it or accept future harm.","point6":"Surrender can feel frightening or vulnerable, especially if control has helped you feel safe. Move gently; it does not mean abandoning effort or responsibility. Keep a light hold: do what is yours to do without insisting on a specific result. If you notice yourself gripping again, remind yourself that you can reconsider and choose anew. Surrender does not mean dropping boundaries or letting someone mistreat you. A calming phrase such as “I can do my part and let the rest unfold” may help, if it feels true to you.","point7":"Spiritually, surrender can mean releasing the wish to control life and making room for trust in a larger presence, if that fits your beliefs. This card invites cooperation with life rather than a claim that the universe has a perfect plan. Open hands can receive, but they can also take action and ask for what you need. Let go where you can, keep your boundaries, and remain willing to act. Trust can be a relationship with uncertainty, not a guarantee that miracles will follow."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '29', 'en', 'Unicorn of Strength', '力量獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Strength","Resilience","Courage","Steadiness","Perseverance"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Strength"}', '{"point1":"This card reminds you of the strength you carry, like a unicorn that is gentle yet steadfast. Strength is not only physical force, aggression, or dominance; it can be inner steadiness, emotional resilience, courage in the face of fear, and the ability to find your center during a storm. You may have more capacity than you realize, built through challenges you have already faced. Strength does not mean you will overcome every challenge alone; it can include resting, adapting, and asking for help.","point2":"Dear soul, you may feel weak or overwhelmed by what is in front of you. Life''s setbacks or other people''s words can make it difficult to remember your own capability. Look back at challenges you have navigated and recognize what helped you through. This is not proof that you must be able to endure anything; it is evidence that you have learned and adapted before. Your strength is not something others must grant you, and you are allowed to lean on people who support you.","point3":"The energy of strength can feel stable and grounded, like a mountain or a tree with deep roots. It can come from a connection to your values and sense of self. When you connect with this quality, you may feel more upright, breathe more deeply, or remember that you can take one step. This is not aggression or becoming hard; it can be a flexible strength, like water shaping stone or bamboo bending without breaking. A steady inner voice may say, “I can meet this with support.”","point4":"Your current lesson may be building and reconnecting with inner strength. Strength is not only muscle or power over others; it can be knowing what matters to you and staying connected to it. Recall moments when you faced a difficulty, weathered a storm, or acted with courage, and use those memories as anchors. Emotional resilience does not mean avoiding feelings or never being overwhelmed. It can mean letting yourself feel, seeking support, and taking time to recover before deciding what comes next.","point5":"Write down five difficult moments you have navigated and what helped you through each one. You might create a grounded affirmation, such as “I have handled hard things, and I can ask for help with this.” Stand comfortably, feel your feet on the floor, and take a few slow breaths. Choose one small action that takes courage. When fear says “I can''t,” ask whether there is a manageable first step. Connect with people, music, memories, or practices that help you feel supported and capable.","point6":"Building strength is a long process, not a single decision. Feeling weak sometimes does not mean you lack strength; it may mean you need rest, support, or time to recover. True strength is not the same as becoming rigid. Boundaries can be strong without building walls, and vulnerability can take courage. You do not need to prove your strength to anyone or compare it with someone else''s. Notice your own ways of coping, adapting, and reaching for help.","point7":"Spiritually, strength may reflect a belief in an enduring inner essence. This card invites you to remember your values and capacity without claiming that no one can harm you or that every challenge was chosen by your soul. You are not responsible for everything that happens to you. Your resilience may inspire others, but you do not need to become invulnerable or save anyone. Let strength include gentleness toward yourself, connection with others, and the freedom to seek help."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '30', 'en', 'Unicorn of Intuition', '直覺獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Intuition","Inner Knowing","Guidance","Insight","Trust"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Intuition"}', '{"point1":"This card invites you to pay attention to intuition, like a unicorn sensing what may not be immediately visible. You can sometimes know something before you can explain how, drawing on subtle cues, past experience, bodily sensations, dreams, or reflection. Inner knowing can be one source of information, alongside logic and evidence. Listen to what you notice without assuming every feeling is a message from a higher self or that intuition is always right. Let it prompt useful questions and exploration.","point2":"Dear soul, you may ignore or distrust a feeling that something is off, or an impression that you know what matters to you. Perhaps you rely heavily on logic or have been told you are overthinking when you tried to share a concern. This card gives you permission to take your feelings seriously. They are real experiences and may contain information, though they can also be shaped by fear, hope, stress, or past events. Consider your intuition along with facts and trusted perspectives, especially for important decisions.","point3":"The energy of intuition can feel subtle and quiet, like a compass pointing toward a direction. It may show up as a bodily sensation, an image, a dream, or a sudden thought. These signals can be useful prompts, but they do not have universal meanings: an expanded feeling is not always “yes,” and a tight feeling is not always “no.” Give yourself quiet enough to notice what is happening, then ask what else could explain it. Reflection and evidence can help you understand an impression.","point4":"Your current lesson may be noticing, evaluating, and making room for intuition. Practice asking how a choice feels before you decide, then identify the reasons behind that feeling. Distinguish intuition from fear by considering the context, but do not assume one is always calm and the other always loud. Try low-stakes choices first and reflect on what you noticed and how it turned out. For major decisions, combine feelings with relevant evidence, time, and advice from trusted people; do not rely on a first reaction alone.","point5":"Create a quiet moment and ask yourself what you need to consider, without expecting a special answer. Notice your first reaction when you meet someone or face a choice, then write it down alongside the facts you know. Keep an intuition journal if useful, returning later to see what you learned rather than only counting hits. Try a body scan and notice what sensations arise, without treating them as instructions. Coincidences can feel meaningful, but they are not reliable predictions. Let curiosity guide you instead of demanding certainty.","point6":"Learning to trust intuition takes practice and patience. At first it may be hard to distinguish it from fear, hope, or imagination. Notice what you feel, what you believe it means, and what evidence supports that interpretation. Your first impression may be helpful, but later reflection can add important information. If you ignored a feeling, review the situation without blaming yourself; you may learn more about your patterns. Quiet can help you reflect, but busyness or media are not inherently contaminating. Build trust gradually, starting with decisions where the risks are low.","point7":"Spiritually, you may understand intuition as communication with a higher self, guides, or a sacred source. This card honors that belief as a personal framework, not as a guarantee that an inner message is infallible. Your intuition is one part of how you navigate life, alongside reason, experience, and other people. Use it to ask better questions, check your assumptions, and choose thoughtfully. You are not alone in making decisions, and it is okay to seek outside guidance. Trust yourself enough to listen, and stay open to being mistaken."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '31', 'en', 'Unicorn of Purpose', '使命獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Purpose","Meaning","Calling","Contribution","Direction"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Purpose"}', '{"point1":"This card invites you to reflect on your sense of purpose, like a unicorn embodying a distinctive reason for being. You do not have to believe you arrived in the world with a predetermined mission to know that your life has meaning. Purpose may come through your gifts, interests, relationships, and the contributions you choose to make. It is not necessarily about achievement or fame; it can be about living in a way that feels true to you. This card asks you to explore what matters and how you want to express it.","point2":"Dear soul, you may feel lost or unsure why you are here. Perhaps you have tried many things without finding a lasting sense of fit, or you know what draws you but are afraid to follow it because it feels risky or unconventional. Purpose may be found in what makes you feel engaged, even when it is difficult, but it does not have to be one fixed calling. Experiences of pain can sometimes shape what you care about, yet you do not need to turn your suffering into a gift for others. Take a step toward what feels meaningful, and let your understanding evolve.","point3":"A sense of purpose can feel like meaning, direction, or alignment: “This matters to me.” It may bring energy and motivation, even when the work is challenging. You might feel both excited and nervous because something is important. Like a river moving toward the sea or a seed growing into a plant, these images can suggest development, but your path need not be predetermined. Purpose can change as your life changes. Listen to what feels meaningful while leaving room for curiosity and revision.","point4":"Your current lesson may be discovering and living by what gives your life meaning. Explore what makes you feel engaged, what you might do without external praise, and what themes keep returning. Look at your life story—your difficulties, gifts, passions, and recurring interests—not as proof of a destiny, but as useful clues. Do not compare your purpose with someone else''s. Every person''s contributions can matter in different ways. You can begin living more intentionally even before you have a clear answer.","point5":"Write about a few questions: What would I like to do if money were not the only factor? What makes me feel engaged? What change or problem do I care about? What have my experiences taught me about what matters? Look for recurring themes, then list your strengths—not only skills, but also qualities such as empathy, humor, or perseverance. You might ask someone you trust what they value about you. Rather than imagining what you want people to say at your funeral, consider what you want to contribute this week.","point6":"Discovering purpose is a journey, not necessarily a single revelation. What feels meaningful can change across stages of life. You do not have to wait until everything is clear; follow curiosity one step at a time and learn along the way. Purpose need not be your job. It may also show up in how you care, create, or participate in community. Big and small contributions can both matter. If fear asks who you are to try, answer by taking a modest, thoughtful step. Living with purpose is a practice, not a final destination.","point7":"Spiritually, you may understand purpose as a mission your soul chose before birth. This card can honor that belief as a source of meaning without claiming that your path is predetermined or that every hardship was chosen. You do not need to fulfill a cosmic contract to deserve a place in the world. Your particular gifts and choices can contribute to the lives around you. Trust yourself to explore what you value, and let your purpose be something you shape over time."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '32', 'en', 'Unicorn of Peace', '和平獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Peace","Stillness","Calm","Serenity","Centering"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Peace"}', '{"point1":"This card invites you to find moments of inner peace, like a unicorn holding stillness within a chaotic world. Peace does not depend on everything around you being perfect, and it does not mean there is no storm. It can be a moment of steadiness from which you choose how to respond. This is not a guarantee that you can always feel calm, nor does it mean external problems are unimportant. The card invites you to nurture a place of grounding inside yourself and return to it when possible.","point2":"Dear soul, you may be living with a lot of inner activity: anxious thoughts, strong emotions, or endless planning. It is tempting to think, “When this problem is solved, then I will have peace,” but life often brings new concerns. This card gently suggests that you can practice calm even while circumstances are unsettled. Peace is not a way to escape or deny what is happening; it can help you respond from a more grounded place. You do not have to choose calm in every moment or blame yourself when you cannot.","point3":"The energy of peace can feel quiet and spacious, a moment of stillness even when there is noise around you. Slow breathing or relaxing your shoulders may help you notice that feeling. This quality can soften tension and make room for presence rather than urgency. When you connect with it, you might remind yourself, “I am here, in this moment.” Peace does not mean that everything is fine or that you must accept harmful circumstances; it means allowing a pause before deciding what to do.","point4":"Your current lesson may be cultivating inner steadiness without relying on external life being completely settled. Notice whether resistance to reality is adding to your distress, and see whether acknowledging “this is how things are right now” helps you find your next step. Acceptance does not mean approval or giving up. You can return to the present through breathing, meditation, nature, or gratitude if those practices help. Use them as anchors, not as a reason to ignore problems that need action.","point5":"Try a short peace practice today: pause once in a while, close your eyes if comfortable, and take a few slow breaths. When you feel unsettled, name what is happening and remind yourself, “This is the situation right now; I can choose my next step.” Create a quiet place in your home if you have room. Take a walk in nature or sit without your phone for a few minutes. When triggered, pause before responding. A phrase like “May you be safe; may I be safe” can support goodwill without requiring reconciliation.","point6":"Cultivating peace is an ongoing practice because life continues to challenge your center. You will have moments when you lose your calm; that is normal. Peace does not mean having no feelings or thoughts, and anger can alert you to a boundary or injustice. Let emotions exist without being defined by them, and make room to respond honestly. Sometimes protecting your peace means leaving a harmful situation, setting limits, or asking for help. Prioritize calm without using it to silence yourself or others.","point7":"Spiritually, you may experience peace as a deep part of your nature or a connection to the sacred. This card invites you to return to stillness when you can, but does not claim that distress is merely superficial or that you are always peaceful beneath it. Your calm may help you relate to others with more care, though it is not your job to absorb or resolve collective anxiety. Let peace be a practice of presence, truthful action, and compassion—not a demand to remain serene at all costs."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '33', 'en', 'Unicorn of Authenticity', '真實獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Authenticity","Honesty","Genuineness","Courage","Selfhood"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Authenticity"}', '{"point1":"This card calls you toward authenticity, like a unicorn that does not pretend to be another creature. Your strength and joy may grow when you live closer to your values and express who you are. Not who you think you should be, or who others expect, but the person you are becoming. Masks, people-pleasing, and pretending can take energy, yet they may also have helped you stay safe or belong. This card invites you to explore what feels genuine and to express it with care.","point2":"Dear soul, you may have been pretending for so long that you are unsure what feels like the real you. You may have learned to fit in, seek approval, or hide feelings to avoid conflict. Shifting how you act in different settings is normal; it does not mean you are false. But if you feel exhausted or lonely because people do not know you well, consider sharing a little more with someone trustworthy. Some people may not respond as you hope, and others may meet you with care. Choose vulnerability thoughtfully.","point3":"The energy of authenticity can feel freeing and aligned, like taking a deep breath after wearing something too tight. It may bring relief from constantly monitoring how you appear, along with a desire to be seen. It can also bring fear: “What if they see the real me?” Authenticity does not require revealing everything or being unfiltered with everyone. You can be true to yourself while choosing what to share, when, and with whom. “This is who I am today” can be enough.","point4":"Your current lesson may be recognizing and expressing more of your authentic self. Notice where you feel you are wearing a mask—in work, family, friendships, or online—and ask what you are protecting. Explore your real feelings, beliefs, hopes, and fears without judging them. Then share selectively, perhaps first with a person or in a setting that feels safe. Speaking honestly, admitting imperfection, and allowing yourself to be known can take courage, but you are not obligated to disclose private parts of yourself.","point5":"Practice authenticity in one small, safe situation today. You might say “Actually, I feel…” instead of giving an automatic “I''m fine,” or tell a trusted person about something you usually hide. Write a list of your preferences, dislikes, quirks, hopes, and fears to learn more about yourself. Before people-pleasing, ask what response would reflect your values while considering your needs and responsibilities. You can accept yourself without needing to post private details online or make a dramatic change.","point6":"Living authentically is an ongoing practice that takes courage. There is a real risk of criticism or rejection, so choose where and with whom you share. It is not the case that anyone who leaves was never meant to be in your life; relationships can change for many reasons. Authenticity also does not mean dropping boundaries or expressing every feeling without regard for others. Your understanding of yourself can evolve, and it is okay for what feels true now to differ from what felt true last year. Celebrate each honest moment.","point7":"Spiritually, authenticity can mean aligning your life with what feels most true and meaningful to you. You are worthy of care without needing to be perfect or perform a role. This card invites self-respect, not self-indulgence: your choices also affect other people. When you are honest with care, you may make it easier for others to be genuine too. Your distinct perspective can contribute to the world, but authenticity is a choice you make for yourself, not a destiny you must prove."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '34', 'en', 'Unicorn of Boundaries', '界限獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Boundaries","Protection","Self-Love","Saying No","Respect"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Boundaries"}', '{"point1":"This card offers an important lesson in healthy boundaries, like a unicorn guarding a sacred space. Boundaries are not selfishness, coldness, or a lack of love; they can express self-respect and care. You cannot and need not say yes to everyone and everything. Your time, energy, body, and attention matter. Without limits, you may become depleted or lose sight of your own needs. This card invites you to practice clear, firm, and respectful boundaries that protect your well-being.","point2":"Dear soul, you may struggle to say no, feel responsible for keeping everyone happy, or sacrifice your needs to avoid conflict. Perhaps you fear that a boundary will make someone angry, cause them to leave, or make you seem selfish. You may not have been taught that your comfort and needs matter. This card reminds you that you have a right to protect your time, body, energy, and privacy. “No” can be a complete answer, though you may choose to explain more when it is safe or useful.","point3":"The energy of boundaries can feel clear, steady, and self-respecting, like a wall around a garden or the skin protecting a body. It is not aggression or hardness; it can be a gentle but firm “this is okay, and that is not.” When you connect with this quality, you may feel more able to speak plainly and protect your needs. Boundaries can help create safety, but they do not control other people''s behavior. You can decide what you will do if a limit is not respected.","point4":"Your current lesson may be identifying, setting, and maintaining healthy boundaries. Notice where you feel intruded upon, resentful, or pressured to say yes when you mean no. Give yourself permission to set a limit; it is not inherently selfish. Communicate it simply: “I can''t do that,” “I need time alone,” or “Please don''t speak to me that way.” When it is safe, repeat the boundary consistently. You can teach people how you expect to be treated, but you cannot guarantee how they will respond.","point5":"Identify one situation where you want a clearer boundary. Decide what you are and are not willing to do, then communicate it briefly and calmly: “I can''t take this on,” “I need some time to myself,” or “Please stop.” Practice saying no in a low-stakes situation, such as declining an offer you do not want. If guilt appears, remind yourself that caring for your own needs is allowed. Write down boundaries that are important to you, and respect other people''s boundaries as well.","point6":"Setting boundaries can be difficult, especially if you are used to people-pleasing or caregiving. Guilt, fear, and unease are common, but they do not automatically mean you are doing something wrong. Other people are responsible for how they respond to your limits. If someone becomes angry or manipulative, take that seriously and consider support or a safety plan; their reaction alone does not tell the whole story, but repeated disrespect may show that stronger steps are needed. You do not owe a debate about every boundary. Start small and recognize each time you protect your needs.","point7":"Spiritually, boundaries can be a way of honoring your body, time, and life as worthy of care. Caring for others while abandoning yourself is not the only form of service. Love can include self-love, and sustainable care starts with noticing your own capacity. When you set limits, you may model respect for yourself and others. Protecting your energy can help you remain engaged, but you are allowed to rest or step back. A boundary is a practical act of self-respect, not a measure of your spiritual worth."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '35', 'en', 'Unicorn of Patience', '耐心獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Patience","Waiting","Trust","Timing","Growth"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Patience"}', '{"point1":"This card is a reminder of patience, like a unicorn understanding that growth takes time. In a world of instant results and constant responses, patience can be a valuable quality. Relationships deepen, healing unfolds, skills develop, and plans mature at different paces. You cannot rush every meaningful process, but you can decide how to use the time. This card invites you to work with life''s rhythms where possible instead of fighting every delay.","point2":"Dear soul, you may feel impatient with the process, other people, yourself, or the time it takes to see results. You might want to skip difficult parts, avoid learning, or arrive at the destination immediately. Impatience can show up as anxiety, frustration, pushing too hard, or giving up early. Ask what is making you feel rushed. Perhaps you are struggling to be present while longing for a different situation. Patience can be a way to stay engaged with the present and trust your ability to respond as things develop.","point3":"The energy of patience can feel steady, present, and accepting, like a gardener tending a seed or waiting for a new season. It is not passive stagnation; it can include preparing, learning, and growing while you wait. When you connect with this quality, you may breathe more slowly and feel less urgency. Patience might sound like “I can take my time with this.” Some things do have a natural pace, while others can be changed through action. Notice which is true in your situation.","point4":"Your current lesson may be practicing patience, especially in uncertainty or while waiting. Notice the cost of impatience: rushed decisions, damaging something still developing, missing parts of the process, or living under constant stress. When you feel uncomfortable, try pausing before you rush to fix or change everything. Ask what this period offers and how you might use it. Patience is not doing nothing; it can mean taking the steps available and allowing time to do what you cannot.","point5":"When impatience arises—while waiting in a line, for a reply, or for change—notice it and take a slow breath. Use the feeling as a reminder to return to the present rather than as a problem to condemn. Try slowing down one ordinary activity, such as eating, walking, or speaking. Be patient with someone who is learning, including yourself, while still communicating your needs. Ask what you can learn or do during the wait. Appreciate the process where you can, not only the result.","point6":"Patience can be hard, particularly when time feels short or circumstances are urgent. It is normal to lose patience; you can begin again without criticizing yourself. Some things respond to your actions, while other people''s growth, external timing, and organic processes do not fully belong to you. Patience does not mean waiting forever for something unlikely to happen. Give a situation reasonable time, gather information, and reassess. Treating yourself kindly when you are impatient is part of the practice.","point7":"Spiritually, patience may reflect trust in divine timing or in a larger rhythm of life. Seasons, tides, and life cycles can remind you that not everything unfolds on demand, but they do not prove that every event happens at a perfect time. This card invites you to be present and make room for uncertainty. Your patience may help you be a steady presence for others, but you are not responsible for soothing everyone. Practice patience while staying attentive to your needs and choices."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '36', 'en', 'Unicorn of Confidence', '自信獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Confidence","Self-Worth","Assurance","Self-Belief","Strength"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Confidence"}', '{"point1":"This card calls you toward inner confidence, like a unicorn walking with quiet steadiness. Confidence does not have to come from achievements, approval, or flawless performance; it can grow from recognizing your worth as a person. You are enough without having to prove your value. This is not arrogance or superiority, but a grounded sense that you deserve to be here and can learn what you need. This card invites you to build confidence from within, one experience at a time.","point2":"Dear soul, you may doubt yourself, rely on outside approval, compare yourself with others, or feel like an impostor. It is easy to imagine, “Once I succeed, change my appearance, or find love, then I''ll feel confident.” But a particular achievement may not silence every doubt. You deserve respect now, before reaching a future milestone. Confidence is not always an inborn trait; it can be practiced. Begin by noticing the ways you already show up, learn, and keep going.","point3":"The energy of confidence can feel steady, clear, and self-assured, like a rooted tree or a calm lake reflecting what is there. It can come from a sense of your own values rather than outside proof. When you connect with this quality, you may stand a little taller or feel a quiet “I can try.” You do not need to be loud or certain about everything. Confidence can include acknowledging what you know, what you can learn, and where you need help.","point4":"Your current lesson may be building healthy confidence and self-worth from within. Instead of waiting for approval from others, practice recognizing your own effort and strengths. When your inner critic says “You''re not good enough,” ask whether that is a fact or a familiar judgment. Recall qualities you value, things you have learned, and difficulties you have navigated—not as proof that your worth must be earned, but as reminders of your capabilities. Let go of comparison and focus on your own growth.","point5":"Write down ten qualities you appreciate in yourself, including character traits, skills, or ways you treat people. Read them aloud if that feels comfortable. Try a grounded affirmation such as “I am learning, I deserve respect, and I can take a next step.” Look back at a challenge you have met to remind yourself that you can adapt. Do one small thing outside your comfort zone, with reasonable care. When comparison appears, remind yourself that another person''s path is not yours. Celebrate small wins without using them as a measure of your value.","point6":"Confidence is an ongoing practice, and life will test it. Failure or criticism does not define your worth. Setbacks can offer information for learning, but you do not have to reframe every painful experience as a lesson. Confidence is not the absence of fear; it can mean acting thoughtfully while afraid. You can reduce dependence on constant approval while still accepting sincere compliments—“Thank you” is enough. Confident people can also admit they do not know or have made a mistake. Your basic worth does not need proof.","point7":"Spiritually, you may connect confidence with a belief in your sacred worth or your relationship to a larger source. This card invites quiet assurance, not a claim that you are perfect or beyond human limits. You can honor your distinct gifts and still learn from others. Your confidence may give others permission to believe in themselves, but you do not need to be an example for everyone. Trust your capacity while remaining humble, connected, and open to growth."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '37', 'en', 'Unicorn of Presence', '臨在獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Presence","The Present","Mindfulness","Awareness","This Moment"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Presence"}', '{"point1":"This card is a strong invitation to meet the present moment, like a unicorn giving its full attention to where it is. The past cannot be changed, and the future has not happened yet; the present is where you can notice what is here and choose what to do. Life, strength, peace, and joy are not available only now, but attention to the present can help you experience them. If you are caught in regret or worry, this card gently invites you to return to what is happening around you and within you.","point2":"Dear soul, your mind may spend much of its time in the past—replaying, missing, or remembering—or in the future—worrying, planning, or anticipating. You might think about work while eating or about somewhere else while spending time with someone. That can leave you feeling anxious or disconnected. This card reminds you that life is also happening now, in ordinary moments. You do not need to force your mind to stay present constantly; notice when it wanders and gently return to this moment.","point3":"The energy of presence can feel clear, quiet, and attentive, like an animal alert to its surroundings or a child absorbed in play. It may interrupt mental chatter and bring you closer to direct experience. When you connect with this quality, time may seem to slow down, your senses may feel sharper, or you may simply notice, “I am here.” Thoughts will still come; mindfulness is not an empty mind. It is the practice of noticing what is happening without needing to follow every thought.","point4":"Your current lesson may be practicing awareness of the present. Regret about the past and worry about the future can be painful, but not all distress comes from being unmindful; real circumstances may also need care or action. Try returning to your breath, senses, and body when you notice your thoughts wandering. Gently say, “I am here, now.” Presence is not a goal you achieve once; it is a repeated return, and each moment offers another chance to notice.","point5":"Try a few simple presence practices today. Pause now and then to take three comfortable breaths and feel your body. When eating, slow down enough to notice taste and texture. In a conversation, give the other person your attention without planning your reply, while still honoring your own needs. Do one task at a time if practical. Feel your feet on the ground, or notice the sounds around you. When your mind goes to the past or future, acknowledge it and gently return to what is happening here.","point6":"Presence is a lifelong practice because the mind naturally wanders. Do not judge yourself for noticing distraction; returning is part of mindfulness. Being present does not mean avoiding memory or planning. You can learn from the past and prepare for the future while staying connected to what you are doing now. Some moments are painful, boring, or difficult to sit with; you can choose support or an appropriate action rather than forcing yourself to endure them. The present can be a source of information, not a command to stay still.","point7":"Spiritually, presence is central to many paths of awakening. You may experience the present as a doorway to connection with the sacred, or simply as a way to engage more fully with life. This card invites you to notice what is happening without treating memories, plans, or thoughts as your whole identity. You do not need to make the ego disappear or become a pure observer. You are a person with a past and future, meeting this moment as best you can. Return to now when it helps, and let it be enough for this moment."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '38', 'en', 'Unicorn of Release', '釋放獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Release","Letting Go","Clearing","Freedom","Goodbye"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Release"}', '{"point1":"This card offers a deep invitation to release what you are ready to put down, like a unicorn making room for new growth. Holding tightly to a relationship, belief, possession, identity, emotion, or expectation can sometimes add to pain, especially when it no longer serves you. Life changes, and you may be ready to make space for something new. Letting go is not always the right choice, and it need not happen all at once. Consider what you want to loosen and what you still need to protect or honor.","point2":"Dear soul, you may know that something needs to change but still feel attached to what is familiar, fear the emptiness, or grieve what has passed. You may be holding onto possessions, a relationship, hurt, resentment, or an old self-image. This card gently asks what holding on is doing for you and whether it is also making something harder. Release is not always a loss; sometimes it creates room. But you do not have to trust that the “right” thing will arrive afterward. You can choose change because it better fits your needs now.","point3":"The energy of release can feel lighter and freer, like breathing out stale air or a tree dropping leaves in autumn. It may involve unclenching, relaxing, and opening your hands. When you connect with this quality, you may feel relief, or grief may arise too. Both can be part of letting go. Release does not erase what happened or mean that something never mattered. It can mean deciding not to carry it in the same way, with support and time as needed.","point4":"Your current lesson may be noticing what you are ready to release. Look honestly at relationships that drain you, beliefs that limit you, possessions that crowd your space, or feelings you are holding tightly. Do not assume that a difficult relationship must end; you might need a boundary, honest conversation, or outside support. It can hurt to let go of something that once mattered. You can appreciate what it meant and still decide what is healthy for you now. Release may be an act of care for yourself, not a judgment of the past.","point5":"Choose one area to reflect on: possessions, relationships, beliefs, or emotions. Identify one small thing you are ready to release. You might donate an item you no longer use, set a boundary, or write down a belief you want to question. If you have strong feelings, write a private letter to them and keep it, tear it up, or dispose of it safely if that feels meaningful. A simple phrase such as “Thank you for what this taught me; I am ready to change my relationship to it” can mark an intention. Let practical steps accompany any ritual.","point6":"Release is a process, not always a single event. You may need to return to it, especially with grief, painful memories, or long relationships. If you find yourself holding on again, meet yourself gently and ask what you need. Letting go does not mean forgetting or no longer caring; it can mean loosening the hold something has on your present. You may feel emptiness afterward, and you do not have to rush to fill it. Give yourself time to notice what comes next, without expecting the universe to replace what you released.","point7":"Spiritually, release can connect with teachings about impermanence and change. You do not have to believe that attachment is the cause of all suffering or that people and possessions are merely borrowed. This card invites you to notice where holding on is helping and where it is hurting. Each act of release may create room for change, but it is not a spiritual test or proof of maturity. Let yourself choose what to keep, what to change, and what to set down with compassion."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '39', 'en', 'Unicorn of Renewal', '更新獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Renewal","Rebirth","Freshness","Vitality","Restoration"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Renewal"}', '{"point1":"This card celebrates renewal, like a unicorn bringing the freshness of spring to a forest. You may be entering a period of new energy after a demanding season, or simply finding a chance to begin again. Like spring following winter or rest helping a tired body, renewal may come through time, care, and changed routines. It does not have to be dramatic or guaranteed. This card invites you to welcome a fresh start and support the conditions that help you recover and reconnect with what gives you energy.","point2":"Dear soul, you may feel tired, depleted, or disconnected from interests that once mattered to you. The weight of daily life or caring for others may have left little room for your own needs. Perhaps your old way of doing things is no longer sustainable. This card offers encouragement: recovery and renewal may be possible, though they may take time and support. You do not have to stay exhausted forever, and you also do not need to force yourself to feel energetic right away. Give yourself the time and space you need.","point3":"The energy of renewal can feel fresh, light, and full of life, like the first flower of spring or clean air after rain. It may bring hope, interest, or a wish to move and create again. When you connect with this quality, notice any small shifts in energy or mood without expecting them to continue perfectly. A renewed sense of vitality can be encouraging, but it is not proof that a health concern has resolved. Seek appropriate care if fatigue or loss of interest is persistent or concerning.","point4":"Your current lesson may be allowing and supporting your own cycles of renewal. Rest is not a luxury; it can be one important need among many. Look for conditions that help you recover: adequate sleep, time outdoors, nourishing meals, joyful activities, or supportive people. Consider reducing commitments or changing routines that leave you depleted, where possible. Listen to your body and give it care rather than pushing through every signal. Taking care of yourself is not selfish; it can help make your life more sustainable.","point5":"Support renewal with one restorative choice today. Take a genuine break, spend time in nature, or do something that tends to bring you energy—movement, music, dance, singing, or making something. Clear a small part of your space if that feels refreshing. Try a new activity or shift one routine. Eat and drink in ways that support your needs. Connect with someone who encourages you, and set limits where you can with demands that drain you. Let yourself say, “I am making room for renewal,” without expecting a sudden transformation.","point6":"Renewal has its own pace and cannot always be forced, though you can support it. Sometimes rest needs to come before motivation returns. If you do not notice change right away, that does not mean you have failed or that nothing is happening. Avoid returning to an exhausting pattern before you have had time to recover. Small, regular moments of care may be more sustainable than waiting until you are depleted. Notice gradual changes and seek help if you continue to feel unable to function or persistently unwell. You deserve more than simply surviving, but recovery may take support.","point7":"Spiritually, renewal reflects life''s cycles—seasons, moon phases, sleep and waking, endings and beginnings. You are part of these rhythms, not a machine that must produce continuously. This card invites you to align with cycles of effort and rest without assuming every dark period guarantees a spring. Each fresh start can be a chance to grow, and your renewal may positively affect those around you. Welcome new beginnings at a pace that honors your real needs and circumstances."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '40', 'en', 'Unicorn of Harmony', '和諧獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Harmony","Coordination","Balance","Flow","Alignment"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Harmony"}', '{"point1":"This card calls you toward a more harmonious life, like a unicorn in a balanced forest. Harmony does not mean that differences or conflict disappear; it means different parts can work together, like instruments in an orchestra. When life feels more aligned, you may experience less friction between your values, relationships, and surroundings. Conflict can be tiring, but it can also reveal needs that have not been heard. This card invites you to notice where an adjustment might help create more cooperation and balance.","point2":"Dear soul, you may feel discord in your life: an inner conflict between what you want and what you do, relationship tension, or an imbalance such as too much work and too little rest. These strains can create ongoing stress. You may also be pushing your own will and finding more resistance. This card suggests that harmony often takes listening, adjustment, compromise, and common ground rather than forcing everyone to agree. It can begin with aligning your choices more closely with your values, then extend into your relationships and routines.","point3":"The energy of harmony can feel fluid, coordinated, and beautiful, like dancers moving together or melodies blending. It may help different parts of life support one another. When you connect with this quality, you may notice ease, rhythm, or smoother communication. Harmony does not mean everything is always in the right place or that all friction is gone. It is an ongoing way of responding to differences and making adjustments that work for the people involved.","point4":"Your current lesson may be creating and maintaining harmony within yourself and your relationships. First notice where tension, imbalance, or friction is coming from. Consider whether your actions align with your values, whether your time includes both work and rest, and whether you are giving and receiving. In relationships, communicate, listen, and look for shared needs without giving up important boundaries. In your environment, a calm and welcoming space may help. Harmony takes awareness and effort, but it does not require self-erasure.","point5":"Take a quick look at major areas of life—work, relationships, health, play, and meaning. Which need more attention, and which are taking too much? Choose one small adjustment today. In a tense relationship, try a sincere conversation: listen to understand, then share your own perspective and look for common ground. Check whether one action fits your values. Tidy a space if that would help you feel settled. Stretch or move in a way that feels good. Focus on one task at a time when possible, rather than adding more activity to an already busy day.","point6":"Harmony is maintained through ongoing adjustment, not achieved once and kept forever. Life changes, so needs and priorities change too. When you feel friction or stress, ask what might need to shift. Sometimes harmony requires ending a relationship or changing an environment, but it may also mean setting a boundary or having an honest conversation. Harmony is not silencing your own voice or always compromising; it respects and integrates different needs. Your inner steadiness can help you respond, but you are not responsible for controlling everyone else''s behavior.","point7":"Spiritually, harmony may reflect a sense of order or balance in nature. This card invites you to see conflict not only as something to avoid, but also as information about where adjustment or growth may be needed. Harmony is not guaranteed to return automatically; it may take work, support, and changed conditions. Your choices can contribute to more cooperation around you, but you cannot create collective harmony alone. Seek coordination without erasing difference, and let beauty emerge from people and parts working together."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '41', 'en', 'Unicorn of Inspiration', '靈感獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Inspiration","Encouragement","Creativity","Insight","Ideas"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Inspiration"}', '{"point1":"This card celebrates the flow of inspiration, like a unicorn carrying a spark of creative possibility. Inspiration may feel as if it arrives from beyond you, or it may grow from curiosity, experience, and the things you notice. It can appear as a sudden idea, an urge to create, an insight into a problem, or an artistic image. This card invites you to stay open to those sparks and explore them. You do not need to know whether inspiration is a message from the universe in order to make something meaningful with it.","point2":"Dear soul, perhaps you are waiting for inspiration to happen, or you have been too busy, analytical, or tired to notice a new idea. Inspiration often benefits from space: quiet, play, rest, curiosity, and openness. When your attention is crowded and every moment is scheduled, it can be harder to explore. Create room for unstructured time and notice what draws your interest. A spark may arrive in the shower, on a walk, or while resting. Write it down and give it a chance, without treating every idea as a sacred instruction.","point3":"The energy of inspiration can feel exciting and expansive, like an “aha” moment when pieces suddenly fit together. It may make you feel alive, connected, and eager to act. When you connect with this quality, you might notice a quicker heartbeat or a strong desire to begin. These feelings can signal interest, but they do not prove an idea is right or destined. Let excitement motivate exploration, then consider the effort, resources, and consequences involved.","point4":"Your current lesson may be staying open to inspiration and acting on ideas that matter to you. Create conditions that support it—meditation, time in nature, art, play, or new experiences. Notice a spark of curiosity or excitement and capture it before it fades. Then try one small step rather than waiting for the perfect moment or analyzing the idea forever. You are not required to act on every impulse. Reflection can help you distinguish a thoughtful creative direction from a reaction driven by fear or urgency.","point5":"Make some open space for inspiration today. Look at art, listen to music, read poetry, or visit somewhere that feels beautiful to you. Try something new and keep a notebook or phone nearby to record ideas. Ask a question that interests you, then let it rest while you do something else. When a spark arrives, take one small action: write, sketch, begin, or share it with someone you trust. You might set an intention to stay curious, without assuming an outside force will send a specific answer.","point6":"Inspiration has its own rhythm; it cannot always be forced. Some days bring ideas and others are quieter. Do not criticize yourself for a fallow period—rest and new experiences can replenish attention. Not every idea needs immediate action; some need time to develop. At the same time, ideas benefit from being tested and worked on rather than collected forever. Learn what inspiration feels like for you, and balance enthusiasm with consideration. Celebrate the moments that help you see a possibility, whether or not you pursue it.","point7":"Spiritually, you may experience inspiration as connection with a sacred source or as a gift passing through you. This card honors that sense of meaning without claiming that every great artistic, scientific, or spiritual idea comes from outside the person who creates it. Your own history, skill, and effort shape how ideas take form. What inspires you may also encourage others, but you do not need to feel chosen or responsible for a ripple effect. Respect your ideas, explore them, and let them move into the world through your work."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '42', 'en', 'Unicorn of Manifestation', '顯化獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Manifestation","Creation","Attraction","Realization","Intention"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Manifestation"}', '{"point1":"This card invites you to create with intention, like a unicorn turning an imagined possibility into a story. You are not only a passive recipient of life: your choices, habits, beliefs, and actions can shape parts of your experience. You may be “manifesting” in the everyday sense of bringing a goal into reality through attention and effort. This does not mean that thoughts alone control outcomes or that you are responsible for everything that happens. Consider what you want to build and what steps could move you toward it.","point2":"Dear soul, you may be focusing on what you do not want or feeling discouraged when a goal does not appear. This card reminds you that your choices have influence, but your inner world is not a mirror that determines every external event. Positive thinking cannot guarantee results, and difficult circumstances do not mean you attracted them. Get clear about what matters to you, notice beliefs that may be limiting your choices, and take practical action where possible. Stay open to support and to outcomes that differ from your original plan.","point3":"The energy of manifestation can feel clear and purposeful, like tending a seed while it grows. It is not the same as already possessing everything you want; it can be a steady sense of direction that helps you act consistently. When you connect with this quality, you may feel focused and more naturally motivated. Visualization can help you imagine a goal and clarify your reasons, but it cannot make the outcome certain. Let intention support effort, flexibility, and realistic planning.","point4":"Your current lesson may be bringing a desired change into focus and taking steps toward it. Clarify what you want and why it matters, then examine what beliefs, resources, or obstacles are involved. You do not have to raise your vibration, eliminate every doubt, or believe without question. Take actions that align with your goal, seek help when needed, and accept that other people and circumstances affect the result. You can take responsibility for your choices without blaming yourself for things outside your control.","point5":"Choose one goal to explore and write it down clearly. Visualize what progress might look like, then identify a concrete step you can take this week. Notice any self-limiting belief and ask whether it is entirely true; you do not need to replace it with an unrealistic affirmation. Take action that fits your time and resources. Let go of needing to know exactly how or when the outcome will happen, while continuing to plan. You can be grateful for support along the way without pretending the goal is already achieved.","point6":"Bringing a goal to life is not a magic formula; it often involves reflection, patience, and action. If you are not seeing results, review your approach, seek feedback, adjust expectations, or consider whether the goal still fits. Do not assume a hidden belief or low vibration is blocking success, and do not blame yourself for setbacks. It can help to set an intention and remain flexible about the route. Celebrate real progress, including learning and support, even when the final outcome remains uncertain.","point7":"Spiritually, manifestation can represent the creative potential you bring to life. You may understand your efforts as co-creating with a sacred source, while recognizing that outcomes are shaped by many factors. Your choices can affect your community, but you are not responsible for creating all your circumstances or changing collective reality alone. The deepest goal may be not only acquiring something, but becoming more aligned with your values through the process. You can create, adapt, and keep learning without needing to be a magician."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '43', 'en', 'Unicorn of Service', '服務獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Service","Contribution","Giving","Purpose","Helping"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Service"}', '{"point1":"This card calls you toward service, like a unicorn using its healing horn to help a creature in need. Lasting meaning and joy can come not only from receiving, but also from giving and contributing. Your skills, experience, and insight may benefit others when you choose to share them. Asking “What can I offer?” rather than only “What can I get?” may help you find a sense of purpose and connection. Service does not require a grand mission or self-sacrifice; it can begin with one act of care.","point2":"Dear soul, you may be focused on your needs, goals, and success, and that is not wrong; self-care matters. Yet you may also long for more meaning or want to help but not know where to begin. Perhaps you worry that your contribution is too small. This card reminds you that service can be simple: ask how you might help, then offer what you genuinely have to give. It can be part of your work, your way of showing up, or a small kindness. Give from a place that respects your capacity; you do not have to empty yourself to be useful.","point3":"The energy of service can feel compassionate, generous, and connected, like a river nourishing the land. It may bring a warm sense of openness and the question, “How can I help?” When you connect with this quality, giving may feel natural rather than forced. Healthy service does not blur all boundaries or require you to ignore your own needs. Let generosity flow in ways that are mutual and sustainable. Meaning may come from giving, while receiving support is also part of a healthy exchange.","point4":"Your current lesson may be finding meaning through contribution without losing yourself. Notice your skills, experience, passions, and resources, then ask how they might help someone. Look for opportunities through volunteering, work, everyday kindness, or simply listening. Give from your capacity rather than from guilt or emptiness. Service includes caring for yourself, and sometimes it means saying something honest, setting a boundary, or allowing another person to learn without rescuing them. Your way of contributing does not need to resemble anyone else''s.","point5":"Choose one skill or resource you have and ask who might benefit from it. Offer something small today: help a neighbor, share useful knowledge, donate within your means, volunteer for an hour, or give someone your full attention. In everyday interactions, consider whether a kind word or practical help would be welcome. If your work does not feel like service, reflect on who benefits from it and what you value about your contribution, without forcing yourself to stay in a job that does not fit. Longer-term service might include mentoring or volunteering regularly. Kindness in how you show up can also matter.","point6":"A common trap is giving so much that you become depleted, or giving only from obligation. Sustainable service includes rest, consent, and boundaries. It is not martyrdom or always saying yes; it is sharing what you can genuinely offer. You do not need to cling to results or gratitude, but it is reasonable to hope your efforts help and to notice whether a role is sustainable. Sometimes service means telling the truth, setting a limit, or allowing someone to work through a challenge rather than rescuing them. Small kindnesses can matter even when you do not see their full effect. Keep giving in ways that are healthy for you.","point7":"Spiritually, many traditions regard service as a meaningful practice of compassion and love. If this resonates, helping another person may deepen your sense of connection, but service does not guarantee spiritual growth or require believing everyone is one. Your talents and care can support others without being part of a predetermined soul contract. Give in ways that respect the dignity and choices of the people you serve. Let service be a freely chosen act of care, balanced with receiving and caring for yourself."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('unicorns', '44', 'en', 'Unicorn of Blessing', '祝福獨角獸', '{"keywords":["Blessings","Grace","Abundance","Gratitude","Recognition"],"nameEn":"Unicorn of Blessing"}', '{"point1":"This card is a reminder to notice what feels like a blessing in your life, like the unicorn as a symbol of grace. A blessing may be an unexpected kindness, a relationship, a skill, a beautiful experience, or a moment of rest. Life itself may feel like a gift to you. Even challenges can sometimes bring insight, but they are not automatically blessings in disguise, and you do not have to be grateful for painful experiences. Shift your attention from only what is missing toward what is present, while allowing both truths to exist.","point2":"Dear soul, you may be focused on what is absent, wrong, or incomplete and overlook what you have received. The mind often notices problems first, but that does not mean you have caused hardship by paying attention to it. Perhaps you believe you do not deserve good things, or that your blessings are smaller than someone else''s. This card gently reminds you that care and joy do not have to be earned through perfection. Your life may include large and small sources of support. Notice them without comparing or denying what you still need.","point3":"The energy of blessing can feel grateful, abundant, and full of wonder, like a child seeing snow for the first time or someone appreciating health after recovery. It can help you notice the sacred in ordinary life and feel more connected to what you value. When you connect with this quality, you may feel full, moved, or deeply thankful. These feelings are meaningful, but gratitude does not prove that everything is divinely arranged. Let appreciation arise honestly, without forcing yourself to feel lucky.","point4":"Your current lesson may be recognizing and receiving blessings while keeping a full view of your life. You can practice turning your attention toward sources of care, meaning, or beauty without denying challenges. Actively look for what you appreciate in a day or in a person. Practice receiving a compliment or kindness instead of minimizing it. You may also recognize that your presence or actions are a blessing to someone else. Gratitude is a way to appreciate what matters, not a technique that guarantees more good fortune.","point5":"Write a list of things you appreciate, from large to small: a friend, a home, food, a skill, a memory, or a moment of ease. Add to it over time. When something kind happens, pause and acknowledge it: “I appreciate this.” Notice what you value about yourself without turning it into another performance. Tell someone you love that they matter to you. At the end of the day, write down three moments you are glad you experienced. If you face something difficult, you do not have to call it a blessing to learn from it.","point6":"Noticing blessings can be especially difficult during a painful time, and that is understandable. Do not use gratitude to deny pain; both can exist together: “This is hard, and I still appreciate this one source of support.” Sometimes a blessing is subtle, such as someone checking in or the ability to ask for help. Avoid comparing your life with another person''s. Notice what you value now rather than waiting until it is gone. Gratitude may support a sense of perspective, but it does not operate as a universal law that makes more blessings flow. You are worthy of care regardless of how grateful you feel.","point7":"Spiritually, you may experience life as a blessing or a gift from a sacred source. This card honors that perspective without claiming that you were chosen to experience every hardship or that each event is grace. A breath, a relationship, or an ordinary moment may feel precious to you. Gratitude can create a cycle of appreciation and generosity, and you can also be a blessing to others through care and presence. You do not have to earn love or justify your existence. Let yourself receive care and recognize the value you offer."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '1', 'en', 'Ra - Sun God', '拉神 - 太陽之神', '{"titleEn":"Ra - Sun God","symbol":"Falcon-headed figure crowned with a solar disk"}', '{"godStory":"Ra is one of ancient Egypt''s most prominent solar deities. In myth, he travels across the sky in a solar barque, bringing light and life to the world. He is often depicted with a falcon''s head and a solar disk, imagery associated with royal power, creation, and divine light. The rising sun can symbolize renewal and a new beginning, while its warmth and brightness evoke vitality and the possibility of seeing through darkness and uncertainty.","coreMeaning":"Ra represents vitality, creative power, and the courage to realize your potential. This card is about rekindling your inner fire, expressing yourself, and pursuing a meaningful aspiration. Like the sun that does not hide, Ra encourages you to let your abilities be seen. It may point to a breakthrough, a fresh start, or confidence and energy that grow from reconnecting with what matters to you.","coreEnergy":"Solar vitality, creativity, life force, leadership, confidence, recognition, and achievement. Ra''s energy is active, expressive, and passionate. It can inspire you to create, lead, or take up space. This is the forward momentum of dawn: a reminder that your light can be visible, even when you have felt overlooked. Let confidence remain grounded in your values and respect for others.","guidance":"This may be a good time to act. Ra calls you to step forward and stop hiding your talents or aspirations. Rekindle your enthusiasm and give your creativity room to move. Begin the project you have been postponing, express an honest thought, or take a leadership role where it fits. The sun does not wait for perfect conditions, and you do not need to wait for perfection either. Trust your ability to take a first step and learn as you go.","soulReminder":"Your presence has value, and what you bring may be meaningful to the world around you. Do not make yourself smaller solely because you fear other people''s opinions, but remain attentive to the space and needs of others. Each day can offer a chance to begin again, whatever happened yesterday. You have creative potential and vitality; give them room to grow. True strength includes being genuine, not performing confidence for approval.","questions":"What would I like to create? Where does my enthusiasm come alive? What helps me feel energized? Where have I been holding back? Am I ready to let others see more of who I am? How do I express my vitality? What makes it difficult to step forward? What would it look like to live more courageously and authentically?","energyFocus":"Focus on creating rather than only waiting, and on taking a step rather than endlessly planning. Give attention to what you hope to build while acknowledging the risks and resources involved. Practice confidence through one action that feels meaningful and manageable. Connect your enthusiasm with a goal that matters to you. Let your energy support the direction you choose, as the sun illuminates without judgment."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '2', 'en', 'Isis - Mother Goddess', '伊西斯 - 母親女神', '{"titleEn":"Isis - Mother Goddess","symbol":"A crown shaped like a throne and protective outstretched wings"}', '{"godStory":"Isis was one of ancient Egypt''s most beloved goddesses. Often shown wearing a throne-shaped crown, she is associated with kingship, motherhood, and feminine power. In myth, her outstretched wings protect those in her care. She is linked with magic, healing, and devotion; in the story of Osiris, her magic restores him to life. Isis is both a nurturing mother and a powerful magician, an image of strength held within tenderness.","coreMeaning":"Isis represents receptive wisdom, intuition, healing, and the power to nurture. This card is about love''s capacity to transform, empathy, and caring connection with yourself and others. Isis reminds you that care does not need to be controlling. Listen inwardly, trust your considered intuition, and treat each living being—including yourself—with gentleness and respect.","coreEnergy":"Receptivity, intuition, healing, empathy, magic, maternal love, wisdom, and protection. Isis''s energy is deep, embracing, and transformative. Like moonlight, it can feel gentle while still carrying strength. It invites you to understand pain, tend to what has been hurt, and bring care into a difficult situation. Her presence in this reading can symbolize the comfort of being met with compassion.","guidance":"Slow down and listen to what is happening within you. Your intuition may be drawing attention to something important, so consider it alongside your needs and the evidence around you. This may be a time to tend to an old hurt and nourish yourself. Allow emotions to be felt rather than pushed away. Remember to care for yourself; you cannot give without limit. Use empathy to understand others while maintaining healthy boundaries. Begin with caring for your own needs.","soulReminder":"Love can be a powerful source of change, and you can choose to act with care. Your empathy is not weakness; it can be a deep strength. Gentleness can be powerful, and magic here is an image of love''s transformative capacity. You do not need to carry everything alone; let yourself receive support and affection. Trust your intuition while staying open to new information and the perspectives of people you trust.","questions":"What is my intuition drawing my attention to? Which parts of my life need care? How can I nourish myself more fully? Are my boundaries healthy? Am I willing to receive love and support? How does my empathy serve me and others? What hurt might need attention? How can I connect with nurturing or feminine energy in a way that feels right to me?","energyFocus":"Turn some attention inward rather than focusing only on external achievement. Make room for feeling, connection, and reflection alongside thinking and doing. You might cultivate intuition through meditation, journaling, or quiet time. Practice self-care and self-compassion in a way that is realistic for you. Stay open to giving and receiving support; healing can involve both. Invest in relationships with mutual care and respect, and let empathy inform your actions without replacing boundaries."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '3', 'en', 'Osiris - Lord of the Afterlife', '奧西里斯 - 冥界之主', '{"titleEn":"Osiris - Lord of the Afterlife","symbol":"An enthroned figure with crook and flail, often shown with green skin"}', '{"godStory":"Osiris is shown holding a crook and flail, often wrapped in mummy bandages, imagery associated with kingship, death, and renewal. His green skin evokes vegetation and the return of life. In Egyptian myth, Osiris is killed and restored, and becomes a ruler of the afterlife who presides over the dead. His story speaks to mortality, renewal, and the journey through darkness; in this reading, it can also offer a metaphor for change and the possibility of beginning again.","coreMeaning":"Osiris represents profound transformation, necessary endings, and cycles of death and renewal. This need not refer to physical death; it may describe an old identity, habit, or pattern coming to an end so something new can develop. Osiris teaches that some chapters close before new life can begin. In this space between endings and beginnings, you may set down what no longer serves you and prepare for a different way forward.","coreEnergy":"Transformation, renewal, release, deep change, and the symbolism of life''s endings and beginnings. Osiris''s energy is solemn, deep, and transformative. It invites you to acknowledge natural cycles and allow yourself to change. New growth can follow a period of darkness, but the process may be difficult and does not have to be rushed. This is a call to meaningful reflection rather than a superficial change of appearance.","guidance":"It may be time to let go of something that has reached its end, whether a relationship, job, belief, or way of living. Do not resist change simply because it is painful, but do not force an ending before you are ready or safe. Allow yourself to grieve and take time to process what you are losing. During a transition, it is normal to feel uncertain while the old has ended and the new has not yet taken shape. Seek support and take the next step when you can; darkness does not define the whole of your future.","soulReminder":"You can change and grow through difficult transitions, even when the way forward is not yet clear. An ending can open a door, but it does not erase the loss or guarantee that something better is waiting. Give yourself time to become someone new, or to discover what parts of you remain. Trust that you can meet change with support and care, without believing that hardship was destined or required. Let transformation happen at a pace you can live with.","questions":"What am I ready to let go of? What has reached its end, even though I am still holding on? What kind of ending do I fear? What might renewal mean to me? Am I ready to consider a new version of myself? Which old pattern no longer fits? How can I support myself through change? What beliefs do I hold about death, endings, and renewal?","energyFocus":"Focus on loosening your grip rather than tightening it, and on accepting change without rushing it. Give yourself room to grieve what has ended. Spend time in the uncertainty instead of filling every open space immediately. A symbolic release ritual—writing what you are ready to leave behind and safely disposing of the paper—may help mark an intention. Notice what is ending and what may be beginning. Let darkness be a time for rest and reflection, not proof that nothing new can grow."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '4', 'en', 'Thoth - God of Wisdom', '托特 - 智慧之神', '{"titleEn":"Thoth - God of Wisdom","symbol":"Ibis-headed figure holding a writing palette and reed pen"}', '{"godStory":"Thoth is often depicted with the head of an ibis, holding a writing palette and reed pen as a record-keeper of knowledge. He is associated with writing, magic, learning, and the moon. In some creation stories, words help bring the world into being, reflecting the sacred power attributed to language. Thoth also serves as a divine scribe and mediator, known for wisdom and fairness. His image invites you to look beyond appearances and seek a fuller understanding of the truth.","coreMeaning":"Thoth represents wisdom, knowledge, communication, learning, and the power of language. This card is about expanding your mind, seeking truth, and gaining strength through understanding. Thoth reminds you that words can shape how you and others experience the world. He encourages deep study, clear communication, and thoughtful use of language. Wisdom comes not only from books but also from observation, listening, and careful reflection.","coreEnergy":"Intellect, clarity, truth, communication, learning, writing, language, and lunar wisdom. Thoth''s energy is discerning, rational, and insightful. It can help you organize thoughts, gather knowledge, and express yourself accurately. This is the energy of cutting through confusion and naming what you see. Words can feel like spells because they influence thought and relationship; knowledge can be powerful when used responsibly.","guidance":"This may be a good time to learn and expand your knowledge. Study a subject that interests you; read, explore, and ask questions. Pay attention to your words as well: they can affect your perspective and relationships, so speak with care about the world you want to help create. Notice negative self-talk or habitual complaints without shaming yourself. If you are seeking answers, consult books, teachers, and your own reflection. Record thoughts, dreams, or insights as material to consider, not as unquestionable facts.","soulReminder":"You can keep learning throughout your life, and curiosity can open new paths. Your words are tools: they can clarify, connect, encourage, or wound, so use them thoughtfully. Wisdom is more than collecting facts; it includes understanding context and knowing what you do not know. Listening can teach as much as speaking. Learning is an ongoing journey, so keep a student''s mind—curious, discerning, and open to revision.","questions":"What would I like to learn? How do my words shape my experience and relationships? Am I speaking in ways that empower or limit me? What message do I need to communicate? How can I express it more clearly? Do my thought patterns serve me? What kind of wisdom am I seeking? How can I use language more responsibly?","energyFocus":"Develop your mind through reading, learning, thinking, and analysis. Practice clear reasoning and precise expression. Choose words intentionally, including the way you speak to yourself. Writing in a journal, taking notes, or doing creative writing can help organize your thoughts. Learn from teachers and from daily experience. Put knowledge into practice, and let action test and deepen your understanding. Speak carefully, as if your words matter—because they do."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '5', 'en', 'Anubis - Guardian of Souls', '阿努比斯 - 靈魂守護者', '{"titleEn":"Anubis - Guardian of Souls","symbol":"Black jackal-headed figure holding scales"}', '{"godStory":"Anubis is depicted with the head of a black jackal and is associated with tombs and the threshold of the afterlife. In Egyptian belief, he guides the dead through the underworld and oversees the weighing of the heart. In the judgment scene, the heart is weighed against the feather of Ma''at, a symbol of truth and right order. Anubis appears as both guardian and guide, accompanying the dead through darkness. In this reading, his image can also symbolize support during uncertain transitions.","coreMeaning":"Anubis represents protection, guidance, transition, honesty, and the courage to face what is true. This card may speak to being supported between stages of life: an old chapter has ended, while a new one has not yet begun. During this vulnerable period, seek guidance and be honest about your motives, choices, and inner truth. You can move through uncertainty without pretending to know exactly where you are headed.","coreEnergy":"Protection, guidance, transition, truth, honesty, and companionship through darkness. Anubis''s energy is steady, protective, and guiding. His image can remind you to look for reliable support when you feel vulnerable or lost. This is a grounded presence through difficult times, not a guarantee that nothing painful will happen. The card also asks for honesty: to look clearly at your actions and intentions with fairness rather than harsh self-condemnation.","guidance":"Trust that you can seek guidance even when the path ahead is unclear. You do not have to face a transition alone; ask a trusted person, mentor, or professional for support. This may also be a time for honest self-reflection: Are your choices aligned with your values? Do your actions reflect what you say matters to you? The image of the heart being weighed can prompt this reflection without turning it into a judgment of your worth. If you are experiencing loss or major change, give yourself time and support as you move through it.","soulReminder":"Feeling lost does not mean you are without direction or support. Even in a dark period, you can look for trustworthy people and practical resources to guide you. Transitions can be part of growth, but they need not be interpreted as something you were destined to endure. Honesty may feel uncomfortable at first, yet it can help you make choices that fit your values. Treat yourself fairly as you face what is true, and seek guidance when you need it.","questions":"What transition am I moving through? What kind of guidance would help me? Am I being honest with myself? What feels heavy, and what feels aligned with my values? Is there a truth I have been avoiding? Do my actions reflect what matters to me? Can I trust someone to support me through uncertainty? How might I find steadiness when the future is unclear?","energyFocus":"Focus on honesty and authenticity. Review the different parts of your life with fairness and curiosity. Face a truth you may have been avoiding, while seeking support if it feels difficult. Allow yourself to be vulnerable during a transition rather than pretending to be unaffected. Guidance may come through reflection, dreams, a spiritual mentor, or a trusted friend; consider each source thoughtfully. Let truth be a compass, and let compassion accompany it."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '6', 'en', 'Bastet - Cat Goddess', '芭絲特 - 貓女神', '{"titleEn":"Bastet - Cat Goddess","symbol":"Cat-headed goddess with an elegant, poised presence"}', '{"godStory":"Bastet is often depicted with a cat''s head and a graceful, poised presence. In some traditions, she is associated with the lioness goddess Sekhmet, with stories reflecting a movement between fierce protection and gentler domestic life. She is linked with music, celebration, protection of the home, and care for children and women. Bastet can represent both a guardian and one who enjoys life''s pleasures, reminding you that life needs room for joy and play as well as responsibility.","coreMeaning":"Bastet represents joy, play, grace, independence, protection of home and family, and feminine power. This card is about bringing more lightness and happiness into your life, balancing work with play, and moving with the ease of a cat. Bastet reminds you that life is not only responsibilities; it also includes enjoying the present and relaxing. Like a cat, you can have boundaries: choosing when to draw close and when to take space to protect your energy and comfort.","coreEnergy":"Joy, play, grace, independence, protection, feminine power, sensory pleasure, music, and dance. Bastet''s energy is light, enjoyable, and elegant. It represents knowing how to enjoy life, find humor amid seriousness, and meet challenges with poise. Like a cat, this energy can be gentle yet strong, independent yet affectionate, relaxed yet alert. Let pleasure and rest have a place without treating them as rewards you must earn.","guidance":"It may be time to lighten up. Set down some tension and do something that genuinely brings you joy: dance, sing, play a game, enjoy a favorite meal, listen to music, or rest. You may have focused so much on responsibility that pleasure has slipped away. Bastet also reminds you to protect your time, energy, and space. Like a cat, notice when you need solitude and when you want company. Set healthy boundaries; you do not owe everyone unlimited access to your attention.","soulReminder":"You deserve to enjoy life''s pleasures. Laughter is not a sin, and play is not automatically wasted time. Do not wait until every task is complete to allow yourself joy; there will always be more to do. Feminine energy—regardless of your gender—can include grace, intuition, and independence. Strength can be soft, and independence can include knowing when to connect. Move through life with poise, mystery, and room for delight.","questions":"When did I last play or enjoy myself? What brings me joy? Do I allow myself to enjoy life? Are my boundaries clear? How do I balance work with play? Is there enough laughter in my life? How can I move through a challenge with more grace? When do I want solitude, and when do I want connection?","energyFocus":"Give attention to what brings you joy. Make room for play, relaxation, and enjoyment. Add music, dance, or art to everyday life. Practice a calm and graceful pace rather than rushing or tensing. Stretch, rest, and notice pleasant sensory experiences. Protect your space and energy with clear boundaries. Embrace independence without needing constant approval. Let laughter and lightness find their way back into your life."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '7', 'en', 'Horus - Sky God', '荷魯斯 - 天空之神', '{"titleEn":"Horus - Sky God","symbol":"Falcon-headed deity with eyes associated with the sun and moon"}', '{"godStory":"Horus is often depicted with the head of a falcon. In some traditions, his eyes are associated with the sun and moon, giving him a view across day and night. With broad wings, he soars above the land. In myth, Horus fights his uncle Seth after the death of his father, Osiris, and eventually becomes a legitimate ruler of Egypt. The Eye of Horus became a powerful symbol of protection and kingship. In this reading, it can invite you to look carefully beyond appearances and question what is true.","coreMeaning":"Horus represents perspective, insight, leadership, justice, perseverance, and protection. This card invites you to step back from the details and consider the larger picture. Horus teaches that a wider view may reveal patterns you could not see up close. He encourages you to develop your leadership, stand up for values you believe in, and protect what matters to you. Progress can come through persistence and thoughtful action, even when the path is challenging.","coreEnergy":"Vision, insight, leadership, justice, courage, protection, and perseverance. Horus''s energy is far-seeing, clear, and brave. It can symbolize rising above immediate difficulties enough to notice facts and possibilities, then acting with resolve. Like a falcon, this energy combines careful observation with timely action. Leadership here is not domination; it includes responsibility, fairness, and care for those affected by your decisions.","guidance":"Try viewing your situation from a wider perspective. Step back from details and ask what the overall pattern might be, while checking your assumptions. You may be ready to take a leadership role at work, at home, or in your own life. Stand up for a value or person you believe in, and consider what protection or support is actually needed. Challenges do not require you to prove your strength; act with courage and judgment, and protect your own goals as well as the people you care about.","soulReminder":"You may have more perspective and strength than you realize, but stay open to the possibility that you do not yet see the whole truth. Leadership is not control; it can be service, fairness, and protection. Standing up for justice can take patience and discernment. Progress may be slow, and setbacks do not mean the truth will automatically prevail. Keep going in ways that align with your values, and let courage be guided by humility and care.","questions":"From what perspective am I viewing this situation? Have I considered the larger picture? Where might I develop my leadership? What value am I standing up for? What or whom am I trying to protect? What does my careful observation suggest? Am I ready to speak or act? How can I advocate for truth with courage and fairness?","energyFocus":"Raise your perspective enough to see relationships and patterns without dismissing important details. Develop leadership skills, including listening and taking responsibility. Stand up for your values with courage and respect. Protect your goals and the people you care about using practical steps. Observe carefully and check what you believe you see. Like a falcon, combine focus with flexibility; progress may call for both strategy and persistence."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '8', 'en', 'Hathor - Goddess of Love', '哈索爾 - 愛之女神', '{"titleEn":"Hathor - Goddess of Love","symbol":"Cow goddess crowned with a solar disk between her horns"}', '{"godStory":"Hathor is often depicted as a cow goddess crowned with a solar disk between her horns, imagery associated with nourishment and abundance. As a sky goddess, she is connected with the stars. She is also associated with music, dance, celebration, love, and joy. In her temples, these arts could be part of worship and celebration. Hathor''s image can hold many roles—nurturer, beloved, and source of pleasure—reminding you that life can include beauty and celebration as well as responsibility.","coreMeaning":"Hathor represents love, beauty, joy, abundance, celebration, music, art, and the good in life. This card is about opening your heart to love and appreciating beauty around you. Hathor teaches that love can be a powerful source of connection, and that everyone deserves care and respect. She encourages you to welcome the richness of life—not only material resources, but also affection, beauty, creativity, and joy.","coreEnergy":"Love, beauty, joy, abundance, celebration, nourishment, music, art, sensory pleasure, and openness. Hathor''s energy is warm, generous, and joyful. It invites you to embrace life, open your heart, and give and receive care. Like nourishment shared with a child, this energy can evoke tenderness and belonging. Abundance here can mean emotional and creative richness, not a promise of unlimited material wealth.","guidance":"Open yourself to love and the good things that may be present. You can lower your guard gradually, in ways that feel safe, and allow different forms of love—romantic, friendship, family, or self-love—to reach you. Celebrate small moments worth celebrating. Listen to music, make art, savor a meal, or spend time with something beautiful in nature. You deserve joy and care, and you do not have to earn them through constant positivity. Share affection and appreciation without expecting it to guarantee a return.","soulReminder":"You are worthy of love and care as you are. You do not need to prove your value before allowing yourself to receive kindness. Life can hold celebration even when it is not perfect; you do not have to wait until every task is done to enjoy a good moment. There is beauty, love, and joy in the world, though access to them can vary. When you give love, it does not diminish your worth, and you may also let yourself receive it. Let Hathor''s joy remind you to make room for pleasure.","questions":"Is my heart open or guarded right now? Am I willing to receive love? When did I last celebrate? Do I notice beauty in my life? Where do I feel rich or depleted? How can I share care with others? What makes it difficult to receive good things? How can I make life feel more celebratory?","energyFocus":"Notice love and beauty in your surroundings. Open up gradually to giving and receiving affection, while maintaining boundaries that feel safe. Bring music, art, or other beauty into daily life. Celebrate small wins, joys, and moments of ease. Practice gratitude for what is genuinely meaningful to you. Offer sincere care, praise, or encouragement. Enjoy sensory experiences without suppressing delight, and let love guide choices that respect both you and others."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '9', 'en', 'Sekhmet - Warrior Goddess', '塞赫邁特 - 戰士女神', '{"titleEn":"Sekhmet - Warrior Goddess","symbol":"Lioness goddess with fire in her eyes"}', '{"godStory":"Sekhmet is a fierce lioness goddess, often shown with fire in her eyes and associated with formidable power. In one myth, she is the Eye of Ra, sent to punish humanity for its rebellion; her fury becomes so great that it threatens to destroy humankind. Sekhmet is also associated with healing, reflecting the way her force can be both dangerous and protective. A lotus may symbolize renewal after destruction. Her fire can represent the power to end what is harmful and make room for change.","coreMeaning":"Sekhmet represents strength, courage, anger, boundaries, healing, and transformation. This card invites you to call on your inner warrior to stand up for yourself, say no, and face what needs attention. Sekhmet suggests that gentleness and strength can coexist, and that healing sometimes requires confronting pain. Anger is not automatically destructive; it can signal a boundary or injustice. What matters is how you listen to it and choose to respond.","coreEnergy":"Strength, courage, anger, boundaries, protection, healing, fire, transformation, and the warrior spirit. Sekhmet''s energy is powerful, fierce, and unwilling to tolerate harm. It may help you say “enough” and protect what matters. Like fire, it can destroy or transform depending on how it is handled. This is both warrior and healer energy: the courage to act, and the care to avoid turning that force against yourself or others.","guidance":"Call on your strength and courage. It may be time to stand up for yourself, set a clear boundary, or speak honestly. You do not have to let anyone undermine your dignity or worth. If a difficult conversation is needed, prepare what you want to say and choose a safe time and setting. Sekhmet''s fire can symbolize resolve, not permission to harm. At the same time, make room to understand and process anger rather than suppressing it. Ask what the feeling is signaling, then express it safely and constructively.","soulReminder":"You may be stronger than you think, and you do not have to be endlessly gentle, agreeable, or yielding. Anger is not a sin; it can be a signal that something feels wrong or a boundary has been crossed. You have the right to protect yourself, say no, and ask for respect. Healing does not mean pretending everything is fine; it can mean facing pain and seeking support. Let your strength illuminate a way forward without burning you or anyone else. You can be both a protector and a healer.","questions":"Where do I need to be firmer? Are my boundaries clear? Am I suppressing anger? What value or person am I standing up for? Where does my strength show up? Do I allow myself to be powerful? What needs to change or be released? How can I balance strength with gentleness?","energyFocus":"Focus on your capacity rather than only on vulnerability. Practice saying no and setting boundaries, even when someone may dislike them. Let yourself feel anger, then choose a safe way to process it, such as movement, writing, or talking with someone you trust. Face a difficult situation or conversation with preparation. Develop a protective warrior spirit, not an attacking one. A fire ritual may symbolize releasing an old pattern; follow fire safety. Your strength is valuable when guided by care."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '10', 'en', 'Ptah - Creator God', '普塔 - 造物主', '{"titleEn":"Ptah - Creator God","symbol":"Enshrouded figure holding a staff, with hands visible"}', '{"godStory":"Ptah is an ancient Egyptian creator god, often shown wrapped in a close-fitting garment with only his hands visible, holding a staff. In a creation account associated with Memphis, he conceives the world in his heart and brings it forth through speech. He is also a patron of craftspeople, builders, and artists. His image evokes the process of shaping an idea into form: imagining, planning, and making. His temple was a center of worship and craft in Memphis.","coreMeaning":"Ptah represents creativity, making, craft, and the movement from an idea to something tangible. This card asks how you might bring a dream into the world through thought, words, and action. You are a builder of your life in the sense that your decisions and effort shape some of your experiences. Ptah suggests beginning with a clear vision, then using focus and skill to work toward it. Thoughts alone cannot guarantee an outcome; making requires practice and real-world steps.","coreEnergy":"Creation, building, craftsmanship, intention, practical wisdom, and patience. Ptah''s energy is steady, focused, and constructive. It can help you turn an idea into a tangible result through clear aims, careful planning, practiced skill, and sustained effort. This is the craftsperson''s energy, attentive to quality, detail, and what will endure. Allow for revision: good work often takes time to shape.","guidance":"You have the ability to work toward a dream. First clarify what you want to create and take time to picture its practical details. Then turn the vision into a plan with steps you can take. Your thoughts and words can influence your choices, so use language that supports rather than undermines your effort. Replace harsh self-talk with realistic encouragement, and remember that setbacks do not mean you have failed to manifest correctly. Use your hands: write, draw, build, cook, or practice a craft. Let action help bring an idea into reality.","soulReminder":"You can shape parts of your life through your choices and creative work. Do not underestimate your potential, but remember that outcomes also depend on resources, circumstances, and other people. Lasting creations take time; a pyramid was not built in a day. Be patient and focused, and work on your dream one step at a time. Words can help set direction, while practice and action do the building. Begin with a clear intention and follow through with care.","questions":"What would I like to create? Is my vision clear enough to take a first step? Do my thoughts support my goal? Are my words encouraging or limiting? What action am I ready to take? What skills and tools can I use or develop? How can I stay focused? What lasting value would I like my work to have?","energyFocus":"Clarify the vision you want to build, and give it enough detail to guide action. Practice realistic, encouraging self-talk. Create a specific plan and break the dream into manageable tasks. Work with your hands or materials; making something tangible can help you understand the process. Keep showing up consistently and make time for your goal. Trust the work you can do, and revise as you learn."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '11', 'en', 'Ma''at - Goddess of Truth', '瑪特 - 真理女神', '{"titleEn":"Ma''at - Goddess of Truth","symbol":"Goddess wearing an ostrich feather and holding a staff"}', '{"godStory":"Ma''at is often shown wearing an ostrich feather, a symbol associated with truth, and holding a staff and an ankh. She represents cosmic order, balance, and harmony. In ancient Egyptian funerary belief, a deceased person''s heart was weighed against her feather; this image became a powerful symbol of judgment and moral accountability. Ma''at is more than a goddess in these traditions: her name also describes the order and truth sustaining the world. In this reading, she invites integrity, fairness, and balance.","coreMeaning":"Ma''at represents truth, justice, balance, honesty, and order. This card invites you to live with integrity, seek balance in daily life, and act in keeping with your conscience. Ma''at teaches that choices have consequences and that disregarding truth can disrupt trust and relationships. She encourages honesty with yourself and others, and fairness in the situations you face. Truth can be freeing, though it may also require care and courage to express.","coreEnergy":"Truth, justice, balance, harmony, honesty, moral integrity, order, and fairness. Ma''at''s energy is steady and impartial. It seeks a clear view of what happened and what is fair, helping you restore balance where possible. The feather offers an image of lightness and truth; rather than judging yourself as pure or impure, use it as a prompt to examine your actions with honesty and compassion.","guidance":"Be honest with yourself and others. Review your life: Are your choices aligned with your values? Is there a truth you need to communicate? This may be a time to restore trust through integrity and courage. If you have been concealing something or avoiding an honest conversation, consider what a responsible next step would be. Ma''at also invites balance across life: work and rest, giving and receiving, material needs and meaning. Seek fairness in relationships and situations, including fairness toward yourself.","soulReminder":"Truth and integrity can help you feel lighter, though facing a difficult fact may be uncomfortable at first. You do not have to be perfect to act honestly. Your actions have consequences, and you can take responsibility, repair harm where possible, and make a different choice. Aim for a life that is honest, balanced, and fair, while allowing for complexity and mistakes. You cannot control every outcome, but you can choose to meet yourself and others with integrity.","questions":"Am I being honest with myself? Where in my life do I need more balance? Do my actions reflect my values? What truth might I need to express? What am I avoiding? How can I treat myself and others more fairly? What is weighing on my conscience?","energyFocus":"Practice honesty in your interactions and review where your life feels out of balance. Adjust what you can, one area at a time. Build the courage to tell the truth with care, especially when it is difficult. Make decisions with fairness and consider the needs of everyone affected. Reflect on whether your actions align with your beliefs. Restore inner and outer balance where possible, and let integrity guide your next step."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '12', 'en', 'Nephthys - Dark Mother', '奈芙蒂斯 - 黑暗母親', '{"titleEn":"Nephthys - Dark Mother","symbol":"Goddess wearing a headdress with a house symbol and protective wings"}', '{"godStory":"Nephthys wears a headdress associated with a house or temple sign and is sister to Isis in Egyptian tradition. She is connected with the night and hidden realms. Often shown with protective wings, she is associated with mourning and with accompanying the dead through darkness. Her image can evoke what is hidden, unseen, or difficult to acknowledge. As a mourner and guardian, she symbolizes companionship during the darkest moments, rather than requiring you to face them alone.","coreMeaning":"Nephthys represents shadow work, hidden insight, suppressed emotions, transformation, and inward exploration. This card invites you to notice parts of yourself you may avoid or disown, and to approach them with care. Nephthys teaches that darkness is not necessarily evil; it can be a quiet space for rest, grief, and change. Explore your inner life at a pace that feels safe, and seek support if painful material becomes overwhelming.","coreEnergy":"Shadow, hidden wisdom, depth, protection in darkness, difficult emotions, inward reflection, grief, and mystery. Nephthys''s energy is deep and transformative. It does not turn away from what is difficult, but it meets it with protection and patience. This energy can help you face fears, understand emotions, and tend to parts of yourself that have gone unnoticed. It is not a reason to force painful memories to surface or to interpret distress as a spiritual requirement.","guidance":"You do not have to fear exploring parts of yourself that you usually avoid, but move gently. Feelings you have denied or pushed away may deserve acknowledgment. You might reflect on fear, anger, jealousy, or other emotions you have judged as “negative,” asking what they need or what they are signaling. These feelings are not enemies, and they do not define you. Sometimes withdrawing into quiet is useful for rest and reflection. If this work brings up trauma or intense distress, pause and consider support from a qualified therapist or trusted person.","soulReminder":"Difficult or hidden parts of yourself may hold information about what you need, but you do not have to explore them alone or all at once. Darkness can be a place of rest and transformation, not proof that something is wrong with you. The parts you find hard to accept deserve compassion, not condemnation. Integration is about becoming more whole, not becoming dark. Like the moon in its hidden phase, you remain yourself even when you cannot see every part clearly.","questions":"What am I avoiding? Which feelings have I pushed aside? What makes me feel ashamed, and why? Are there parts of myself I deny? What might I learn from sitting with an emotion safely? What support would help me explore this? Am I ready to approach this slowly? How can I grow during private or unseen moments?","energyFocus":"Turn inward with care and explore an area you usually avoid, only as far as feels manageable. Journaling can help; dream reflection may be meaningful if you hold interpretations lightly. A therapist or trusted support person can accompany deeper work. Let emotions arise without judging them or demanding that they lead to an insight. Spend time in solitude and quiet when it supports you, and take breaks when needed. Welcome your complexity, including parts you once labeled “bad,” with boundaries and compassion."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '13', 'en', 'Set - God of Chaos', '賽特 - 混沌之神', '{"titleEn":"Set - God of Chaos","symbol":"Deity with the distinctive long-eared Set animal head"}', '{"godStory":"Set is depicted with a distinctive animal head, long ears, and a curved snout, an image associated with the unknown and the wild. He is connected with the desert, storms, and disorder, and is a powerful, unpredictable figure. In myth, he kills his brother Osiris; in some interpretations, Set also represents disruptive forces and necessary change. His image evokes untamed energy and the challenge to established order, while reminding us that disruption can bring harm as well as transformation.","coreMeaning":"Set represents disruption, wildness, change, breaking constraints, and unpredictable forces. This card asks where a rigid structure may need to change and where you may be holding back a part of yourself. Set can remind you that old patterns sometimes need to end before a new arrangement can take shape. Destruction is not inherently necessary or good; choose change deliberately, and consider who may be affected. Make room for uncertainty while protecting what matters.","coreEnergy":"Disruption, untamed energy, strength, change, challenge, unpredictability, and rebellion. Set''s energy is wild and difficult to control, like a storm that can clear a path while also causing damage. It may symbolize questioning rules or releasing a pattern that has become restrictive. Use this force with discernment: challenge authority when it is warranted, but do not confuse impulsive harm with freedom. Change can be powerful without being reckless.","guidance":"Stay open to change and uncertainty. If life feels rigid or stagnant, consider a new approach rather than waiting for a crisis to force change. You may need to loosen control, but make choices that protect your safety and responsibilities. Set also invites you to express an independent or unconventional side of yourself. You do not have to be agreeable at all times, yet rebellion is most useful when guided by your values and care for others. Let disruption make room for something constructive.","soulReminder":"You may have a wild, energetic part of yourself that does not need to be suppressed. Disruption is not always bad, but it can also hurt people, so choose carefully what you are willing to challenge. You have the capacity to change and rebuild patterns that no longer serve you. Let your independence create more room for honest living rather than harm. After a storm, the air may feel clearer, but you do not need to create a storm to make change possible.","questions":"What structure or habit may need to change? Where have I become too rigid? What part of myself have I been holding back? Am I afraid of uncertainty? What needs to end before something new can begin? How can I question a rule constructively? Where does my untamed energy show up?","energyFocus":"Allow some flexibility into an area of life that feels overcontrolled. Question routines or assumptions and try a new approach, while considering the consequences. Find a safe outlet for physical or creative energy, such as exercise, dancing, or making art. Ask why a rule exists before deciding to challenge it. Welcome uncertainty without surrendering your judgment. Look for ways to turn disruption into constructive change and release stagnation without creating unnecessary harm."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '14', 'en', 'Nut - Sky Goddess', '努特 - 天空女神', '{"titleEn":"Nut - Sky Goddess","symbol":"Goddess arched across the sky, her body filled with stars"}', '{"godStory":"Nut''s body arches over the earth to form the sky, her hands and feet reaching toward the horizon and stars spread across her. In one myth, she swallows the sun each evening and gives birth to it again at dawn. As a sky goddess, she evokes vastness, cycles, and renewal. Her image can represent limitless possibility and the shelter of a wide sky, inviting you to imagine more room for growth while honoring the real conditions of your life.","coreMeaning":"Nut represents possibility, protection, renewal, a wider perspective, hope, and maternal care. This card invites you to look beyond current limitations and imagine what else may be possible. Even after a dark period, a new day can come, though it may not arrive on a predictable schedule. Nut encourages you to look up from immediate constraints and make room for a broader vision, while taking practical steps toward it.","coreEnergy":"Vastness, possibility, protection, cycles, renewal, inclusion, hope, care, and freedom. Nut''s energy is expansive and embracing, like the sky that holds stars and weather alike. It can evoke a sense of room to breathe and options beyond what you currently see. This image may help you feel supported, though it cannot guarantee protection from hardship. Use the sense of possibility to imagine and pursue meaningful choices.","guidance":"Expand your perspective and revisit the size of your dreams. Have fear or past experience led you to make them smaller? Consider what you might want if you gave yourself more room to imagine, then identify a realistic next step. The sky is vast, but your resources and circumstances are real; plan with both in view. If you feel vulnerable, seek support from people and resources you trust. Like the sun''s return in the myth, you can find ways to begin again after a difficult period, at your own pace.","soulReminder":"Your potential may be broader than you currently believe, and you do not have to accept someone else''s definition of what is possible for you. Dark periods can change, though not always on a schedule you can predict. You can seek care and support rather than feeling you must be protected by an unseen force. Allow yourself to dream widely while making choices that respect your needs. Look up, notice the open sky, and remember that more than one path may be available.","questions":"Do my dreams have room to grow? Where am I limiting myself? Can I imagine more than one possibility? What support helps me feel safe? Am I willing to begin again? What keeps me from widening my perspective? How could I live with more openness?","energyFocus":"Let your perspective reach beyond immediate obstacles. Revisit a vision for your life without editing it too quickly, then identify practical steps toward it. Spend time looking at the sky and notice a sense of spaciousness. Remember that cycles of change can include endings and new starts, without assuming each ending guarantees a better beginning. Seek support and let yourself feel protected through trusted relationships and practical care. Release assumptions that unnecessarily limit your options."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '15', 'en', 'Geb - Earth God', '蓋布 - 大地之神', '{"titleEn":"Geb - Earth God","symbol":"Earth deity reclining beneath the sky, his body forming the land"}', '{"godStory":"Geb is depicted reclining beneath the sky, his body forming the contours of the earth; his green skin evokes growing plants. He is a foundation for life and a source of support. In Egyptian myth, Geb is paired with the sky goddess Nut, and the space between them is where life unfolds. His image represents the material world, practical foundations, and the strength of being grounded. The earth nurtures life and provides a place to stand.","coreMeaning":"Geb represents stability, foundations, the material world, practicality, grounding, fertility, and security. This card asks you to build a steady base and attend to practical parts of life. Geb reminds you that dreams benefit from foundations. He encourages attention to finances, health, home, and other everyday needs, bringing spiritual values into daily routines rather than using them to escape material concerns.","coreEnergy":"Stability, foundations, practicality, the material world, grounding, fertility, support, security, earth, and patience. Geb''s energy is solid, reliable, and supportive. It evokes deep roots and a steady place to stand. Like the earth carrying life, this energy may offer a feeling of stability. It is concrete and tangible: the routines, resources, and care that help you feel supported.","guidance":"Return to the basics and strengthen your foundations. Attend to practical matters such as finances, physical well-being, or your living environment. These needs deserve attention alongside dreams and spiritual interests. Spend time outdoors or with the natural world; notice the ground beneath your feet and let it help you feel present. If you feel scattered or anxious, try a simple grounding practice and identify one practical next step. Seek appropriate professional advice for health or financial decisions.","soulReminder":"Steady foundations can support growth and freedom, like a tree whose roots allow its branches to reach higher. Do not neglect practical parts of life; they can support your broader aspirations. Spirituality does not require escaping the material world; meaning can be lived through ordinary care and responsibilities. Attend to your body and practical needs as valuable parts of your life. Grounding is not a cure for every difficulty, but it can help you reconnect with what is here and what you can do.","questions":"Do I feel stable in the foundations of my life? How are my finances and daily routines? Am I caring for my body? Do I feel connected to the earth? What practical issue needs attention? Have I been too focused on ideas and not enough on implementation? How can I feel more grounded? Where do I find support?","energyFocus":"Give attention to concrete, tangible things. Make one practical step on finances, health, or your living space. Spend time outside, garden, or touch soil if that is available to you. Try a grounding practice by noticing your feet and the support beneath you. Attend to bodily needs with nourishing food, hydration, rest, and appropriate care. Build a stable routine that can flex when life changes. Bring your values into the material world through everyday choices."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '16', 'en', 'Sobek - Crocodile God', '索貝克 - 鱷魚之神', '{"titleEn":"Sobek - Crocodile God","symbol":"Crocodile-headed deity with an alert gaze and powerful jaws"}', '{"godStory":"Sobek is a strong crocodile-headed deity, often shown with powerful jaws and an alert gaze. He is associated with the Nile, a force that could nourish and sustain life as well as carry danger. The crocodile waits in the water, ready to respond; this image can evoke instinctive awareness and survival wisdom. Sobek is connected with protection, territory, and vigilance in the face of risk. His power is formidable, and it calls for discernment in how it is used.","coreMeaning":"Sobek represents boundaries, protection, instinct, alertness, survival wisdom, and personal territory. This card invites you to make your boundaries clear, protect your space and energy, and pay attention to your instincts. Sobek reminds you that you can be direct when a limit is crossed. Notice a feeling of unease, then consider what may be causing it and what practical information you have before deciding how to respond.","coreEnergy":"Protection, boundaries, instinct, alertness, ancient wisdom, territory, strength, survival, and wildness. Sobek''s energy is watchful, protective, and instinctive. It may symbolize being prepared to protect your space without assuming that every unfamiliar person or situation is a threat. Like a crocodile alert in the water, this energy calls for noticing your surroundings, responding thoughtfully, and protecting yourself when needed.","guidance":"Protect your boundaries and personal space. Has someone crossed a limit or taken advantage of your kindness? This may be a good time to state your needs clearly. You do not have to apologize for protecting your time, privacy, or energy. Also listen to your instincts: if someone or something makes you uneasy, take that feeling seriously and look for context, even if you cannot explain it immediately. You can step away, seek advice, or gather more information. Your boundaries express your right to choose what access others have to you.","soulReminder":"You have the right to protect your space, and your boundaries deserve respect. You do not have to let someone cross them to avoid being seen as unfriendly. Trust your instincts as signals worth noticing, while allowing for the possibility that you may need more information. Stay alert without becoming fearful or aggressive. Protect yourself without attacking others. Knowing when to make a boundary clear is one form of strength and self-respect.","questions":"Are my boundaries clear? Has someone crossed one? Do I listen to my instincts? What situations make me uneasy? How do I protect my time and energy? Am I too open in a way that feels uncomfortable? What helps me stay alert without becoming fearful? Where do I need more space?","energyFocus":"Practice setting and maintaining clear boundaries. Say no when needed, even if someone is disappointed. Notice instinctive signals and explore them rather than dismissing or treating them as proof. Protect your time, space, and energy; be thoughtful about who you let close. Consider creating more distance from a relationship or situation that consistently depletes or disrespects you. Practice watchfulness without suspicion. Like a crocodile, know when to wait and when to act."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '17', 'en', 'Khnum - Creator Potter', '庫努姆 - 造物陶匠', '{"titleEn":"Khnum - Creator Potter","symbol":"Ram-headed deity shaping a figure at a potter''s wheel"}', '{"godStory":"Khnum is a ram-headed creator god, shown at a potter''s wheel shaping human forms from clay. As an ancient maker deity, he embodies creation as a process that takes time, patience, and skill. In his hands, raw material takes shape. The potter''s wheel is an image of transformation from substance to form, and of the care involved in making something. Khnum''s work is gradual and precise, honoring the process as much as the finished creation.","coreMeaning":"Khnum represents patient creation, craftsmanship, time, and attention to detail. This card is about understanding that meaningful work cannot always be rushed. Khnum''s image invites you to treat your life and projects as works in progress, shaped through repeated effort and adjustment. Each person is unique, but you do not have to believe that every detail of life was designed in advance. Cultivate what you are making layer by layer, and allow it time to develop.","coreEnergy":"Patience, craft, creation, shaping, detail, time, skill, precision, process, and art. Khnum''s energy is patient, focused, and attentive. It understands that substantial work takes time and does not panic because progress is gradual. Like a potter shaping clay, this energy attends to each step and detail. Perfection is not required; care, practice, and revision help the work become what it can be.","guidance":"Shape your creation patiently. Do not give up just because results are not immediate. Like pottery, a project or goal may need layers of work, adjustment, and refinement. Focus on the craft and on what you can learn from the process, not only the final result. You can also reshape parts of your life that no longer fit by making small, deliberate changes. You are not required to redesign everything at once. Remember: your efforts shape your path, while many factors remain outside your control.","soulReminder":"Your life is still taking shape, and change can require time, patience, and care. Do not compare your pace with someone else''s; people work with different circumstances and timelines. Meaningful work is rarely completed in one stroke. Value each step, including the ones that teach you what to adjust. You can begin again and make changes more than once. Create with your hands, give yourself time to practice, and bring care to what you are making.","questions":"What am I creating or developing? Am I giving it enough time? Do I respect the process? Where could more attention to detail help? What would I like to reshape in my life? Am I becoming impatient with gradual progress? How can I enjoy the act of making? What skills am I developing?","energyFocus":"Focus on the process rather than only the outcome, and find value in each step. Practice patience with yourself and the work. Pay attention to craft and details without demanding perfection. Make something tangible with your hands: write, draw, sculpt, weave, cook, or repair. Change an area of life gradually, one adjustment at a time. Respect the time things need, avoid forcing quick results, and care for what you are creating."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '18', 'en', 'Tefnut - Goddess of Moisture', '泰芙努特 - 濕氣女神', '{"titleEn":"Tefnut - Goddess of Moisture","symbol":"Lioness-headed goddess associated with moisture and dew"}', '{"godStory":"Tefnut is a lioness-headed goddess associated with moisture, dew, and the water essential to life. As a daughter of Ra in Egyptian mythology, she brings moisture and vitality to the dry landscape. In this reading, water can symbolize emotional movement, tears, and the need for nourishment. Just as living things depend on water, people need ways to feel and express emotion. Tefnut''s moistening energy evokes care for a heart that has felt dry or overextended.","coreMeaning":"Tefnut represents emotional flow, emotional well-being, tears, nourishment, softness, and permission to feel and express emotion. This card invites you to let feelings move rather than suppressing or accumulating them. Tefnut reminds you that tears are not weakness; they can be one natural response to what you are experiencing. She encourages you to bring care to areas of life that feel dry, rigid, or neglected, and to make room for more flexibility and emotional expression.","coreEnergy":"Flow, feeling, nourishment, softness, tears, release, healing, water, and care. Tefnut''s energy is fluid, nourishing, and gentle. It allows emotions to be noticed and expressed rather than bottled up. Like rain on dry land, this image can suggest bringing softness to a guarded heart. Emotional well-being can include many responses, not only crying; find forms of expression that feel safe and supportive for you.","guidance":"Let yourself feel emotions without judging them. If you need to cry, you may allow it; if you feel sadness, anger, or something else, find a safe and healthy way to express it. You do not have to lock feelings away. Like rain nourishing the earth, tears can be one part of processing an experience, but they are not required for healing. Notice areas of life that feel dry or rigid and consider bringing in more rest, connection, flexibility, or care. Attend to ordinary needs such as drinking water, without expecting it to resolve emotional distress.","soulReminder":"Your tears are a natural human response, and you do not need to feel ashamed of crying. Emotions are not your enemies, though they can be hard to carry. With support, you can let a feeling move through you without needing to obey it or be overwhelmed by it. Like water, feelings may seek expression; writing, art, movement, conversation, or rest can offer a safe outlet. Softness can be a strength. Give your inner life care and let it move at its own pace.","questions":"Am I suppressing feelings? Do I allow myself to cry if I need to? How is my emotional well-being? Which parts of life feel dry or rigid? What feeling might need expression? How do I relate to water and nature? Where could I be more flexible? What helps me feel emotionally supported?","energyFocus":"Support healthy emotional expression without suppressing feelings or becoming overwhelmed by them. Let tears come if they do, without judging them. Try journaling, art, movement, or conversation as ways to process what you feel. Spend time near water, bathe, swim, or listen to rainfall if those experiences soothe you. Care for your body''s basic needs, including hydration and rest. Bring more flexibility into routines that feel rigid. Like water, adapt and flow while honoring your needs and limits."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '19', 'en', 'Shu - God of Air', '舒 - 風神', '{"titleEn":"Shu - God of Air","symbol":"Figure holding apart the sky and creating space to breathe"}', '{"godStory":"Shu is the god of air who separates the sky goddess Nut from the earth god Geb, creating the space in which life can exist. In depictions, he holds up the sky and gives the world room to breathe. He represents air, breath, distance, and freedom. Without the space between sky and earth, they would press together and leave no room for life. His story evokes the importance of appropriate space for growth.","coreMeaning":"Shu represents space, breath, distance, clarity, separation, freedom, and the element of air. This card is about creating room for people and ideas to exist and grow. Appropriate distance can be healthy; it is not necessarily rejection or coldness, but can allow both people to breathe and develop. Shu invites you to make space in a suffocating relationship or situation so that fresh air, clarity, and choice can enter.","coreEnergy":"Space, breath, separation, clarity, freedom, air, openness, lightness, and movement. Shu''s energy is light and circulating. It can represent clearing stagnation, creating room for a new perspective, and allowing more freedom. This is the wisdom of distance: stepping back is not always abandonment; sometimes it helps you see clearly and return with care.","guidance":"Give yourself and others more room. Are you too closely entangled with someone or something to hear your own needs? Consider stepping back or creating more breathing space. This need not be rejection; it can be a healthy boundary. Take a few comfortable breaths and notice what changes in your body and thoughts. If your mind feels crowded, a pause may help you sort through it. Open a window if practical and let fresh air into your space. Sometimes a little room is what you need to see more clearly.","soulReminder":"You need room to grow, like a plant needs space to extend its branches. Distance is not automatically a lack of love; it can allow each person to be more fully themselves. Closeness without room to breathe can become difficult, and caring relationships make space for individual needs. Remember your breath when you feel anxious or overwhelmed. Creating space is not creating emptiness; it can create possibility. You have the right to breathe, pause, and decide what feels right.","questions":"Do I have enough space? Do I feel crowded or overwhelmed? Are my relationships too entangled? Would some distance help? Am I breathing consciously? What needs more movement or openness? How can I create room for myself? Do I allow others space to breathe?","energyFocus":"Create and maintain the space you need. Step back from a suffocating situation and allow everyone room to breathe. Practice a few slow, comfortable breaths, especially during stress. Open a window or go outdoors for fresh air when possible. Clear physical clutter or make open time in your schedule. Remember that distance can bring clarity and renewal. Let your choices feel spacious, flexible, and light."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '20', 'en', 'Wadjet - Cobra Goddess', '瓦吉特 - 眼鏡蛇女神', '{"titleEn":"Wadjet - Cobra Goddess","symbol":"Cobra goddess, associated with the uraeus on the royal crown"}', '{"godStory":"Wadjet is a cobra goddess associated with the uraeus, the rearing cobra on the royal crown, a symbol of sovereignty and divine protection. A cobra raises its hood when threatened, a display that warns others and prepares it to defend itself. Wadjet can represent decisive protection, authority, and firm boundaries. Venom is both a weapon and a defense in the natural world; as a symbol, it reminds us that power calls for discernment and that protecting your territory does not require aggression.","coreMeaning":"Wadjet represents authority, protection, decisiveness, boundaries, and the courage to defend yourself. This card invites you to protect your needs and claim your space. Wadjet teaches that gentleness is not the only way to respond; sometimes a clear, firm limit is needed. When a boundary is crossed, you can state it plainly and decide what action to take. This card also evokes kundalini energy in some spiritual traditions; treat that as a personal symbol or practice, not a guaranteed force or a reason to push your body.","coreEnergy":"Authority, protection, decisiveness, strength, boundaries, sovereignty, and fierce self-respect. Wadjet''s energy is powerful, clear, and unwilling to accept intrusion. It can represent responding promptly and firmly to a crossed boundary. Like the cobra''s warning display, this energy can communicate limits without attacking. Authority here means knowing your worth and choices, not controlling other people.","guidance":"Protect yourself decisively when someone belittles you or crosses a boundary. If possible, state the limit clearly and calmly, and decide what you will do if it is ignored. You do not need to apologize for taking your needs seriously. Wadjet also invites you to connect with your own vitality. If practices such as yoga or meditation interest you, approach them gently and safely; you do not need to awaken a specific energy to claim your strength. Stand firmly in your values and choices.","soulReminder":"You have the right to protect your boundaries and deserve to be treated with respect. You do not need to accept belittling behavior to seem kind. Gentleness is valuable, and firmness may also be necessary. Your inner vitality is yours to explore at your own pace; no one can promise a particular spiritual awakening. You can be alert, strong, and beautiful without being dangerous. Let your authority protect your choices and dignity without taking away anyone else''s.","questions":"Am I defending my boundaries? Where do I need to use my voice or authority? Am I allowing someone to belittle me? How do I experience my own vitality? Can I be more decisive? What does strength look like without aggression? When should I step away rather than confront?","energyFocus":"Practice clear, firm communication. When a boundary is crossed, respond as promptly and safely as the situation allows. Stand comfortably, make eye contact if appropriate, and speak in a steady voice. Explore yoga, meditation, or movement only in ways that feel safe and suitable for you; avoid forcing intense practices. Do not apologize for your strength, but use it responsibly. Let protection and authority be grounded in respect for yourself and others."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '21', 'en', 'Neith - Weaver Goddess', '奈特 - 織女神', '{"titleEn":"Neith - Weaver Goddess","symbol":"Goddess with a loom and bow and arrows"}', '{"godStory":"Neith is an ancient creator goddess depicted with a loom and bow, joining the images of maker and warrior. She is described as weaving the structure of the world, where each thread contributes to a larger pattern. She is also associated with hunting and strategy. Her loom evokes deliberate creation, while her arrows suggest focus and direction. Together, these symbols point to the wisdom of planning and the choices that shape what comes next.","coreMeaning":"Neith represents creativity, pattern-making, strategy, wisdom, autonomy, and intentional design. This card invites you to notice the patterns formed by your choices and consider which ones you want to continue. Neith reminds you that your decisions influence your life, while circumstances beyond your control also play a part. She encourages creative and strategic thinking so you can respond to challenges and build toward a life that reflects your values.","coreEnergy":"Creation, weaving, patterns, strategy, wisdom, autonomy, creativity, and long-range thinking. Neith''s energy is intentional and resourceful. Like a weaver, it notices how separate threads connect and how a design takes shape over time. This is thoughtful creativity: not random or fully controllable, but shaped by attention, skill, and willingness to revise.","guidance":"Look at patterns in your life. Which ones support you, and which would you like to change? Each choice can influence what happens next, though no one controls every outcome. If you face a challenge, think strategically instead of simply pushing harder. A different route or connection may help. Neith also invites hands-on creativity: weaving, sewing, or another craft that combines separate elements into a whole. Use planning and imagination together, then adapt as you learn.","soulReminder":"You have agency in the choices you make, and you can begin changing a pattern even if the past was different. You are not passively bound to a fixed destiny, nor are you solely responsible for everything that happens. Every choice is a thread, but the whole tapestry also includes circumstance and other people. Creation takes patience, skill, and a vision that can evolve. Treat your life as something you can shape with care, one decision at a time.","questions":"What patterns am I creating or repeating? What choices could shape the future I want? Am I responding actively or passively? Is my life design intentional? What pattern would I like to change? How could strategy help me? Where does my creativity show up? What story am I weaving?","energyFocus":"Make choices with intention and consider their longer-term effects. Notice your recurring patterns and decide which to keep or change. Think strategically before acting, and allow yourself to revise a plan. Try a practical creative activity such as weaving, sewing, or another craft. Connect different ideas and see how they might work together. Hold a clear vision while building it thread by thread. You are the artist of your choices, and your life remains a work in progress."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '22', 'en', 'Khonsu - Moon God', '孔蘇 - 月神', '{"titleEn":"Khonsu - Moon God","symbol":"Young moon deity, associated with the waxing and full moon"}', '{"godStory":"Khonsu is a youthful moon god, often shown with lunar symbols that evoke the passage of time and its cycles. In myth and imagery, he travels across the night sky and offers light in the darkness. The moon waxes and wanes, suggesting natural rhythms and change. Khonsu is also associated with healing and timekeeping. His gentle light may be enough to help you find a path through a dark moment, even when it does not illuminate everything at once.","coreMeaning":"Khonsu represents cycles, timing, rhythm, change, the moon, and light in darkness. This card invites you to respect life''s changing phases and recognize that different times may call for planting, growth, harvest, or rest. Khonsu encourages you to work with your own rhythms rather than against them. When you feel lost, a small source of hope or support can help you find the next step.","coreEnergy":"Cycles, timing, rhythm, change, the moon, time, patience, healing, and light in darkness. Khonsu''s energy is cyclical and responsive. It reminds you that circumstances and energy can change, and that no single phase lasts forever. This is the wisdom of allowing time and choosing when to act, wait, or rest, rather than assuming every moment is suited to the same effort.","guidance":"Work with the rhythm of your life. Not every moment is right for action; sometimes you need rest, reflection, or patience. Notice what phase you may be in: beginning, growing, gathering results, or letting go. Respond to that phase instead of forcing a step that does not fit. You can use moon phases as a reflective framework if it resonates—perhaps setting intentions at a new moon or reviewing what you are ready to release at a full moon. If you feel lost, seek a small source of light, support, or information to guide your next step.","soulReminder":"Everything changes, and no single phase lasts forever. Like the moon, your energy and circumstances may shift. Do not demand that you shine at full brightness all the time; quieter phases can also have value. Darkness does not guarantee that light will return on a specific schedule, but it need not be the whole story. Be patient while staying attentive to choices and support available to you. Respect your rhythms and the rhythms of life around you.","questions":"What phase am I in right now? Is this a time for action or rest? Am I respecting my natural rhythm? Do lunar cycles hold meaning for me? Am I forcing something before it is ready? Can I be patient with change? What is shifting in my life? How can I respond more flexibly to timing?","energyFocus":"Pay attention to timing and rhythm. Notice the natural cycles in your energy and routine. If moon phases are meaningful to you, use them as reminders for reflection rather than rules. Respect changes in your capacity instead of demanding constant productivity. Identify the phase you are in and choose a fitting action, or rest when needed. Practice patience while remaining engaged with your life. Work with changing conditions instead of fighting them."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '23', 'en', 'Meskhenet - Birth Goddess', '梅斯肯特 - 誕生女神', '{"titleEn":"Meskhenet - Birth Goddess","symbol":"Birth bricks representing the moment a new life begins"}', '{"godStory":"Meskhenet is a goddess associated with childbirth and the beginning of life. In ancient Egyptian imagery, she is connected with birth bricks used during delivery and is described as present at a child''s birth, sometimes determining or speaking to that child''s fate. Her image honors beginnings: the moment something comes into being, from a child to an idea or a new version of oneself. It evokes potential and the first breath of a new chapter.","coreMeaning":"Meskhenet represents beginnings, potential, birth, hope, and new possibilities. Something new may be taking shape in your life. Each beginning carries uncertainty as well as promise. Meskhenet invites you to treat new projects, relationships, or identities gently, allowing time for them to develop. A beginning can be meaningful without being destined or guaranteed to succeed. Trust the process enough to take a first step, and give it care as it grows.","coreEnergy":"New life, beginnings, potential, hope, possibility, vulnerability, freshness, and wonder. Meskhenet''s energy is new and full of promise. It celebrates a start and the care needed to protect it. Like a newborn, a new idea may be vulnerable and benefit from time and support. A fresh beginning can open options, though it does not reveal the whole future at once.","guidance":"Welcome a new beginning. Something may be forming in your life—a project, relationship, identity, or understanding. Treat it gently and allow it time to develop. Do not expect immediate maturity; just as learning to walk takes time, a new start needs room to grow. If you are developing an idea or plan, take a small, supportive step. Trust the process enough to keep exploring, even when it includes uncertainty or effort. Celebrate a beginning without assuming you know its final shape.","soulReminder":"You may be witnessing or experiencing a meaningful beginning. New things can be vulnerable and need patience and care. Do not rush growth; allow time and space. Every great creation began small. A new start holds potential, even if you cannot see the whole picture yet. Give it attention and let your understanding develop. Welcome beginnings as invitations to explore, not promises about what fate has already decided.","questions":"What is beginning in my life? Am I ready to explore a new start? Am I treating something new with care? Have I allowed enough time? What potential is waiting to unfold? Do I trust this process enough to take a first step? How can I celebrate a beginning? What direction might this new chapter take?","energyFocus":"Notice what is beginning and offer it gentle care. Give a new project, relationship, or part of yourself time, space, and nourishment. Avoid rushing for results; celebrate small milestones and the learning along the way. Protect a vulnerable idea from premature criticism if that helps, while remaining open to thoughtful feedback. Trust that potential can unfold gradually. Honor the beginning without needing to know its entire future."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '24', 'en', 'Serket - Scorpion Goddess', '塞爾凱特 - 蠍子女神', '{"titleEn":"Serket - Scorpion Goddess","symbol":"Scorpion associated with the goddess and protective power"}', '{"godStory":"Serket is a scorpion goddess associated with protection and healing. The scorpion''s venom can harm, while some venoms have also been studied or used in medicine; this contrast makes it an image of danger and healing held together. Serket was invoked for protection from venomous creatures and other dangers. Her story can symbolize the courage to face what feels poisonous or difficult, while remembering that healing requires care and appropriate support, not exposure to harm.","coreMeaning":"Serket represents protection, courage, transformation, and the work of facing pain. This card invites you to notice what feels harmful in your life—perhaps a relationship dynamic, a recurring thought, or an unresolved hurt—and consider how to respond. Serket teaches that healing may require courage to acknowledge pain rather than avoid it. Pain itself is not medicine, and you do not need to remain in a harmful situation to transform it. Boundaries and support can be part of healing.","coreEnergy":"Protection, courage, deep reflection, transformation, and the complexity of healing. Serket''s energy is profound and brave. It faces difficult material carefully rather than turning away. Like venom that can have different effects depending on context and use, painful experiences can leave lasting effects and may also inform what support you need. This card does not promise that every wound becomes wisdom; it honors the courage of tending to what hurts.","guidance":"Notice what feels harmful and consider a safe way to address it. Avoiding a problem can sometimes let it grow, but confronting it does not mean putting yourself in danger. Ask whether a relationship or situation needs a boundary, more support, or distance. If you are dealing with trauma, intense distress, or a health concern, seek help from a qualified professional rather than trying to treat it through spiritual work alone. You can protect yourself while beginning to understand what has happened.","soulReminder":"Your pain matters, and you deserve support in facing it. You do not have to turn suffering into a lesson or prove your strength by handling it alone. With time and care, you may learn from what happened, but healing is not guaranteed to follow a specific path. A wound can inform your wisdom without defining your worth. Serket symbolizes protection as well as courage; let both guide you as you decide what to face and what help you need.","questions":"What in my life feels harmful or draining? Am I avoiding a difficult issue? What support would help me face it safely? What have my experiences taught me, if anything? How can I protect myself while seeking healing? Am I ready to explore this, or do I need more time? What boundaries are needed?","energyFocus":"Notice what feels harmful and respond with care. Consider support from a therapist, doctor, or trusted person for difficult experiences. Treat pain as information, not as an enemy or a teacher you must obey. Protect yourself with clear boundaries and distance when needed. If you choose a reflective practice, keep it gentle and grounded. Healing may involve patience, practical care, and support. You can face what happened without exposing yourself to further harm."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '25', 'en', 'Bes - Dwarf God', '貝斯 - 侏儒神', '{"titleEn":"Bes - Dwarf God","symbol":"Dwarf deity shown making a playful face and wearing a lion skin"}', '{"godStory":"Bes is a protective household deity, often depicted with a distinctive face, playful expression, and lion skin. He is associated with the protection of homes, children, and women, and with music, dance, and humor. In ancient Egyptian life, images of Bes could offer comfort and protection in everyday settings. His story reminds us not to judge by appearance: kindness and strength can be found in unexpected forms. He guards ordinary but meaningful parts of life.","coreMeaning":"Bes represents joy, humor, household protection, simple pleasures, inner kindness, and the magic of everyday life. This card is about noticing small happiness instead of overlooking it. Bes teaches that magic need not be grand; it can be found in laughter, music, and affection. He invites you to care for the playful, curious part of yourself and to look beyond appearances when judging people or situations.","coreEnergy":"Joy, humor, protection, simplicity, family, laughter, music, dance, open-mindedness, and everyday wonder. Bes''s energy is cheerful, protective, and unpretentious. It finds strength in humor and small pleasures. Like Bes''s unexpected appearance paired with kindness, this energy reminds you that outward impressions do not tell the whole story. Ordinary life can hold sacred meaning.","guidance":"Make room for joy and simple pleasures. Have you been so serious that fun has disappeared? Do something playful: sing, dance, joke, or enjoy a favorite activity. Humor can help shift a heavy mood, though it does not replace addressing a real problem. Also tend to your home and the people you care about; create a space that feels warm and safe. Protect your inner child—the curious, playful part of you. Do not judge yourself or others by appearance; character is shown in care and action.","soulReminder":"Your worth is not determined by appearance or by meeting someone else''s standard. Kindness, humor, and care matter. Life is short, so leave room for play and laughter. Simple joys can be deeply meaningful, and warmth at home may matter more than outside recognition. Nurture your inner child, the part of you that knows how to be curious and enjoy a moment. Look beyond appearances, in yourself and others, and notice the goodness that may be there.","questions":"Do I allow myself to feel joy? Is there enough laughter in my life? How do I care for my home and loved ones? Am I judging someone by appearance? Is my inner child getting room to play? Do I notice wonder in ordinary life? Have I become too serious? How could I bring more humor into a challenge?","energyFocus":"Notice simple pleasures and do something that makes you smile. Bring more music, dance, or humor into your daily routine. Make your home feel welcoming and safe. Nourish your inner child with play and curiosity. Look for kindness and character beyond appearances. Use laughter to create connection when appropriate, not to dismiss someone''s pain. Celebrate small moments; they are part of what makes life meaningful."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '26', 'en', 'Taweret - Hippo Goddess', '塔沃瑞特 - 河馬女神', '{"titleEn":"Taweret - Hippo Goddess","symbol":"Protective hippo goddess, fierce yet nurturing"}', '{"godStory":"Taweret is a hippo goddess associated with protecting pregnant people and newborns. Her composite form draws on powerful animals, and she can look fierce while acting as a guardian. Female hippos are known to defend their young, making the animal a vivid symbol of protective care. Taweret represents fierce, nurturing protection and the resolve to care for those you love. Her image honors guardianship, while reminding us that care can take many forms.","coreMeaning":"Taweret represents protective care, nurturing, new life, fierce love, and creative abundance. This card invites you to protect and nurture something that is growing, whether a child, a creative project, or a new part of yourself. Care can be both tender and strong. Taweret encourages you to create a supportive environment for what matters to you, without assuming that protecting it means controlling every outcome.","coreEnergy":"Nurturing, protection, fierce love, creativity, care, strength, and guardianship. Taweret''s energy combines power with tenderness. It represents standing up for someone or something you care about while also providing nourishment and steadiness. This protective instinct can be valuable, and it works best when guided by judgment, respect, and attention to everyone''s needs.","guidance":"Protect and nurture what you are bringing into being. Are you developing a project, idea, relationship, or new sense of self? Give it a supportive space in which to grow, without feeling pressured to reveal it before you are ready. Connect with your nurturing capacity, regardless of gender. It includes tenderness and a willingness to protect, but does not require self-sacrifice. Care for your own body and needs, too. If pregnancy or fertility is personally relevant, seek qualified medical care rather than relying on a spiritual reading.","soulReminder":"You have the capacity to create and protect what matters to you. You do not need to apologize for having protective instincts, and you can stand up for people you love. Creativity can bring new things into your life, whether or not they are children. Nurturing is not weakness, and strong protection need not become control. Guard your boundaries, care for your own needs, and let your heart remain tender as you support what is growing.","questions":"Am I protecting what I am creating? What new thing needs nurturing? How do I express my caring or maternal side? Where do I need both gentleness and strength? Am I making room for something new to grow? Do I care for my own body and needs? How can I balance protection with trust?","energyFocus":"Create a supportive environment for something that is developing. Give a project, relationship, or new aspect of yourself room to grow. Connect with nurturing energy in a way that feels authentic to you, regardless of gender. Protect your boundaries and what you care about, while remaining open to other people''s autonomy. Be gentle where care is needed and firm where protection is appropriate. Look after your own well-being as part of the process."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '27', 'en', 'Ammit - Devourer', '阿米特 - 吞噬者', '{"titleEn":"Ammit - Devourer","symbol":"Composite being with crocodile head, lion forequarters, and hippo hindquarters"}', '{"godStory":"Ammit is a composite being, combining the head of a crocodile, the forequarters of a lion, and the hindquarters of a hippopotamus. In Egyptian funerary belief, she waits near the judgment of the dead and devours the heart of a person who fails the weighing against Ma''at''s feather. She is not simply a symbol of evil; she represents the serious consequences of judgment in that religious tradition. In this reading, her image can prompt reflection on accountability and the truths we may avoid.","coreMeaning":"Ammit represents consequences, truth, accountability, and the parts of a false image we may need to release. This card invites you to recognize that actions can affect other people and that avoiding responsibility may deepen harm. Ammit''s myth is a reminder to examine yourself honestly, take responsibility where appropriate, and let go of a mask that no longer reflects you. This is not a claim that the universe punishes every mistake or that you should condemn yourself; accountability can include repair and change.","coreEnergy":"Consequences, truth, justice, transformation, honesty, responsibility, and release of pretense. Ammit''s energy is stern and direct, asking for genuine reflection. Like the devourer in myth, it can symbolize letting an untrue self-presentation fall away so that what remains is more honest. No one is exempt from consequences, but consequences are not always fair or predictable. Use this energy to face reality, not to threaten or shame yourself.","guidance":"Face a truth and consider the consequences of your actions. If you have acted dishonestly or hurt someone, take responsibility and consider what repair is possible. Do not evade the issue or rationalize harm, but also avoid defining yourself only by a mistake. Ammit invites you to examine where you wear a mask or act against your values. You can choose a more honest way forward. Let go of a role that no longer feels genuine, but do not make a drastic change without considering your safety and responsibilities.","soulReminder":"You can face consequences and still be worthy of care and change. You do not need to hide from what happened, and you do not need to reduce yourself to your worst choice. Accountability can include listening, making amends where possible, and changing future behavior. Be honest without becoming cruel to yourself. Let go of pretense and keep what is genuine. When something needs clearing, take responsibility at a pace that is safe and constructive.","questions":"What responsibility do I need to take? Is there an issue I am avoiding? Am I being honest with myself? What mask might I be wearing? Do my actions reflect my values? Is there harm I can repair? Am I ready to face a difficult truth? What would a more genuine choice look like?","energyFocus":"Focus on honesty and accountability. Face the consequences of your actions without evasion or self-condemnation. If you have caused harm, consider a sincere apology or a practical repair, respecting the other person''s boundaries. Examine any pretense in your life and decide what no longer fits. Return to what feels genuine, even if that means letting go of an old identity. Let responsibility, honesty, and care guide the process."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '28', 'en', 'Apep - Serpent of Chaos', '阿佩普 - 混沌之蛇', '{"titleEn":"Apep - Serpent of Chaos","symbol":"Vast serpent of chaos trying to swallow the sun"}', '{"godStory":"Apep is a vast serpent of chaos who, in myth, tries each night to swallow the solar barque of Ra and prevent the sun from rising. He represents primordial disorder, darkness, and obstacles to renewal. In ancient stories, the gods struggle against him to maintain order and the sun''s journey. In this reading, Apep can symbolize a difficult challenge or force that seems to disrupt your progress. The myth also reminds us that confronting obstacles can require courage, persistence, and support.","coreMeaning":"Apep represents serious challenges, uncertainty, and the effort required to move through darkness. This card acknowledges that some obstacles are real and need practical attention. Apep''s myth suggests that light and order may require ongoing care; progress is not always permanent or effortless. It invites you to recognize what you are facing, gather support, and keep going where possible, without assuming that every challenge has a simple victory waiting at the end.","coreEnergy":"Challenge, darkness, disorder, persistence, courage, and the work of overcoming obstacles. Apep''s energy is confrontational and difficult. It can symbolize a threat or barrier that asks you to respond with care and resolve. Like the serpent opposing the sun, this image can represent a recurring struggle. Remember that not every obstacle can be defeated by willpower alone; strategy, allies, rest, and changing course may also be necessary.","guidance":"Face a challenge with courage, but first assess what it requires. Do not minimize the difficulty or let it overwhelm you. Gather the resources, skills, and support you need; you do not have to face it alone. Some problems return and need ongoing attention, while others may call for boundaries, help, or a different route. After making progress, keep caring for the conditions that support it. Balance vigilance with rest so the struggle does not consume your whole life.","soulReminder":"You may be more capable than you feel, and persistence can help you through a difficult period. You do not have to treat every recurring challenge as a battle or believe that victory is guaranteed. Progress may be gradual, and asking for help is part of strength. Let the image of dawn offer hope without demanding that you overcome everything alone. Face darkness with care, and remember to seek light, allies, and rest along the way.","questions":"What real challenge am I facing? What do I need to work through? Do I have the support and resources I need? Am I underestimating the difficulty or letting it overwhelm me? Where can persistence help, and where might another approach be wiser? What has helped me face darkness before? How can I protect my energy while addressing this?","energyFocus":"Identify the obstacle clearly rather than denying or minimizing it. Gather the people, resources, and information that can help. Develop resilience, while recognizing that the challenge may require sustained effort or a different strategy. Stay attentive without becoming consumed by fear. Celebrate progress and rest when you need to recover. Keep choosing actions that support clarity and hope, without treating each day as a battle you must win."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '29', 'en', 'Meretseger - Mountain Goddess', '梅瑞特瑟爾 - 山神', '{"titleEn":"Meretseger - Mountain Goddess","symbol":"Cobra goddess associated with the mountain and silence"}', '{"godStory":"Meretseger, whose name is often translated as “She Who Loves Silence,” was associated with the pyramid-shaped peak above the Theban necropolis. A cobra goddess, she could be understood as both compassionate and stern. In the beliefs of the community that honored her, she protected the burial grounds and was connected with justice. Her mountain suggests stillness, solitude, and a steady presence. This card evokes the wisdom that can come from quiet reflection, without requiring you to withdraw from people who care about you.","coreMeaning":"Meretseger represents silence, solitude, reflection, insight, steadiness, and integrity. This card invites you to find a quiet place amid the noise of the world and listen to your own thoughts. Not every answer comes from outside; sometimes reflection helps you discover what you already know or what questions you still need to ask. Meretseger encourages solitude as a chosen space for clarity, balanced with connection and support.","coreEnergy":"Silence, solitude, reflection, the mountain, stability, depth, integrity, and inner listening. Meretseger''s energy is quiet, steady, and profound. It does not need outside validation or constant activity. Like a mountain, it evokes a stable place from which to observe. Quiet can help you hear yourself, though being alone is not always wise or healing; choose the amount of solitude that supports your well-being.","guidance":"Seek some quiet and time alone if you need it. Step away from noise and find a peaceful place, whether outdoors or within your home. In stillness, you may notice something that was obscured by distraction. This may be a time for reflection rather than more social activity, but do not isolate yourself if you need support. Meditation, a solitary walk, or journaling may help you reconnect. You do not need to explain or defend every choice; sometimes a pause is enough. Stay steady without closing yourself off.","soulReminder":"Quiet can hold strength, and solitude can create room for insight. Being alone by choice is not the same as being isolated or unsupported. You do not need to continually prove or explain who you are. Like a mountain, you can seek steadiness while still allowing yourself to change. Listening can bring wisdom, and reaching out can also be wise. Find the balance between inner silence and the connection you need.","questions":"Do I have enough quiet in my life? Am I making room for solitude? What do I notice when things are quiet? What is my inner voice saying? What inner challenge am I ready to explore? Is there too much noise or stimulation? What can silence teach me? How can I feel more steady?","energyFocus":"Make intentional space for silence and reflection. Reduce stimulation for a while and spend time alone in a way that feels restorative. Try quiet meditation or a solo walk in nature. Listen inwardly without demanding that a truth appear immediately. Practice steadiness by returning to one meaningful value or task. You do not need to explain every feeling or decision, but stay connected to people who support you. Let solitude nourish rather than isolate you."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '30', 'en', 'Imhotep - Architect Sage', '伊姆霍特普 - 建築聖賢', '{"titleEn":"Imhotep - Architect Sage","symbol":"Architect and sage holding a design instrument"}', '{"godStory":"Imhotep was a historical official, architect, and healer who was later revered as a god. He is associated with the Step Pyramid of Djoser at Saqqara, an early monumental stone structure. His legacy represents human learning, innovation, and the possibility of making lasting contributions through skill and service. Imhotep''s story links knowledge with practical application, problem-solving, and work that benefits others.","coreMeaning":"Imhotep represents human potential, applied wisdom, innovation, healing arts, and meaningful contribution through effort. This card reminds you that knowledge and skill can be used to make a difference. Imhotep encourages you to apply what you have learned to create, care, build, or solve a real problem. Lasting value need not be monumental; it can come from work done thoughtfully and in service of others.","coreEnergy":"Wisdom, innovation, healing, practice, contribution, skill, problem-solving, and human potential. Imhotep''s energy is wise, practical, and inventive. It applies knowledge to real situations and builds useful solutions. Like an architect, this energy turns a vision into a structure through planning and execution. This is human potential expressed through work, not a guarantee that effort alone will make someone famous or immortal.","guidance":"Use your knowledge and skills. You can contribute through what you know, what you practice, and how you serve. Do not underestimate your potential, but set goals suited to your experience and circumstances. This may be a good time to build, heal, or create using what you have learned. If you are developing a skill, continue practicing. If your work involves caring for others, let your expertise guide you while respecting professional limits. Be willing to innovate and test a new approach when the old one is not working.","soulReminder":"You are human, and you can still do meaningful work. Wisdom, effort, and service can create something valuable without turning you into a deity or requiring a grand legacy. You do not need to be unusually gifted before you begin. Do not only dream—practice. Do not only study—apply what you learn. Build with your hands, use your knowledge with care, and solve problems one step at a time. Your contribution is found in the actions you take now.","questions":"How can I apply what I know? How might my skills serve others? What am I building that could be useful? Am I making use of my potential? Where could I innovate? What contribution do I want to make? Am I ready to keep practicing? How can I make my ideas more practical?","energyFocus":"Focus on practical application rather than theory alone. Use your knowledge and skills to address real needs. Develop creative solutions without dismissing established methods that work. Deepen a professional or craft skill through practice. Aim for lasting value rather than only short-term recognition. Let service inform your work while maintaining appropriate boundaries. Keep learning and recognize each useful contribution you make."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '31', 'en', 'Seshat - Scribe Goddess', '塞莎特 - 書記女神', '{"titleEn":"Seshat - Scribe Goddess","symbol":"Goddess wearing a star emblem and holding writing tools"}', '{"godStory":"Seshat is the goddess associated with writing, record-keeping, mathematics, and architecture, and is often regarded as Thoth''s female counterpart. She wears a star emblem and holds writing tools and a measuring cord. In Egyptian imagery, she records royal years, victories, and building projects. Seshat represents the value of accurate records, preserving knowledge, planning, and measurement. As a guardian of memory, she helps us imagine wisdom being kept for future generations.","coreMeaning":"Seshat represents record-keeping, knowledge, planning, measurement, accuracy, memory, and the power of writing. This card invites you to record experiences and insights so you can learn from them later. Writing and records can preserve knowledge across time. Seshat also encourages careful planning before action, while leaving room to adjust when circumstances change. Your notes may become a useful resource for future decisions.","coreEnergy":"Recording, preservation, writing, planning, measurement, accuracy, memory, knowledge, organization, and precision. Seshat''s energy is organized and attentive to detail. It recognizes that records can preserve useful knowledge and help bring order to complexity. This is the energy of planning and precise execution, balanced with an understanding that a record is a tool—not a substitute for judgment or new information.","guidance":"Write things down so useful ideas and experiences do not disappear from memory. Start a journal or keep notes on dreams, thoughts, lessons, and progress. If you have a project, plan it carefully: measure, calculate, organize, and prepare before acting. You do not need to wait for a flawless plan, but writing one down can make the next step clearer. Seshat also encourages learning and teaching. This can be a good time to study something new or share knowledge you have gained.","soulReminder":"Your experiences and insights are worth remembering. Writing them down can become a gift to your future self or to someone else. Notes and stories may preserve wisdom, though their value comes from how thoughtfully you use them. Good plans can support success, and careful measurements can improve precision, but not every detail is predictable. Respect the importance of preparation. Like Seshat, organize, record, and preserve what is useful.","questions":"Do I record what I learn? How do I preserve useful knowledge? Is my plan detailed enough for the next step? Do I value accuracy? What might I write about? How is my memory supported? How can I organize what I know? Could something I record help another person?","energyFocus":"Give attention to recording and writing. Keep a journal of experiences, insights, and learning. Write down dreams, goals, and plans if useful. Create a detailed plan for a project and check the measurements or assumptions that matter. Organize information so it is easy to find and update. Keep learning and share knowledge responsibly. Value accuracy and detail while remembering to adapt when new information appears. Treat your writing as a useful tool."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '32', 'en', 'Hapy - Nile God', '哈比 - 尼羅河神', '{"titleEn":"Hapy - Nile God","symbol":"Personification of the Nile, often shown with an abundant body"}', '{"godStory":"Hapy is the personification of the Nile and is often shown with a full figure associated with fertility and nourishment. He represents the Nile''s annual inundation, which deposited fertile silt and supported agriculture in ancient Egypt. Hapy evokes nature''s cycles of renewal, nourishment, and abundance. Without the Nile''s waters, life in the region would have been very different. His image reminds us that communities depend on natural systems and the resources that sustain them.","coreMeaning":"Hapy represents nourishment, life-giving resources, natural cycles, gratitude, and the flow of giving and receiving. Abundance is not only money; it can include care, health, opportunity, community, and support. This card invites you to notice what sustains you and how you can participate in cycles of mutual care. It also reminds you that resources are finite and unevenly available, so abundance is not a guarantee that everyone has enough. Share when you can, receive help when you need it, and respect the sources that nourish life.","coreEnergy":"Nourishment, giving, receiving, cycles, fertility, gratitude, nature''s gifts, and the sources of life. Hapy''s energy is generous and flowing. Like a river that renews the land, it evokes the ways resources can circulate and support life. This is not an assurance that abundance is limitless or always returns in equal measure. It is a reminder to appreciate support, share responsibly, and care for the systems that make life possible.","guidance":"Notice what nourishment is available to you and what you may need to receive. Let go of scarcity beliefs where they no longer fit, but do not deny real financial or material constraints. There may be enough to share in some areas and a need to ask for help in others. If you have resources to spare, consider giving in a way that is sustainable for you—money, time, care, or knowledge. Giving and receiving can both be part of a healthy community. Stay attentive to natural rhythms and the people and places that sustain you.","soulReminder":"You can notice sources of nourishment without pretending that resources are unlimited. Gratitude may help you appreciate what is present, and asking for support is also allowed. Giving does not guarantee that the same thing will return, but mutual care can help people and communities thrive. Respect the natural world that sustains life. You are worthy of nourishment, and you can participate in the flow of care in ways that fit your capacity.","questions":"Am I open to receiving support? What nourishment is already present in my life? How can I share responsibly? What scarcity beliefs do I hold? What am I grateful for? Where might I need help? How does abundance show up beyond money? Am I in a respectful relationship with the natural world?","energyFocus":"Notice resources and support rather than focusing only on what is missing, while staying honest about unmet needs. Practice gratitude by naming what sustains you. Give within your capacity and receive help without shame. Pay attention to ways care, time, opportunity, and knowledge move through your life. Connect with nature and respect its limits. Let generosity be mutual and sustainable, like a flow that nourishes both people and community."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '33', 'en', 'Renenutet - Harvest Goddess', '芮內努特 - 豐收女神', '{"titleEn":"Renenutet - Harvest Goddess","symbol":"Cobra goddess associated with protecting crops and harvests"}', '{"godStory":"Renenutet is a cobra goddess associated with harvests, grain, and the nourishment of children. She was honored during harvest time and connected with agricultural abundance and the food supply. Renenutet evokes the reward of sustained effort, the joy of gathering a crop, and the patience involved in waiting for results. Her story also reminds us that harvest depends on many conditions—not only hard work—including weather, resources, and community support.","coreMeaning":"Renenutet represents harvest, the fruits of effort, nourishment, patience, celebration, and gratitude. This card may point to results from something you have tended over time. Success often takes effort and time, but outcomes are not guaranteed or solely under your control. Renenutet encourages you to keep caring for projects, relationships, or personal growth, and to recognize and celebrate progress when it appears. Let yourself receive credit for your work without assuming every result was earned alone.","coreEnergy":"Harvest, results, abundance, effort, patience, nourishment, celebration, gratitude, and success. Renenutet''s energy is nourishing and celebratory. It invites you to notice the results of work and care, enjoy what has come to fruition, and appreciate the support that helped. This is a moment to recognize progress, while remembering that no one controls every condition involved in a harvest.","guidance":"Notice what your effort has helped grow. If results are arriving, take time to celebrate and receive recognition rather than minimizing your contribution. If the harvest is not yet here, keep tending what matters and consider whether anything needs adjustment. Growth takes time, and sometimes circumstances affect the outcome. Continue watering and weeding your project, and share your success when you can. Let celebration and gratitude include the support you received and the work you did.","soulReminder":"Your effort matters, and you may be entering a time to recognize what you have accomplished. You do not need to question whether you deserve every good result. Receive your progress with pride, celebrate, and share what you can. Harvest is also a chance to nourish others, but generosity should not require self-deprivation. Remember the cycle of planting, tending, waiting, and gathering. Enjoy what you have grown while staying open to what still needs care.","questions":"What is coming to fruition? Am I allowing myself to receive recognition? Do I celebrate progress? What am I grateful for? Which projects still need tending? How can I share what I have without overextending? Has my effort received support? Am I ready to acknowledge this season''s results?","energyFocus":"Notice results and celebrate what you have helped make possible, however small. Receive recognition without minimizing it. Appreciate the people and circumstances that supported your progress. Continue tending projects that are still growing, rather than assuming one success completes everything. Share resources when it fits your capacity. Let gratitude and satisfaction have space, and enjoy the fruits of your effort."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '34', 'en', 'Heka - Magic Personified', '赫卡 - 魔法之神', '{"titleEn":"Heka - Magic Personified","symbol":"Personification of magic and creative power from creation"}', '{"godStory":"Heka is the personification of magic in ancient Egyptian religion and is present in creation stories from the beginning of the world. He represents creative power, intention, and the ritual use of words. In ancient Egypt, magic was not necessarily viewed as supernatural, but as part of how the world worked and could be engaged through knowledge and ritual. Heka''s image suggests that intention, language, and practice can shape experience. It also reminds us that spiritual ritual is a belief practice, not a guarantee of changing external events.","coreMeaning":"Heka represents magic, creativity, intention, words, ritual, and conscious participation in life. This card invites you to notice how thoughts, speech, and action influence your choices and relationships. Heka teaches that intention can guide what you make and how you act. Use your creative capacity with care, choosing clear intentions, supportive language, and focused effort. This is a spiritual metaphor and practice, not a claim that thoughts alone control reality.","coreEnergy":"Magic, creativity, intention, language, ritual, transformation, and conscious making. Heka''s energy is imaginative and creative. It can symbolize bringing intention, words, and actions together to shape a result. This is not a promise that a ritual or belief will make an outcome certain. It is an invitation to participate mindfully in what you can influence, and to consider the effects your choices may have.","guidance":"Use your creative power with intention. Clarify what you want to work toward, express it in words that support you, and take actions consistent with that goal. Your thoughts and speech can shape your perspective and influence your choices, but they cannot guarantee an outcome. Consider a ritual, meditation, or affirmation if it helps you focus, and let it complement practical action. Create a meaningful space for reflection if you like. Magic here is not an escape from reality; it is a way of acting consciously within it.","soulReminder":"You can help shape your life through thought, speech, and action, and that influence carries responsibility. Your words can build understanding or cause harm, so use them with care. Rituals can focus attention and mark an intention, but they do not guarantee results or make you responsible for everything that happens. Let creativity serve your values and the well-being of others. You are a participant in life, able to make meaningful choices without needing supernatural certainty.","questions":"How am I using my creative power? Is my intention clear? What effect do my words have? Am I acting consciously? What practice helps me focus? Do I trust my ability to take a next step? What outcomes are within my influence? How can I use creativity responsibly?","energyFocus":"Practice intentional creation in grounded ways. Write down a clear goal and identify the next practical action. Use supportive language that feels honest rather than making promises to yourself. A personal ritual can provide a meaningful moment of focus; keep it safe and let it support, not replace, action. Notice how your thoughts, speech, and behavior affect your experience. Use your creativity in service of what matters, and stay open to changing course as you learn."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '35', 'en', 'The Balance - Cosmic Equilibrium', '天秤 - 宇宙平衡', '{"titleEn":"The Balance - Cosmic Equilibrium","symbol":"Scales of Ma''at weighing a heart against a feather"}', '{"godStory":"This card depicts the scales of Ma''at, used in ancient Egyptian funerary belief to weigh a person''s heart against the feather of truth. The scales are a powerful symbol of balance, justice, and accountability. They suggest that actions and intentions matter and can affect relationships and communities. This image invites reflection on fairness and truth, without claiming that every real-world outcome is perfectly balanced or that people always receive what they deserve.","coreMeaning":"The Balance represents equilibrium, fairness, consequences, harmony, and the many parts of life that need attention. This card invites you to review your balance and the effects of your choices. Some areas may be receiving too much attention while others are neglected. Ma''at''s image suggests seeking fairness in how you give and receive, how you work and rest, and how you meet material and emotional needs. Balance is not identical treatment in every situation; it is thoughtful adjustment to what is needed.","coreEnergy":"Balance, fairness, harmony, accountability, order, moderation, truth, and proportion. This energy seeks a fair view rather than favoring one side without reflection. Like scales, it asks you to weigh different needs and consequences. Balance is not perfect stillness; it changes as circumstances do. Where something is excessive or lacking, you may be able to make an adjustment and restore greater harmony.","guidance":"Review the main areas of your life honestly. Is there balance between work and rest, giving and receiving, material needs and meaning, or self and others? Notice where you may need to add support or reduce an unsustainable demand. Your choices have consequences, so make them with care and consider the longer term. Trust your sense of fairness, but do not rely on the belief that the universe will automatically correct every injustice. Where you can act, seek practical and compassionate ways to restore balance.","soulReminder":"Your life may need ongoing adjustment to feel more balanced. Balance is dynamic, not a fixed state: you will keep responding to changing needs. Your choices matter, but they do not determine every outcome, and fairness is not always guaranteed. Live with integrity, listen to different perspectives, and be willing to make repairs when needed. You can seek harmony without pretending that every situation is already fair. Let balance be a practice, not a judgment of your worth.","questions":"Does my life feel balanced? Which areas need more or less attention? What effects do my choices have? Am I acting fairly? Where could I restore harmony? How can I make a decision with a longer view? What does balance mean for me right now?","energyFocus":"Notice where your life feels out of balance and identify one adjustment. Seek moderation without forcing everything into equal portions. Consider fairness and long-term consequences when making decisions. Practice honesty and integrity in relationships and situations. Let truth guide your choices while allowing for complexity. Restore inner and outer balance where you can, and accept that this is an ongoing practice."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('egyptian_gods', '36', 'en', 'The Ankh - Key of Life', '安卡 - 生命之鑰', '{"titleEn":"The Ankh - Key of Life","symbol":"Ankh: a cross topped with a loop, symbol of life"}', '{"godStory":"The ankh is one of ancient Egypt''s most recognizable symbols, shaped like a cross with a loop at the top. It is associated with life, vitality, and divine power; Egyptian deities are often shown holding it. The ankh can be understood as a key to life or as an image of enduring spirit within Egyptian belief. In this reading, it reminds you that life is precious and that breath, connection, and vitality deserve attention and care.","coreMeaning":"The Ankh represents life, vitality, breath, renewal, and the sacredness of existence. This card invites you to reconnect with what makes you feel alive and to honor the life you have. It may encourage rest, movement, time in nature, or other activities that restore your sense of vitality. The ankh can symbolize eternal life in spiritual traditions, but this reading cannot establish immortality or promise that energy is limitless. It celebrates being here now.","coreEnergy":"Life, vitality, breath, renewal, sacredness, presence, and affirmation. The Ankh''s energy symbolizes life''s force and the wish to restore vitality. It can invite you to notice what nourishes you and to celebrate existence. Like a key opening a door, the symbol may help you focus on possibilities for renewal. It is a spiritual image, not a guarantee that meditation or breathwork will resolve health concerns or create endless energy.","guidance":"Reconnect with what helps you feel alive. If you feel tired or disconnected, consider rest, comfortable breathing, time outdoors, or an activity that brings meaning and enjoyment. Choose practices that are safe and suitable for you. The Ankh also invites celebration: notice the fact that you are here, and honor ordinary moments. Some people understand it as a reminder of the soul''s enduring nature; you can hold that belief while staying present in this life and caring for your body and needs.","soulReminder":"Your life is precious, and each breath can be a reason to pause and appreciate being here. Try not to take life for granted, while remembering that you do not have to be energetic or joyful every moment. You can seek renewal and meaning, and you deserve support when you feel depleted. Your identity and worth are more than your physical state, but your body and health still matter. Celebrate the life you have in ways that feel genuine to you.","questions":"Do I feel connected to my vitality? What helps me feel alive? Do I celebrate being here? What kind of rest or renewal do I need? How can I care for my body? What meaning does the Ankh hold for me? How might I live more fully today?","energyFocus":"Pay attention to life and vitality in grounded ways. Take a few comfortable breaths and notice your body. Spend time in nature or do an activity that helps you feel present. Celebrate your existence and small moments of joy. Care for your health with appropriate rest and support. Reflect on beliefs about the soul or eternal life as spiritual meaning, not as a reason to neglect this life. Let your choices honor the preciousness of being here."}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('work_your_light', '1', 'en', 'The Ever-unfolding Rose', '永恆綻放的玫瑰', '{"titleEn":"The Ever-unfolding Rose","suit":"Confirmation Card"}', '{"coreMeaning":"Your heart may be opening through what you have lived. Life''s challenges can hurt, and they do not happen because you deserve them; still, over time, you may find ways to grow through pain. The card''s rose unfolds layer by layer, an image of change that asks for patience and care. Be gentle with yourself and let trusted support help you feel grounded. You do not have to stay open to people or situations that are unsafe.","actionGuidance":"Treat yourself with tenderness. Let yourself feel what is present, rest when you need to, and seek support from people you trust. You do not need to rush healing or turn pain into a lesson. Notice one small way to care for yourself today.","inquiryPrompt":null,"activationPrayer":null,"transmissionPrayer":null,"deepInterpretation":{"coreMeaning":"This card symbolizes an opening heart and the gradual process of becoming more fully yourself. Like a rose unfolding petal by petal, you may be moving through change and growth. Even in difficult moments, you can care for the parts of yourself that feel tender. Pain is real and does not automatically make a person wiser, but with time and support, you may find meaning or strength in how you respond. Your experiences can shape you without defining all of who you are. Ask what would help you feel safe enough to remain open to life in a way that respects your boundaries.","higherSelfMessage":"You do not have to prove your strength by letting life break you. Vulnerability can be a source of connection when it is shared in a safe and chosen way. If you choose to see your path as spiritual, you may find that difficult experiences can also make room for new understanding. You are allowed to grieve, pause, and seek help. Let more light in at your own pace; wholeness does not require denying what hurt.","spiritualGuidance":"This is a time to treat yourself gently. Give yourself space to feel, recover, and make sense of your experiences. Do not rush to close your heart, but do not force yourself to remain exposed where you feel unsafe. Ground yourself through nature, rest, supportive relationships, or a reflective practice that suits you. Like a rose needing sunlight, water, and time, you may need consistent care. Practice self-compassion and let tenderness coexist with clear boundaries.","energyQualities":"This card evokes a gentle yet resilient quality, like a rose that is soft but still has thorns. It invites care, patience, and gradual opening. In tarot and oracle symbolism, the rose is often associated with the heart, love, and renewal. You may use this image to reflect on old hurts and what helps you feel acceptance. This is not a promise that every wound will disappear; it is an invitation to support change without demanding a particular pace.","suitableQuestions":"This card may resonate when you feel heartbroken, hurt, or tempted to close yourself off. It can support reflection during loss, the end of a relationship, or any situation that leaves you vulnerable. You might ask: “How can I care for myself through this pain?” “What would help me feel safe enough to stay open to life?” “What support do I need?” “How can I treat myself more gently?” It can also be useful when exploring self-acceptance, emotional healing, and finding strength while honoring vulnerability."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('work_your_light', '2', 'en', 'No', '不', '{"titleEn":"No","suit":"Confirmation Card"}', '{"coreMeaning":"If something does not feel aligned, forcing yourself to say yes may leave you depleted. Not having clear guidance can also be a reason to pause. You may be in a waiting period, with room to rest, gather information, and let your choice become clearer. A card cannot decide for you, but it can prompt you to consider whether “no,” “not now,” or “I need more time” would better honor your needs.","actionGuidance":"Consider saying no, postponing your answer, or taking time to reflect. Check your practical needs, values, and boundaries before deciding.","inquiryPrompt":null,"activationPrayer":null,"transmissionPrayer":null,"deepInterpretation":{"coreMeaning":"This card explores the importance of being able to say no. When you do not feel a clear yes, agreeing under pressure may drain your energy or take you away from your own needs. That does not mean every uncertain choice is wrong; sometimes more information or time is needed. Silence and waiting can create space to reflect, recover, and decide. You are allowed to trust uncertainty enough not to rush, without assuming that the universe is arranging a better opportunity.","higherSelfMessage":"You may be learning about boundaries and self-respect. Saying no is not inherently selfish or cowardly; it can be honest about what you need or can offer. When you decline something, you create room for choices that fit better, though there is no guarantee a particular alternative will appear. Not every opportunity is right for you. Practice recognizing what belongs to your priorities and what does not, without judging yourself for either choice.","spiritualGuidance":"Give yourself permission to say “no,” “not yet,” or “let me think about it.” You do not have to go against your own judgment to meet someone else''s expectations. A period of waiting can be a useful time to rest and consider your options. Trust your body''s signals as information, not as an infallible verdict. Tightness, heaviness, or a lack of enthusiasm may be worth exploring, alongside practical facts and the advice of people you trust. Rest and renew your energy before making a choice if you can.","energyQualities":"This card evokes protection and boundaries, like a screen that helps you decide what to let in. It can support the practice of reclaiming energy from overcommitment or people-pleasing. Notice what responsibilities are yours and what you may have taken on unnecessarily. The image of fallow ground suggests that quiet periods can allow recovery and preparation. Rest is valuable, but it does not mean you must wait passively or assume that a specific opportunity is coming.","suitableQuestions":"This card may help when you need to make a decision but feel unclear. If you feel pressured to answer or are unsure whether an opportunity fits, ask: “Would it be okay to say no right now?” “Would more time help?” “What boundary do I need?” “What information is missing?” “Does this choice reflect my priorities?” It can also help you reflect on rest, energy management, and staying honest under pressure."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
INSERT INTO card_localizations (deck_id, card_key, locale, name, name_secondary, preview_payload, gated_payload) VALUES ('work_your_light', '3', 'en', 'Yes', '是', '{"titleEn":"Yes","suit":"Confirmation Card"}', '{"coreMeaning":"This card offers an encouraging yes: you may be ready to move forward with a choice that feels clear and meaningful. It is not a guarantee that every detail will work out or a reason to ignore risks. Instead of overthinking, consider whether your values, practical circumstances, and inner sense are aligned enough to take a next step.","actionGuidance":"If the choice feels right after thoughtful consideration, take a manageable next step. You do not need a perfect plan, but you can keep your judgment and boundaries in view.","inquiryPrompt":null,"activationPrayer":null,"transmissionPrayer":null,"deepInterpretation":{"coreMeaning":"This card offers an encouraging signal to consider moving forward. It may feel as though conditions are coming together, but you do not need to treat it as a guarantee or stop evaluating your choice. When you have considered what matters, the risks, and what you can reasonably prepare for, a next step may be more useful than endless analysis. You can trust yourself enough to begin while staying willing to learn and adjust.","higherSelfMessage":"Perhaps you have considered this possibility for some time and are ready to explore it. Doubt and fear can sometimes be loud, but they are not always proof that a choice is wrong; likewise, excitement does not prove it is right. Listen to your own values and experience, and consider advice or evidence relevant to the decision. Saying yes can be a way of trusting yourself while remembering that you may revise your path as new information appears.","spiritualGuidance":"If you feel a clear, considered pull toward this choice, take a grounded step. Notice how your body responds, but do not treat expansion, excitement, or calm as infallible signs. You do not need every detail to be settled before beginning, though preparation matters when the stakes are high. The next step may teach you more. Acknowledge what you are grateful for, then move forward at a pace that respects your needs and responsibilities.","energyQualities":"This card evokes momentum, confidence, and openness to possibility, like a favorable wind behind a sail. It can help you feel more willing to act and cross a threshold. That energy may support courage, but it does not remove every obstacle or ensure success. Use the sense of possibility to identify a first step, then meet the real process with patience, flexibility, and care.","suitableQuestions":"This card may be useful when you want encouragement around a choice you have been considering. Ask: “Does this decision fit my values?” “Is now a reasonable time to take a step?” “What would accepting this opportunity require?” “What preparation or support do I need?” “Am I ready to explore this, even if I cannot see the whole path?” Let the card prompt reflection rather than serve as the only basis for a major decision."}}') ON CONFLICT(deck_id, card_key, locale) DO UPDATE SET name = excluded.name, name_secondary = excluded.name_secondary, preview_payload = excluded.preview_payload, gated_payload = excluded.gated_payload, updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP;
